{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg69Cib9qq27h2hiNkbyw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HweUKQxRxHfymTT1oo2xx6","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5426,"cache_read_input_tokens":41327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5426},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab594185-c31c-412a-a5f0-563328d811ca","uuid":"66095f4d-befe-4481-893d-05a7838e32c8","timestamp":"2026-10-16T15:20:27.539Z","request_id":"req_011Cg69CiMmDYSLyLxVTo4m4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HweUKQxRxHfymTT1oo2xx6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-1 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tIntake's detected stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`) is treated as a\n6\tstrong prior. All decisions below confirm or refine it against the FR/NFR\n7\tlist; none diverge from intake's detection because the PRD pins versions and\n8\tlibraries explicitly (greenfield, `--tech-stack react`, Next.js 14 fixed).\n9\t\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## ADR-1: Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + TypeScript strict\n13\t\n14\t**Context:** FR-1 through FR-3, NFR-7, NFR-8 require a scaffolded app with a\n15\tfast, scriptable dev loop (`npm install && db:migrate && db:seed && dev` in\n16\tunder 5 minutes) and clean lint/typecheck/test gates on a fresh clone.\n17\t\n18\t**Decision:** Use Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict mode,\n19\tESLint (`next/core-web-vitals` + `@typescript-eslint/recommended`), Prettier,\n20\tand a `@/*` → `src/*` path alias. No deviation from intake's detection —\n21\tthe PRD fixes these versions explicitly, there is no \"does it fit\" question\n22\tto re-litigate.\n23\t\n24\t**Consequences:** App Router gives server components and route groups\n25\t(`(app)`, `(public)`) for free, which the app-shell/public-layout split\n26\t(FR-30, FR-36) needs anyway. Strict TS + ESLint gates are required for\n27\tNFR-8's clean-clone CI bar.\n28\t\n29\t---\n30\t\n31\t## ADR-2: PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Docker Compose for local dev\n32\t\n33\t**Context:** FR-4 (docker-compose Postgres 16), FR-7 (Prisma schema,\n34\tsingleton `SchoolSettings`), FR-8 (cached Prisma client surviving hot\n35\treload), FR-9 (idempotent seed), NFR-7 (5-minute fresh-clone bring-up).\n36\t\n37\t**Decision:** PostgreSQL 16 in Docker Compose with a named volume;\n38\tPrisma as the sole ORM/migration tool (`db:migrate`, `db:deploy`, `db:seed`,\n39\t`db:reset` npm scripts map directly to Prisma CLI commands).\n40\t\n41\t**Consequences:** `src/server/db.ts` must cache the client on\n42\t`globalThis` in development to avoid exhausting Postgres connections across\n43\thot reloads — a standard Next.js + Prisma pattern, not a new abstraction.\n44\tSeed idempotency (FR-9) means seed logic must upsert, not create.\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## ADR-3: Zod for env validation and all request/response parsing\n49\t\n50\t**Context:** FR-6 (startup env validation with readable errors), FR-14/FR-15\n51\t(pagination + body/query parsing in `http.ts`), FR-13 (`ZodError` →\n52\t`VALIDATION_ERROR` mapping), NFR-6 (test coverage of `env.ts` validation).\n53\t\n54\t**Decision:** Zod is the single validation library, used both for\n55\t`src/lib/env.ts` (process.env schema) and for all API request parsing via\n56\t`parseBody`/`parseQuery`. No duplicate validation layer (e.g., no Joi,\n57\tno hand-rolled checks).\n58\t\n59\t**Consequences:** One error-shape convention (`ZodError`) flows through the\n60\twhole API surface, which keeps `withHandler`'s error-mapping switch (FR-13)\n61\tto a handful of cases instead of per-route error handling.\n62\t\n63\t---\n64\t\n65\t## ADR-4: Centralized API helpers in `src/server/http.ts`\n66\t\n67\t**Context:** FR-10 through FR-16 define `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`,\n68\t`withHandler`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`/`parseQuery` as one cohesive\n69\tmodule; FR-16 (health check) and every future PRD's route handlers depend on\n70\tthis contract.\n71\t\n72\t**Decision:** One shared `src/server/http.ts` module is the only sanctioned\n73\tway routes build responses or parse input — no per-route reimplementation of\n74\tpagination clamping or error mapping.\n75\t\n76\t**Consequences:** Every route handler is a thin wrapper around\n77\t`withHandler(fn)`; Prisma error codes (P2002, P2025) are mapped once, here,\n78\tnot scattered across route files. This is the reuse boundary later PRDs'\n79\troute handlers must respect.\n80\t\n81\t---\n82\t\n83\t## ADR-5: Material UI v9 as the exclusive UI/styling library\n84\t\n85\t**Context:** NFR-1 mandates MUI as the only UI library and bans a long list\n86\tof alternatives (Tailwind, Radix, Chakra, shadcn/ui, Ant Design, etc.) via\n87\tESLint `no-restricted-imports` (FR-19). FR-17/FR-18 pin exact MUI v9\n88\tpackages + the `react-is@18.3.1` override for React 18 compatibility.\n89\tNFR-2 (LCP < 2.5s), NFR-3 (WCAG 2.1 AA), NFR-4 (360–1920px responsive) all\n90\tconstrain how that UI layer is built.\n91\t\n92\t**Decision:** MUI v9 (`@mui/material`, `@mui/material-nextjs`,\n93\t`@mui/icons-material`, `@mui/x-data-grid`, `@mui/x-date-pickers`,\n94\t`@mui/x-charts`) + Emotion for styling, `AppRouterCacheProvider` for SSR\n95\tstyle injection, `cssVariables` theme mode for the light/dark toggle. No\n96\tsecond styling system (no Tailwind, no CSS Modules) — intake's\n97\t`cssPreprocessor: css` fallback reflects \"no CSS-in-JS enum option\", not an\n98\tactual second system.\n99\t\n100\t**Consequences:** All thirteen shared components (FR-20–FR-29) are MUI\n101\tcompositions, not custom-built primitives — this is a library-reuse\n102\tdecision the whole design-system layer inherits. The ESLint ban (FR-19) is\n103\tthe enforcement mechanism, not a style guideline; it fails the build.\n104\t\n105\t---\n106\t\n107\t## ADR-6: React Hook Form for all form state\n108\t\n109\t**Context:** FR-25 requires `FormField` helpers binding React Hook Form's\n110\t`Controller` to MUI inputs (TextField, Select, Autocomplete, Checkbox,\n111\tSwitch, RadioGroup, DatePicker/DateTimePicker).\n112\t\n113\t**Decision:** React Hook Form is the sole form-state library; Zod schemas\n114\t(ADR-3) double as RHF resolvers via `@hookform/resolvers`, keeping one\n115\tvalidation source instead of separate client/server schemas.\n116\t\n117\t**Consequences:** No uncontrolled/ad-hoc form state in any shared component;\n118\tevery form field goes through `Controller`.\n119\t\n120\t---\n121\t\n122\t## ADR-7: Vitest + Testing Library + Playwright + axe-core for testing\n123\t\n124\t**Context:** NFR-6 lists unit/component coverage (withHandler, parsePagination,\n125\tformatInSchoolTz, env.ts, DataTable/ConfirmDialog/useToast, the ESLint rule)\n126\tand Playwright e2e scenarios; NFR-3 requires `@axe-core/playwright` on `/`\n127\tand `/dashboard` with zero serious/critical violations; NFR-8 requires both\n128\t`test` and `test:e2e` npm scripts to pass on a fresh clone.\n129\t\n130\t**Decision:** Vitest + Testing Library for unit/component tests,\n131\tPlaywright (`tests/e2e`) + `@axe-core/playwright` for e2e and accessibility\n132\tgating. No Jest (avoids a second test runner config) — Vitest already\n133\tcovers the Vite/Next toolchain needs with less config.\n134\t\n135\t**Consequences:** Accessibility is a CI gate (zero serious/critical axe\n136\tviolations), not a manual checklist — ties directly to NFR-3's WCAG bar.\n137\t\n138\t---\n139\t\n140\t## ADR-8: Structured logging via a single `src/lib/logger.ts`\n141\t\n142\t**Context:** FR-40 requires `logger.info|warn|error(message, meta?)`\n143\temitting JSON lines in production and readable lines in development.\n144\t\n145\t**Decision:** One logger module, no external logging library (e.g., no\n146\tpino/winston) — the required shape (JSON-in-prod, readable-in-dev, three\n147\tlevels, optional meta) is small enough that a dependency would be\n148\tover-engineering for what `console.*` + a format branch already covers.\n149\t\n150\t**Consequences:** `withHandler` (ADR-4) routes uncaught errors through this\n151\tlogger before returning `INTERNAL` to the client (FR-13), keeping stack\n152\ttraces server-side only.\n153\t\n154\t---\n155\t\n156\t## ADR-9: Security headers and CSP in `next.config.js`, not middleware\n157\t\n158\t**Context:** NFR-5 requires `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`,\n159\t`X-Frame-Options`, and a restrictive CSP.\n160\t\n161\t**Decision:** Set headers via Next.js's built-in `headers()` config\n162\tfunction in `next.config.js` rather than a custom middleware — it's the\n163\tnative platform mechanism for static security headers and needs no request-\n164\ttime logic.\n165\t\n166\t**Consequences:** CSP must explicitly allow `'unsafe-inline'` for styles\n167\t(Emotion/MUI inject inline `<style>` tags at runtime) while keeping\n168\tscript-src restricted to `'self'`.\n169\t\n170\t---\n171\t\n172\t## Status\n173\t\n174\tAll nine decisions trace to at least one FR/NFR id above. No open\n175\tquestions block `arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n176\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab594185-c31c-412a-a5f0-563328d811ca","uuid":"7f0f68e4-fb6f-4f94-a191-d2a7a81ed398","timestamp":"2026-10-16T15:20:27.543Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-1 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n\nIntake's detected stack (`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`) is treated as a\nstrong prior. All decisions below confirm or refine it against the FR/NFR\nlist; none diverge from intake's detection because the PRD pins versions and\nlibraries explicitly (greenfield, `--tech-stack react`, Next.js 14 fixed).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Next.js 14 App Router + React 18 + TypeScript strict\n\n**Context:** FR-1 through FR-3, NFR-7, NFR-8 require a scaffolded app with a\nfast, scriptable dev loop (`npm install && db:migrate && db:seed && dev` in\nunder 5 minutes) and clean lint/typecheck/test gates on a fresh clone.\n\n**Decision:** Use Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict mode,\nESLint (`next/core-web-vitals` + `@typescript-eslint/recommended`), Prettier,\nand a `@/*` → `src/*` path alias. No deviation from intake's detection —\nthe PRD fixes these versions explicitly, there is no \"does it fit\" question\nto re-litigate.\n\n**Consequences:** App Router gives server components and route groups\n(`(app)`, `(public)`) for free, which the app-shell/public-layout split\n(FR-30, FR-36) needs anyway. Strict TS + ESLint gates are required for\nNFR-8's clean-clone CI bar.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Docker Compose for local dev\n\n**Context:** FR-4 (docker-compose Postgres 16), FR-7 (Prisma schema,\nsingleton `SchoolSettings`), FR-8 (cached Prisma client surviving hot\nreload), FR-9 (idempotent seed), NFR-7 (5-minute fresh-clone bring-up).\n\n**Decision:** PostgreSQL 16 in Docker Compose with a named volume;\nPrisma as the sole ORM/migration tool (`db:migrate`, `db:deploy`, `db:seed`,\n`db:reset` npm scripts map directly to Prisma CLI commands).\n\n**Consequences:** `src/server/db.ts` must cache the client on\n`globalThis` in development to avoid exhausting Postgres connections across\nhot reloads — a standard Next.js + Prisma pattern, not a new abstraction.\nSeed idempotency (FR-9) means seed logic must upsert, not create.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Zod for env validation and all request/response parsing\n\n**Context:** FR-6 (startup env validation with readable errors), FR-14/FR-15\n(pagination + body/query parsing in `http.ts`), FR-13 (`ZodError` →\n`VALIDATION_ERROR` mapping), NFR-6 (test coverage of `env.ts` validation).\n\n**Decision:** Zod is the single validation library, used both for\n`src/lib/env.ts` (process.env schema) and for all API request parsing via\n`parseBody`/`parseQuery`. No duplicate validation layer (e.g., no Joi,\nno hand-rolled checks).\n\n**Consequences:** One error-shape convention (`ZodError`) flows through the\nwhole API surface, which keeps `withHandler`'s error-mapping switch (FR-13)\nto a handful of cases instead of per-route error handling.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Centralized API helpers in `src/server/http.ts`\n\n**Context:** FR-10 through FR-16 define `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`,\n`withHandler`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`/`parseQuery` as one cohesive\nmodule; FR-16 (health check) and every future PRD's route handlers depend on\nthis contract.\n\n**Decision:** One shared `src/server/http.ts` module is the only sanctioned\nway routes build responses or parse input — no per-route reimplementation of\npagination clamping or error mapping.\n\n**Consequences:** Every route handler is a thin wrapper around\n`withHandler(fn)`; Prisma error codes (P2002, P2025) are mapped once, here,\nnot scattered across route files. This is the reuse boundary later PRDs'\nroute handlers must respect.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Material UI v9 as the exclusive UI/styling library\n\n**Context:** NFR-1 mandates MUI as the only UI library and bans a long list\nof alternatives (Tailwind, Radix, Chakra, shadcn/ui, Ant Design, etc.) via\nESLint `no-restricted-imports` (FR-19). FR-17/FR-18 pin exact MUI v9\npackages + the `react-is@18.3.1` override for React 18 compatibility.\nNFR-2 (LCP < 2.5s), NFR-3 (WCAG 2.1 AA), NFR-4 (360–1920px responsive) all\nconstrain how that UI layer is built.\n\n**Decision:** MUI v9 (`@mui/material`, `@mui/material-nextjs`,\n`@mui/icons-material`, `@mui/x-data-grid`, `@mui/x-date-pickers`,\n`@mui/x-charts`) + Emotion for styling, `AppRouterCacheProvider` for SSR\nstyle injection, `cssVariables` theme mode for the light/dark toggle. No\nsecond styling system (no Tailwind, no CSS Modules) — intake's\n`cssPreprocessor: css` fallback reflects \"no CSS-in-JS enum option\", not an\nactual second system.\n\n**Consequences:** All thirteen shared components (FR-20–FR-29) are MUI\ncompositions, not custom-built primitives — this is a library-reuse\ndecision the whole design-system layer inherits. The ESLint ban (FR-19) is\nthe enforcement mechanism, not a style guideline; it fails the build.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: React Hook Form for all form state\n\n**Context:** FR-25 requires `FormField` helpers binding React Hook Form's\n`Controller` to MUI inputs (TextField, Select, Autocomplete, Checkbox,\nSwitch, RadioGroup, DatePicker/DateTimePicker).\n\n**Decision:** React Hook Form is the sole form-state library; Zod schemas\n(ADR-3) double as RHF resolvers via `@hookform/resolvers`, keeping one\nvalidation source instead of separate client/server schemas.\n\n**Consequences:** No uncontrolled/ad-hoc form state in any shared component;\nevery form field goes through `Controller`.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Vitest + Testing Library + Playwright + axe-core for testing\n\n**Context:** NFR-6 lists unit/component coverage (withHandler, parsePagination,\nformatInSchoolTz, env.ts, DataTable/ConfirmDialog/useToast, the ESLint rule)\nand Playwright e2e scenarios; NFR-3 requires `@axe-core/playwright` on `/`\nand `/dashboard` with zero serious/critical violations; NFR-8 requires both\n`test` and `test:e2e` npm scripts to pass on a fresh clone.\n\n**Decision:** Vitest + Testing Library for unit/component tests,\nPlaywright (`tests/e2e`) + `@axe-core/playwright` for e2e and accessibility\ngating. No Jest (avoids a second test runner config) — Vitest already\ncovers the Vite/Next toolchain needs with less config.\n\n**Consequences:** Accessibility is a CI gate (zero serious/critical axe\nviolations), not a manual checklist — ties directly to NFR-3's WCAG bar.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Structured logging via a single `src/lib/logger.ts`\n\n**Context:** FR-40 requires `logger.info|warn|error(message, meta?)`\nemitting JSON lines in production and readable lines in development.\n\n**Decision:** One logger module, no external logging library (e.g., no\npino/winston) — the required shape (JSON-in-prod, readable-in-dev, three\nlevels, optional meta) is small enough that a dependency would be\nover-engineering for what `console.*` + a format branch already covers.\n\n**Consequences:** `withHandler` (ADR-4) routes uncaught errors through this\nlogger before returning `INTERNAL` to the client (FR-13), keeping stack\ntraces server-side only.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Security headers and CSP in `next.config.js`, not middleware\n\n**Context:** NFR-5 requires `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`,\n`X-Frame-Options`, and a restrictive CSP.\n\n**Decision:** Set headers via Next.js's built-in `headers()` config\nfunction in `next.config.js` rather than a custom middleware — it's the\nnative platform mechanism for static security headers and needs no request-\ntime logic.\n\n**Consequences:** CSP must explicitly allow `'unsafe-inline'` for styles\n(Emotion/MUI inject inline `<style>` tags at runtime) while keeping\nscript-src restricted to `'self'`.\n\n---\n\n## Status\n\nAll nine decisions trace to at least one FR/NFR id above. No open\nquestions block `arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n","numLines":176,"startLine":1,"totalLines":176}}}
