 },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-4\",\n      \"description\": \"audit() insert-only helper in src/server/audit.ts: writes an AuditLog row, captures IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on failure instead), never writes password hashes/raw tokens/full passwords into metadata.\",\n      \"files\": [\"src/server/audit.ts\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"TASK-1\"],\n      \"estimateHours\": 2,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-24\", \"NFR-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-5\",\n      \"description\": \"In-memory sliding-window rate limiter (src/server/rate-limit.ts) with a configurable key, covering both the sign-in limit (10/IP/5min) and the forgot-password limits (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) from one exported implementation.\",\n      \"files\": [\"src/server/rate-limit.ts\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimateHours\": 2,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-6\", \"FR-17\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-6\",\n      \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail() stub in src/server/email/send-auth-email.ts logging recipient/subject/link via logger.info, with a stable signature so PRD-04 can swap the implementation later without touching call sites.\",\n      \"files\": [\"src/server/email/send-auth-email.ts\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimateHours\": 1,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-27\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-7\",\n      \"description\": \"Shared token helper (src/server/auth/tokens.ts): crypto.randomBytes(32) base64url generation, crypto.createHash('sha256') hashing, crypto.timingSafeEqual lookup comparison, and revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type) — the one producer both the invite and reset flows call, so the reset-specific invalidate-on-reissue rule doesn't leak into the invite path.\",\n      \"files\": [\"src/server/auth/tokens.ts\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"TASK-1\"],\n      \"estimateHours\": 2,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-1\", \"FR-12\", \"FR-18\", \"NFR-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n   