{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiarAitcMUL3mqDsZb7YVz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T21:45:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t\n7\t  \"sharedEnvelope\": {\n8\t    \"description\": \"Two families of endpoint exist in this PRD. (1) Auth.js (NextAuth v5)'s own catch-all route (/api/auth/callback/credentials, /api/auth/session, /api/auth/signout, /api/auth/csrf) — its request/response wire format is owned by the library, not src/server/http.ts, and is documented per-endpoint below only at the level dev-planning needs (inputs, outcomes, which FRs they satisfy). (2) Four new form-submission endpoints (invite/accept, forgot-password, reset-password, change-password) that are genuinely ours and MUST route through the existing src/server/http.ts chokepoint (ok/apiError/withHandler/parseBody) per NFR-7 — no parallel envelope. That chokepoint's ApiErrorCode union currently only has VALIDATION_ERROR/NOT_FOUND/CONFLICT/INTERNAL (see src/server/http.ts); this PRD needs three more values, which dev-planning/dev must EXTEND that union and errorCodeToStatus map with, not fork a second error-mapping file.\",\n9\t    \"success\": { \"data\": \"<payload>\" },\n10\t    \"error\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object (optional)\" } },\n11\t    \"errorCodeToStatus\": {\n12\t      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n13\t      \"NOT_FOUND\": 404,\n14\t      \"CONFLICT\": 409,\n15\t      \"INTERNAL\": 500,\n16\t      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429,\n17\t      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n18\t      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410\n19\t    },\n20\t    \"newErrorCodesForThisPrd\": {\n21\t      \"RATE_LIMITED\": \"Sign-in and forgot-password rate limiters (FR-6, FR-17) short-circuit to this before any DB work.\",\n22\t      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": \"Defense-in-depth on change-password's requireUser() guard (FR-20, FR-23) — middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests, this is the handler-level backstop.\",\n23\t      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": \"Invite/reset token is missing, wrong type, expired, or already used (FR-12, FR-18, FR-19) — distinct from NOT_FOUND because the token row may exist but be unusable; mapped to 410 Gone.\"\n24\t    },\n25\t    \"notModeledAsEndpoints\": \"Component 9's service functions (createUser, createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser — FR-22) are an internal module surface called by prisma/seed.ts (FR-28) and by later PRDs' admin UI, not by any form in this PRD. No endpoint is defined for them here; inventing an admin API now would be scope creep past NFR-8. Likewise /invite/[token] and /reset-password/[token]'s GET render (token validity check for FR-12) happens inside the Server Component itself via a direct Prisma lookup, not a client-side API call — no GET endpoint is defined for that for the same reason.\",\n26\t    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n27\t  },\n28\t\n29\t  \"endpoints\": [\n30\t    {\n31\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n32\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n33\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider callback, invoked internally by signIn('credentials') from the /login page. Runs the authorize() chokepoint: rate-limit check (10/IP/5min) before any DB work, email normalize, status/lockout branch (dummy bcrypt-compare for timing safety on a non-existent user), bcrypt compare (cost 12), failedLoginCount/lockedUntil mutation, audit() writes, and on success stamps id/role/firstName/lastName/email into the JWT. Wire format (form-encoded body, redirect-based response) is owned by Auth.js, not src/server/http.ts.\",\n34\t      \"requestSchema\": {\n35\t        \"email\": \"string\",\n36\t        \"password\": \"string\",\n37\t        \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\",\n38\t        \"callbackUrl\": \"string\"\n39\t      },\n40\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n41\t        \"redirectSuccess\": \"same-origin callbackUrl if relative, else /dashboard (FR-7)\",\n42\t        \"redirectFailure\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — same generic message for unknown-user and wrong-password (FR-4)\",\n43\t        \"redirectLocked\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — locked-account message includes remaining minutes (FR-4)\",\n44\t        \"redirectDisabled\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — distinct disabled-account message (FR-4)\",\n45\t        \"redirectRateLimited\": \"/login?error=RateLimited — 'Too many attempts' message (FR-6)\"\n46\t      },\n47\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\"]\n48\t    },\n49\t    {\n50\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n51\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",\n52\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js session read. The jwt callback applies the passwordChangedAt invalidation check (throttled to once per 5 minutes per token) before returning session.user; a token issued before the latest passwordChangedAt comes back null, forcing re-login on that device.\",\n53\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n54\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n55\t        \"data\": {\n56\t          \"user\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\" }\n57\t        },\n58\t        \"orNull\": \"null when unauthenticated or invalidated by passwordChangedAt\"\n59\t      },\n60\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-9\", \"FR-10\"]\n61\t    },\n62\t    {\n63\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n64\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n65\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out, clears the session cookie. Invoked by the top-bar user menu's 'Sign out' action, which then redirects to /login.\",\n66\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\" },\n67\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"redirect\": \"/login\" },\n68\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-25\"]\n69\t    },\n70\t    {\n71\t      \"method\": \"GET\",\n72\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n73\t      \"description\": \"Auth.js CSRF token issuance, consumed by every auth form (sign-in, sign-out, and this PRD's own POST endpoints reuse the same Auth.js session's CSRF protection) per NFR-1.\",\n74\t      \"requestSchema\": {},\n75\t      \"responseSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string\" },\n76\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-1\"]\n77\t    },\n78\t    {\n79\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n80\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/invite/accept\",\n81\t      \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit from /invite/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash of the submitted token (must be type INVITE, unused, within 7-day expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, then as one service-layer step: hashes it, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, marks the token used, signs the user in, and audits auth.invite.accepted — kept atomic so a failure partway doesn't leave a used token with no activated account.\",\n82\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n83\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n84\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/dashboard\" } },\n85\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n86\t        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n87\t      },\n88\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-15\"]\n89\t    },\n90\t    {\n91\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n92\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n93\t      \"description\": \"Always responds 200 with the same generic message regardless of whether the account exists (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2's intent). Rate-limited 3/email/hr and 10/IP/hr via component 3's limiter — the limiter key is the submitted email/IP itself, not account existence, so a 429 here doesn't leak whether an account exists. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issues a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry), revokes that user's older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\",\n94\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"email\": \"string\" },\n95\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n96\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } },\n97\t        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Try again later.\" } }\n98\t      },\n99\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\"]\n100\t    },\n101\t    {\n102\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n103\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n104\t      \"description\": \"Submit from /reset-password/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash (must be type PASSWORD_RESET, unused, within 60-min expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, sets the new hash and passwordChangedAt, clears failedLoginCount/lockedUntil, marks the token used, and audits auth.password.reset.\",\n105\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n106\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n107\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/login\" } },\n108\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n109\t        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n110\t      },\n111\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-19\"]\n112\t    },\n113\t    {\n114\t      \"method\": \"POST\",\n115\t      \"path\": \"/api/auth/change-password\",\n116\t      \"description\": \"Submit from /account/security, behind requireUser() (FR-23) — the route handler re-checks the session as a backstop even though middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests. Checks the current password against the stored hash (wrong value is a field-level VALIDATION_ERROR, not a generic failure), validates the new password against the shared policy module, bumps passwordChangedAt (invalidating every other session via the jwt callback's check), and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out by their own action.\",\n117\t      \"requestSchema\": { \"currentPassword\": \"string\", \"newPassword\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n118\t      \"responseSchema\": {\n119\t        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"Password updated.\" } },\n120\t        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n121\t        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"message\": \"string\" } }\n122\t      },\n123\t      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-23\"]\n124\t    }\n125\t  ],\n126\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n127\t}\n128\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97520f4c-ae80-4db0-b68a-6ea625258a9f","uuid":"eb9e96ed-e7e6-4945-be65-b64847cef534","timestamp":"2026-10-16T17:38:47.368Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/api-contracts.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T21:45:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"sharedEnvelope\": {\n    \"description\": \"Two families of endpoint exist in this PRD. (1) Auth.js (NextAuth v5)'s own catch-all route (/api/auth/callback/credentials, /api/auth/session, /api/auth/signout, /api/auth/csrf) — its request/response wire format is owned by the library, not src/server/http.ts, and is documented per-endpoint below only at the level dev-planning needs (inputs, outcomes, which FRs they satisfy). (2) Four new form-submission endpoints (invite/accept, forgot-password, reset-password, change-password) that are genuinely ours and MUST route through the existing src/server/http.ts chokepoint (ok/apiError/withHandler/parseBody) per NFR-7 — no parallel envelope. That chokepoint's ApiErrorCode union currently only has VALIDATION_ERROR/NOT_FOUND/CONFLICT/INTERNAL (see src/server/http.ts); this PRD needs three more values, which dev-planning/dev must EXTEND that union and errorCodeToStatus map with, not fork a second error-mapping file.\",\n    \"success\": { \"data\": \"<payload>\" },\n    \"error\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object (optional)\" } },\n    \"errorCodeToStatus\": {\n      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n      \"NOT_FOUND\": 404,\n      \"CONFLICT\": 409,\n      \"INTERNAL\": 500,\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429,\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410\n    },\n    \"newErrorCodesForThisPrd\": {\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": \"Sign-in and forgot-password rate limiters (FR-6, FR-17) short-circuit to this before any DB work.\",\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": \"Defense-in-depth on change-password's requireUser() guard (FR-20, FR-23) — middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests, this is the handler-level backstop.\",\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": \"Invite/reset token is missing, wrong type, expired, or already used (FR-12, FR-18, FR-19) — distinct from NOT_FOUND because the token row may exist but be unusable; mapped to 410 Gone.\"\n    },\n    \"notModeledAsEndpoints\": \"Component 9's service functions (createUser, createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser — FR-22) are an internal module surface called by prisma/seed.ts (FR-28) and by later PRDs' admin UI, not by any form in this PRD. No endpoint is defined for them here; inventing an admin API now would be scope creep past NFR-8. Likewise /invite/[token] and /reset-password/[token]'s GET render (token validity check for FR-12) happens inside the Server Component itself via a direct Prisma lookup, not a client-side API call — no GET endpoint is defined for that for the same reason.\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider callback, invoked internally by signIn('credentials') from the /login page. Runs the authorize() chokepoint: rate-limit check (10/IP/5min) before any DB work, email normalize, status/lockout branch (dummy bcrypt-compare for timing safety on a non-existent user), bcrypt compare (cost 12), failedLoginCount/lockedUntil mutation, audit() writes, and on success stamps id/role/firstName/lastName/email into the JWT. Wire format (form-encoded body, redirect-based response) is owned by Auth.js, not src/server/http.ts.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"email\": \"string\",\n        \"password\": \"string\",\n        \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\",\n        \"callbackUrl\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"redirectSuccess\": \"same-origin callbackUrl if relative, else /dashboard (FR-7)\",\n        \"redirectFailure\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — same generic message for unknown-user and wrong-password (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectLocked\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — locked-account message includes remaining minutes (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectDisabled\": \"/login?error=CredentialsSignin — distinct disabled-account message (FR-4)\",\n        \"redirectRateLimited\": \"/login?error=RateLimited — 'Too many attempts' message (FR-6)\"\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js session read. The jwt callback applies the passwordChangedAt invalidation check (throttled to once per 5 minutes per token) before returning session.user; a token issued before the latest passwordChangedAt comes back null, forcing re-login on that device.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"data\": {\n          \"user\": { \"id\": \"string\", \"role\": \"Role\", \"firstName\": \"string\", \"lastName\": \"string\", \"email\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"orNull\": \"null when unauthenticated or invalidated by passwordChangedAt\"\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-9\", \"FR-10\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out, clears the session cookie. Invoked by the top-bar user menu's 'Sign out' action, which then redirects to /login.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string (Auth.js-issued)\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"redirect\": \"/login\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-25\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js CSRF token issuance, consumed by every auth form (sign-in, sign-out, and this PRD's own POST endpoints reuse the same Auth.js session's CSRF protection) per NFR-1.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"csrfToken\": \"string\" },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/invite/accept\",\n      \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit from /invite/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash of the submitted token (must be type INVITE, unused, within 7-day expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, then as one service-layer step: hashes it, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, marks the token used, signs the user in, and audits auth.invite.accepted — kept atomic so a failure partway doesn't leave a used token with no activated account.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/dashboard\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-15\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Always responds 200 with the same generic message regardless of whether the account exists (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2's intent). Rate-limited 3/email/hr and 10/IP/hr via component 3's limiter — the limiter key is the submitted email/IP itself, not account existence, so a 429 here doesn't leak whether an account exists. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issues a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry), revokes that user's older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"email\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } },\n        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Try again later.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-18\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Submit from /reset-password/[token]. Looks up the AuthToken by SHA-256 hash (must be type PASSWORD_RESET, unused, within 60-min expiry), validates the new password against the shared policy module, sets the new hash and passwordChangedAt, clears failedLoginCount/lockedUntil, marks the token used, and audits auth.password.reset.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"token\": \"string\", \"password\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"redirectTo\": \"/login\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-19\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/change-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Submit from /account/security, behind requireUser() (FR-23) — the route handler re-checks the session as a backstop even though middleware.ts already blocks unauthenticated (app) requests. Checks the current password against the stored hash (wrong value is a field-level VALIDATION_ERROR, not a generic failure), validates the new password against the shared policy module, bumps passwordChangedAt (invalidating every other session via the jwt callback's check), and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out by their own action.\",\n      \"requestSchema\": { \"currentPassword\": \"string\", \"newPassword\": \"string\", \"confirmPassword\": \"string\" },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"message\": \"Password updated.\" } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": \"object\" } } },\n        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\", \"message\": \"string\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-15\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-23\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":128,"startLine":1,"totalLines":128}}}
