{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012S1uKXk5e9GWABcr2CuN8Y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n3\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n4\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n5\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n6\t\n7\t  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n8\t    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: User (email, passwordHash, role, status, lockout fields), AuthToken (invite/reset tokens, SHA-256 hash, expiry) and AuditLog (actor, action, entity, metadata, IP) via the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n9\t    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"/login page built from MUI patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email/password fields, submitting via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 1\" },\n10\t    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"authorize() lower-cases/trims the email, rejects a non-existent user, a user whose status is not ACTIVE, an archived user, or a locked user, and otherwise compares the password with bcrypt (cost 12).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 2\" },\n11\t    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in failure messaging: the same 'Email or password is incorrect.' message for unknown-user/wrong-password, a distinct locked-account message with the remaining minutes, and a distinct disabled-account message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 3\" },\n12\t    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"Lockout counter: increment failedLoginCount on a wrong password; at 5 failures set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the counter; on success reset the counter to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 4\" },\n13\t    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in rate limit of 10 attempts per IP per 5-minute sliding window (in-memory, src/server/rate-limit.ts, exported for reuse); exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and a 'Too many attempts' message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 5\" },\n14\t    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl when it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 6\" },\n15\t    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout for the relevant sign-in outcomes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 7\" },\n16\t    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"JWT session strategy, 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the token and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 1\" },\n17\t    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"If passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time the session is treated as invalid, forcing re-login on every device after a password change; checked at most once every 5 minutes per token in the jwt callback.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 2\" },\n18\t    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated requests for any (app)-group path to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 JSON for /api/* paths except /api/health, /api/auth/* and paths listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 3\" },\n19\t    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] looks the token up by SHA-256 hash; it must be type INVITE, unused and not expired (7-day expiry), otherwise show the invalid/expired-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 1\" },\n20\t    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation form shows the invited user's name and email read-only plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 2\" },\n21\t    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, marks the token used, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 3\" },\n22\t    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy (src/lib/validators/auth.ts): 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, must not equal the user's email, must not appear in the bundled 1,000 most-common-passwords list.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 1\" },\n23\t    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live password-strength checklist under the password field shows each policy rule as met or unmet as the user types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 2\" },\n24\t    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password always returns the same 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' message regardless of whether the account exists; rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 1\" },\n25\t    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user, create a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, base64url, 60-minute expiry), invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 2\" },\n26\t    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] sets the new password hash and passwordChangedAt, clears lockout fields, marks the token used, audits auth.password.reset, and redirects to /login with a success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 3\" },\n27\t    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"/account/security change-password form: current/new/confirm-password fields; a wrong current password shows a field error; success shows a toast, invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 1\" },\n28\t    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the user menu, linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 2\" },\n29\t    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Service functions in src/server/services/users.ts for later PRDs: createUser (throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Service functions for later PRDs\" },\n30\t    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Permission helpers in src/server/auth/permissions.ts: getCurrentUser(), requireUser() (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to /login in server pages), requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to /forbidden); no generic can() helper is built — explicit role checks plus later per-entity helpers are the sanctioned pattern.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Permissions\" },\n31\t    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Audit helper audit() in src/server/audit.ts inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on error), and never writes password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords into metadata.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Audit helper\" },\n32\t    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"App shell top-bar user menu shows the real signed-in user's name, role badge and avatar initials; 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 1\" },\n33\t    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"navigation.ts filtering now uses the real session role in place of the PRD-00 placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 2\" },\n34\t    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Until PRD-04 lands, sendAuthEmail() logs the recipient, subject and link via logger.info instead of sending a real email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope, item 3\" },\n35\t    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, two teachers, two students, one parent; password SchoolHub123! for all) plus one INVITED user, logging the invited user's invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n36\t  ],\n37\t\n38\t  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n39\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and all auth forms carry CSRF protection supplied by Auth.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Security)\" },\n40\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Sign-in response time for 'no such user' and 'wrong password' must be similar (a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist) to prevent user-enumeration via timing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Security)\" },\n41\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },\n42\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },\n43\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n44\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },\n45\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n46\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n47\t  ],\n48\t\n49\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n50\t  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n51\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n52\t}\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97520f4c-ae80-4db0-b68a-6ea625258a9f","uuid":"1057c88a-f9ff-49bc-8c52-bef9920b420b","timestamp":"2026-10-16T17:38:56.644Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: User (email, passwordHash, role, status, lockout fields), AuthToken (invite/reset tokens, SHA-256 hash, expiry) and AuditLog (actor, action, entity, metadata, IP) via the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"/login page built from MUI patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email/password fields, submitting via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"authorize() lower-cases/trims the email, rejects a non-existent user, a user whose status is not ACTIVE, an archived user, or a locked user, and otherwise compares the password with bcrypt (cost 12).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in failure messaging: the same 'Email or password is incorrect.' message for unknown-user/wrong-password, a distinct locked-account message with the remaining minutes, and a distinct disabled-account message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"Lockout counter: increment failedLoginCount on a wrong password; at 5 failures set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the counter; on success reset the counter to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in rate limit of 10 attempts per IP per 5-minute sliding window (in-memory, src/server/rate-limit.ts, exported for reuse); exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and a 'Too many attempts' message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl when it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout for the relevant sign-in outcomes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"JWT session strategy, 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the token and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"If passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time the session is treated as invalid, forcing re-login on every device after a password change; checked at most once every 5 minutes per token in the jwt callback.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated requests for any (app)-group path to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 JSON for /api/* paths except /api/health, /api/auth/* and paths listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] looks the token up by SHA-256 hash; it must be type INVITE, unused and not expired (7-day expiry), otherwise show the invalid/expired-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation form shows the invited user's name and email read-only plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, marks the token used, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy (src/lib/validators/auth.ts): 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, must not equal the user's email, must not appear in the bundled 1,000 most-common-passwords list.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live password-strength checklist under the password field shows each policy rule as met or unmet as the user types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password always returns the same 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' message regardless of whether the account exists; rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user, create a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, base64url, 60-minute expiry), invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] sets the new password hash and passwordChangedAt, clears lockout fields, marks the token used, audits auth.password.reset, and redirects to /login with a success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"/account/security change-password form: current/new/confirm-password fields; a wrong current password shows a field error; success shows a toast, invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the user menu, linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Service functions in src/server/services/users.ts for later PRDs: createUser (throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Service functions for later PRDs\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Permission helpers in src/server/auth/permissions.ts: getCurrentUser(), requireUser() (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to /login in server pages), requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to /forbidden); no generic can() helper is built — explicit role checks plus later per-entity helpers are the sanctioned pattern.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Permissions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Audit helper audit() in src/server/audit.ts inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on error), and never writes password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords into metadata.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Audit helper\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"App shell top-bar user menu shows the real signed-in user's name, role badge and avatar initials; 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"navigation.ts filtering now uses the real session role in place of the PRD-00 placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Until PRD-04 lands, sendAuthEmail() logs the recipient, subject and link via logger.info instead of sending a real email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, two teachers, two students, one parent; password SchoolHub123! for all) plus one INVITED user, logging the invited user's invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and all auth forms carry CSRF protection supplied by Auth.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Sign-in response time for 'no such user' and 'wrong password' must be similar (a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist) to prevent user-enumeration via timing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":53,"startLine":1,"totalLines":53}}}
