{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017fjeR3huFnVR3k8YSd4dgg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n6\t`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\n7\tfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\n8\tand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\n9\tReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\n10\tevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\n11\treal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\n12\treports no blockers.\n13\t\n14\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n15\t\n16\t- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n17\t  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n18\t  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n19\t  passing with no scope creep.\n20\t- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n21\t  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n22\t- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n23\t  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n24\t  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n25\t\n26\t## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n27\t\n28\t- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n29\t  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n30\t  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n31\t- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n32\t  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n33\t  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n34\t- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n35\t  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n36\t  browser before anything hits the network.\n37\t\n38\t## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n39\t\n40\t- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n41\t  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n42\t- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n43\t  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n44\t  table.\n45\t- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n46\t  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n47\t  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n48\t  request lifetime).\n49\t\n50\t## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n51\t\n52\t- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n53\t  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n54\t  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n55\t  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n56\t- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n57\t  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n58\t  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n59\t- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n60\t  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n61\t\n62\t## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n63\t\n64\t- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n65\t  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n66\t  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n67\t  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n68\t- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n69\t  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n70\t  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n71\t  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n72\t  wrapper design-system package.\n73\t- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n74\t\n75\t## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n76\t\n77\t- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n78\t  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n79\t  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n80\t- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n81\t  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n82\t  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n83\t- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n84\t  queries unaffected.\n85\t\n86\t## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n87\t\n88\t- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n89\t  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n90\t  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n91\t- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n92\t  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n93\t  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n94\t  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n95\t- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n96\t  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n97\t\n98\t## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n99\t\n100\t- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n101\t  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n102\t  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n103\t  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n104\t- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n105\t  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n106\t  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n107\t  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n108\t  user service.\n109\t- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n110\t  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n111\t  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n112\t  re-implements.\n113\t\n114\t## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n115\t\n116\t- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n117\t  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n118\t- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n119\t  not generated at request time.\n120\t- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n121\t  edit, not a code change.\n122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58cb2461-07a2-4908-85eb-953f83a6620f","uuid":"629dcceb-4c86-4b76-806d-f664b46edbe3","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:42:17.320Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n\nBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\nfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\nand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\nevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\nreal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\nreports no blockers.\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n\n- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n  passing with no scope creep.\n- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n\n## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n\n- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n  browser before anything hits the network.\n\n## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n\n- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n  table.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n  request lifetime).\n\n## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n\n- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n\n## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n\n- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n  wrapper design-system package.\n- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n\n## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n\n- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n  queries unaffected.\n\n## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n\n- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n\n## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n\n- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n  user service.\n- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n  re-implements.\n\n## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n\n- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n  not generated at request time.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n  edit, not a code change.\n","numLines":122,"startLine":1,"totalLines":122}}}
