ngine Requirements**: node >=18.18.0\n- **Async Style**: async/await dominant\n\n## Dependencies\n### Production\n| Package | Version |\n|---------|---------|\n| @emotion/react | 11.13.3 |\n| @emotion/styled | 11.13.0 |\n| @hookform/resolvers | 3.9.0 |\n| @mui/icons-material | 9.5.0 |\n| @mui/material | 9.5.0 |\n| @mui/material-nextjs | 9.5.0 |\n| @mui/x-charts | 9.5.0 |\n| @mui/x-data-grid | 9.5.0 |\n| @mui/x-date-pickers | 9.5.0 |\n| @prisma/client | 5.20.0 |\n| bcrypt | ^6.0.0 |\n| date-fns | 3.6.0 |\n| date-fns-tz | 3.2.0 |\n| next | 14.2.18 |\n| next-auth | ^5.0.0-beta.25 |\n| papaparse | ^5.4.1 |\n| react | 18.3.1 |\n| react-dom | 18.3.1 |\n| react-hook-form | 7.53.0 |\n| react-is | 18.3.1 |\n\n### Development\n| Package | Version |\n|---------|---------|\n| @axe-core/playwright | 4.10.0 |\n| @playwright/test | 1.47.2 |\n| @testing-library/jest-dom | 6.5.0 |\n| @testing-library/react | 16.0.1 |\n| @testing-library/user-event | 14.5.2 |\n| @types/bcrypt | ^6.0.0 |\n| @types/node | 20.14.10 |\n| @types/papaparse | ^5.3.14 |\n| @types/react | 18.3.3 |\n| @types/react-dom | 18.3.0 |\n\n## Testing\n- **Framework**: vitest\n- **Test Files**: 9\n- **Structure**: tests/\n\n## Build & Deploy\n```bash\n# Apply .sql scripts via your DB client    # Build\nnpm start    # Run\nnpm test    # Test\n```\nCI/CD: docker-compose\n\n## Key Areas\n\n### Large Files\n| File | Lines |\n|------|-------|\n| `src/server/services/users.ts` | 392 |\n\n## Dependency Graph\n- **Nodes**: 82 files\n- **Edges**: 7 import relationships\n- **Entry Points**: 76 files\n\n### Most-Imported Files\n| File | Imported By |\n|------|------------|\n| `src/server/services/dateRange.ts` | 2 files |\n| `prisma/migrations/20261019000000_init/migration.sql` | 1 files |\n| `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` | 1 files |\n| `src/components/Toast/useToast.ts` | 1 files |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` | 1 files |\n| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | 1 files |\n\n### Entry Points (not imported by other files)\n- `next-env.d.ts`\n- `next.config.js`\n- `playwright.config.ts`\n- `prisma/migrations/20261019151500_user_management_profiles/migration.sql`\n- `prisma/seed.ts`\n- `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx`\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`\n- `src/app/(public)/layout.tsx`\n- `src/app/(public)/page.tsx`\n- `src/app/api/academic-years/[id]/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/academic-years/[id]/set-current/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/academic-years/[id]/terms/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/academic-years/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/audit-logs/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/health/route.ts`\n- _...and 61 more_\n\n## Brittle Areas\n\n### God Files (>15 exports)\n- `src/lib/validators/users.ts` (20 exports)\n\n## Project Decisions\nNo decisions recorded yet.\n\n## Established Patterns\nNo patterns recorded yet.\n\n## Known Issues\nNo known issues.# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment\n\nTicket: abcd-05 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Status: complete\n\nBase platform (from `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`, confidence 100%):\nNext.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nMUI v9 + emotion, `zod` for input validation, `date-fns`. This PRD is\nbrownfield on top of that stack — intake's detection notes already confirm\nit \"adds no new frontend framework or dependency,\" only new Prisma models\nand pages. The decisions below are the implementation-pattern deltas this\nPRD's requirements force, not a re-litigation of the base stack. No new\nruntime dependency is added by this PRD.\n\n## ADR-1: Bulk enroll/drop writes — `Prisma.$transaction` with batched\n`createMany`/`updateMany`, no job queue\n\n**Context.** NFR-3 requires adding 30 students to a section with 8 core\ncourses (240 resulting enrollments) to complete in under 1 second. FR-7–\nFR-10 describe enroll-on-add, drop-on-remove, move-section, and\ncreate-core-course as all-or-nothing operations touching many `Enrollment`\nrows at once.\n\n**Decision.** Implement each of these as a single `prisma.$transaction`\nthat computes the affected (studentId, courseId) pairs in memory first,\nthen issues one `enrollment.createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for new\nACTIVE rows and one `enrollment.updateMany` (keyed on the unique\n`[courseId, studentId]`) to reactivate previously-DROPPED rows, instead of\nlooping `create`/`update` calls per student per course. This is plain\nPrisma batch-write API already in the installed `@prisma/client` — no\nqueue, no background worker, no new dependency. 240 rows in one\n`createMany` plus one `updateMany` comfortably clears the 1-second bar on\nPostgres; a per-row loop (240 round-trips) would not.\n\n**Consequences.** Business logic that decides \"create vs. reactivate\" for\neach pair must be computed with a single prior `findMany`, not per-row\nqueries, to keep the whole operation at a small constant number of\nround-trips. If a future PRD needs enroll/drop across thousands of rows\n(bulk import), that's a new ADR for chunking or a background job — not a\nretrofit of this one.\n\n_Cites: FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10, NFR-3_\n\n## ADR-2: Capacity + uniqueness enforcement — DB unique constraints for\nidentity, in-transaction count check for capacity, no distributed lock\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 requires the one-section-per-student-per-year rule to be\na database constraint, not just app logic. FR-11 requires capacity\nenforcement (section and course) that refuses with CONFLICT unless an\nexplicit \"Override capacity\" flag is set, under concurrent admin actions.\n\n**Decision.** Identity/duplication rules (`@@unique([studentId,\nacademicYearId])` on `SectionMember`, `@@unique([courseId, studentId])` on\n`Enrollment`) are enforced by Postgres unique indexes already specified in\nFR-1; application code catches the Prisma `P2002` violation and maps it to\nthe existing CONFLICT error envelope rather than pre-checking existence\nfirst (avoids a check-then-insert race). Capacity, which is a *computed*\ncount rather than a stored invariant, is checked inside the same\n`$transaction` that performs the insert — `count()` the current\nmembers/enrollments, compare to `capacity`, and only then\n`create`/`createMany`, so a concurrent request either serializes behind the\ntransaction or re-checks and fails cleanly. No advisory lock, no Redis, no\ndistributed-lock library: Postgres's own transactional read-your-writes\nwithin one `$transaction` is sufficient at this app's scale (a school\nadmin console, not a high-concurrency storefront).\n\n**Consequences.** Capacity checks are \"good enough\" serialization, not a\nhard guarantee under extreme concurrent load from multiple admins hitting\nthe exact same section simultaneously; acceptable because this is an\ninternal admin tool with low write concurrency. If that ever changes,\nupgrading the capacity check to `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` on a row is a small\nfollow-up, not a new ADR.\n\n_Cites: FR-1, FR-11, NFR-2_\n\n## ADR-3: No new dependency for the admin UI (tables, dialogs, pickers)\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 mandates every visible element in the sections/courses/\nenrollment screens come from `@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, or MUI\nX, with no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select,\netc.). FR-2–FR-6, FR-13–FR-19 describe filtered tables, create/edit\ndialogs, multi-select pickers, tabs, and card grids.\n\n**Decision.** Build all of it from the already-installed MUI v9 set plus\nthe existing shared components (`DataTable`, `UserPicker`, `ConfirmDialog`,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub-prds/020b7a6e-6236-4f8d-a760-9a7fb50fdcce/tool-results/buge1cfgw.txt","persistedOutputSize":36777},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Nu6pG93mD3mutKvCPvPYES","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
