{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A1bWcRGThv8LNemn9oqt3e","type":"tool_result","content":"### [Grid](#grid)\n\n#### `direction=\"column\"` and `direction=\"column-reverse\"` removed\n\nThe `Grid` component no longer accepts `direction=\"column\"` or `direction=\"column-reverse\"`. These values were unsupported in practice in earlier versions and are now removed from the TypeScript types and prop validation.\n\n`Grid` is designed to subdivide a layout into **columns**, not rows. For vertical stacking, use the [Stack](/material-ui/react-stack/) component instead (including inside a `Grid` item when needed). See the [Grid column direction limitation](/material-ui/react-grid/#column-direction) for details.\n\n```diff\n-import Grid from '@mui/material/Grid';\n+import Stack from '@mui/material/Stack';\n\n-<Grid container direction=\"column\" spacing={2}>\n-  <Grid size={12}>First item</Grid>\n-  <Grid size={12}>Second item</Grid>\n-</Grid>\n+<Stack spacing={2}>\n+  <div>First item</div>\n+  <div>Second item</div>\n+</Stack>\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nIf you still need horizontal column subdivision, keep using `Grid` with `direction=\"row\"` (the default) or `direction=\"row-reverse\"`.\n\n### [List](#list)\n\nThe `ListItemIcon` default min-width has changed to `36px` (previously `56px`) to be consistent with the menu item, and now uses `theme.spacing` instead of a hardcoded number.\n\n### [Material Icons](#material-icons)\n\n23 legacy icon exports that ended with `Outline` (without the \"d\") have been removed. These were exact duplicates of their `Outlined` counterparts (for example, `InfoOutline` had the same SVG as `InfoOutlined`).\n\nTo migrate, rename the import to use the `Outlined` suffix:\n\n```diff\n-import InfoOutlineIcon from '@mui/icons-material/InfoOutline';\n+import InfoOutlinedIcon from '@mui/icons-material/InfoOutlined';\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nThe full list of removed exports: `AddCircleOutline`, `ChatBubbleOutline`, `CheckCircleOutline`, `DeleteOutline`, `DoneOutline`, `DriveFileMoveOutline`, `ErrorOutline`, `HelpOutline`, `InfoOutline`, `LabelImportantOutline`, `LightbulbOutline`, `LockOutline`, `MailOutline`, `ModeEditOutline`, `PauseCircleOutline`, `PeopleOutline`, `PersonOutline`, `PieChartOutline`, `PlayCircleOutline`, `RemoveCircleOutline`, `StarOutline`, `WorkOutline`, `WorkspacesOutline`.\n\nTheme variants of these icons (for example, `InfoOutlineRounded`, `DeleteOutlineSharp`) are **not** affected and remain available.\n\n### [Menu and MenuList](#menu-and-menulist)\n\nWhen using `variant=\"selectedMenu\"`, the `tabindex` attribute for each menu item will change on Arrow Key, Home / End or Character Key navigation. Previously, keyboard navigation moved DOM focus without updating `tabindex` on focused items. Now, we move DOM focus and also add `tabindex=\"0\"` to the focused element. The previously focused element will have its `tabindex` updated to `-1` in order to keep only one focusable `MenuItem` at a time.\n### [Tabs](#tabs)\n\nThe `tabindex` attribute for each tab will be changed on Arrow Key or Home / End navigation. Previously, keyboard navigation moved DOM focus without updating `tabindex` on the focused `Tab`. Now, we move DOM focus and also add the `tabindex=\"0\"` to the focused `Tab`. Other tabs will have `tabindex=\"-1\"` to keep only one focusable `Tab` at a time.\n\nSelecting a `Tab` will update the focus and `tabindex` as before.\n\n`Tab`s not placed inside `Tabs` will now throw an error.\n\n### [TextField](#textfield)\n\nWhen specifying `<TextField select />` to render a `<Select>`, the underlying `<InputLabel>` renders a `<div>` instead of a native `<label>` element. This does not affect `<InputLabel>` on its own.\n\n### [Theme](#theme)\n\n`MuiTouchRipple` has been removed from the theme `components` types (`ComponentsProps`, `ComponentsOverrides`, and `ComponentsVariants`). TouchRipple has been an internal component since v5 and never consumed theme overrides or default props, so the types were misleading.\n### [ListItemText props](#listitemtext-props)\n\nUse the [list-item-text-props codemod](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/tree/HEAD/packages/mui-codemod#list-item-text-props) below to migrate the code as described in the following section:\n\n```bash\nnpx @mui/codemod@latest deprecations/list-item-text-props <path>\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nThe following deprecated props have been removed:\n\n- `primaryTypographyProps` — use `slotProps.primary` instead\n- `secondaryTypographyProps` — use `slotProps.secondary` instead\n\n```diff\n <ListItemText\n-  primaryTypographyProps={{ variant: 'h6' }}\n-  secondaryTypographyProps={{ color: 'textSecondary' }}\n+  slotProps={{\n+    primary: { variant: 'h6' },\n+    secondary: { color: 'textSecondary' },\n+  }}\n />\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\n2530:### [TextField props](#textfield-props)\n2531-\n2532-Use the [text-field-props codemod](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/tree/HEAD/packages/mui-codemod#text-field-props) below to migrate the code as described in the following section:\n2533-\n2534-```bash\n2535-npx @mui/codemod@latest deprecations/text-field-props <path>\n2536-\n2537-```\n2538-\n2539-CopyCopied(or C)\n2540-\n2541-The following deprecated props have been removed from the `TextField` component:\n2542-\n2543-- `InputProps` → use `slotProps.input`\n2544-- `inputProps` → use `slotProps.htmlInput`\n2545-- `SelectProps` → use `slotProps.select`\n2546-- `InputLabelProps` → use `slotProps.inputLabel`\n2547-- `FormHelperTextProps` → use `slotProps.formHelperText`\n2548-\n2549-```diff\n2550- <TextField\n2551--  InputProps={CustomInputProps}\n2552--  inputProps={CustomHtmlInputProps}\n2553--  SelectProps={CustomSelectProps}\n2554--  InputLabelProps={CustomInputLabelProps}\n2555--  FormHelperTextProps={CustomFormHelperTextProps}\n2681-CopyCopied(or C)\n2682-\n2683:### [System props](#system-props)\n2684-\n2685-Use the [system-props codemod](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/blob/master/packages/mui-codemod/README.md#system-props) below to migrate the code as described in the following section:\n2686-\n2687-```bash\n2688-npx @mui/codemod@latest v9.0.0/system-props <path/to/folder>\n2689-\n2690-```\n2691-\n2692-CopyCopied(or C)\n2693-\n2694-Use `--jsx` to specify extra JSX tags to migrate, bypassing import detection:\n2695-\n--\n2703-This is useful if your project uses auto-import plugins (for example `unplugin-auto-import`) where Material UI components are available without explicit import statements.\n2704-\n2705:The deprecated system props have been removed from the following components:\n2706-\n2707-- `Box`\n2708-- `DialogContentText`\n2709-- `Grid`\n2710-- `Link`\n2711-- `Stack`\n2712-- `Typography`\n2713-- `TimelineContent`\n2714-- `TimelineOppositeContent`\n2715-\n2716-```diff\n2717--<Box mt={2} color=\"primary.main\" />","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"020b7a6e-6236-4f8d-a760-9a7fb50fdcce","uuid":"46006753-9818-4847-8d68-8d396153a219","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:38:35.067Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### [Grid](#grid)\n\n#### `direction=\"column\"` and `direction=\"column-reverse\"` removed\n\nThe `Grid` component no longer accepts `direction=\"column\"` or `direction=\"column-reverse\"`. These values were unsupported in practice in earlier versions and are now removed from the TypeScript types and prop validation.\n\n`Grid` is designed to subdivide a layout into **columns**, not rows. For vertical stacking, use the [Stack](/material-ui/react-stack/) component instead (including inside a `Grid` item when needed). See the [Grid column direction limitation](/material-ui/react-grid/#column-direction) for details.\n\n```diff\n-import Grid from '@mui/material/Grid';\n+import Stack from '@mui/material/Stack';\n\n-<Grid container direction=\"column\" spacing={2}>\n-  <Grid size={12}>First item</Grid>\n-  <Grid size={12}>Second item</Grid>\n-</Grid>\n+<Stack spacing={2}>\n+  <div>First item</div>\n+  <div>Second item</div>\n+</Stack>\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nIf you still need horizontal column subdivision, keep using `Grid` with `direction=\"row\"` (the default) or `direction=\"row-reverse\"`.\n\n### [List](#list)\n\nThe `ListItemIcon` default min-width has changed to `36px` (previously `56px`) to be consistent with the menu item, and now uses `theme.spacing` instead of a hardcoded number.\n\n### [Material Icons](#material-icons)\n\n23 legacy icon exports that ended with `Outline` (without the \"d\") have been removed. These were exact duplicates of their `Outlined` counterparts (for example, `InfoOutline` had the same SVG as `InfoOutlined`).\n\nTo migrate, rename the import to use the `Outlined` suffix:\n\n```diff\n-import InfoOutlineIcon from '@mui/icons-material/InfoOutline';\n+import InfoOutlinedIcon from '@mui/icons-material/InfoOutlined';\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nThe full list of removed exports: `AddCircleOutline`, `ChatBubbleOutline`, `CheckCircleOutline`, `DeleteOutline`, `DoneOutline`, `DriveFileMoveOutline`, `ErrorOutline`, `HelpOutline`, `InfoOutline`, `LabelImportantOutline`, `LightbulbOutline`, `LockOutline`, `MailOutline`, `ModeEditOutline`, `PauseCircleOutline`, `PeopleOutline`, `PersonOutline`, `PieChartOutline`, `PlayCircleOutline`, `RemoveCircleOutline`, `StarOutline`, `WorkOutline`, `WorkspacesOutline`.\n\nTheme variants of these icons (for example, `InfoOutlineRounded`, `DeleteOutlineSharp`) are **not** affected and remain available.\n\n### [Menu and MenuList](#menu-and-menulist)\n\nWhen using `variant=\"selectedMenu\"`, the `tabindex` attribute for each menu item will change on Arrow Key, Home / End or Character Key navigation. Previously, keyboard navigation moved DOM focus without updating `tabindex` on focused items. Now, we move DOM focus and also add `tabindex=\"0\"` to the focused element. The previously focused element will have its `tabindex` updated to `-1` in order to keep only one focusable `MenuItem` at a time.\n### [Tabs](#tabs)\n\nThe `tabindex` attribute for each tab will be changed on Arrow Key or Home / End navigation. Previously, keyboard navigation moved DOM focus without updating `tabindex` on the focused `Tab`. Now, we move DOM focus and also add the `tabindex=\"0\"` to the focused `Tab`. Other tabs will have `tabindex=\"-1\"` to keep only one focusable `Tab` at a time.\n\nSelecting a `Tab` will update the focus and `tabindex` as before.\n\n`Tab`s not placed inside `Tabs` will now throw an error.\n\n### [TextField](#textfield)\n\nWhen specifying `<TextField select />` to render a `<Select>`, the underlying `<InputLabel>` renders a `<div>` instead of a native `<label>` element. This does not affect `<InputLabel>` on its own.\n\n### [Theme](#theme)\n\n`MuiTouchRipple` has been removed from the theme `components` types (`ComponentsProps`, `ComponentsOverrides`, and `ComponentsVariants`). TouchRipple has been an internal component since v5 and never consumed theme overrides or default props, so the types were misleading.\n### [ListItemText props](#listitemtext-props)\n\nUse the [list-item-text-props codemod](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/tree/HEAD/packages/mui-codemod#list-item-text-props) below to migrate the code as described in the following section:\n\n```bash\nnpx @mui/codemod@latest deprecations/list-item-text-props <path>\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nThe following deprecated props have been removed:\n\n- `primaryTypographyProps` — use `slotProps.primary` instead\n- `secondaryTypographyProps` — use `slotProps.secondary` instead\n\n```diff\n <ListItemText\n-  primaryTypographyProps={{ variant: 'h6' }}\n-  secondaryTypographyProps={{ color: 'textSecondary' }}\n+  slotProps={{\n+    primary: { variant: 'h6' },\n+    secondary: { color: 'textSecondary' },\n+  }}\n />\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\n2530:### [TextField props](#textfield-props)\n2531-\n2532-Use the [text-field-props codemod](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/tree/HEAD/packages/mui-codemod#text-field-props) below to migrate the code as described in the following section:\n2533-\n2534-```bash\n2535-npx @mui/codemod@latest deprecations/text-field-props <path>\n2536-\n2537-```\n2538-\n2539-CopyCopied(or C)\n2540-\n2541-The following deprecated props have been removed from the `TextField` component:\n2542-\n2543-- `InputProps` → use `slotProps.input`\n2544-- `inputProps` → use `slotProps.htmlInput`\n2545-- `SelectProps` → use `slotProps.select`\n2546-- `InputLabelProps` → use `slotProps.inputLabel`\n2547-- `FormHelperTextProps` → use `slotProps.formHelperText`\n2548-\n2549-```diff\n2550- <TextField\n2551--  InputProps={CustomInputProps}\n2552--  inputProps={CustomHtmlInputProps}\n2553--  SelectProps={CustomSelectProps}\n2554--  InputLabelProps={CustomInputLabelProps}\n2555--  FormHelperTextProps={CustomFormHelperTextProps}\n2681-CopyCopied(or C)\n2682-\n2683:### [System props](#system-props)\n2684-\n2685-Use the [system-props codemod](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/blob/master/packages/mui-codemod/README.md#system-props) below to migrate the code as described in the following section:\n2686-\n2687-```bash\n2688-npx @mui/codemod@latest v9.0.0/system-props <path/to/folder>\n2689-\n2690-```\n2691-\n2692-CopyCopied(or C)\n2693-\n2694-Use `--jsx` to specify extra JSX tags to migrate, bypassing import detection:\n2695-\n--\n2703-This is useful if your project uses auto-import plugins (for example `unplugin-auto-import`) where Material UI components are available without explicit import statements.\n2704-\n2705:The deprecated system props have been removed from the following components:\n2706-\n2707-- `Box`\n2708-- `DialogContentText`\n2709-- `Grid`\n2710-- `Link`\n2711-- `Stack`\n2712-- `Typography`\n2713-- `TimelineContent`\n2714-- `TimelineOppositeContent`\n2715-\n2716-```diff\n2717--<Box mt={2} color=\"primary.main\" />","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A1bWcRGThv8LNemn9oqt3e","p