{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TXibBTjdtohVaqqf2opsfV","type":"tool_result","content":"Ticket abcd-05: execute the dev phase (task dev-main). Read prior phase artifacts under artifacts/, follow dev.md, and write this phase's artifacts to artifacts/dev/.\n\nContinue. Remaining: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5, TASK-6, TASK-7, TASK-8, TASK-9, TASK-10, TASK-11, TASK-12, TASK-13, TASK-14, TASK-15, TASK-16, TASK-17, TASK-18, TASK-19# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic\nstructure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03\n(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04\n(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both\nresolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps.\n\n**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s\n`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the\nfirst requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"\nunder an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the\ngrouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional\nfield, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small\nMUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;\nitems without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change\nthat satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages\nregistry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add\n`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they\nland, with no further schema change.\n\n**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from\nPRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described\nin the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new\n`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around\n`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object\n`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and\ndoes **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.\nConsolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is\nexplicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not\nschedule that consolidation here.\n\n**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two\nservice-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:\nFR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section\nrequired iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity\nchecks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same\n`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted\nas good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write\nconcurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to\nfix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on\nthese two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,\nhomeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)\n`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus\n`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including\nall four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what\nFR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below\nreads/writes.\n\n### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`\nThe single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,\nFR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions\n(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens\nits own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per\ntech-stack ADR-1):\n\n- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`\n  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below\n  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A\n  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per\n  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per\n  route.\n- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing\n  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs\n  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no\n  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip\n  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row\n  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course\n  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).\n- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:\n  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE\n  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls\n  `audit()`.\n- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then\n  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,\n  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`.\n\nFR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both\ncreate `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the\nsection's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry\npoints, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic.\n\nFR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active\nrosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter\napplied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,\ncourse roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes.\n\n### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,\nFR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)\nand the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level\nadvanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not\nreusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot\nstructural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on\n`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement\nenroll/drop.\n\n### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`\n(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"\nvalidator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side\ncheck and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a\nrefinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on\na non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`\ncreate/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,\nreused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this\npicker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead.\n\n### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`\nFR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and\n`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per\nDecision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by\n`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster\nendpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once\nhere, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's\nstated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this\nPRD's scope.\n\n### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\nFR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER\nbranch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section\nmembership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/\nPRD-04 callers unchanged.\n\n### Course public surface\n`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing\n`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers\n`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;\nSTUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`\nfiltering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a\nread-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.\n\n**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'\nnames only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query\n(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when\n`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component\nand `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the\ndata layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.\n\n### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)\nRead view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query\n(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE\nenrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,\ngrouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —\nno new parent-fanout code).\n\n### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)\n`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible\nflat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get\n`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.\n\n### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)\nNew \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +\nteacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses\nFR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the\nstudent page (no new access function).\n\n### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`\nEvery route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`\n→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the\nexisting success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route\nlayer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside\nthe same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it\ninternally so routes don't duplicate the call.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**\n`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST\n/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens\n`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →\n`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the\nuniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course\n`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →\ncommit → envelope response.\n\n**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →\n`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping\n`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old\nCORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for\nthe whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.\n\n**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →\n`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`\n(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course\nagainst current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.\n\n**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET\n/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service\n.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →\nenvelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.\n\n**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST\n/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`\nexisting → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural\n`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no\n`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |\n| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |\n| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |\n| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |\n| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |\n| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |\n| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |\n| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |\n| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |\n| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |\n| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |\n| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |\n| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |\n| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |\n| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |\n| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |\n| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |\n| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |\n| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |\n| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |\n| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |\n| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |\n| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |\n| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |\n| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |\n\n## Status\n\n`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no\nopen gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond\nthe NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker).\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-05\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Section, SectionMember, Course and Enrollment, plus enums CourseKind (CORE/ELECTIVE) and EnrollmentStatus (ACTIVE/DROPPED), exactly per the schema block given, including the @@unique([academicYearId, name]) on Section, @@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember, @@unique([academicYearId, code]) on Course and @@unique([courseId, studentId]) + @@index([studentId, status]) on Enrollment.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Build /admin/sections: filtered by academic year (defaults to current, reusing the existing AcademicYear model), with a table of name, grade level, homeroom teacher, room, members/capacity (warning colour at >=90%), and course count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"Section create/edit dialog: grade level, name, homeroom teacher (UserPicker filtered to role=TEACHER — the existing src/components/UserPicker already supports a role filter), room, capacity; a teacher may be homeroom teacher of at most one section per academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; verified against existing src/components/UserPicker/UserPicker.tsx which already accepts a `role` prop\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Build /admin/sections/[id]: members table with add (multi-select student picker filtered to the section's grade level and to students without a section this year) and remove; the section's course list; a 'Create core courses' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"'Create core courses' dialog: lists all active (non-archived) subjects with a checkbox and a teacher picker per subject; submitting creates one CORE course per checked subject with the default name/code pattern and enrolls all current section members in each created course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"'Copy sections to next year' action on /admin/sections, enabled only when a non-current, future academic year exists; copies section name, grade level advanced to the next GradeLevel by `order`, room and capacity, without members or teacher assignments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Auto-enroll on section add: adding a student to a section enrolls them ACTIVE in every non-archived CORE course of that section; a previously DROPPED enrollment in one of those courses is reactivated rather than duplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Auto-drop on section removal: removing a student from a section sets every ACTIVE enrollment in that section's CORE courses to DROPPED with droppedAt = now; elective enrollments are left untouched.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"'Move to section…' single action performs the FR-7 enroll and FR-8 drop steps for the destination/source sections in one database transaction, exposed via POST /api/students/:id/move-section.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3; API table row POST /api/students/:id/move-section\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Creating a new CORE course on a section enrolls all of that section's current members (ACTIVE) in the new course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Capacity enforcement: adding a student beyond section or course capacity is refused with a CONFLICT error, message pattern 'Section 7A is full (30/30).', unless the admin explicitly ticks 'Override capacity'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criteria #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Dropped enrollments retain all historical data (attendance, grades) visible to admins and teachers, but dropped students disappear from active rosters and from add-student pickers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses: filters for academic year, grade level, subject, teacher, kind, and free-text search by name/code; table of code, name, subject colour chip (reusing Subject.color, already on the model), section, teacher, enrolled count, kind.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1; verified Subject.color already exists on the Subject model in prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (optional, required when kind=CORE), teacher, up to 3 co-teachers, name, code (auto-filled from subject+section, editable, forced uppercase), kind, capacity, description.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses/[id]/enrollment: enrolled-students table with drop/reactivate row actions and an 'Add students' picker; for CORE courses show an info note that membership is managed via the section instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /courses/[courseId] header: subject colour band, course name, code, teacher(s) (including co-teachers), section, room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add a course-tabs registry at src/config/course-tabs.ts (same shape as the existing src/config/student-tabs.ts, with a `roles` field) rendered as a scrollable MUI Tabs on the course home page; this PRD registers 'Overview' (description/teachers/counts, all roles that can view the course) and 'Roster' (TEACHER/ADMIN: full student list with avatar/name/admission number/link to student page/status; STUDENT: classmates' names only; PARENT: tab not shown).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; verified against the existing (empty) src/config/student-tabs.ts pattern this PRD is told to mirror\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add src/server/auth/course-access.ts exporting assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN: all; TEACHER: teacher or co-teacher; STUDENT: has an ACTIVE enrollment; PARENT: any linked child has an ACTIVE enrollment) and assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN, teacher, co-teacher) for later write operations.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Build /my-courses: TEACHER sees MUI Cards in a responsive Grid for each non-archived course they teach/co-teach this year (name, section, enrolled count); STUDENT sees cards for their ACTIVE enrollments (name, teacher); PARENT sees the same cards grouped by child.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Add sidebar nav entries: 'My courses' for TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT, and 'Sections'/'Courses' grouped under an 'Administration' section for ADMIN. NavItem currently has no grouping field — src/config/navigation.ts (verified) is a flat array with only Dashboard/Notifications/Email log entries and no 'group' concept, and no admin-facing pages exist yet for the PRD-02/PRD-03 entities (academic years, subjects, rooms, grade levels, users) that would also belong in such a group. The Architect must decide whether to add a lightweight `group` field to NavItem now or ship Sections/Courses as flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav grouping PRD lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; cross-checked against the current flat src/config/navigation.ts and the absence of an 'Administration' grouping or admin pages anywhere under src/app/(app)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Register student tab 'Courses' in src/config/student-tabs.ts (visible to every role that can view the student): a table of the student's courses this year with teacher and enrollment status, plus their section and homeroom teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing getAccessibleStudentIds(user) in src/server/auth/student-access.ts so a TEACHER additionally gets students with ACTIVE enrollments in courses they teach or co-teach, plus members of the section they are homeroom teacher of.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1; verified getAccessibleStudentIds already exists and is exported from src/server/auth/student-access.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Expose the full REST surface from the API table: sections CRUD + members + move-section + core-courses + copy-to-year; courses CRUD + roster + enrollments + enrollment status PATCH; GET /api/me/courses — each with the role gating shown in the table and the existing success/list/error response envelope and pagination/sort/search query conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Every write (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*) records an AuditLog row via the existing audit() helper.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table footnote 'All writes audit (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*)'; verified audit() already exists and is exported from src/server/audit.ts\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element in the section/course/enrollment screens is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the MUI X packages (DataGrid via the existing shared DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, Snackbar+Alert via useToast()); every component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select, etc.) in this PRD's code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD); Compliance Rule 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Integrity: the one-section-per-student-per-year rule is enforced by the database unique constraint (@@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember), not only in application code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: adding 30 students to a section with 8 core courses (240 resulting enrollments) completes in under 1 second.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Privacy: on the course Roster tab and GET /api/courses/:id/roster, students see classmates' names only — no emails, admission numbers or profile links in the response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3; Acceptance Criteria #7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Scope containment: no timetable slots (PRD-06), no course content (PRD-08), no prerequisite or course-request workflows, and no automatic year-to-year student promotion — only the manual 'Copy sections to next year' shortcut.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization gap carried forward from PRD-01/PRD-04: the Platform Context describes src/server/auth/permissions.ts exposing requireUser()/requireRole(...roles), but only src/server/auth/requireRole.ts and student-access.ts exist today (no permissions.ts, no requireUser()). New route handlers in this PRD must use the existing requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)-style stand-in (as PRD-04's handoff also flagged) rather than invent a new auth helper, until PRD-01 lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement), cross-checked against the current contents of src/server/auth/ (only requireRole.ts and student-access.ts present)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6e489fc-abc2-4cf6-8575-95ca4cd13810","uuid":"4f736101-1019-4899-bd94-2aae65d3ad6f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:42:54.655Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Ticket abcd-05: execute the dev phase (task dev-main). Read prior phase artifacts under artifacts/, follow dev.md, and write this phase's artifacts to artifacts/dev/.\n\nContinue. Remaining: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5, TASK-6, TASK-7, TASK-8, TASK-9, TASK-10, TASK-11, TASK-12, TASK-13, TASK-14, TASK-15, TASK-16, TASK-17, TASK-18, TASK-19# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic\nstructure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03\n(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04\n(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both\nresolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps.\n\n**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s\n`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the\nfirst requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"\nunder an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the\ngrouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional\nfield, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small\nMUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;\nitems without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change\nthat satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages\nregistry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add\n`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they\nland, with no further schema change.\n\n**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from\nPRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described\nin the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new\n`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around\n`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object\n`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and\ndoes **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.\nConsolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is\nexplicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not\nschedule that consolidation here.\n\n**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two\nservice-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:\nFR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section\nrequired iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity\nchecks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same\n`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted\nas good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write\nconcurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to\nfix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on\nthese two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,\nhomeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)\n`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus\n`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including\nall four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what\nFR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below\nreads/writes.\n\n### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`\nThe single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,\nFR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions\n(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens\nits own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per\ntech-stack ADR-1):\n\n- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`\n  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below\n  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A\n  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per\n  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per\n  route.\n- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing\n  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs\n  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no\n  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip\n  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row\n  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course\n  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).\n- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:\n  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE\n  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls\n  `audit()`.\n- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then\n  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,\n  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`.\n\nFR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both\ncreate `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the\nsection's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry\npoints, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic.\n\nFR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active\nrosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter\napplied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,\ncourse roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes.\n\n### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,\nFR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)\nand the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level\nadvanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not\nreusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot\nstructural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on\n`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement\nenroll/drop.\n\n### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`\n(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"\nvalidator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side\ncheck and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a\nrefinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on\na non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`\ncreate/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,\nreused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this\npicker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead.\n\n### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`\nFR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and\n`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per\nDecision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by\n`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster\nendpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once\nhere, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's\nstated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this\nPRD's scope.\n\n### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\nFR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER\nbranch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section\nmembership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/\nPRD-04 callers unchanged.\n\n### Course public surface\n`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing\n`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers\n`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;\nSTUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`\nfiltering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a\nread-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.\n\n**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'\nnames only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query\n(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when\n`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component\nand `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the\ndata layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.\n\n### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)\nRead view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query\n(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE\nenrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,\ngrouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —\nno new parent-fanout code).\n\n### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)\n`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible\nflat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get\n`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.\n\n### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)\nNew \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +\nteacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses\nFR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the\nstudent page (no new access function).\n\n### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`\nEvery route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`\n→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the\nexisting success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route\nlayer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside\nthe same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it\ninternally so routes don't duplicate the call.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**\n`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST\n/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens\n`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →\n`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the\nuniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course\n`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →\ncommit → envelope response.\n\n**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →\n`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping\n`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old\nCORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for\nthe whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.\n\n**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →\n`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`\n(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course\nagainst current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.\n\n**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET\n/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service\n.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →\nenvelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.\n\n**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST\n/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`\nexisting → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural\n`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no\n`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |\n| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |\n| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |\n| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |\n| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |\n| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |\n| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |\n| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |\n| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |\n| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |\n| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |\n| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |\n| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |\n| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |\n| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |\n| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |\n| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |\n| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |\n| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |\n| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |\n| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |\n| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |\n| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |\n| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |\n| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |\n\n## Status\n\n`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no\nopen gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond\nthe NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker).\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-05\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Section, SectionMember, Course and Enrollment, plus enums CourseKind (CORE/ELECTIVE) and EnrollmentStatus (ACTIVE/DROPPED), exactly per the schema block given, including the @@unique([academicYearId, name]) on Section, @@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember, @@unique([academicYearId, code]) on Course and @@unique([courseId, studentId]) + @@index([studentId, status]) on Enrollment.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Build /admin/sections: filtered by academic year (defaults to current, reusing the existing AcademicYear model), with a table of name, grade level, homeroom teacher, room, members/capacity (warning colour at >=90%), and course count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"Section create/edit dialog: grade level, name, homeroom teacher (UserPicker filtered to role=TEACHER — the existing src/components/UserPicker already supports a role filter), room, capacity; a teacher may be homeroom teacher of at most one section per academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; verified against existing src/components/UserPicker/UserPicker.tsx which already accepts a `role` prop\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Build /admin/sections/[id]: members table with add (multi-select student picker filtered to the section's grade level and to students without a section this year) and remove; the section's course list; a 'Create core courses' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"'Create core courses' dialog: lists all active (non-archived) subjects with a checkbox and a teacher picker per subject; submitting creates one CORE course per checked subject with the default name/code pattern and enrolls all current section members in each created course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"'Copy sections to next year' action on /admin/sections, enabled only when a non-current, future academic year exists; copies section name, grade level advanced to the next GradeLevel by `order`, room and capacity, without members or teacher assignments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Auto-enroll on section add: adding a student to a section enrolls them ACTIVE in every non-archived CORE course of that section; a previously DROPPED enrollment in one of those courses is reactivated rather than duplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Auto-drop on section removal: removing a student from a section sets every ACTIVE enrollment in that section's CORE courses to DROPPED with droppedAt = now; elective enrollments are left untouched.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"'Move to section…' single action performs the FR-7 enroll and FR-8 drop steps for the destination/source sections in one database transaction, exposed via POST /api/students/:id/move-section.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3; API table row POST /api/students/:id/move-section\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Creating a new CORE course on a section enrolls all of that section's current members (ACTIVE) in the new course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Capacity enforcement: adding a student beyond section or course capacity is refused with a CONFLICT error, message pattern 'Section 7A is full (30/30).', unless the admin explicitly ticks 'Override capacity'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criteria #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Dropped enrollments retain all historical data (attendance, grades) visible to admins and teachers, but dropped students disappear from active rosters and from add-student pickers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses: filters for academic year, grade level, subject, teacher, kind, and free-text search by name/code; table of code, name, subject colour chip (reusing Subject.color, already on the model), section, teacher, enrolled count, kind.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1; verified Subject.color already exists on the Subject model in prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (optional, required when kind=CORE), teacher, up to 3 co-teachers, name, code (auto-filled from subject+section, editable, forced uppercase), kind, capacity, description.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses/[id]/enrollment: enrolled-students table with drop/reactivate row actions and an 'Add students' picker; for CORE courses show an info note that membership is managed via the section instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /courses/[courseId] header: subject colour band, course name, code, teacher(s) (including co-teachers), section, room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add a course-tabs registry at src/config/course-tabs.ts (same shape as the existing src/config/student-tabs.ts, with a `roles` field) rendered as a scrollable MUI Tabs on the course home page; this PRD registers 'Overview' (description/teachers/counts, all roles that can view the course) and 'Roster' (TEACHER/ADMIN: full student list with avatar/name/admission number/link to student page/status; STUDENT: classmates' names only; PARENT: tab not shown).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; verified against the existing (empty) src/config/student-tabs.ts pattern this PRD is told to mirror\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add src/server/auth/course-access.ts exporting assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN: all; TEACHER: teacher or co-teacher; STUDENT: has an ACTIVE enrollment; PARENT: any linked child has an ACTIVE enrollment) and assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN, teacher, co-teacher) for later write operations.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Build /my-courses: TEACHER sees MUI Cards in a responsive Grid for each non-archived course they teach/co-teach this year (name, section, enrolled count); STUDENT sees cards for their ACTIVE enrollments (name, teacher); PARENT sees the same cards grouped by child.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Add sidebar nav entries: 'My courses' for TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT, and 'Sections'/'Courses' grouped under an 'Administration' section for ADMIN. NavItem currently has no grouping field — src/config/navigation.ts (verified) is a flat array with only Dashboard/Notifications/Email log entries and no 'group' concept, and no admin-facing pages exist yet for the PRD-02/PRD-03 entities (academic years, subjects, rooms, grade levels, users) that would also belong in such a group. The Architect must decide whether to add a lightweight `group` field to NavItem now or ship Sections/Courses as flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav grouping PRD lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; cross-checked against the current flat src/config/navigation.ts and the absence of an 'Administration' grouping or admin pages anywhere under src/app/(app)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Register student tab 'Courses' in src/config/student-tabs.ts (visible to every role that can view the student): a table of the student's courses this year with teacher and enrollment status, plus their section and homeroom teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing getAccessibleStudentIds(user) in src/server/auth/student-access.ts so a TEACHER additionally gets students with ACTIVE enrollments in courses they teach or co-teach, plus members of the section they are homeroom teacher of.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1; verified getAccessibleStudentIds already exists and is exported from src/server/auth/student-access.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Expose the full REST surface from the API table: sections CRUD + members + move-section + core-courses + copy-to-year; courses CRUD + roster + enrollments + enrollment status PATCH; GET /api/me/courses — each with the role gating shown in the table and the existing success/list/error response envelope and pagination/sort/search query conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Every write (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*) records an AuditLog row via the existing audit() helper.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table footnote 'All writes audit (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*)'; verified audit() already exists and is exported from src/server/audit.ts\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element in the section/course/enrollment screens is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the MUI X packages (DataGrid via the existing shared DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, Snackbar+Alert via useToast()); every component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select, etc.) in this PRD's code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD); Compliance Rule 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Integrity: the one-section-per-student-per-year rule is enforced by the database unique constraint (@@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember), not only in application code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: adding 30 students to a section with 8 core courses (240 resulting enrollments) completes in under 1 second.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Privacy: on the course Roster tab and GET /api/courses/:id/roster, students see classmates' names only — no emails, admission numbers or profile links in the response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3; Acceptance Criteria #7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Scope containment: no timetable slots (PRD-06), no course content (PRD-08), no prerequisite or course-request workflows, and no automatic year-to-year student promotion — only the manual 'Copy sections to next year' shortcut.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization gap carried forward from PRD-01/PRD-04: the Platform Context describes src/server/auth/permissions.ts exposing requireUser()/requireRole(...roles), but only src/server/auth/requireRole.ts and student-access.ts exist today (no permissions.ts, no requireUser()). New route handlers in this PRD must use the existing requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)-style stand-in (as PRD-04's handoff also flagged) rather than invent a new auth helper, until PRD-01 lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement), cross-checked against the current contents of src/server/auth/ (only requireRole.ts and student-access.ts present)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TXibBTjdtohVaqqf2opsfV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
