{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DUK9q8gH1UnGekGjudxFxd","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:03:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"conventions\": {\n    \"basePath\": \"/api (existing project convention; no /api/v1 prefix - NFR-9 forbids renaming routes)\",\n    \"successEnvelope\": { \"data\": \"<responseSchema>\" },\n    \"errorEnvelope\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"string\", \"message\": \"string\", \"details\": \"object?\" } },\n    \"errorCodes\": {\n      \"VALIDATION_ERROR\": 400,\n      \"UNAUTHENTICATED\": 401,\n      \"FORBIDDEN\": 403,\n      \"INVALID_TOKEN\": 410,\n      \"RATE_LIMITED\": 429\n    },\n    \"handlerPattern\": \"withHandler(parseBody(zodSchema) -> service -> ok()) from src/server/http.ts\",\n    \"csrf\": \"src/middleware.ts rejects non-GET/HEAD /api/* requests whose Origin header is present and differs from the app origin (403 FORBIDDEN). The Auth.js endpoints also use their own CSRF token. Session cookie: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in prod.\",\n    \"unauthenticatedApi\": \"src/middleware.ts returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED for /api/* outside PUBLIC_API_PATHS ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']\",\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\", \"NFR-9\", \"FR-12\"]\n  },\n\n  \"endpoints\": [\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint, served by the /api/auth/[...nextauth] catch-all (handlers.GET). Returns the CSRF token that signIn()/signOut() use. Public.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" } } },\n      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native (not the {data} envelope)\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"GET\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint (catch-all). Returns the current session or null. Public. Middleware does not gate it.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {},\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"oneOf\": [\n          { \"type\": \"null\" },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"user\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"id\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                  \"role\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"ADMIN\", \"TEACHER\", \"STUDENT\", \"PARENT\"] },\n                  \"firstName\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                  \"lastName\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                  \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\" }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\"id\", \"role\", \"firstName\", \"lastName\", \"email\"]\n              },\n              \"expires\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\" }\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-10\", \"FR-34\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js Credentials sign-in (catch-all handlers.POST). Credentials.authorize delegates to authorizeCredentials(): IP rate limit (10 / 5 min) -> trim + lower-case the email -> exactly one bcrypt compare (DUMMY_HASH if the user is missing) -> status/archived/lock checks -> lockout bookkeeping -> audit. On success the jwt callback sets {id, role, firstName, lastName, email, authTime, checkedAt}, maxAge 8h, updateAge 15m. The client calls it through signIn('credentials', {redirect:false}) and reads the error code.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public (Auth.js CSRF token)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\", \"transform\": \"trim + toLowerCase\" },\n          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"callbackUrl\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"note\": \"sanitised by safeCallbackUrl(): only a relative path starting with '/' and not '//' or '/\\\\'; otherwise /dashboard\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"email\", \"password\", \"csrfToken\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"success\": { \"sets-cookie\": \"authjs.session-token (__Secure- prefix in prod)\", \"url\": \"safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)\" },\n        \"failure\": {\n          \"type\": \"object\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"error\": { \"const\": \"CredentialsSignin\" },\n            \"code\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"enum\": [\"invalid\", \"disabled\", \"locked:<minutes>\", \"rate_limited\"],\n              \"uiMessages\": {\n                \"invalid\": \"Email or password is incorrect.\",\n                \"disabled\": \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\",\n                \"locked:N\": \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\",\n                \"rate_limited\": \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"sideEffects\": [\n        \"wrong password: failedLoginCount += 1; at 5 -> lockedUntil = now + 15 min, failedLoginCount = 0\",\n        \"success: failedLoginCount = 0, lastLoginAt = now\",\n        \"audit auth.login.success | auth.login.failure {email, reason} | auth.lockout, with the IP from x-forwarded-for\"\n      ],\n      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-3\", \"FR-4\", \"FR-5\", \"FR-6\", \"FR-7\", \"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-4\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\",\n      \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out (catch-all). Clears the session cookie. The shell calls it through signOut({redirectTo:'/login'}).\",\n      \"auth\": \"public (Auth.js CSRF token)\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": { \"csrfToken\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"callbackUrl\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n        \"required\": [\"csrfToken\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": { \"url\": \"/login\" },\n      \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\",\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-32\", \"FR-34\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/accept-invite\",\n      \"description\": \"Activates an invited account. Flow: verifyToken(token, 'INVITE') -> assertPasswordAllowed -> bcrypt.hash(12) -> one transaction {passwordHash, status=ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt=now} + consumeToken -> audit auth.invite.accepted. It does NOT mint a session: on 200 the client calls signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo:'/dashboard'}). Public via the /api/auth/ prefix and protected by the middleware origin check.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/accept-invite/route.ts -> services/auth.acceptInvite\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"zod\": \"acceptInviteSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"token\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"raw base64url token from /invite/<token>\" },\n          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"≥1 letter, ≥1 digit, != email, not in common-passwords.txt\" },\n          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"must equal password (client and zod refine)\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"token\", \"password\", \"confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\" } }, \"required\": [\"email\"] } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"password\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\", \"message\": \"Cross-origin request rejected\" } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-13\", \"FR-16\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"FR-37\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Requests a password-reset link. Over 10 requests per IP per hour -> 429. Over 3 requests per email per hour -> silent generic 200 (no enumeration). Only an existing ACTIVE user gets createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min), which invalidates older unused reset tokens, plus sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). Unknown or inactive emails write nothing. The response body is always identical.\",\n      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/forgot-password/route.ts -> services/auth.requestPasswordReset\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"zod\": \"forgotPasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": { \"email\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\", \"transform\": \"trim + toLowerCase\" } },\n        \"required\": [\"email\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"message\": { \"const\": \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" } } } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"email\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n        \"429\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"RATE_LIMITED\", \"message\": \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-2\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-19\", \"FR-20\", \"FR-22\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-3\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\",\n      \"description\": \"Completes a reset. Flow: verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET') -> assertPasswordAllowed -> hash -> one transaction {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt=now, failedLoginCount=0, lockedUntil=null} + consumeToken -> audit auth.password.reset. The client then redirects to /login?reset=1, which shows a useToast success toast. Existing sessions are revoked within 5 min by the jwt callback (passwordChangedAt > authTime).\",\n      \"auth\": \"public + origin check\",\n      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/reset-password/route.ts -> services/auth.resetPassword\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"zod\": \"resetPasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"token\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"password\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"same as accept-invite\" },\n          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"token\", \"password\", \"confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"ok\": { \"const\": true } } } },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"password\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\" } },\n        \"410\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"INVALID_TOKEN\", \"message\": \"This reset link is invalid or has expired.\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-11\", \"FR-13\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-21\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"NFR-1\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"path\": \"/api/account/password\",\n      \"description\": \"Changes the signed-in user's password. Flow: await requireUser() -> bcrypt-compare currentPassword -> assertPasswordAllowed(newPassword, email) -> hash -> update {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt=now} -> audit auth.password.changed -> unstable_update({reauth:true}), so this session's authTime moves past passwordChangedAt. Other sessions fail the jwt check within 5 min. The UI shows the 'Password updated' toast.\",\n      \"auth\": \"session required (middleware 401 + requireUser())\",\n      \"handler\": \"src/app/api/account/password/route.ts -> services/auth.changePassword\",\n      \"requestSchema\": {\n        \"zod\": \"changePasswordSchema\",\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"currentPassword\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"newPassword\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"same as accept-invite\" },\n          \"confirm\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"currentPassword\", \"newPassword\", \"confirm\"]\n      },\n      \"responseSchema\": {\n        \"200\": { \"data\": { \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": { \"ok\": { \"const\": true } } }, \"sets-cookie\": \"re-issued session token\" },\n        \"400\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"details\": { \"fieldErrors\": { \"currentPassword\": [\"Current password is incorrect.\"], \"newPassword\": [\"string\"], \"confirm\": [\"string\"] } } } },\n        \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\" } },\n        \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\", \"message\": \"Cross-origin request rejected\" } }\n      },\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-11\", \"FR-17\", \"FR-23\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-30\", \"FR-31\", \"NFR-2\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-8\"]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"changedBehaviourOnExistingEndpoints\": {\n    \"description\": \"Every existing route handler (33 route.ts files) changes from requireRole(...) to await requireRole(...), backed by the real session. Paths, request shapes and response shapes don't change. New possible responses on all of them:\",\n    \"responses\": {\n      \"401\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"UNAUTHENTICATED\" }, \"source\": \"middleware (no session) or requireUser/requireRole (session revoked)\" },\n      \"403\": { \"error\": { \"code\": \"FORBIDDEN\" }, \"source\": \"requireRole role mismatch, or the middleware cross-origin check on mutations\" }\n    },\n    \"unchanged\": [\"/api/health stays public\"],\n    \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-12\", \"FR-28\", \"FR-29\", \"NFR-7\", \"NFR-9\"]\n  },\n\n  \"explicitlyAbsent\": [\n    { \"item\": \"No sign-up / register endpoint\", \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-37\"] },\n    { \"item\": \"No admin user-management, SSO, MFA or magic-link endpoints\", \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-11\"] },\n    { \"item\": \"No /api/v1 prefix; existing /api convention kept\", \"requirementIds\": [\"NFR-9\"] }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"schoolhub\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=18.18.0\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"next dev\",\n    \"build\": \"next build\",\n    \"start\": \"next start\",\n    \"lint\": \"next lint\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:e2e\": \"playwright test\",\n    \"db:migrate\": \"prisma migrate dev\",\n    \"db:deploy\": \"prisma migrate deploy\",\n    \"db:seed\": \"tsx prisma/seed.ts\",\n    \"db:reset\": \"prisma migrate reset --force\",\n    \"worker:email\": \"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\",\n    \"format\": \"prettier --write .\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@emotion/react\": \"11.13.3\",\n    \"@emotion/styled\": \"11.13.0\",\n    \"@hookform/resolvers\": \"3.9.0\",\n    \"@mui/icons-material\": \"9.5.0\",\n    \"@mui/material\": \"9.5.0\",\n    \"@mui/material-nextjs\": \"9.5.0\",\n    \"@