{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W2phwogqtbYn6345mgnFW3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"method\": \"GET\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\", \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint, served by the /api/auth/[...nextauth] catch-all (handlers.GET). Returns the CSRF token that signIn()/signOut() use. Public.\", \"auth\": \"public\", \"requestSchema\": {}, \"responseSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"csrfToken\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}}, \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native (not the {data} envelope)\", \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\"]}\n\n{\"method\": \"GET\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\", \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint (catch-all). Returns the current session or null. Public. Middleware does not gate it.\", \"auth\": \"public\", \"requestSchema\": {}, \"responseSchema\": {\"oneOf\": [{\"type\": \"null\"}, {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"user\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"role\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"ADMIN\", \"TEACHER\", \"STUDENT\", \"PARENT\"]}, \"firstName\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"lastName\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"email\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"role\", \"firstName\", \"lastName\", \"email\"]}, \"expires\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\"}}}]}, \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\", \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-10\", \"FR-34\"]}\n\n{\"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/callback/credentials\", \"description\": \"Auth.js Credentials sign-in (catch-all handlers.POST). Credentials.authorize delegates to authorizeCredentials(): IP rate limit (10 / 5 min) -> trim + lower-case the email -> exactly one bcrypt compare (DUMMY_HASH if the user is missing) -> status/archived/lock checks -> lockout bookkeeping -> audit. On success the jwt callback sets {id, role, firstName, lastName, email, authTime, checkedAt}, maxAge 8h, updateAge 15m. The client calls it through signIn('credentials', {redirect:false}) and reads the error code.\", \"auth\": \"public (Auth.js CSRF token)\", \"requestSchema\": {\"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"email\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\", \"transform\": \"trim + toLowerCase\"}, \"password\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"csrfToken\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"callbackUrl\": \n\n{\"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/signout\", \"description\": \"Auth.js sign-out (catch-all). Clears the session cookie. The shell calls it through signOut({redirectTo:'/login'}).\", \"auth\": \"public (Auth.js CSRF token)\", \"requestSchema\": {\"contentType\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"csrfToken\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"callbackUrl\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"csrfToken\"]}, \"responseSchema\": {\"url\": \"/login\"}, \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native\", \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-32\", \"FR-34\"]}\n\n{\"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/accept-invite\", \"description\": \"Activates an invited account. Flow: verifyToken(token, 'INVITE') -> assertPasswordAllowed -> bcrypt.hash(12) -> one transaction {passwordHash, status=ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt=now} + consumeToken -> audit auth.invite.accepted. It does NOT mint a session: on 200 the client calls signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo:'/dashboard'}). Public via the /api/auth/ prefix and protected by the middleware origin check.\", \"auth\": \"public + origin check\", \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/accept-invite/route.ts -> services/auth.acceptInvite\", \"requestSchema\": {\"zod\": \"acceptInviteSchema\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"token\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"raw base64url token from /invite/<token>\"}, \"password\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"\\u22651 letter, \\u22651 digit, != email, \n\n{\"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/forgot-password\", \"description\": \"Requests a password-reset link. Over 10 requests per IP per hour -> 429. Over 3 requests per email per hour -> silent generic 200 (no enumeration). Only an existing ACTIVE user gets createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min), which invalidates older unused reset tokens, plus sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). Unknown or inactive emails write nothing. The response body is always identical.\", \"auth\": \"public + origin check\", \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/forgot-password/route.ts -> services/auth.requestPasswordReset\", \"requestSchema\": {\"zod\": \"forgotPasswordSchema\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"email\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"email\", \"transform\": \"trim + toLowerCase\"}}, \"required\": [\"email\"]}, \"responseSchema\": {\"200\": {\"data\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"message\": {\"const\": \"If an account exists fo\n\n{\"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/reset-password\", \"description\": \"Completes a reset. Flow: verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET') -> assertPasswordAllowed -> hash -> one transaction {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt=now, failedLoginCount=0, lockedUntil=null} + consumeToken -> audit auth.password.reset. The client then redirects to /login?reset=1, which shows a useToast success toast. Existing sessions are revoked within 5 min by the jwt callback (passwordChangedAt > authTime).\", \"auth\": \"public + origin check\", \"handler\": \"src/app/api/auth/reset-password/route.ts -> services/auth.resetPassword\", \"requestSchema\": {\"zod\": \"resetPasswordSchema\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"token\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"password\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"same as accept-invite\"}, \"confirm\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"token\", \"password\", \"confirm\"]}, \"res\n\n{\"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"/api/account/password\", \"description\": \"Changes the signed-in user's password. Flow: await requireUser() -> bcrypt-compare currentPassword -> assertPasswordAllowed(newPassword, email) -> hash -> update {passwordHash, passwordChangedAt=now} -> audit auth.password.changed -> unstable_update({reauth:true}), so this session's authTime moves past passwordChangedAt. Other sessions fail the jwt check within 5 min. The UI shows the 'Password updated' toast.\", \"auth\": \"session required (middleware 401 + requireUser())\", \"handler\": \"src/app/api/account/password/route.ts -> services/auth.changePassword\", \"requestSchema\": {\"zod\": \"changePasswordSchema\", \"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"currentPassword\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"newPassword\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 10, \"maxLength\": 128, \"policy\": \"same as accept-invite\"}, \"confirm\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46abff3e-324d-47c1-a451-e45bcb70c7c7","uuid":"ab0e3c0a-98b1-4f3e-9859-7734004964c1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:51:28.893Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"method\": \"GET\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/csrf\", \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint, served by the /api/auth/[...nextauth] catch-all (handlers.GET). Returns the CSRF token that signIn()/signOut() use. Public.\", \"auth\": \"public\", \"requestSchema\": {}, \"responseSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"csrfToken\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}}, \"envelope\": \"Auth.js native (not the {data} envelope)\", \"requirementIds\": [\"FR-34\", \"NFR-2\"]}\n\n{\"method\": \"GET\", \"path\": \"/api/auth/session\", \"description\": \"Auth.js protocol endpoint (catch-all). Returns the current session or null. Public. Middleware does not gate it.\", \"auth\": \"public\", \"requestSchema\": {}, \"responseSchema\": {\"oneOf\": [{\"type\": \"null\"}, {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"user\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"role\"