{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UdduoVU83pajTvRcdL3udK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),\n6\t`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),\n7\t`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n8\t`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (brownfield facts B1–B11).\n9\t\n10\t## Overview\n11\t\n12\tPRD-04 adds two delivery channels on top of the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 app:\n13\t\n14\t1. **In-app notifications.** These are `Notification` rows, shown by a polling bell in the shell, a\n15\t   `/notifications` page and a `/account/notifications` preferences page.\n16\t2. **Transactional email through a DB outbox.** Requests only *insert* `EmailOutbox` rows. A\n17\t   dispatcher, run from a cron-hit route or a tsx worker loop, claims them with\n18\t   `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and sends them through Nodemailer or the console transport.\n19\t\n20\tProducers use a single entry point, `notify()`. The only other producer is the existing\n21\t`sendAuthEmail()` seam, which now enqueues instead of logging. **No new dependencies,\n22\tno schema edits and no new infrastructure** are needed. One additive migration creates the\n23\talready-declared tables.\n24\t\n25\t### Intake blockers and how this design handles them\n26\t\n27\t| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n28\t|---|---|\n29\t| FR-1: models declared but no migration | **Resolved.** One migration, `notifications_email`, generated from the unchanged `schema.prisma`. The additive `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `EmailOutbox.updatedAt` is the SENDING timestamp for NFR-5 (ADR-1). |\n30\t| FR-4/FR-16: auth emails bypass notify()? | **Confirmed.** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly, with no Notification row and no preference lookup. `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are registered as `emailOnly: true` and are hidden from preferences (FR-28, FR-37) and rejected by the PUT (FR-38). Unlike notify(), `sendAuthEmail` **keeps throwing on failure**. Both callers already await it, and a silently lost invite or reset is worse than a 500. |\n31\t| FR-40: seed count ambiguous | **Default accepted:** 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread), linking to `/dashboard`. **New finding (B2):** `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` do not exist in `prisma/seed.ts`. The seed looks each user up by email and **skips with a log line** if the user is missing. It does not create identity data that another PRD owns. For idempotency, the seed skips a user who already has any `system.test` notification. |\n32\t| NFR-10: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Carried to dev as a precondition.** mui-mcp is reachable at architect time, and dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` per component before writing UI. If mui-mcp is unreachable during dev, that is a hard stop. |\n33\t\n34\t### New blocker-level finding (B1)\n35\t\n36\t`src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for every `/api/*` request without a session unless\n37\t`isPublicPath()` matches. Cron calls carry no cookie, so `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\n38\twould never reach its handler. **Add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** in\n39\t`src/config/public-routes.ts`. The trailing slash gives a prefix match. The handler's CRON_SECRET check\n40\tthen becomes the sole gate (NFR-8), so it must be strict (timing-safe, unset secret → 401).\n41\t\n42\t## Component Breakdown\n43\t\n44\t### 1. Data layer (FR-1)\n45\t\n46\t- `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/migration.sql` is generated with\n47\t  `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name notifications_email` and must sort after `*_auth_reconcile`.\n48\t- The tables are `Notification` (index `[userId, readAt, createdAt]`, cascade FK), `NotificationPreference`\n49\t  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).\n50\t- `type` stays a plain `String` (ADR-2). Notification has no `category` column, so the category is\n51\t  derived from the registry at query time.\n52\t\n53\t### 2. Notification type registry: `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (FR-2..5)\n54\t\n55\t```ts\n56\texport const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT','ACADEMIC','ATTENDANCE','COMMUNICATION','FINANCE','SYSTEM'] as const;\n57\texport type NotificationCategory = typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES[number];\n58\ttype NotificationTypeDef = { label; description; category: NotificationCategory; defaultEmail: boolean;\n59\t  mandatoryInApp: boolean; roles: readonly Role[]; emailOnly?: true };\n60\texport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {\n61\t  'account.invite':         { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n62\t  'account.password_reset': { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n63\t  'system.test':            { category: 'SYSTEM',  defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, roles: ALL },\n64\t} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;\n65\texport type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\t- The module must stay **client-safe**, with no `prisma` or `env` imports. Role values are imported as a type, or\n69\t  as string literals, so the validators and client pages can import it (ADR-2).\n70\t- Helpers in the same file: `visibleTypesFor(role)` filters `roles.includes(role) && !emailOnly`, and\n71\t  `typesInCategory(cat)` returns keys for the FR-34 filter.\n72\t- Later PRDs add keys to this object. There is no runtime registration API.\n73\t\n74\t### 3. Shared validators: `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` (FR-41, NFR-6, NFR-18)\n75\t\n76\t- `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` returns true only if the string starts with `/`, `s[1]` is not `/` or `\\`, it contains no `\\`\n77\t  anywhere and it has no control characters (ADR-10).\n78\t- `listNotificationsQuery` defines `unread?: 'true'|'false'` and `category?: z.enum(NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)`. Pagination\n79\t  goes through the existing `parsePagination`.\n80\t- `updatePreferenceBody` is `{ type: z.string(), inApp: z.boolean(), email: z.boolean() }`. The service checks\n81\t  `type` against the registry and the role (see §6).\n82\t- `TITLE_MAX = 140` and `BODY_MAX = 500`.\n83\t\n84\t### 4. Notify service: `src/server/notifications/` (FR-6..12, NFR-1, NFR-18)\n85\t\n86\t| File | Exports | Notes |\n87\t|---|---|---|\n88\t| `preferences.ts` | `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }` (pure), `getPreferencesFor(user)`, `updatePreference(user, body)` | `inApp = def.mandatoryInApp \\|\\| (row?.inApp ?? true)`; `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` |\n89\t| `notify.ts` | `notify(input)`, `notifyStudentAndParents(input)`, `expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links)` (pure) | see flow below |\n90\t| `purge.ts` | `purgeOldNotifications(now)` | `deleteMany({ createdAt: { lt: now − 180d } })` |\n91\t\n92\t`notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })` works as follows:\n93\t\n94\t1. Normalise the input. Dedupe `userIds`. Truncate the title to 140 characters and the body to 500, with `logger.warn` on truncation (NFR-18).\n95\t   Drop an unsafe `link` (store `null`, `logger.warn`) (NFR-6).\n96\t2. **Round-trip 1:** `user.findMany({ id in, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` (FR-7).\n97\t3. **Round-trip 2:** `notificationPreference.findMany({ userId in, type })` (FR-7).\n98\t4. `resolvePrefs` per user gives the in-app and email recipient lists.\n99\t5. **Round-trip 3:** `notification.createMany(inAppRows)` (FR-8). 1,000 rows × about 7 columns is well under the\n100\t   65,535 parameter limit, so there is no chunking.\n101\t6. If any email recipients have `user.email`, fetch `SchoolSettings` once, render the template **once per call**\n102\t   (ADR-6), then **round-trip 4:** `emailOutbox.createMany(rows)` with the shared html/text (FR-9).\n103\t   That makes 2 round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, within FR-10's limit of 3 each.\n104\t7. The whole body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`. It returns `void` and **never throws** (FR-11). The JSDoc\n105\t   says: \"call after your transaction commits\".\n106\t\n107\t`notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` makes one `parentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call,\n108\tpasses the result through `expandStudentRecipients` (students ∪ parents, deduped with a `Set`), then calls `notify` (FR-12).\n109\t\n110\t*Generic emails have no per-recipient greeting.* That is what makes render-once possible and keeps NFR-1 under 2 s.\n111\tA later PRD that wants personalisation must revisit NFR-1.\n112\t\n113\t### 5. Email subsystem: `src/server/email/` (FR-13..21, NFR-3..5, NFR-7, NFR-9)\n114\t\n115\t| File | Responsibility |\n116\t|---|---|\n117\t| `templates/BaseLayout.tsx` | Header with logo and name, then content, then a footer with the address, a \"Manage email preferences\" link to `${APP_URL}/account/notifications` and the fixed sentence (FR-14). Props: `school: Pick<SchoolSettings,'name'\\|'shortName'\\|'logoUrl'\\|'addressLine1'\\|'addressLine2'>`. |\n118\t| `templates/Invite.tsx` | Name, school name, accept button and expiry date (FR-15). |\n119\t| `templates/PasswordReset.tsx` | Link plus \"This link expires in 60 minutes.\" (FR-15) |\n120\t| `templates/GenericNotification.tsx` | Title, body (`white-space: pre-line`, as text) and a CTA to `APP_URL + link` (FR-15). |\n121\t| `render.ts` | `TEMPLATES = { invite, 'password-reset', 'generic-notification' }` and `renderEmail(template, data, school) → Promise<{html,text}>`, which awaits both `render()` calls (`@react-email/render` 1.x is async). No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` anywhere (NFR-7). |\n122\t| `outbox.ts` | `enqueueEmail({ toEmail, toName, subject, html, text })` → `emailOutbox.create`. Used by `sendAuthEmail`. `notify()` uses `createMany` directly. |\n123\t| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |\n124\t| `transport.ts` | `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`. `if (env.EMAIL_TRANSPORT === 'smtp')` uses a lazily created Nodemailer transport with `from: EMAIL_FROM` and `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' }`. Otherwise it uses `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text (FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11). A missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` throws inside `sendMail`, so the dispatcher records it as a retryable failure. |\n125\t| `dispatch.ts` | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 } = {}) → { sent, failed, retried }` (FR-17). See the data flow below. |\n126\t\n127\t**Auth email seam (FR-16).** In `src/server/auth/email.ts`, only the body of `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` changes.\n128\tIt loads SchoolSettings, calls `renderEmail(kind, …)`, then calls `enqueueEmail({ toEmail: user.email, toName: user.firstName, subject: SUBJECTS[kind], … })`.\n129\tThe invite expiry date is `now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS`. Move the literal `{ days: 7 }` in `users.ts:384`\n130\tto an exported `INVITE_TTL = { days: 7 }` in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, used by both, so the email cannot drift\n131\tfrom the real token TTL. The signature and both call sites (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`) stay unchanged.\n132\tThe raw link is no longer logged.\n133\t\n134\t### 6. HTTP API: thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok` / `paginated` (NFR-8, NFR-11)\n135\t\n136\t| Route file | Guard | Service call |\n137\t|---|---|---|\n138\t| `src/app/api/notifications/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `listNotifications(me, query, page)`, with `where: { userId: me.id, readAt: unread ? null : undefined, type: category ? { in: typesInCategory(c) } : undefined }` and `orderBy createdAt desc` (FR-34) |\n139\t| `src/app/api/notifications/unread-count/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `count({ userId, readAt: null })`, which is index-only (FR-35, NFR-2) |\n140\t| `src/app/api/notifications/read-all/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null }, { readAt: now })` (FR-36) |\n141\t| `src/app/api/notifications/[id]/read/route.ts` POST, `[id]/unread/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ id, userId: me.id })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, so the existence of other users' rows is not revealed (FR-36) |\n142\t| `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` GET / PUT | `requireUser` | GET: `getPreferencesFor(me)` → `visibleTypesFor(me.role)` merged with rows (FR-37). PUT: `updatePreference(me, body)` rejects unknown, emailOnly or role-invisible types and `inApp:false` on mandatory types with `VALIDATION_ERROR`, then upserts on `userId_type` (FR-38) |\n143\t| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` GET | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | Paginated `emailOutbox.findMany` with an optional `status` filter, ordered by `createdAt desc`, **selecting no html or text** (FR-39) |\n144\t| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |\n145\t| `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title: 'Test notification', body, link: '/dashboard', email: { template: 'generic-notification', … } })` (FR-33) |\n146\t| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` POST | CRON_SECRET bearer (timing-safe, unset → 401) | `dispatchEmails()`, then the best-effort purge if more than 24 h have passed since the module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-19, FR-27). The purge has its own `try/catch` and never fails the response |\n147\t\n148\tThe service functions for the user and admin routes live in `src/server/notifications/service.ts` (list, count,\n149\tmark read/unread, read-all) and `src/server/email/admin.ts` (log list, retry). These are thin Prisma calls, kept\n150\tout of the route files so the routes stay thin, per the NFR-11 convention.\n151\t\n152\t### 7. Background job: `scripts/worker-email.ts` (FR-20, NFR-3)\n153\t\n154\t`while (running) { try { await dispatchEmails() } catch (e) { logger.error } await sleep(15_000) }`. A SIGINT\n155\tor SIGTERM sets `running = false` and disconnects Prisma. The loop calls the service directly. It does not purge,\n156\tbecause only the endpoint runs the purge. It runs through the existing `npm run worker:email` script.\n157\t\n158\t### 8. UI: MUI v9 only, using `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before each component (NFR-10)\n159\t\n160\t| Surface | File(s) | Components and behaviour |\n161\t|---|---|---|\n162\t| Bell (FR-22..25) | `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` (`'use client'`). In `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, replace the placeholder `Tooltip > IconButton > NotificationsNoneIcon` with `<NotificationBell />` | `IconButton` + `Badge max={9}` gives \"9+\" natively. One `useEffect` runs `setInterval(30s)` while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`, clears it on hidden and refetches on visible. When the `Popover` opens, it fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10`. Rows use `List` / `ListItemButton`, with bold text and a dot for unread items, `Typography` with a 2-line `WebkitLineClamp`, and `formatDistanceToNowStrict`. On click: `POST /:id/read` → `router.push(link)` (only if `isSafeRelativeLink`) → close → refetch the count. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n163\t| Notifications page (FR-26) | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `NotificationsList.tsx` (client) | `PageHeader`, `Tabs` (All / Unread), a category `Select`, a `List` with a per-row read/unread `IconButton`, `Pagination` with a page size of 20, a bulk \"Mark all as read\" and `EmptyState`. |\n164\t| Preferences (FR-28..30) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `PreferencesTable.tsx` (client) | A `Table` with one full-width `TableRow` header per category. Columns: label, description, an \"In app\" `Switch` and an \"Email\" `Switch`. Mandatory rows show a disabled Switch inside `<span>` inside `Tooltip \"Required by the school\"`. Changes update local state optimistically, call `PUT`, and revert plus `useToast` error on failure. |\n165\t| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |\n166\t\n167\tThe server pages pass `SchoolSettings.timezone` down as a prop for absolute times (NFR-12). Relative times do\n168\tnot depend on the timezone. Navigation entries already exist and are not touched (NFR-13).\n169\t\n170\t### 9. Seed: append to `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-40)\n171\t\n172\tFor each of `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`: run `findUnique`. If the user is missing, `console.log` a skip\n173\tmessage, since the seed is a script and is outside the NFR-11 logger rule. If the user already has `system.test` notifications, skip.\n174\tOtherwise, `createMany` 3 rows linking to `/dashboard`, 1 read and 2 unread.\n175\t\n176\t### 10. Tests (NFR-14..16, ADR-9)\n177\t\n178\t- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: covers `resolvePrefs`, `nextRetry`, `isSafeRelativeLink` (including `//evil`, `/\\evil`,\n179\t  `http://x` and control characters) and `expandStudentRecipients` dedupe.\n180\t- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`: uses `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`.\n181\t  Add `'tests/integration/**/*.test.ts'` to `vitest.config.ts` `include`. The cases are 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails()` calls\n182\t  over 10 PENDING rows, with `sendMail` mocked, asserting each id is sent exactly once (AC-4), and a SENDING row with `updatedAt`\n183\t  set to now − 11 min returning to PENDING.\n184\t- `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`: admin test button → bell count +1 → mark all read → count 0. Then toggle a\n185\t  preference, reload and check that it persisted.\n186\t\n187\t## Data Flow\n188\t\n189\t### A. Producer → in-app and outbox (request path, no SMTP; NFR-3)\n190\t\n191\t```\n192\tcaller service (after its tx commits)\n193\t  └─ notify()/notifyStudentAndParents()\n194\t       ├─ normalise (truncate, safe link)          NFR-6, NFR-18\n195\t       ├─ users.findMany (active only)             FR-7\n196\t       ├─ prefs.findMany → resolvePrefs            FR-7\n197\t       ├─ notification.createMany                  FR-8, FR-10\n198\t       └─ renderEmail once → emailOutbox.createMany FR-9, FR-13\n199\t  errors → logger.error, never thrown             FR-11\n200\t\n201\tusers.ts sendInvite / auth.ts requestPasswordReset\n202\t  └─ sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)  → renderEmail(invite|password-reset) → emailOutbox.create   FR-16\n203\t```\n204\t\n205\t### B. Dispatcher (cron route or worker; FR-17, FR-18, NFR-4, NFR-5)\n206\t\n207\t```\n208\tdispatchEmails({ batchSize: 50 })\n209\t 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5\n210\t 2. claim:    $queryRaw`UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\", \"updatedAt\"=now()\n211\t              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()\n212\t                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n213\t              RETURNING *`        -- single autocommit stmt; no lock held during SMTP     NFR-4\n214\t 3. for each claimed row (sequential):\n215\t      sendMail(row)  ok   → update { status: SENT, sentAt: now }                 → sent++\n216\t                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →\n217\t                              PENDING + nextAttemptAt (retried++) | FAILED (failed++)   FR-18\n218\t 4. return { sent, failed, retried }\n219\t```\n220\t\n221\tTriggers: the `worker:email` 15 s loop, **or** cron calling `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` at least once a minute. Either path\n222\tmeets NFR-3's 60 s delivery limit. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING, and step 1 recovers it, giving at-least-once delivery on crash.\n223\t\n224\t### C. Consumer UI\n225\t\n226\t```\n227\tBell ──30s poll (visible only)──► GET /api/notifications/unread-count  (index [userId, readAt, createdAt])\n228\t     ──open──► GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10\n229\t     ──click──► POST /api/notifications/:id/read → router.push(link)\n230\t     ──footer──► POST /api/notifications/read-all | Link /notifications\n231\tPrefs page ──► GET/PUT /api/me/notification-preferences (optimistic, rollback + toast)\n232\tEmail log  ──► GET /api/admin/email-log?status= | POST /:id/retry | POST /api/admin/notifications/test\n233\t```\n234\t\n235\t### D. Housekeeping\n236\t\n237\tThe dispatch route runs `purgeOldNotifications()` at most once per 24 h per process\n238\t(`// ponytail: in-memory lastPurgeAt, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`) (FR-27).\n239\t\n240\t## Files\n241\t\n242\t- **New:** the migration; `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,service,purge}.ts`;\n243\t  `src/server/email/{render,outbox,backoff,transport,dispatch,admin}.ts`; `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`;\n244\t  `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`; the 9 route files in §6; `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`;\n245\t  the 3 pages plus their client components in §8; `scripts/worker-email.ts`; and the tests in §10.\n246\t- **Modified:** `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only); `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` (+`INVITE_TTL`) and `src/server/services/users.ts:384`\n247\t  (use it); `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (the bell); `src/config/public-routes.ts` (+`'/api/internal/'`); `prisma/seed.ts` (append); and\n248\t  `vitest.config.ts` (+integration glob).\n249\t- **Untouched:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `.env.example`, `src/config/navigation.ts` and `package.json`.\n250\t\n251\t## Out of scope (NFR-17)\n252\t\n253\tNo SMS, push, websockets, digests, channel abstraction, queue library, rate limit on the test button or\n254\tper-recipient email personalisation.\n255\t\n256\t## Requirements Traceability\n257\t\n258\t| Req | Design element |\n259\t|---|---|\n260\t| FR-1 | §1 migration `notifications_email` (ADR-1) |\n261\t| FR-2 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` |\n262\t| FR-3 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` / `NotificationCategory` |\n263\t| FR-4 | §2 `account.invite`, `account.password_reset` (`emailOnly`), `system.test` |\n264\t| FR-5 | §2 `NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` |\n265\t| FR-6 | §4 `notify()` in `notify.ts` |\n266\t| FR-7 | §4 steps 2–4, `resolvePrefs` in `preferences.ts` |\n267\t| FR-8 | §4 step 5, `notification.createMany` |\n268\t| FR-9 | §4 step 6, `emailOutbox.createMany` |\n269\t| FR-10 | §4 round-trip budget (2 notification, 3 email) |\n270\t| FR-11 | §4 step 7 try/catch, never throws |\n271\t| FR-12 | §4 `notifyStudentAndParents` + `expandStudentRecipients` |\n272\t| FR-13 | §5 `templates/*.tsx` + `render.ts` |\n273\t| FR-14 | §5 `BaseLayout.tsx` |\n274\t| FR-15 | §5 `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification` |\n275\t| FR-16 | §5 auth email seam (`sendAuthEmail` body → `enqueueEmail`) |\n276\t| FR-17 | §5 `dispatch.ts`, Data Flow B |\n277\t| FR-18 | §5 `backoff.ts` `nextRetry`, Data Flow B step 3 |\n278\t| FR-19 | §6 `api/internal/email/dispatch` route, B1 allowlist |\n279\t| FR-20 | §7 `scripts/worker-email.ts` |\n280\t| FR-21 | §5 `transport.ts` |\n281\t| FR-22 | §8 Bell, `Badge max={9}`, shell.tsx replacement |\n282\t| FR-23 | §8 Bell visibility-gated 30 s poll |\n283\t| FR-24 | §8 Bell Popover list |\n284\t| FR-25 | §8 Bell click and footer actions |\n285\t| FR-26 | §8 Notifications page |\n286\t| FR-27 | §5/§6 `purge.ts`, Data Flow D |\n287\t| FR-28 | §8 Preferences table, `visibleTypesFor` (§2) |\n288\t| FR-29 | §8 disabled Switch + Tooltip \"Required by the school\" |\n289\t| FR-30 | §8 optimistic PUT + rollback toast |\n290\t| FR-31 | §8 Admin email log |\n291\t| FR-32 | §6 retry route, §8 \"Retry now\" |\n292\t| FR-33 | §6 admin test route, §8 header button |\n293\t| FR-34 | §6 `GET /api/notifications` |\n294\t| FR-35 | §6 `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` |\n295\t| FR-36 | §6 `[id]/read`, `[id]/unread`, `read-all` |\n296\t| FR-37 | §6 `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` |\n297\t| FR-38 | §6 `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`, §3 `updatePreferenceBody` |\n298\t| FR-39 | §6 admin email-log GET + retry |\n299\t| FR-40 | §9 seed (lookup-or-skip, idempotent) |\n300\t| FR-41 | §3 `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` |\n301\t| NFR-1 | §4 render-once + `createMany`, Overview note on personalisation |\n302\t| NFR-2 | §6 unread-count on `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index |\n303\t| NFR-3 | Data Flow A (enqueue only), §7 15 s worker / ≤1 min cron |\n304\t| NFR-4 | Data Flow B step 2 `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claim |\n305\t| NFR-5 | Data Flow B step 1 stuck-SENDING recovery via `updatedAt` |\n306\t| NFR-6 | §3 `isSafeRelativeLink`, §4 step 1, §8 bell `router.push` guard |\n307\t| NFR-7 | §5 JSX escaping, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |\n308\t| NFR-8 | §6 guard column; Overview B1 + timing-safe CRON_SECRET |\n309\t| NFR-9 | §5 `transport.ts` html + text + `List-Unsubscribe` |\n310\t| NFR-10 | §8 MUI-only, mui-mcp precondition (Overview blockers) |\n311\t| NFR-11 | §6 thin handlers, services under `src/server/{notifications,email}`, logger |\n312\t| NFR-12 | §8 `formatInSchoolTz` with timezone prop |\n313\t| NFR-13 | Files section: untouched list, additive changes only |\n314\t| NFR-14 | §10 unit tests |\n315\t| NFR-15 | §10 integration tests (gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) |\n316\t| NFR-16 | §10 Playwright spec |\n317\t| NFR-17 | Out of scope section |\n318\t| NFR-18 | §3 `TITLE_MAX` / `BODY_MAX`, §4 step 1 truncation |\n319\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1921163e-32be-4c5c-99f3-b230ef406493","uuid":"7b8adeda-77c7-4d77-90f2-aea7d1039d06","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:54:44.671Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (brownfield facts B1–B11).\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 adds two delivery channels on top of the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 app:\n\n1. **In-app notifications.** These are `Notification` rows, shown by a polling bell in the shell, a\n   `/notifications` page and a `/account/notifications` preferences page.\n2. **Transactional email through a DB outbox.** Requests only *insert* `EmailOutbox` rows. A\n   dispatcher, run from a cron-hit route or a tsx worker loop, claims them with\n   `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and sends them through Nodemailer or the console transport.\n\nProducers use a single entry point, `notify()`. The only other producer is the existing\n`sendAuthEmail()` seam, which now enqueues instead of logging. **No new dependencies,\nno schema edits and no new infrastructure** are needed. One additive migration creates the\nalready-declared tables.\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design handles them\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1: models declared but no migration | **Resolved.** One migration, `notifications_email`, generated from the unchanged `schema.prisma`. The additive `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `EmailOutbox.updatedAt` is the SENDING timestamp for NFR-5 (ADR-1). |\n| FR-4/FR-16: auth emails bypass notify()? | **Confirmed.** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly, with no Notification row and no preference lookup. `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are registered as `emailOnly: true` and are hidden from preferences (FR-28, FR-37) and rejected by the PUT (FR-38). Unlike notify(), `sendAuthEmail` **keeps throwing on failure**. Both callers already await it, and a silently lost invite or reset is worse than a 500. |\n| FR-40: seed count ambiguous | **Default accepted:** 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread), linking to `/dashboard`. **New finding (B2):** `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` do not exist in `prisma/seed.ts`. The seed looks each user up by email and **skips with a log line** if the user is missing. It does not create identity data that another PRD owns. For idempotency, the seed skips a user who already has any `system.test` notification. |\n| NFR-10: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Carried to dev as a precondition.** mui-mcp is reachable at architect time, and dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` per component before writing UI. If mui-mcp is unreachable during dev, that is a hard stop. |\n\n### New blocker-level finding (B1)\n\n`src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for every `/api/*` request without a session unless\n`isPublicPath()` matches. Cron calls carry no cookie, so `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\nwould never reach its handler. **Add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** in\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`. The trailing slash gives a prefix match. The handler's CRON_SECRET check\nthen becomes the sole gate (NFR-8), so it must be strict (timing-safe, unset secret → 401).\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data layer (FR-1)\n\n- `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/migration.sql` is generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name notifications_email` and must sort after `*_auth_reconcile`.\n- The tables are `Notification` (index `[userId, readAt, createdAt]`, cascade FK), `NotificationPreference`\n  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).\n- `type` stays a plain `String` (ADR-2). Notification has no `category` column, so the category is\n  derived from the registry at query time.\n\n### 2. Notification type registry: `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (FR-2..5)\n\n```ts\nexport const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT','ACADEMIC','ATTENDANCE','COMMUNICATION','FINANCE','SYSTEM'] as const;\nexport type NotificationCategory = typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES[number];\ntype NotificationTypeDef = { label; description; category: NotificationCategory; defaultEmail: boolean;\n  mandatoryInApp: boolean; roles: readonly Role[]; emailOnly?: true };\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {\n  'account.invite':         { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'account.password_reset': { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'system.test':            { category: 'SYSTEM',  defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, roles: ALL },\n} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;\nexport type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;\n```\n\n- The module must stay **client-safe**, with no `prisma` or `env` imports. Role values are imported as a type, or\n  as string literals, so the validators and client pages can import it (ADR-2).\n- Helpers in the same file: `visibleTypesFor(role)` filters `roles.includes(role) && !emailOnly`, and\n  `typesInCategory(cat)` returns keys for the FR-34 filter.\n- Later PRDs add keys to this object. There is no runtime registration API.\n\n### 3. Shared validators: `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` (FR-41, NFR-6, NFR-18)\n\n- `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` returns true only if the string starts with `/`, `s[1]` is not `/` or `\\`, it contains no `\\`\n  anywhere and it has no control characters (ADR-10).\n- `listNotificationsQuery` defines `unread?: 'true'|'false'` and `category?: z.enum(NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)`. Pagination\n  goes through the existing `parsePagination`.\n- `updatePreferenceBody` is `{ type: z.string(), inApp: z.boolean(), email: z.boolean() }`. The service checks\n  `type` against the registry and the role (see §6).\n- `TITLE_MAX = 140` and `BODY_MAX = 500`.\n\n### 4. Notify service: `src/server/notifications/` (FR-6..12, NFR-1, NFR-18)\n\n| File | Exports | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `preferences.ts` | `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }` (pure), `getPreferencesFor(user)`, `updatePreference(user, body)` | `inApp = def.mandatoryInApp \\|\\| (row?.inApp ?? true)`; `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` |\n| `notify.ts` | `notify(input)`, `notifyStudentAndParents(input)`, `expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links)` (pure) | see flow below |\n| `purge.ts` | `purgeOldNotifications(now)` | `deleteMany({ createdAt: { lt: now − 180d } })` |\n\n`notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })` works as follows:\n\n1. Normalise the input. Dedupe `userIds`. Truncate the title to 140 characters and the body to 500, with `logger.warn` on truncation (NFR-18).\n   Drop an unsafe `link` (store `null`, `logger.warn`) (NFR-6).\n2. **Round-trip 1:** `user.findMany({ id in, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` (FR-7).\n3. **Round-trip 2:** `notificationPreference.findMany({ userId in, type })` (FR-7).\n4. `resolvePrefs` per user gives the in-app and email recipient lists.\n5. **Round-trip 3:** `notification.createMany(inAppRows)` (FR-8). 1,000 rows × about 7 columns is well under the\n   65,535 parameter limit, so there is no chunking.\n6. If any email recipients have `user.email`, fetch `SchoolSettings` once, render the template **once per call**\n   (ADR-6), then **round-trip 4:** `emailOutbox.createMany(rows)` with the shared html/text (FR-9).\n   That makes 2 round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, within FR-10's limit of 3 each.\n7. The whole body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`. It returns `void` and **never throws** (FR-11). The JSDoc\n   says: \"call after your transaction commits\".\n\n`notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` makes one `parentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call,\npasses the result through `expandStudentRecipients` (students ∪ parents, deduped with a `Set`), then calls `notify` (FR-12).\n\n*Generic emails have no per-recipient greeting.* That is what makes render-once possible and keeps NFR-1 under 2 s.\nA later PRD that wants personalisation must revisit NFR-1.\n\n### 5. Email subsystem: `src/server/email/` (FR-13..21, NFR-3..5, NFR-7, NFR-9)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `templates/BaseLayout.tsx` | Header with logo and name, then content, then a footer with the address, a \"Manage email preferences\" link to `${APP_URL}/account/notifications` and the fixed sentence (FR-14). Props: `school: Pick<SchoolSettings,'name'\\|'shortName'\\|'logoUrl'\\|'addressLine1'\\|'addressLine2'>`. |\n| `templates/Invite.tsx` | Name, school name, accept button and expiry date (FR-15). |\n| `templates/PasswordReset.tsx` | Link plus \"This link expires in 60 minutes.\" (FR-15) |\n| `templates/GenericNotification.tsx` | Title, body (`white-space: pre-line`, as text) and a CTA to `APP_URL + link` (FR-15). |\n| `render.ts` | `TEMPLATES = { invite, 'password-reset', 'generic-notification' }` and `renderEmail(template, data, school) → Promise<{html,text}>`, which awaits both `render()` calls (`@react-email/render` 1.x is async). No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` anywhere (NFR-7). |\n| `outbox.ts` | `enqueueEmail({ toEmail, toName, subject, html, text })` → `emailOutbox.create`. Used by `sendAuthEmail`. `notify()` uses `createMany` directly. |\n| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |\n| `transport.ts` | `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`. `if (env.EMAIL_TRANSPORT === 'smtp')` uses a lazily created Nodemailer transport with `from: EMAIL_FROM` and `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' }`. Otherwise it uses `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text (FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11). A missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` throws inside `sendMail`, so the dispatcher records it as a retryable failure. |\n| `dispatch.ts` | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 } = {}) → { sent, failed, retried }` (FR-17). See the data flow below. |\n\n**Auth email seam (FR-16).** In `src/server/auth/email.ts`, only the body of `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` changes.\nIt loads SchoolSettings, calls `renderEmail(kind, …)`, then calls `enqueueEmail({ toEmail: user.email, toName: user.firstName, subject: SUBJECTS[kind], … })`.\nThe invite expiry date is `now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS`. Move the literal `{ days: 7 }` in `users.ts:384`\nto an exported `INVITE_TTL = { days: 7 }` in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, used by both, so the email cannot drift\nfrom the real token TTL. The signature and both call sites (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`) stay unchanged.\nThe raw link is no longer logged.\n\n### 6. HTTP API: thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok` / `paginated` (NFR-8, NFR-11)\n\n| Route file | Guard | Service call |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/notifications/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `listNotifications(me, query, page)`, with `where: { userId: me.id, readAt: unread ? null : undefined, type: category ? { in: typesInCategory(c) } : undefined }` and `orderBy createdAt desc` (FR-34) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/unread-count/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `count({ userId, readAt: null })`, which is index-only (FR-35, NFR-2) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/read-all/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null }, { readAt: now })` (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/[id]/read/route.ts` POST, `[id]/unread/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ id, userId: me.id })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, so the existence of other users' rows is not revealed (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` GET / PUT | `requireUser` | GET: `getPreferencesFor(me)` → `visibleTypesFor(me.role)` merged with rows (FR-37). PUT: `updatePreference(me, body)` rejects unknown, emailOnly or role-invisible types and `inApp:false` on mandatory types with `VALIDATION_ERROR`, then upserts on `userId_type` (FR-38) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` GET | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | Paginated `emailOutbox.findMany` with an optional `status` filter, ordered by `createdAt desc`, **selecting no html or text** (FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title: 'Test notification', body, link: '/dashboard', email: { template: 'generic-notification', … } })` (FR-33) |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` POST | CRON_SECRET bearer (timing-safe, unset → 401) | `dispatchEmails()`, then the best-effort purge if more than 24 h have passed since the module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-19, FR-27). The purge has its own `try/catch` and never fails the response |\n\nThe service functions for the user and admin routes live in `src/server/notifications/service.ts` (list, count,\nmark read/unread, read-all) and `src/server/email/admin.ts` (log list, retry). These are thin Prisma calls, kept\nout of the route files so the routes stay thin, per the NFR-11 convention.\n\n### 7. Background job: `scripts/worker-email.ts` (FR-20, NFR-3)\n\n`while (running) { try { await dispatchEmails() } catch (e) { logger.error } await sleep(15_000) }`. A SIGINT\nor SIGTERM sets `running = false` and disconnects Prisma. The loop calls the service directly. It does not purge,\nbecause only the endpoint runs the purge. It runs through the existing `npm run worker:email` script.\n\n### 8. UI: MUI v9 only, using `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before each component (NFR-10)\n\n| Surface | File(s) | Components and behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bell (FR-22..25) | `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` (`'use client'`). In `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, replace the placeholder `Tooltip > IconButton > NotificationsNoneIcon` with `<NotificationBell />` | `IconButton` + `Badge max={9}` gives \"9+\" natively. One `useEffect` runs `setInterval(30s)` while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`, clears it on hidden and refetches on visible. When the `Popover` opens, it fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10`. Rows use `List` / `ListItemButton`, with bold text and a dot for unread items, `Typography` with a 2-line `WebkitLineClamp`, and `formatDistanceToNowStrict`. On click: `POST /:id/read` → `router.push(link)` (only if `isSafeRelativeLink`) → close → refetch the count. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| Notifications page (FR-26) | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `NotificationsList.tsx` (client) | `PageHeader`, `Tabs` (All / Unread), a category `Select`, a `List` with a per-row read/unread `IconButton`, `Pagination` with a page size of 20, a bulk \"Mark all as read\" and `EmptyState`. |\n| Preferences (FR-28..30) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `PreferencesTable.tsx` (client) | A `Table` with one full-width `TableRow` header per category. Columns: label, description, an \"In app\" `Switch` and an \"Email\" `Switch`. Mandatory rows show a disabled Switch inside `<span>` inside `Tooltip \"Required by the school\"`. Changes update local state optimistically, call `PUT`, and revert plus `useToast` error on failure. |\n| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |\n\nThe server pages pass `SchoolSettings.timezone` down as a prop for absolute times (NFR-12). Relative times do\nnot depend on the timezone. Navigation entries already exist and are not touched (NFR-13).\n\n### 9. Seed: append to `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-40)\n\nFor each of `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`: run `findUnique`. If the user is missing, `console.log` a skip\nmessage, since the seed is a script and is outside the NFR-11 logger rule. If the user already has `system.test` notifications, skip.\nOtherwise, `createMany` 3 rows linking to `/dashboard`, 1 read and 2 unread.\n\n### 10. Tests (NFR-14..16, ADR-9)\n\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: covers `resolvePrefs`, `nextRetry`, `isSafeRelativeLink` (including `//evil`, `/\\evil`,\n  `http://x` and control characters) and `expandStudentRecipients` dedupe.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`: uses `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`.\n  Add `'tests/integration/**/*.test.ts'` to `vitest.config.ts` `include`. The cases are 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails()` calls\n  over 10 PENDING rows, with `sendMail` mocked, asserting each id is sent exactly once (AC-4), and a SENDING row with `updatedAt`\n  set to now − 11 min returning to PENDING.\n- `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`: admin test button → bell count +1 → mark all read → count 0. Then toggle a\n  preference, reload and check that it persisted.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n### A. Producer → in-app and outbox (request path, no SMTP; NFR-3)\n\n```\ncaller service (after its tx commits)\n  └─ notify()/notifyStudentAndParents()\n       ├─ normalise (truncate, safe link)          NFR-6, NFR-18\n       ├─ users.findMany (active only)             FR-7\n       ├─ prefs.findMany → resolvePrefs            FR-7\n       ├─ notification.createMany                  FR-8, FR-10\n       └─ renderEmail once → emailOutbox.createMany FR-9, FR-13\n  errors → logger.error, never thrown             FR-11\n\nusers.ts sendInvite / auth.ts requestPasswordReset\n  └─ sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)  → renderEmail(invite|password-reset) → emailOutbox.create   FR-16\n```\n\n### B. Dispatcher (cron route or worker; FR-17, FR-18, NFR-4, NFR-5)\n\n```\ndispatchEmails({ batchSize: 50 })\n 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5\n 2. claim:    $queryRaw`UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\", \"updatedAt\"=now()\n              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()\n                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n              RETURNING *`        -- single autocommit stmt; no lock held during SMTP     NFR-4\n 3. for each claimed row (sequential):\n      sendMail(row)  ok   → update { status: SENT, sentAt: now }                 → sent++\n                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →\n                              PENDING + nextAttemptAt (retried++) | FAILED (failed++)   FR-18\n 4. return { sent, failed, retried }\n```\n\nTriggers: the `worker:email` 15 s loop, **or** cron calling `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` at least once a minute. Either path\nmeets NFR-3's 60 s delivery limit. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING, and step 1 recovers it, giving at-least-once delivery on crash.\n\n### C. Consumer UI\n\n```\nBell ──30s poll (visible only)──► GET /api/notifications/unread-count  (index [userId, readAt, createdAt])\n     ──open──► GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10\n     ──click──► POST /api/notifications/:id/read → router.push(link)\n     ──footer──► POST /api/notifications/read-all | Link /notifications\nPrefs page ──► GET/PUT /api/me/notification-preferences (optimistic, rollback + toast)\nEmail log  ──► GET /api/admin/email-log?status= | POST /:id/retry | POST /api/admin/notifications/test\n```\n\n### D. Housekeeping\n\nThe dispatch route runs `purgeOldNotifications()` at most once per 24 h per process\n(`// ponytail: in-memory lastPurgeAt, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`) (FR-27).\n\n## Files\n\n- **New:** the migration; `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,service,purge}.ts`;\n  `src/server/email/{render,outbox,backoff,transport,dispatch,admin}.ts`; `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`;\n  `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`; the 9 route files in §6; `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`;\n  the 3 pages plus their client components in §8; `scripts/worker-email.ts`; and the tests in §10.\n- **Modified:** `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only); `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` (+`INVITE_TTL`) and `src/server/services/users.ts:384`\n  (use it); `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (the bell); `src/config/public-routes.ts` (+`'/api/internal/'`); `prisma/seed.ts` (append); and\n  `vitest.config.ts` (+integration glob).\n- **Untouched:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `.env.example`, `src/config/navigation.ts` and `package.json`.\n\n## Out of scope (NFR-17)\n\nNo SMS, push, websockets, digests, channel abstraction, queue library, rate limit on the test button or\nper-recipient email personalisation.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §1 migration `notifications_email` (ADR-1) |\n| FR-2 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` / `NotificationCategory` |\n| FR-4 | §2 `account.invite`, `account.password_reset` (`emailOnly`), `system.test` |\n| FR-5 | §2 `NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` |\n| FR-6 | §4 `notify()` in `notify.ts` |\n| FR-7 | §4 steps 2–4, `resolvePrefs` in `preferences.ts` |\n| FR-8 | §4 step 5, `notification.createMany` |\n| FR-9 | §4 step 6, `emailOutbox.createMany` |\n| FR-10 | §4 round-trip budget (2 notification, 3 email) |\n| FR-11 | §4 step 7 try/catch, never throws |\n| FR-12 | §4 `notifyStudentAndParents` + `expandStudentRecipients` |\n| FR-13 | §5 `templates/*.tsx` + `render.ts` |\n| FR-14 | §5 `BaseLayout.tsx` |\n| FR-15 | §5 `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification` |\n| FR-16 | §5 auth email seam (`sendAuthEmail` body → `enqueueEmail`) |\n| FR-17 | §5 `dispatch.ts`, Data Flow B |\n| FR-18 | §5 `backoff.ts` `nextRetry`, Data Flow B step 3 |\n| FR-19 | §6 `api/internal/email/dispatch` route, B1 allowlist |\n| FR-20 | §7 `scripts/worker-email.ts` |\n| FR-21 | §5 `transport.ts` |\n| FR-22 | §8 Bell, `Badge max={9}`, shell.tsx replacement |\n| FR-23 | §8 Bell visibility-gated 30 s poll |\n| FR-24 | §8 Bell Popover list |\n| FR-25 | §8 Bell click and footer actions |\n| FR-26 | §8 Notifications page |\n| FR-27 | §5/§6 `purge.ts`, Data Flow D |\n| FR-28 | §8 Preferences table, `visibleTypesFor` (§2) |\n| FR-29 | §8 disabled Switch + Tooltip \"Required by the school\" |\n| FR-30 | §8 optimistic PUT + rollback toast |\n| FR-31 | §8 Admin email log |\n| FR-32 | §6 retry route, §8 \"Retry now\" |\n| FR-33 | §6 admin test route, §8 header button |\n| FR-34 | §6 `GET /api/notifications` |\n| FR-35 | §6 `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` |\n| FR-36 | §6 `[id]/read`, `[id]/unread`, `read-all` |\n| FR-37 | §6 `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` |\n| FR-38 | §6 `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`, §3 `updatePreferenceBody` |\n| FR-39 | §6 admin email-log GET + retry |\n| FR-40 | §9 seed (lookup-or-skip, idempotent) |\n| FR-41 | §3 `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` |\n| NFR-1 | §4 render-once + `createMany`, Overview note on personalisation |\n| NFR-2 | §6 unread-count on `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index |\n| NFR-3 | Data Flow A (enqueue only), §7 15 s worker / ≤1 min cron |\n| NFR-4 | Data Flow B step 2 `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claim |\n| NFR-5 | Data Flow B step 1 stuck-SENDING recovery via `updatedAt` |\n| NFR-6 | §3 `isSafeRelativeLink`, §4 step 1, §8 bell `router.push` guard |\n| NFR-7 | §5 JSX escaping, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |\n| NFR-8 | §6 guard column; Overview B1 + timing-safe CRON_SECRET |\n| NFR-9 | §5 `transport.ts` html + text + `List-Unsubscribe` |\n| NFR-10 | §8 MUI-only, mui-mcp precondition (Overview blockers) |\n| NFR-11 | §6 thin handlers, services under `src/server/{notifications,email}`, logger |\n| NFR-12 | §8 `formatInSchoolTz` with timezone prop |\n| NFR-13 | Files section: untouched list, additive changes only |\n| NFR-14 | §10 unit tests |\n| NFR-15 | §10 integration tests (gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) |\n| NFR-16 | §10 Playwright spec |\n| NFR-17 | Out of scope section |\n| NFR-18 | §3 `TITLE_MAX` / `BODY_MAX`, §4 step 1 truncation |\n","numLines":319,"startLine":1,"totalLines":319}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UdduoVU83pajTvRcdL3udK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
