{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016oipa1XBjWa9mrrEaxx9k4","type":"tool_result","content":"42-}\n43-\n44:enum EmailStatus {\n45-  PENDING\n46-  SENDING\n47-  SENT\n48-  FAILED\n49-}\n50-\n51-/// Every authenticated person. passwordHash is nullable because an INVITED\n52-/// user has no password until they accept their invite (TASK-8's\n53-/// acceptInvite step sets both passwordHash and status=ACTIVE together).\n54-/// phone and archivedAt are added here (PRD-03/TASK-1) because they are the\n55-/// only task in this PRD that owns schema.prisma: phone is FR-3's common\n56-/// field shared by every role, archivedAt backs FR-13's archive/restore\n57-/// (separate from status so a DISABLED-but-not-archived user stays distinct\n58-/// from an archived one).\n59-model User {\n60-  id                      String                   @id @default(cuid())\n61-  email                   String                   @unique\n62-  passwordHash            String?\n63-  firstName               String\n64-  lastName                String\n65-  phone                   String?\n66-  role                    Role\n67-  status                  UserStatus               @default(INVITED)\n68-  failedLoginCount        Int                      @default(0)\n69-  lockedUntil             DateTime?\n70-  lastLoginAt             DateTime?\n71-  passwordChangedAt       DateTime?\n72-  archivedAt              DateTime?\n73-  createdAt               DateTime                 @default(now())\n74-  updatedAt               DateTime                 @updatedAt\n--\n285-/// stored here. The composite index backs both getUnreadCount() (NFR-3,\n286-/// <50ms) and listNotifications()'s own-rows-newest-first query.\n287:model Notification {\n288-  id        String    @id @default(cuid())\n289-  userId    String\n290-  user      User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n291-  type      String\n292-  title     String\n293-  body      String?\n294-  link      String?\n295-  readAt    DateTime?\n296-  createdAt DateTime  @default(now())\n297-  updatedAt DateTime  @updatedAt\n298-\n299-  @@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])\n300-}\n301-\n302-/// Per-user, per-type override of the registry's defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp\n303-/// defaults (PRD-04 FR-3). Composite PK instead of a surrogate id/unique\n304-/// index -- there is exactly one row per (userId, type) by construction\n305-/// (notify.ts and the preferences PUT route both upsert on it).\n306:model NotificationPreference {\n307-  userId    String\n308-  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n309-  type      String\n310-  inApp     Boolean  @default(true)\n311-  email     Boolean  @default(true)\n312-  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n313-\n314-  @@id([userId, type])\n315-}\n316-\n317-/// Durable outbox row the dispatcher claims and sends (PRD-04 FR-1/FR-5).\n318-/// No FK to User -- toEmail/toName are a point-in-time snapshot (matches\n319-/// the PRD's schema block exactly) so a later email change or user deletion\n320-/// never blocks a queued send. updatedAt doubles as the \"flipped to\n321-/// SENDING\" timestamp the >10-minute stuck-row recovery checks (NFR-4) --\n322-/// Prisma's @updatedAt already bumps it on that status-flip UPDATE, so no\n323-/// separate column is needed.\n324:model EmailOutbox {\n325-  id            String      @id @default(cuid())\n326-  toEmail       String\n327-  toName        String?\n328-  subject       String\n329-  html          String\n330-  text          String\n331-  status        EmailStatus @default(PENDING)\n332-  attempts      Int         @default(0)\n333-  lastError     String?\n334-  nextAttemptAt DateTime    @default(now())\n335-  sentAt        DateTime?\n336-  createdAt     DateTime    @default(now())\n337-  updatedAt     DateTime    @updatedAt\n338-\n339-  @@index([status, nextAttemptAt])\n340-}\n341-\n342-// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n343-// PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment (FR-1). Shapes match the PRD schema block\n344-// exactly; business rules (capacity, CORE auto-enroll, homeroom-once-per-year)\n345-// live in src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts and the sections/courses\n346-// services, not here.\n347-// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n348-\n349-enum CourseKind {\n350-  CORE\n351-  ELECTIVE\n352-}\n353-\n354-enum EnrollmentStatus {\n187:model SchoolSettings {\n188-  id           String   @id @default(\"singleton\")\n189-  name         String   @default(\"SchoolHub Academy\")\n190-  shortName    String   @default(\"SchoolHub\")\n191-  logoUrl      String?\n192-  timezone     String   @default(\"UTC\")\n193-  addressLine1 String?\n194-  addressLine2 String?\n195-  city         String?\n196-  country      String?\n197-  phone        String?\n198-  email        String?\n199-  website      String?\n200-  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())\n201-  updatedAt    DateTime @updatedAt\n202-}\n203-\n204-/// One school year, e.g. \"2026-2027\". Exactly one row has isCurrent = true\n205-/// at a time -- enforced in src/server/services/academicYears.ts's\n206-/// setCurrentAcademicYear(), never by a DB constraint (Postgres can't\n207-/// express \"exactly one true\" as a simple unique index).\n208-model AcademicYear {\n209-  id        String    @id @default(cuid())\n210-  name      String    @unique\n211-  startDate DateTime  @db.Date\n212-  endDate   DateTime  @db.Date\n59:model User {\n60-  id                      String                   @id @default(cuid())\n61-  email                   String                   @unique\n62-  passwordHash            String?\n63-  firstName               String\n64-  lastName                String\n65-  phone                   String?\n66-  role                    Role\n67-  status                  UserStatus               @default(INVITED)\n68-  failedLoginCount        Int                      @default(0)\n69-  lockedUntil             DateTime?\n70-  lastLoginAt             DateTime?\n71-  passwordChangedAt       DateTime?\n72-  archivedAt              DateTime?\n73-  createdAt               DateTime                 @default(now())\n74-  updatedAt               DateTime                 @updatedAt\n75-  authTokens              AuthToken[]\n76-  auditLogs               AuditLog[]\n77-  studentProfile          StudentProfile?\n78-  teacherProfile          TeacherProfile?\n79-  parentProfile           ParentProfile?\n80-  parentLinks             ParentStudentLink[]      @relation(\"ParentLinks\")\n81-  studentLinks            ParentStudentLink[]      @relation(\"StudentLinks\")\n82-  notifications           Notification[]\n83-  notificationPreferences NotificationPreference[]\n84-  homeroomSections        Section[]                @relation(\"HomeroomTeacher\")\n85-  sectionMemberships      SectionMember[]\n86-  taughtCourses           Course[]                 @relation(\"CourseTeacher\")\n87-  enrollments             Enrollment[]\n88-\n89-  @@index([lastName, firstName, email])\n90-}\n91-\n92-/// Student-specific fields (FR-1). medicalNotes is visible to ADMIN/TEACHER\n93-/// only -- enforced in the service layer (src/server/services/users.ts,\n94-/// src/app/api/students/[id]/route.ts), never by hiding it client-side.\n95-model StudentProfile {\n96-  userId           String     @id\n97-  user             User       @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n98-  admissionNumber  String     @unique\n99-  dateOfBirth      DateTime   @db.Date\n10:enum Role {\n11-  ADMIN\n12-  TEACHER\n13-  STUDENT\n14-  PARENT\n15-}\n16-\n17:enum UserStatus {\n18-  ACTIVE\n19-  INVITED\n20-  DISABLED\n21-  ARCHIVED\n22-}\n23-\n24-enum AuthTokenType {\n25-  INVITE\n133:model ParentStudentLink {\n134-  id           String               @id @default(cuid())\n135-  parentId     String\n136-  parent       User                 @relation(\"ParentLinks\", fields: [parentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n137-  studentId    String\n138-  student      User                 @relation(\"StudentLinks\", fields: [studentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n139-  relationship GuardianRelationship\n140-  isPrimary    Boolean              @default(false)\n141-  createdAt    DateTime             @default(now())\n142-\n143-  @@unique([parentId, studentId])","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1921163e-32be-4c5c-99f3-b230ef406493","uuid":"29c24294-3877-46b1-9570-acec7ba9b81d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:54:54.716Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"42-}\n43-\n44:enum EmailStatus {\n45-  PENDING\n46-  SENDING\n47-  SENT\n48-  FAILED\n49-}\n50-\n51-/// Every authenticated person. passwordHash is nullable because an INVITED\n52-/// user has no password until they accept their invite (TASK-8's\n53-/// acceptInvite step sets both passwordHash and status=ACTIVE together).\n54-/// phone and archivedAt are added here (PRD-03/TASK-1) because they are the\n55-/// only task in this PRD that owns schema.prisma: phone is FR-3's common\n56-/// field shared by every role, archivedAt backs FR-13's archive/restore\n57-/// (separate from status so a DISABLED-but-not-archived user stays distinct\n58-/// from an archived one).\n59-model User {\n60-  id                      String                   @id @default(cuid())\n61-  email                   String                   @unique\n62-  passwordHash            String?\n63-  firstName               String\n64-  lastName                String\n65-  phone                   String?\n66-  role                    Role\n67-  status                  UserStatus               @default(INVITED)\n68-  failedLoginCount        Int                      @default(0)\n69-  lockedUntil             DateTime?\n70-  lastLoginAt             DateTime?\n71-  passwordChangedAt       DateTime?\n72-  archivedAt              DateTime?\n73-  createdAt               DateTime                 @default(now())\n74-  update