{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NisXzjKu6YNityt7VRnsXX","type":"tool_result","content":"FR-14 Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\nFR-15 Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\nFR-18 On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\nFR-21 Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\nFR-22 Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\nFR-24 Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\nFR-25 Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\nFR-26 Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\nFR-29 On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\nFR-31 Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\nFR-33 Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\nFR-40 Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\nNFR-9 Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\n['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prd', 'runMode', 'brownfieldFindings', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'acceptanceCriteria', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'status']","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1921163e-32be-4c5c-99f3-b230ef406493","uuid":"2c43b291-f984-4385-9feb-a5dde0c3d2b6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:56:19.215Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FR-14 Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\nFR-15 Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\nFR-18 On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\nFR-21 Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\nFR-22 Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\nFR-24 Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\nFR-25 Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\nFR-26 Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\nFR-29 On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\nFR-31 Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\nFR-33 Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\nFR-40 Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\nNFR-9 Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\n['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prd', 'runMode', 'brownfieldFindings', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'acceptanceCriteria', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'status']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NisXzjKu6YNityt7VRnsXX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
