{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GhfbEXRdy4GXwMZCWFXnqB","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/intake/requirements.json:26:    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:42:    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:43:    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:56:    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:57:    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:83:    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:93:    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },\nartifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md:22:| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |\nartifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md:51:| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |\nartifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md:52:| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |\nartifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md:80:| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |\nartifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md:89:| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |\nartifacts/architect/system-design.md:49:  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).\nartifacts/architect/system-design.md:123:| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |\nartifacts/architect/system-design.md:144:| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |\nartifacts/architect/system-design.md:165:| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |\nartifacts/architect/system-design.md:209: 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5\nartifacts/architect/system-design.md:211:              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()\nartifacts/architect/system-design.md:212:                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\nartifacts/architect/system-design.md:216:                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →\n156:2. Retry schedule: attempts 1–5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; after the 5th failure set `FAILED`.\n210:- Unit: preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, `notifyStudentAndParents` expansion and dedupe.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1921163e-32be-4c5c-99f3-b230ef406493","uuid":"7c11e60d-84bb-4aa7-b736-1e7b172899ae","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:56:24.653Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"artifacts/intake/requirements.json:26:    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:42:    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:43:    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:56:    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },\nartifacts/intake/requirements.json:57:    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a