{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi6kLXY1ytyY5PAytcpv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FCfiYnBwqyCH6ZsxHgmYC2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime\np='artifacts/dev/dev-log.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns+=\"\"\"- TASK-21: Playwright e2e (bell + preferences) — ✓ complete\n\n### HTTP verification (next dev on :3100, temporary admin, all data removed afterwards)\n- Without a session, `/api/notifications/unread-count` returns 401. Credentials sign-in works.\n- Notification flow:\n  - The admin test button returns `{ok:true}` and the unread count goes from 0 to 1.\n  - The list `category=SYSTEM` filter returns the row; ACADEMIC returns nothing; a bad category returns 400.\n  - read/unread toggles the count. Another user's id returns 404. read-all returns `{count:1}`, then the count is 0.\n- Preferences:\n  - GET returns only `system.test`; the emailOnly types are hidden.\n  - PUT persists the change.\n  - PUT returns VALIDATION_ERROR for `account.invite`, for `__proto__`, and for an extra key.\n- Email log:\n  - The `status` filter works and the response has no html or text.\n  - Retry on a non-FAILED row returns 404; retry on a FAILED row resets it to PENDING.\n- Dispatch:\n  - No token or a wrong token returns 401.\n  - The correct bearer token returns `{sent:1}`.\n- Pages:\n  - `/notifications` and `/account/notifications` render (200).\n  - The SSR markup has `role=\"switch\"` with the label \"Test notification email\" and the bell's \"Notifications\" label, matching the e2e selectors.\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA\n1. **Pre-existing dependency mismatch breaks every DataGrid page.**\n   - Cause: `package-lock.json` resolves `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0` against `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0`, so `./useFirstRender` is not exported.\n   - Effect: `/admin/email-log` (TASK-17) returns 500, and so does the existing `/admin/sections`. It is also why `DataTable.test.tsx` fails.\n   - Not fixed here, because the plan keeps `package.json` untouched.\n   - Fix: align the MUI X versions (for example, install `@mui/x-internals` at the version matching data-grid 9.5.0). After that, the first e2e test can pass, since it starts on `/admin/email-log`.\n2. **The e2e spec was not executed.**\n   - Cause: `@playwright/test@1.47.2` needs chromium revision 1248, but only 1200 is installed locally.\n   - It is listed by `playwright test --list` and its flow was exercised over HTTP as described above.\n   - To run it: `npx playwright install chromium`, then `npm run test:e2e`.\n3. The integration tests need `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. They pass against the local DB on :5433.\n4. The worker and cron route require env to be loaded. tsx does not read `.env` for `env.ts`. The worker happened to work locally because PrismaClient loads `.env` first. In production, set the variables in the process environment.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nm=json.load(open('artifacts/dev/task-completion-markers.json'))\nm['completed']=sorted(set(m['completed']+['TASK-21']), key=lambda x:int(x.split('-')[1]))\nm['timestamp']=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')\njson.dump(m,open('artifacts/dev/task-completion-markers.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint(m['completed'])\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nimport json,os\np=json.load(open('artifacts/dev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json'))\nmiss=[e['path'] for e in p['entries'] if not os.path.exists(e['path'])]\nprint('missing:',miss)\"; grep -c '^- TASK-[0-9]*:.*✓ complete' artifacts/dev/dev-log.md","description":"Finalize dev-log, markers, verify ownership files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1113,"cache_read_input_tokens":233201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1113},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"globa