{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi6mWhzPybWvMJU1zhEM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 21 tasks for SH-4 are implemented, and both `dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` mark all 21 complete. One page doesn't load in this environment: `/admin/email-log` returns a 500 because of a dependency mismatch that was already in the project. The new e2e spec hasn't been run yet.\n\n**What was built**\n- **Database:** an additive migration that only creates the three new tables (notifications, preferences, email outbox), applied to your local dev DB.\n- **Server:** the notification types list, `notify()`, preferences, email templates and rendering, the outbox, the email dispatcher, the 180-day purge, and 10 API routes.\n- **Background sending:** a worker script plus a cron endpoint protected by `CRON_SECRET`.\n- **Auth emails:** invites and password resets now go into the outbox instead of being logged, and the raw link is no longer written to logs.\n- **UI:** the notification bell in the shell, `/notifications`, `/account/notifications` and `/admin/email-log`, written against the mui-mcp v9 docs.\n- **Seed and tests:** demo notifications in the seed, plus unit, integration and e2e tests.\n\n**Verified**\n- **Pipeline:** notifications are created, emails rendered, queued and dispatched to `SENT`, unsafe links are dropped, and HTML in titles is escaped.\n- **Over HTTP:** every API route behaves per the contract when called against a dev server, including the 401 / 404 / validation-error cases.\n- **Worker:** starts and stops cleanly.\n- **Seed:** skips missing users and is idempotent (3 rows per user after two runs).\n- **Tests:** 28 new unit tests and 3 integration tests pass. The integration tests (concurrent dispatch, stuck-row recovery) only run when `TEST_DATABASE_URL` is set.\n- **Cleanup:** the dev DB is back to empty after testing.\n\n**Not working**\n1. **`/admin/email-log` returns 500**, and so does the existing `/admin/sections`. The lockfile pairs `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0` with an incompatible `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0`. The plan says not to touch `package.json`, so I left it. Matching the two versions fixes both pages and the existing `DataTable.test.tsx` failure.\n2. **The e2e spec hasn't been run.** Playwright 1.47 needs a chromium build that isn't installed, and I didn't download it unasked. Run `npx playwright install chromium`, then `npm run test:e2e`. Its first test opens `/admin/email-log`, so it will fail until item 1 is fixed.\n3. **Three failing test files were already broken:** `lockout`, `DataTable` and `useToast`. None of them import code I changed. Two unused-import lint errors in `shell.tsx` also predate this work.\n\n**Behaviour to know**\n- The requirement asks for a 240-minute backoff but also says an email fails after the 5th attempt. I followed the architect's reading, so an email is marked failed on the 5th attempt and the 240-minute wait is never used.\n- The search box built into the shared table does nothing on the email log, because that API has no search.\n\nThe task prompt gave both \"SH-4\" and \"UNKNOWN\" as the ticket ID; I used SH-4 to match all earlier artifacts. Nothing has been committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1815,"cache_read_input_tokens":234314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1815},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1921163e-32be-4c5c-99f3-b230ef406493","uuid":"96166678-8474-4446-a8db-5e2023f86d27","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:10:04.758Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi6mWPtb1gC5km4z6JfV"}
