{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W1MAopThe6gdw15qsvStVn","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T15:09:51Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"completed\": [\n    \"TASK-1\",\n    \"TASK-2\",\n    \"TASK-3\",\n    \"TASK-4\",\n    \"TASK-5\",\n    \"TASK-6\",\n    \"TASK-7\",\n    \"TASK-8\",\n    \"TASK-9\",\n    \"TASK-10\",\n    \"TASK-11\",\n    \"TASK-12\",\n    \"TASK-13\",\n    \"TASK-14\",\n    \"TASK-15\",\n    \"TASK-16\",\n    \"TASK-17\",\n    \"TASK-18\",\n    \"TASK-19\",\n    \"TASK-20\",\n    \"TASK-21\"\n  ]\n}{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T15:10:05.369Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"count\": 3,\n  \"firstPassAccepted\": false\n}# Dev Log — SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure)\n\n## Iteration (continuation run, 2026-11-04)\n\nEarlier iterations left no source files and no dev-log, so this run started from TASK-1.\nEvery artifact uses ticketId `SH-4`, the id on all upstream artifacts. The prompt also said \"UNKNOWN\".\n\n### Progress so far\n- Generated the migration with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` (equivalent to `migrate dev --create-only`, with no shadow DB). It is additive only: EmailStatus enum, 3 tables, 2 indexes, 2 FKs. Applied to the local dev DB with `migrate deploy`.\n- `react.cache` is undefined outside Next, so the email/notify code does not import `services/settings.ts`. `render.ts` exports `getEmailSchool()`, which reads the singleton directly.\n- The dispatcher's raw SQL uses `now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC'` because the columns are `timestamp(3)` without a time zone and hold UTC.\n- Pre-existing `tsc` errors (MUI v9 system props in Enrollment/SectionDetail clients, and users.ts:189-199) are outside this ticket. They are not touched.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Notifications/email migration — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Notification type registry — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: Shared notification validators — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Email templates + render — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Backoff + transport — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: Outbox + auth email seam + INVITE_TTL — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: Preferences + notify service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: Dispatcher + purge — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: User notification service + 5 routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: Preferences API route — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Admin email service + admin routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: Internal dispatch route + '/api/internal/' public path — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Email worker script — ✓ complete\n\nVerification for TASK-1 to TASK-13: a tsx smoke script (in /tmp, not committed) ran against the dev DB with a temporary user, which was deleted afterwards. It checked the following:\n- notify() dedupes ids and drops `//evil.com`.\n- The rendered HTML escapes `<b>`.\n- sendAuthEmail enqueues the invite with \"expires on November 11, 2026\".\n- dispatchEmails returned `{sent:2}` and both rows ended SENT.\n- `scripts/worker-email.ts` starts and stops cleanly on SIGTERM.\n\nFix found while testing: the templates now `import * as React`, because tsx and vitest use the classic JSX runtime (tsconfig `jsx: preserve`). Next was unaffected.\n- TASK-14: NotificationBell + shell wiring — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: /notifications page + NotificationsList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: /account/notifications page + PreferencesTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: /admin/email-log page + EmailLogTable — ✓ complete\n      96 artifacts/dev/dev-log.md\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T06:40:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev-planning\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Add exact-pinned @dnd-kit/core@6.3.1 (npm install --save-exact); add enum PeriodKind and models Period, SchoolDay and TimetableSlot to schema.prisma exactly as in system-design §2, plus the back-relations Course.timetableSlots, Room.timetableSlots and AcademicYear.timetableSlots; generate the additive migration with `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name timetable`, then rename its folder to 20261105000000_timetable and check that it contains only CREATE/INDEX/FK statements\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"package.json\",\n        \"package-lock.json\",\n        \"prisma/schema.prisma\",\n        \"prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimateHours\": 2,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-1\",\n        \"FR-2\",\n        \"FR-3\",\n        \"FR-4\",\n        \"NFR-6\",\n        \"NFR-9\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the Zod schemas in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts per system-design §3.1: hhmm, periodSchema (end>start refine), periodUpdateSchema, periodReorderSchema (no duplicates), schoolDaysSchema (length 7, unique days), slotCreateSchema, slotUpdateSchema (at least one key), timetableQuerySchema, availabilityQuerySchema (optional roomId), freeRoomsQuerySchema (coerce dayOfWeek, optional excludeSlotId) and meTimetableQuerySchema. No academicYearId on slot writes\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/lib/validators/timetable.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-1\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 1,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-39\",\n        \"FR-6\",\n        \"FR-37\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Add pure isomorphic schoolNow(now, tz) → { isoDay, hhmm } (via the existing formatInSchoolTz) and nowAndNext(periods, hhmm) to src/lib/dates.ts. Never use the browser timezone\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/lib/dates.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimateHours\": 1,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-45\",\n        \"FR-26\",\n        \"FR-31\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the pure clash engine src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts (no Prisma import): ClashRule/Clash types, clashesForCell() running all six rules in order (PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, TEACHER incl. co-teachers, ROOM, SECTION, STUDENT) with the exact FR messages, and periodsOverlap(a, b) [start,end). Add unit tests: timetable-clash.test.ts (every rule, co-teacher↔teacher and co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section/room skip, all clashes returned, self slot excluded) and timetable-time.test.ts (periodsOverlap, end>start via periodSchema, schoolNow/nowAndNext under UTC, America/Los_Angeles and Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line weekday case)\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts\",\n        \"tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts\",\n        \"tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-2\",\n        \"TASK-3\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 3,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-9\",\n        \"FR-10\",\n        \"FR-11\",\n        \"FR-12\",\n        \"FR-13\",\n        \"FR-14\",\n        \"FR-6\",\n        \"FR-45\",\n        \"NFR-11\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Create src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient) with the write side: listPeriods/createPeriod/updatePeriod/deletePeriod (409 CONFLICT { slotCount })/reorderPeriods (id-set check, two-phase order write in one tx); listSchoolDays (slotCount groupBy across all years) and updateSchoolDays (one tx: deleteMany for days switched off, then update; returns deletedSlotCount); validateSlot(input, db) → Clash[] (excludeSlotId, one enrollment groupBy); local withSerializableRetry (P2034, 3 attempts, logger.warn); createSlot/moveSlot/deleteSlot in a SERIALIZABLE tx with 409 { clashes }, archived course/room → VALIDATION_ERROR, academicYearId derived from the course. Call audit() after commit for every mutation (D7)\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-4\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 4,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-5\",\n        \"FR-6\",\n        \"FR-7\",\n        \"FR-8\",\n        \"FR-13\",\n        \"FR-14\",\n        \"FR-37\",\n        \"FR-40\",\n        \"NFR-1\",\n        \"NFR-8\",\n        \"NFR-9\",\n        \"NFR-14\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the read side to timetable-service.ts: getAvailability(courseId, roomId?) (fixed query count, in-memory clashesForCell per teaching cell, own slots excluded, returns only clashing cells), getFreeRooms (non-archived, excludeSlotId), getTimetable(view, id, yearId) (one findMany → { periods, days, slots }), assertCanViewTimetable (ADMIN any view; TEACHER own teacher view + D8 sections; else FORBIDDEN), getPersonalTimetable (teacher incl. co-teach / student ACTIVE; current year default), and the exported getScheduleForDate (empty on non-teaching days; PARENT → []; holiday hook comment for PRD-14) and getCurrentSlot (school timezone)\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-5\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 3,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-19\",\n        \"FR-21\",\n        \"FR-24\",\n        \"FR-30\",\n        \"FR-31\",\n        \"FR-35\",\n        \"FR-36\",\n        \"FR-38\",\n        \"FR-45\",\n        \"NFR-2\",\n        \"NFR-3\",\n        \"NFR-7\",\n        \"NFR-15\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-7\",\n      \"description\": \"Create thin route handlers for the bell schedule (withHandler → requireUser/requireRole → parseBody/parseQuery → service → ok()) per api-contracts.json: GET (any user)/POST (ADMIN) /api/periods, PATCH/DELETE /api/periods/[id], POST /api/periods/reorder, GET (any user)/PUT (ADMIN) /api/school-days. Pass request to audit for the IP\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/api/periods/route.ts\",\n        \"src/app/api/periods/[id]/route.ts\",\n        \"src/app/api/periods/reorder/route.ts\",\n        \"src/app/api/school-days/route.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-5\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 2,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-33\",\n        \"FR-34\",\n        \"FR-5\",\n        \"FR-7\",\n        \"FR-8\",\n        \"NFR-7\",\n        \"NFR-8\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Create thin timetable route handlers per api-contracts.json: GET /api/timetable (requireUser + assertCanViewTimetable), GET /api/timetable/availability (ADMIN), GET /api/timetable/free-rooms (ADMIN), POST /api/timetable/slots (ADMIN, 201), PATCH/DELETE /api/timetable/slots/[id] (ADMIN), GET /api/me/timetable (TEACHER own; STUDENT self only; PARENT studentId required when >1 children, defaults to the only child, assertCanViewStudent; ADMIN → { slots: [] })\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/api/timetable/route.ts\",\n        \"src/app/api/timetable/availability/route.ts\",\n        \"src/app/api/timetable/free-rooms/route.ts\",\n        \"src/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts\",\n        \"src/app/api/timetable/slots/[id]/route.ts\",\n        \"src/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-6\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 3,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-21\",\n        \"FR-25\",\n        \"FR-35\",\n        \"FR-36\",\n        \"FR-37\",\n        \"FR-38\",\n        \"NFR-7\",\n        \"NFR-8\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the shared src/components/TimetableGrid/ component (first look up every MUI component via mui-mcp useMuiDocs → fetchDocs; stop if it is unreachable). It is a CSS-grid Box with teaching-day columns and period rows; non-CLASS rows span the full width, are greyed and are not droppable. Cells are focusable Paper elements with aria-labels and subject colour + getContrastText + room Chip. mode read|edit: useDroppable/useDraggable only in edit mode, no DndContext. Clash tint uses error.light + ErrorOutline icon + Tooltip. Highlight uses an outline + a 'Now' Chip. Callbacks: onCellActivate/onSlotActivate/onSlotDelete (Enter/Delete keys). Also TimetablePrintStyles (GlobalStyles @page A4 landscape, hide [data-print=hide], show .print-only), PrintButton (window.print) and an index.ts barrel\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/components/TimetableGrid/TimetableGrid.tsx\",\n        \"src/components/TimetableGrid/TimetablePrintStyles.tsx\",\n        \"src/components/TimetableGrid/PrintButton.tsx\",\n        \"src/components/TimetableGrid/index.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-1\",\n        \"TASK-3\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 4,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-16\",\n        \"FR-19\",\n        \"FR-22\",\n        \"FR-23\",\n        \"FR-24\",\n        \"FR-29\",\n        \"NFR-4\",\n        \"NFR-5\",\n        \"NFR-16\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (requirePageRole('ADMIN'), PageHeader) and the client BellScheduleEditor: an MUI Table of periods with up/down IconButton reorder, an add/edit Dialog with TimeField (HH:mm format/parse) validated by periodSchema, and delete via ConfirmDialog (a 409 → showToast with the slot count). It also has a Teaching days section of 7 ToggleButtons; switching off a day with slotCount>0 → ConfirmDialog 'Remove N slots on <Day>?' → PUT /api/school-days. Use mui-mcp before writing any MUI component\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx\",\n        \"src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/BellScheduleEditor.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-7\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 3,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-5\",\n        \"FR-6\",\n        \"FR-7\",\n        \"FR-8\",\n        \"NFR-5\",\n        \"NFR-9\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-11\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the timetable editor /admin/timetable (requirePageRole('ADMIN')) and the client TimetableEditor. URL state is ?view=section|teacher|room&id=&year=. It has a view ToggleButtonGroup, an entity Autocomplete (sections / UserPicker TEACHER / rooms) and a year Select. Section view: DndContext(PointerSensor distance 5) with a sidebar of draggable non-archived course Cards with a 'placed N' Chip, the grid in edit mode, and a DragOverlay. On drag start, load the availability clash map (cache key courseId:roomId). Drop → POST (roomId = section.roomId) or PATCH. Pessimistic: refetch on 2xx; on 409 showToast with every details.clashes message. Drop outside or Delete → ConfirmDialog → DELETE. Slot click → Popover + Autocomplete of free-rooms → PATCH { roomId }. Enter on an empty cell → 'Place course' Dialog. Teacher and room views are read-only. Includes the PrintButton\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx\",\n        \"src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/TimetableEditor.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-8\",\n        \"TASK-9\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 6,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-15\",\n        \"FR-16\",\n        \"FR-17\",\n        \"FR-18\",\n        \"FR-19\",\n        \"FR-20\",\n        \"FR-21\",\n        \"FR-22\",\n        \"FR-23\",\n        \"FR-29\",\n        \"NFR-4\",\n        \"NFR-5\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-12\",\n      \"description\": \"Create the personal timetable /timetable (requirePageRole TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT). The server resolves the target (PARENT ?studentId= must be a linked child) and passes getPersonalTimetable, the school tz and the now ISO string to the client PersonalTimetable. The client has a Week/Today ToggleButtonGroup, a PARENT child Select when there are >1 childre