 which reads the singleton directly.\n- The dispatcher's raw SQL uses `now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC'` because the columns are `timestamp(3)` without a time zone and hold UTC.\n- Pre-existing `tsc` errors (MUI v9 system props in Enrollment/SectionDetail clients, and users.ts:189-199) are outside this ticket. They are not touched.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Notifications/email migration — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Notification type registry — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: Shared notification validators — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Email templates + render — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Backoff + transport — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: Outbox + auth email seam + INVITE_TTL — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: Preferences + notify service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: Dispatcher + purge — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: User notification service + 5 routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: Preferences API route — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Admin email service + admin routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: Internal dispatch route + '/api/internal/' public path — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Email worker script — ✓ complete\n\nVerification for TASK-1 to TASK-13: a tsx smoke script (in /tmp, not committed) ran against the dev DB with a temporary user, which was deleted afterwards. It checked the following:\n- notify() dedupes ids and drops `//evil.com`.\n- The rendered HTML escapes `<b>`.\n- sendAuthEmail enqueues the invite with \"expires on November 11, 2026\".\n- dispatchEmails returned `{sent:2}` and both rows ended SENT.\n- `scripts/worker-email.ts` starts and stops cleanly on SIGTERM.\n\nFix found while testing: the templates now `import * as React`, because tsx and vitest use the classic JSX runtime (tsconfig `jsx: preserve`). Next was unaffected.\n- TASK-14: NotificationBell + shell wiring — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: /notifications page + NotificationsList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: /account/notifications page + PreferencesTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: /admin/email-log page + EmailLogTable — ✓ complete\n      96 artifacts/dev/dev-log.md\n{\n  \"ticketId\":