{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cah7wBzXnC5kkN49T3VJ3G","type":"tool_result","content":"FR-6 Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\nFR-7 Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\nFR-8 Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\nFR-9 Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\nFR-10 Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\nFR-11 Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\nFR-12 Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\nFR-13 Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\nFR-14 validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\nFR-16 Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\nFR-20 If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\nFR-22 Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\nFR-26 A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\nFR-41 Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\nFR-43 Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\nFR-44 Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df25e571-0ce8-4c8c-9cc6-c89019e911c3","uuid":"c54ab2f4-ffaf-4a34-9c9e-a6b1dd7ec417","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:26:02.852Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FR-6 Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\nFR-7 Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\nFR-8 Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\nFR-9 Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\nFR-10 Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\nFR-11 Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\nFR-12 Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\nFR-13 Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\nFR-14 validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\nFR-16 Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\nFR-20 If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\nFR-22 Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\nFR-26 A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\nFR-41 Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK)