{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MMqkFN98gcKTS4RTwreSXY","type":"tool_result","content":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nAuth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,\ncredentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate\nlimiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +\ntests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new\nAPI endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |\n| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |\n| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |\n| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |\n\nAdditional risks found during design (not in intake):\n\n- **R1: e2e regression (NFR-13).** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` visits `/dashboard` with no session.\n  Middleware (FR-11) and the new `requirePageUser()` in the layout redirect it to `/login`, so it fails.\n  The design extracts the cookie sign-in already used by `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and\n  uses it in `dashboard.spec.ts` (C12).\n- **R2: copy mismatch.** `services/auth.ts` returns `INVALID_LINK = \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"`,\n  but FR-13 requires the invite-specific copy. The **page owns the copy**: it renders the FR-13 string\n  both when `verifyToken` fails up front and when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. The service is not changed.\n- **R3: non-standard error code.** `INVALID_TOKEN` (400) is outside the NFR-10 list. It is existing behaviour\n  and stays as-is; `arch-api-contracts` documents it.\n- **R4: `signOut` signature.** In next-auth v5 `next-auth/react`, the option is `redirectTo`, not\n  `callbackUrl` (ADR-3 wording). Use `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture at a glance\n\n```\nBrowser\n ├─ (auth) route group — public (public-routes.ts)        ← NEW pages\n │    /login  /forgot-password  /reset-password/[token]  /invite/[token]\n │        │ client signIn()/signOut()  (next-auth/react; CSRF fetched by Auth.js)\n │        │ postJson() → existing JSON routes\n ├─ (app) route group — protected\n │    layout.tsx (server) ── requirePageUser() ──► AppShell({ user })   ← MODIFIED\n │    /account/security                                                  ← NEW page\n ▼\nmiddleware.ts (FR-11)  ── unauth page → /login?callbackUrl= ; unauth /api → 401\n ▼\nAPI routes (existing, thin: Zod → service → envelope)\n /api/auth/[...nextauth]  /api/auth/forgot-password  /api/auth/reset-password\n /api/auth/accept-invite  /api/account/password\n ▼\nServer modules (existing, untouched)\n auth.ts / auth.config.ts · credentials.ts · tokens.ts · rate-limit.ts · audit.ts\n services/auth.ts · services/users.ts · email.ts (EmailOutbox) · requireRole.ts\n ▼\nPrisma / PostgreSQL — User, AuthToken, AuditLog, EmailOutbox (+ new index)\n```\n\n**Patterns**\n\n- **Server-first page guard + client form.** Token pages and `/account/security` are Server Components\n  that do the authoritative check (`verifyToken`, `requirePageUser`) and render a client form only when\n  it is allowed (ADR-4, NFR-9).\n- **One current-user source.** The `(app)` layout reads the session with `requirePageUser()` and passes\n  `user` to `AppShell` as a prop. No `SessionProvider` and no `useSession` (ADR-3, FR-25).\n- **Shared schemas.** Every form uses RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas already exported from\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, which the API routes use too (NFR-11).\n- **Reuse the existing form kit.** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`,\n  `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure` (B2). New pages\n  compose these; nothing is re-implemented.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Existing — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` (User, AuthToken, AuditLog, enums) | Data model | FR-1, FR-32 |\n| `src/server/auth/credentials.ts` | `authorizeCredentials`, lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`, `AuthError` codes `invalid` / `disabled` / `rate_limited` / `locked:<N>`, login audits | FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/auth/auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts` | JWT 8h, 5-min recheck, `reauth` update, `pages.signIn='/login'`, redirect sanitising, cookie defaults | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-2 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Page redirect / API 401, public paths, no sign-up route | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` | `createToken` / `verifyToken` / `consumeToken`, SHA-256, constant-time | FR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | Sliding window, `__resetRateLimits()` | FR-6, FR-17 |\n| `src/server/audit.ts` | `audit()`, never throws, `ip` column | FR-24, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/server/services/auth.ts` | `acceptInvite`, `requestPasswordReset`, `resetPassword`, `changePassword`, `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE` | FR-14, FR-17–FR-20 |\n| `src/server/services/users.ts` | `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | FR-22, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/auth/email.ts` | `sendAuthEmail` (EmailOutbox), `authLink(kind, raw)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-31 |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| API routes `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite`, `/api/account/password` | Thin handlers, envelope, `unstable_update({reauth:true})` on change | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` | Centred Card + logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"` | FR-2 (B1) |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist/*` | Checklist, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` | FR-16, NFR-5 |\n| `useToast()` | Snackbar + Alert toasts | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-6 |\n| `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | Out of scope; must not be touched | NFR-13 |\n\n### 3.2 New — auth pages (route group `(auth)`, public)\n\nEvery page renders **only the card body**; the existing `(auth)/layout.tsx` provides Card/Container (B1).\nEvery form has one error `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"` and relies on RHF's default\n`shouldFocusError` (client errors) plus `applyFieldErrors` (server errors) to focus the first invalid\nfield (NFR-5).\n\n**C1 · `/login`** — `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` (server) + `LoginForm.tsx` (client). FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19, NFR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11, NFR-14\n- Page reads `searchParams.callbackUrl` and `searchParams.reset` and passes them to `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm`: RHF + `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. Email `TextField`, password `TextField` with\n  `passwordInputSlot` (show/hide `IconButton`), submit `Button`, link to `/forgot-password`. No\n  \"create account\" link (NFR-14).\n- Submit calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`\n  (ADR-2; CSRF is handled by Auth.js, NFR-2).\n- Error: `loginErrorMessage(result.code)` — an exported pure function in `LoginForm.tsx`:\n\n  | `code` | Message |\n  |---|---|\n  | `locked:<N>` | \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" |\n  | `disabled` | \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\" |\n  | `rate_limited` | \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n  | anything else | \"Email or password is incorrect.\" |\n\n- Success: `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The server\n  `redirect` callback sanitises the same value again.\n- `reset=1`: one `useToast` success toast on mount (\"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\") (FR-19).\n\n**C2 · `/forgot-password`** — `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (client form inside). FR-17, NFR-5, NFR-11\n- RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, email field, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', { email })`.\n- On a 2xx **or** `RATE_LIMITED`, replace the form with a success `Alert` showing `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`.\n  The screen is the same whether the user exists or not (no enumeration). Only `VALIDATION_ERROR` field\n  errors are shown inline. Link back to `/login`.\n\n**C3 · `/reset-password/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-1, NFR-8\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` (read-only). `null` → invalid-link `Alert` + link to\n  `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `SetPasswordForm` with the user's email (needed by\n  `setPasswordSchema(email)` and `PasswordChecklist`).\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })`.\n  Success → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `INVALID_TOKEN` → swap to the invalid-link `Alert`.\n- The raw token is only a prop. It is never logged or put into audit metadata.\n\n**C4 · `/invite/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16, NFR-1\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. `null` → `Alert`: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\n  Ask the school office to send a new one.\" (page-owned copy, R2).\n- Valid → `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name (`firstName lastName`) and email, `submitLabel=\"Activate account\"`.\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite', …)`; on success `signIn('credentials', { email,\n  password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`.\n  `INVALID_TOKEN` → the FR-13 Alert. Reusing the link later fails `verifyToken` because the service consumed it.\n\n### 3.3 New — account page (route group `(app)`, protected)\n\n**C5 · `/account/security`** — `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (server) + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` (client). FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11\n- Page: `const user = await requirePageUser()` (NFR-9); renders `ChangePasswordForm email={user.email}`.\n- Form: RHF + `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`. Current / new / confirm fields using\n  `passwordInputSlot`, `PasswordChecklist` under \"new\".\n- `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` →\n  `applyFieldErrors` shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success → `useToast` \"Password updated\" and\n  `reset()`. Re-issuing the current session and invalidating other sessions already happen on the server\n  (`unstable_update({reauth:true})` + `passwordChangedAt`, FR-10).\n\n### 3.4 Modified — app shell\n\n**C6 · `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`** — FR-25, FR-27, NFR-9\n- Add `const user = await requirePageUser()` (second guard behind middleware) and pass\n  `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`. Keep the existing `schoolSettings` lookup.\n\n**C7 · `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`** — FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27\n- Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Add a `user` prop to `AppShellProps`.\n- `navigationForRole(user.role)`; `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials);\n  menu header shows `fullName` and a role `Chip`.\n- Menu items: keep existing \"Profile\"; add **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link}\n  href=\"/account/security\"`, FR-21); \"Sign out\" calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from\n  `next-auth/react` (FR-26, R4).\n- After this change, `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing (FR-25 check).\n\n### 3.5 Data and seed\n\n**C10 · `prisma/seed.ts`** — FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-12\n- New users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notifications block (which looks up `student@` / `parent@`).\n- `const hash = await bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` once, then `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email },\n  create: { …, role, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash: hash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for:\n\n  | Email | Name | Role |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | admin@schoolhub.test | Alice Admin | ADMIN |\n  | teacher@schoolhub.test | Tom Teacher | TEACHER |\n  | teacher2@schoolhub.test | Tina Tutor | TEACHER |\n  | student@schoolhub.test | Sam Student | STUDENT |\n  | student2@schoolhub.test | Sara Scholar | STUDENT |\n  | parent@schoolhub.test | Pat Parent | PARENT |\n\n- `invited@schoolhub.test` (intake FR-29 gives no name or role. **Architect default:** Ivy Invited, TEACHER. Dev may change it if the PRD seed table says otherwise):\n  upsert with `status: 'INVITED'`, `passwordHash: null`, `update: {}`. If the row is still INVITED,\n  `const { raw } = await createInviteToken(user.id)` and\n  `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. **Do not** call `sendAuthEmail` (FR-31).\n- New seed lines use `logger`; the existing `console.log` lines stay (out of scope).\n\n**C11 · Migration** — FR-33, FR-32\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`.\n- `prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`, generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, containing one `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` unchanged.\n\n### 3.6 Tests\n\n**C12 · Tests** — FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13\n\n| File | Kind | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts` | Vitest unit | `loginErrorMessage`: `locked:7`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `invalid`, unknown/undefined (FR-4, FR-6) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-authorize.test.ts` | Vitest, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated, `@vitest-environment node` | unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked:N, 5th failure sets lockout + `auth.lockout` audit, rate limit, success resets count + `lastLoginAt` + `auth.login.success` (FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-accept-invite.test.ts` | same | happy path → ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, token consumed, `auth.invite.accepted`; reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`; policy violation (FR-13, FR-14, FR-15) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-reset-password.test.ts` | same | request for unknown email creates no token; ACTIVE user gets token + EmailOutbox row; older tokens invalidated; reset clears lockout, consumes token, audits (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-change-password.test.ts` | same | wrong current password → `fieldErrors.currentPassword`; success updates hash + `passwordChangedAt` (FR-20) |\n| `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` | Playwright helper | `signInAs(page, email, password)`: the CSRF + `/api/auth/callback/credentials` cookie flow lifted from `notifications.spec.ts` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (modified) | Playwright | Calls `signInAs` with the seed admin before visiting `/dashboard` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` | Playwright, `mode: 'serial'` | UI sign-in as admin → `/dashboard` with real name in the menu; sign out → `/login`; wrong password message; unauth `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`; forgot → reset for `student2@` (reads newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client`, extracts `/reset-password/…`), then sign in with the new password; one `AxeBuilder` run on `/login` (FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, NFR-5) |\n\nIntegration tests call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`. The forgot → reset e2e test restores\n`student2@`'s password to `SchoolHub123!` in `afterAll` so reruns are not affected.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n**D1 · Sign-in (FR-2–FR-8, FR-11)**\n1. Unauth request to `/grades` → middleware → `302 /login?callbackUrl=%2Fgrades`.\n2. `LoginForm` validates with `signInSchema` → `signIn('credentials', { redirect:false })` → Auth.js fetches\n   CSRF → `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials` → `authorizeCredentials` (rate limit → user lookup →\n   bcrypt / `DUMMY_HASH` → status / lock checks → counter update → audit).\n3. Failure → `{ ok:false, code }` → `loginErrorMessage(code)` → `Alert` (aria-live).\n4. Success → session cookie set → `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl('/grades'))` → `(app)/layout`\n   `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })`.\n\n**D2 · Invite acceptance (FR-12–FR-16)**\n1. Admin `sendInvite` (existing) → EmailOutbox → link `/invite/<raw>`.\n2. Page server-side `verifyToken(raw,'INVITE')` → invalid → FR-13 Alert; valid → `SetPasswordForm` (name, email read-only, checklist).\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → `acceptInvite` (policy, hash, ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, consume, audit).\n4. Client `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`. A revisit → `verifyToken` null → FR-13 Alert.\n\n**D3 · Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n1. `/forgot-password` → `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → rate limits (3/email/h, 10/IP/h) →\n   `requestPasswordReset` (ACTIVE only: invalidate old, `createToken` 60 min, `sendAuthEmail`). The UI\n   shows the same message either way.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `verifyToken` → form → `POST /api/auth/reset-password` → `resetPassword`\n   (hash, `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout, consume, audit) → `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n3. Any other session for the user dies within 5 min through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck (FR-10).\n\n**D4 · Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n`/account/security` (`requirePageUser`) → `POST /api/account/password` (`requireUser`) → `changePassword`\n→ `unstable_update({reauth:true})` keeps this session valid → toast. Other devices are signed out within 5 min.\n\n**D5 · Shell and sign-out (FR-25–FR-27)**\n`(app)/layout` → `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })` → `navigationForRole(user.role)` and the menu.\n\"Sign out\" → `signOut({ redirectTo:'/login' })` → cookie cleared → `/login`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §3.1 schema (existing, unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | C1 `/login` page + `LoginForm` |\n| FR-3 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-4 | C1 `loginErrorMessage`; C12 unit test + e2e wrong-password |\n| FR-5 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `rate-limit.ts`; C1 `rate_limited` mapping; C12 |\n| FR-7 | C1 `safeCallbackUrl` redirect; D1; C12 e2e callbackUrl |\n| FR-8 | §3.1 `credentials.ts` audits; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-9 | §3.1 `auth.ts` (existing) |\n| FR-10 | §3.1 `auth.ts` recheck; D3 step 3, D4 |\n| FR-11 | §3.1 middleware; D1 step 1; C12 e2e unauth redirect |\n| FR-12 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3, C4 server-side `verifyToken` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `/invite/[token]`; R2 page-owned copy |\n| FR-14 | C4 accept → `signIn` → `/dashboard`; D2; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` |\n| FR-15 | §3.1 validators; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` policy case |\n| FR-16 | Existing `PasswordChecklist` used in C3, C4, C5 |\n| FR-17 | C2 `/forgot-password`; D3 step 1; C12 |\n| FR-18 | §3.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C12 `auth-reset-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-19 | C3 `/reset-password/[token]`; C1 `reset=1` toast; D3; C12 e2e forgot → reset |\n| FR-20 | C5 `/account/security`; D4; C12 `auth-change-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" menu item |\n| FR-22 | §3.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only); C10 uses `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-23 | §3.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 use `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §3.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6 + C7 delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`, user prop |\n| FR-26 | C7 name, role Chip, initials, `signOut`; D5; C12 e2e sign-out |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28 | C10 six ACTIVE upserts |\n| FR-29 | C10 INVITED user |\n| FR-30 | C10 `createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))` |\n| FR-31 | §3.1 `email.ts` untouched; C10 avoids `sendAuthEmail` |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 3; C11 keeps `AuditLog.ip` |\n| FR-33 | C11 additive migration |\n| FR-34 | C12 test files |\n| NFR-1 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3/C4 raw token only as prop |\n| NFR-2 | §3.1 cookie defaults; C1 client `signIn` CSRF |\n| NFR-3 | §3.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | §3.1 one bcrypt-12 compare per attempt; no new work on the sign-in path |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 form pattern (aria-live Alert, focus first invalid); C12 axe on `/login` |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 6 mui-mcp gate; `useToast` in C1, C5 |\n| NFR-7 | All UI in C1–C7 is MUI only; existing banned-import test |\n| NFR-8 | C3/C4 never log the token; no new audit calls |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6 `requirePageUser`; existing `requireUser` in API |\n| NFR-10 | §3.1 existing handlers; R3 `INVALID_TOKEN` documented |\n| NFR-11 | C1–C5 RHF + shared Zod schemas |\n| NFR-12 | C10 uses `logger`; no `console.log` in new code |\n| NFR-13 | §3.1 untouched list; R1 e2e regression fix; no new deps (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-14 | C1 no sign-up link; `public-routes.ts` has no sign-up route |\n| NFR-15 | Stock MUI, English copy throughout C1–C7 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File change summary (for dev-planning)\n\n**New:** `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx`,\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`,\n`tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`, `tests/integration/auth-{authorize,accept-invite,reset-password,change-password}.test.ts`,\n`tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n\nToken pages may need a small client wrapper file next to them (for `onSubmit` + `router`) because\n`SetPasswordForm` takes an `onSubmit` callback, which a Server Component cannot pass. Name it\n`InviteClient.tsx` / `ResetClient.tsx` in the same folder.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `prisma/schema.prisma`,\n`prisma/seed.ts`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (and `notifications.spec.ts` may switch to the shared helper; optional).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts`,\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`, `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T12:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev-planning\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"modules\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(auth)/login\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/lib/validators\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\",\n        \"src/components/Toast (useToast)\",\n        \"next-auth/react\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(auth)/forgot-password\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/lib/validators\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth (tokens.ts)\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\",\n        \"src/lib/validators\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth (tokens.ts)\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\",\n        \"src/lib/validators\",\n        \"next-auth/react\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(app)/account/security\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth (requireRole.ts)\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\",\n        \"src/lib/validators\",\n        \"src/components/Toast (useToast)\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(app) (layout.tsx, shell.tsx)\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth (requireRole.ts)\",\n        \"src/config/navigation\",\n        \"src/components/UserAvatar\",\n        \"next-auth/react\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"prisma/seed.ts\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"prisma/schema.prisma\",\n        \"src/server/services/users.ts\",\n        \"src/server/auth/email.ts (authLink)\",\n        \"src/lib/logger\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tests/unit\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/app/(auth)/login\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tests/integration\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth\",\n        \"src/server/services\",\n        \"src/server/rate-limit\",\n        \"prisma/schema.prisma\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tests/e2e\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"tests/e2e/helpers\",\n        \"prisma/seed.ts\",\n        \"src/app/(auth)\",\n        \"src/app/(app)\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3418fb08-df3a-4486-bb21-2c26927907e3","uuid":"7b27d39f-2b86-45b4-ab84-563e295049b9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:59:13.797Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nAuth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,\ncredentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate\nlimiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +\ntests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new\nAPI endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |\n| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |\n| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |\n| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |\n\nAdditional risks found during design (not in intake):\n\n- **R1: e2e regression (NFR-13).** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` visits `/dashboard` with no session.\n  Middleware (FR-11) and the new `requirePageUser()` in the layout redirect it to `/login`, so it fails.\n  The design extracts the cookie sign-in already used by `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and\n  uses it in `dashboard.spec.ts` (C12).\n- **R2: copy mismatch.** `services/auth.ts` returns `INVALID_LINK = \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"`,\n  but FR-13 requires the invite-specific copy. The **page owns the copy**: it renders the FR-13 string\n  both when `verifyToken` fails up front and when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. The service is not changed.\n- **R3: non-standard error code.** `INVALID_TOKEN` (400) is outside the NFR-10 list. It is existing behaviour\n  and stays as-is; `arch-api-contracts` documents it.\n- **R4: `signOut` signature.** In next-auth v5 `next-auth/react`, the option is `redirectTo`, not\n  `callbackUrl` (ADR-3 wording). Use `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture at a glance\n\n```\nBrowser\n ├─ (auth) route group — public (public-routes.ts)        ← NEW pages\n │    /login  /forgot-password  /reset-password/[token]  /invite/[token]\n │        │ client signIn()/signOut()  (next-auth/react; CSRF fetched by Auth.js)\n │        │ postJson() → existing JSON routes\n ├─ (app) route group — protected\n │    layout.tsx (server) ── requirePageUser() ──► AppShell({ user })   ← MODIFIED\n │    /account/security                                                  ← NEW page\n ▼\nmiddleware.ts (FR-11)  ── unauth page → /login?callbackUrl= ; unauth /api → 401\n ▼\nAPI routes (existing, thin: Zod → service → envelope)\n /api/auth/[...nextauth]  /api/auth/forgot-password  /api/auth/reset-password\n /api/auth/accept-invite  /api/account/password\n ▼\nServer modules (existing, untouched)\n auth.ts / auth.config.ts · credentials.ts · tokens.ts · rate-limit.ts · audit.ts\n services/auth.ts · services/users.ts · email.ts (EmailOutbox) · requireRole.ts\n ▼\nPrisma / PostgreSQL — User, AuthToken, AuditLog, EmailOutbox (+ new index)\n```\n\n**Patterns**\n\n- **Server-first page guard + client form.** Token pages and `/account/security` are Server Components\n  that do the authoritative check (`verifyToken`, `requirePageUser`) and render a client form only when\n  it is allowed (ADR-4, NFR-9).\n- **One current-user source.** The `(app)` layout reads the session with `requirePageUser()` and passes\n  `user` to `AppShell` as a prop. No `SessionProvider` and no `useSession` (ADR-3, FR-25).\n- **Shared schemas.** Every form uses RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas already exported from\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, which the API routes use too (NFR-11).\n- **Reuse the existing form kit.** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`,\n  `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure` (B2). New pages\n  compose these; nothing is re-implemented.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Existing — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` (User, AuthToken, AuditLog, enums) | Data model | FR-1, FR-32 |\n| `src/server/auth/credentials.ts` | `authorizeCredentials`, lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`, `AuthError` codes `invalid` / `disabled` / `rate_limited` / `locked:<N>`, login audits | FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/auth/auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts` | JWT 8h, 5-min recheck, `reauth` update, `pages.signIn='/login'`, redirect sanitising, cookie defaults | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-2 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Page redirect / API 401, public paths, no sign-up route | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` | `createToken` / `verifyToken` / `consumeToken`, SHA-256, constant-time | FR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | Sliding window, `__resetRateLimits()` | FR-6, FR-17 |\n| `src/server/audit.ts` | `audit()`, never throws, `ip` column | FR-24, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/server/services/auth.ts` | `acceptInvite`, `requestPasswordReset`, `resetPassword`, `changePassword`, `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE` | FR-14, FR-17–FR-20 |\n| `src/server/services/users.ts` | `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | FR-22, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/auth/email.ts` | `sendAuthEmail` (EmailOutbox), `authLink(kind, raw)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-31 |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| API routes `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite`, `/api/account/password` | Thin handlers, envelope, `unstable_update({reauth:true})` on change | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` | Centred Card + logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"` | FR-2 (B1) |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist/*` | Checklist, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` | FR-16, NFR-5 |\n| `useToast()` | Snackbar + Alert toasts | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-6 |\n| `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | Out of scope; must not be touched | NFR-13 |\n\n### 3.2 New — auth pages (route group `(auth)`, public)\n\nEvery page renders **only the card body**; the existing `(auth)/layout.tsx` provides Card/Container (B1).\nEvery form has one error `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"` and relies on RHF's default\n`shouldFocusError` (client errors) plus `applyFieldErrors` (server errors) to focus the first invalid\nfield (NFR-5).\n\n**C1 · `/login`** — `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` (server) + `LoginForm.tsx` (client). FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19, NFR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11, NFR-14\n- Page reads `searchParams.callbackUrl` and `searchParams.reset` and passes them to `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm`: RHF + `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. Email `TextField`, password `TextField` with\n  `passwordInputSlot` (show/hide `IconButton`), submit `Button`, link to `/forgot-password`. No\n  \"create account\" link (NFR-14).\n- Submit calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`\n  (ADR-2; CSRF is handled by Auth.js, NFR-2).\n- Error: `loginErrorMessage(result.code)` — an exported pure function in `LoginForm.tsx`:\n\n  | `code` | Message |\n  |---|---|\n  | `locked:<N>` | \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" |\n  | `disabled` | \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\" |\n  | `rate_limited` | \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n  | anything else | \"Email or password is incorrect.\" |\n\n- Success: `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The server\n  `redirect` callback sanitises the same value again.\n- `reset=1`: one `useToast` success toast on mount (\"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\") (FR-19).\n\n**C2 · `/forgot-password`** — `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (client form inside). FR-17, NFR-5, NFR-11\n- RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, email field, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', { email })`.\n- On a 2xx **or** `RATE_LIMITED`, replace the form with a success `Alert` showing `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`.\n  The screen is the same whether the user exists or not (no enumeration). Only `VALIDATION_ERROR` field\n  errors are shown inline. Link back to `/login`.\n\n**C3 · `/reset-password/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-1, NFR-8\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` (read-only). `null` → invalid-link `Alert` + link to\n  `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `SetPasswordForm` with the user's email (needed by\n  `setPasswordSchema(email)` and `PasswordChecklist`).\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })`.\n  Success → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `INVALID_TOKEN` → swap to the invalid-link `Alert`.\n- The raw token is only a prop. It is never logged or put into audit metadata.\n\n**C4 · `/invite/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16, NFR-1\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. `null` → `Alert`: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\n  Ask the school office to send a new one.\" (page-owned copy, R2).\n- Valid → `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name (`firstName lastName`) and email, `submitLabel=\"Activate account\"`.\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite', …)`; on success `signIn('credentials', { email,\n  password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`.\n  `INVALID_TOKEN` → the FR-13 Alert. Reusing the link later fails `verifyToken` because the service consumed it.\n\n### 3.3 New — account page (route group `(app)`, protected)\n\n**C5 · `/account/security`** — `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (server) + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` (client). FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11\n- Page: `const user = await requirePageUser()` (NFR-9); renders `ChangePasswordForm email={user.email}`.\n- Form: RHF + `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`. Current / new / confirm fields using\n  `passwordInputSlot`, `PasswordChecklist` under \"new\".\n- `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` →\n  `applyFieldErrors` shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success → `useToast` \"Password updated\" and\n  `reset()`. Re-issuing the current session and invalidating other sessions already happen on the server\n  (`unstable_update({reauth:true})` + `passwordChangedAt`, FR-10).\n\n### 3.4 Modified — app shell\n\n**C6 · `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`** — FR-25, FR-27, NFR-9\n- Add `const user = await requirePageUser()` (second guard behind middleware) and pass\n  `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`. Keep the existing `schoolSettings` lookup.\n\n**C7 · `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`** — FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27\n- Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Add a `user` prop to `AppShellProps`.\n- `navigationForRole(user.role)`; `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials);\n  menu header shows `fullName` and a role `Chip`.\n- Menu items: keep existing \"Profile\"; add **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link}\n  href=\"/account/security\"`, FR-21); \"Sign out\" calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from\n  `next-auth/react` (FR-26, R4).\n- After this change, `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing (FR-25 check).\n\n### 3.5 Data and seed\n\n**C10 · `prisma/seed.ts`** — FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-12\n- New users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notifications block (which looks up `student@` / `parent@`).\n- `const hash = await bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` once, then `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email },\n  create: { …, role, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash: hash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for:\n\n  | Email | Name | Role |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | admin@schoolhub.test | Alice Admin | ADMIN |\n  | teacher@schoolhub.test | Tom Teacher | TEACHER |\n  | teacher2@schoolhub.test | Tina Tutor | TEACHER |\n  | student@schoolhub.test | Sam Student | STUDENT |\n  | student2@schoolhub.test | Sara Scholar | STUDENT |\n  | parent@schoolhub.test | Pat Parent | PARENT |\n\n- `invited@schoolhub.test` (intake FR-29 gives no name or role. **Architect default:** Ivy Invited, TEACHER. Dev may change it if the PRD seed table says otherwise):\n  upsert with `status: 'INVITED'`, `passwordHash: null`, `update: {}`. If the row is still INVITED,\n  `const { raw } = await createInviteToken(user.id)` and\n  `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. **Do not** call `sendAuthEmail` (FR-31).\n- New seed lines use `logger`; the existing `console.log` lines stay (out of scope).\n\n**C11 · Migration** — FR-33, FR-32\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`.\n- `prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`, generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, containing one `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` unchanged.\n\n### 3.6 Tests\n\n**C12 · Tests** — FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13\n\n| File | Kind | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts` | Vitest unit | `loginErrorMessage`: `locked:7`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `invalid`, unknown/undefined (FR-4, FR-6) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-authorize.test.ts` | Vitest, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated, `@vitest-environment node` | unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked:N, 5th failure sets lockout + `auth.lockout` audit, rate limit, success resets count + `lastLoginAt` + `auth.login.success` (FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-accept-invite.test.ts` | same | happy path → ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, token consumed, `auth.invite.accepted`; reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`; policy violation (FR-13, FR-14, FR-15) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-reset-password.test.ts` | same | request for unknown email creates no token; ACTIVE user gets token + EmailOutbox row; older tokens invalidated; reset clears lockout, consumes token, audits (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-change-password.test.ts` | same | wrong current password → `fieldErrors.currentPassword`; success updates hash + `passwordChangedAt` (FR-20) |\n| `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` | Playwright helper | `signInAs(page, email, password)`: the CSRF + `/api/auth/callback/credentials` cookie flow lifted from `notifications.spec.ts` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (modified) | Playwright | Calls `signInAs` with the seed admin before visiting `/dashboard` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` | Playwright, `mode: 'serial'` | UI sign-in as admin → `/dashboard` with real name in the menu; sign out → `/login`; wrong password message; unauth `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`; forgot → reset for `student2@` (reads newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client`, extracts `/reset-password/…`), then sign in with the new password; one `AxeBuilder` run on `/login` (FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, NFR-5) |\n\nIntegration tests call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`. The forgot → reset e2e test restores\n`student2@`'s password to `SchoolHub123!` in `afterAll` so reruns are not affected.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n**D1 · Sign-in (FR-2–FR-8, FR-11)**\n1. Unauth request to `/grades` → middleware → `302 /login?callbackUrl=%2Fgrades`.\n2. `LoginForm` validates with `signInSchema` → `signIn('credentials', { redirect:false })` → Auth.js fetches\n   CSRF → `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials` → `authorizeCredentials` (rate limit → user lookup →\n   bcrypt / `DUMMY_HASH` → status / lock checks → counter update → audit).\n3. Failure → `{ ok:false, code }` → `loginErrorMessage(code)` → `Alert` (aria-live).\n4. Success → session cookie set → `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl('/grades'))` → `(app)/layout`\n   `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })`.\n\n**D2 · Invite acceptance (FR-12–FR-16)**\n1. Admin `sendInvite` (existing) → EmailOutbox → link `/invite/<raw>`.\n2. Page server-side `verifyToken(raw,'INVITE')` → invalid → FR-13 Alert; valid → `SetPasswordForm` (name, email read-only, checklist).\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → `acceptInvite` (policy, hash, ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, consume, audit).\n4. Client `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`. A revisit → `verifyToken` null → FR-13 Alert.\n\n**D3 · Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n1. `/forgot-password` → `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → rate limits (3/email/h, 10/IP/h) →\n   `requestPasswordReset` (ACTIVE only: invalidate old, `createToken` 60 min, `sendAuthEmail`). The UI\n   shows the same message either way.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `verifyToken` → form → `POST /api/auth/reset-password` → `resetPassword`\n   (hash, `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout, consume, audit) → `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n3. Any other session for the user dies within 5 min through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck (FR-10).\n\n**D4 · Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n`/account/security` (`requirePageUser`) → `POST /api/account/password` (`requireUser`) → `changePassword`\n→ `unstable_update({reauth:true})` keeps this session valid → toast. Other devices are signed out within 5 min.\n\n**D5 · Shell and sign-out (FR-25–FR-27)**\n`(app)/layout` → `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })` → `navigationForRole(user.role)` and the menu.\n\"Sign out\" → `signOut({ redirectTo:'/login' })` → cookie cleared → `/login`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §3.1 schema (existing, unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | C1 `/login` page + `LoginForm` |\n| FR-3 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-4 | C1 `loginErrorMessage`; C12 unit test + e2e wrong-password |\n| FR-5 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `rate-limit.ts`; C1 `rate_limited` mapping; C12 |\n| FR-7 | C1 `safeCallbackUrl` redirect; D1; C12 e2e callbackUrl |\n| FR-8 | §3.1 `credentials.ts` audits; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-9 | §3.1 `auth.ts` (existing) |\n| FR-10 | §3.1 `auth.ts` recheck; D3 step 3, D4 |\n| FR-11 | §3.1 middleware; D1 step 1; C12 e2e unauth redirect |\n| FR-12 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3, C4 server-side `verifyToken` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `/invite/[token]`; R2 page-owned copy |\n| FR-14 | C4 accept → `signIn` → `/dashboard`; D2; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` |\n| FR-15 | §3.1 validators; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` policy case |\n| FR-16 | Existing `PasswordChecklist` used in C3, C4, C5 |\n| FR-17 | C2 `/forgot-password`; D3 step 1; C12 |\n| FR-18 | §3.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C12 `auth-reset-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-19 | C3 `/reset-password/[token]`; C1 `reset=1` toast; D3; C12 e2e forgot → reset |\n| FR-20 | C5 `/account/security`; D4; C12 `auth-change-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" menu item |\n| FR-22 | §3.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only); C10 uses `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-23 | §3.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 use `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §3.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6 + C7 delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`, user prop |\n| FR-26 | C7 name, role Chip, initials, `signOut`; D5; C12 e2e sign-out |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28 | C10 six ACTIVE upserts |\n| FR-29 | C10 INVITED user |\n| FR-30 | C10 `createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))` |\n| FR-31 | §3.1 `email.ts` untouched; C10 avoids `sendAuthEmail` |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 3; C11 keeps `AuditLog.ip` |\n| FR-33 | C11 additive migration |\n| FR-34 | C12 test files |\n| NFR-1 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3/C4 raw token only as prop |\n| NFR-2 | §3.1 cookie defaults; C1 client `signIn` CSRF |\n| NFR-3 | §3.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | §3.1 one bcrypt-12 compare per attempt; no new work on the sign-in path |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 form pattern (aria-live Alert, focus first invalid); C12 axe on `/login` |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 6 mui-mcp gate; `useToast` in C1, C5 |\n| NFR-7 | All UI in C1–C7 is MUI only; existing banned-import test |\n| NFR-8 | C3/C4 never log the token; no new audit calls |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6 `requirePageUser`; existing `requireUser` in API |\n| NFR-10 | §3.1 existing handlers; R3 `INVALID_TOKEN` documented |\n| NFR-11 | C1–C5 RHF + shared Zod schemas |\n| NFR-12 | C10 uses `logger`; no `console.log` in new code |\n| NFR-13 | §3.1 untouched list; R1 e2e regression fix; no new deps (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-14 | C1 no sign-up link; `public-routes.ts` has no sign-up route |\n| NFR-15 | Stock MUI, English copy throughout C1–C7 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File change summary (for dev-planning)\n\n**New:** `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx`,\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`,\n`tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`, `tests/integration/auth-{authorize,accept-invite,reset-password,change-password}.test.ts`,\n`tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n\nToken pages may need a small client wrapper file next to them (for `onSubmit` + `router`) because\n`SetPasswordForm` takes an `onSubmit` callback, which a Server Component cannot pass. Name it\n`InviteClient.tsx` / `ResetClient.tsx` in the same folder.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `prisma/schema.prisma`,\n`prisma/seed.ts`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (and `notifications.spec.ts` may switch to the shared helper; optional).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts`,\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`, `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T12:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev-planning\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"modules\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(auth)/login\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/lib/validators\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\",\n        \"src/components/Toast (useToast)\",\n        \"next-auth/react\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(auth)/forgot-password\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/lib/validators\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth (tokens.ts)\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\",\n        \"src/lib/validators\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth (tokens.ts)\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\",\n        \"src/lib/validators\",\n        \"next-auth/react\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(app)/account/security\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth (requireRole.ts)\",\n        \"src/components/PasswordChecklist\",\n        \"src/lib/validators\",\n        \"src/components/Toast (useToast)\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"src/app/(app) (layout.tsx, shell.tsx)\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth (requireRole.ts)\",\n        \"src/config/navigation\",\n        \"src/components/UserAvatar\",\n        \"next-auth/react\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"prisma/seed.ts\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"prisma/schema.prisma\",\n        \"src/server/services/users.ts\",\n        \"src/server/auth/email.ts (authLink)\",\n        \"src/lib/logger\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tests/unit\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/app/(auth)/login\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tests/integration\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"src/server/auth\",\n        \"src/server/services\",\n        \"src/server/rate-limit\",\n        \"prisma/schema.prisma\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tests/e2e\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"tests/e2e/helpers\",\n        \"prisma/seed.ts\",\n        \"src/app/(auth)\",\n        \"src/app/(app)\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MMqkFN98gcKTS4RTwreSXY",