{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015aTgKSekLag2ZkEJ7je1VM","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T17:55:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev-planning\",\n  \"sourceDesign\": \"artifacts/architect/system-design.md (2026-11-05T17:30Z, C1-C9) + api-contracts.json (17:40Z)\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-1\",\n      \"description\": \"C1 /forgot-password. NFR-6 gate: run mui-mcp useMuiDocs -> fetchDocs (@mui/material@9.5.0) for every MUI component used before writing JSX; stop and report if unreachable. page.tsx (server) renders a heading plus ForgotPasswordForm. ForgotPasswordForm.tsx ('use client'): RHF + zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema), TextFormField email, postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email}). 2xx -> success Alert showing data.message (do not retype the copy); 429 -> error Alert 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'; 400 -> applyFieldErrors. Single aria-live='polite' Alert, 'Back to sign in' MUI Link component={NextLink} href='/login'. Same success copy for known and unknown emails (no enumeration).\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx\",\n        \"src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/ForgotPasswordForm.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimateHours\": 1.5,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-17\",\n        \"FR-18\",\n        \"NFR-5\",\n        \"NFR-6\",\n        \"NFR-7\",\n        \"NFR-11\",\n        \"NFR-15\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-2\",\n      \"description\": \"C4 shared TokenPasswordForm ('use client'). NFR-6 gate: run mui-mcp useMuiDocs -> fetchDocs (@mui/material@9.5.0) for every MUI component used before writing JSX; stop and report if unreachable. Props {mode: 'invite'|'reset', token, email, name?, invalidMessage}. Wraps the existing SetPasswordForm({name, email, submitLabel, onSubmit}). onSubmit(password, confirm) -> postJson(mode==='invite' ? '/api/auth/accept-invite' : '/api/auth/reset-password', {token, password, confirm}). The body field is `confirm`, NOT confirmPassword (api-contracts designCorrections). On error.status 410 switch to local invalid state and render an Alert with invalidMessage (plus a link to /forgot-password for reset). Return any other ApiFailure so SetPasswordForm calls applyFieldErrors. Invite success: signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false}) from next-auth/react, then router.replace('/dashboard'). Reset success: router.replace('/login?reset=1') (the existing LoginForm toast fires). Never log the token or password.\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimateHours\": 2,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-14\",\n        \"FR-15\",\n        \"FR-16\",\n        \"FR-19\",\n        \"NFR-2\",\n        \"NFR-5\",\n        \"NFR-6\",\n        \"NFR-8\",\n        \"NFR-12\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-3\",\n      \"description\": \"C2 /reset-password/[token] server page. const v = await verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET') from src/server/auth/tokens.ts (read-only, does not consume). If null, render an Alert 'This link is invalid or has expired.' plus a Link to /forgot-password. Otherwise render <TokenPasswordForm mode='reset' token email={v.user.email} invalidMessage='This link is invalid or has expired.' />. Check the actual verifyToken return shape before use. No hashing outside tokens.ts.\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-2\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 1,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-12\",\n        \"FR-19\",\n        \"NFR-1\",\n        \"NFR-8\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-4\",\n      \"description\": \"C3 /invite/[token] server page. verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE'). If null, render an Alert with the FR-13 copy 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' Otherwise render <TokenPasswordForm mode='invite' token name={firstName + ' ' + lastName} email invalidMessage={FR-13 copy} />. No sign-up affordance (NFR-14).\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-2\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 1,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-12\",\n        \"FR-13\",\n        \"FR-14\",\n        \"NFR-1\",\n        \"NFR-14\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-5\",\n      \"description\": \"C5 /account/security. NFR-6 gate: run mui-mcp useMuiDocs -> fetchDocs (@mui/material@9.5.0) for every MUI component used before writing JSX; stop and report if unreachable. page.tsx (server): const user = await requirePageUser(); render a heading plus <ChangePasswordForm email={user.email} />. ChangePasswordForm.tsx ('use client'): RHF + zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email)); three password TextFields (currentPassword, newPassword, confirm) with passwordInputSlot; PasswordChecklist under newPassword; one aria-live='polite' Alert. Submit with postJson('/api/account/password', {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}). On 400, REMAP details.fieldErrors.password -> newPassword (the common-password policy error uses the `password` key, see api-contracts designCorrections) before applyFieldErrors; fieldErrors.currentPassword shows 'Current password is incorrect.' Success: useToast 'Password updated', reset(), router.refresh().\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx\",\n        \"src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimateHours\": 2.5,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-10\",\n        \"FR-15\",\n        \"FR-16\",\n        \"FR-20\",\n        \"FR-23\",\n        \"NFR-5\",\n        \"NFR-6\",\n        \"NFR-9\",\n        \"NFR-11\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-6\",\n      \"description\": \"C6 + C7 shell wiring (one task because the prop type couples both files). NFR-6 gate: run mui-mcp useMuiDocs -> fetchDocs (@mui/material@9.5.0) for every MUI component used before writing JSX; stop and report if unreachable. layout.tsx: const user = await requirePageUser() (keep the schoolSettings read); pass user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}} to AppShell. shell.tsx: delete PLACEHOLDER_USER; add `user: SessionUser` to AppShellProps (import type from src/server/auth/requireRole); navigationForRole(user.role); UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}; menu header shows full name in Typography plus role Chip; replace the two placeholder MenuItems with 'Account security' (MenuItem component={Link} href='/account/security') and 'Sign out' (signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' }) from next-auth/react, the v5 option; ADR-2's callbackUrl wording is outdated). No SessionProvider or useSession. Done when `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing.\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"src/app/(app)/layout.tsx\",\n        \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-5\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 2,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-21\",\n        \"FR-23\",\n        \"FR-25\",\n        \"FR-26\",\n        \"FR-27\",\n        \"NFR-6\",\n        \"NFR-9\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-7\",\n      \"description\": \"C8 integration tests. '// @vitest-environment node' plus describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL), following tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts. Reset the rate limiter in beforeEach and create or clean up its own users. authorize: unknown email, wrong password, DISABLED, archived, locked -> locked:N, 5th failure locks and audits auth.lockout, rate_limited after 10 per IP, success resets failedLoginCount, sets lastLoginAt and audits auth.login.success. acceptInvite: ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt set, token consumed, reuse -> INVALID_TOKEN. requestPasswordReset: known email -> token + EmailOutbox row; unknown -> no token. resetPassword clears lockout fields; token reuse fails. changePassword: wrong current -> fieldErrors.currentPassword; success bumps passwordChangedAt. Assert that no AuditLog metadata contains 'password' or 'token' values. Also confirms FR-6 (R3): loginErrorMessage already handles rate_limited, so build nothing for it.\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"tests/integration/auth.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"estimateHours\": 3,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-3\",\n        \"FR-5\",\n        \"FR-6\",\n        \"FR-8\",\n        \"FR-10\",\n        \"FR-14\",\n        \"FR-18\",\n        \"FR-19\",\n        \"FR-20\",\n        \"FR-24\",\n        \"FR-34\",\n        \"NFR-3\",\n        \"NFR-8\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-8\",\n      \"description\": \"C9 shared e2e sign-in (R1). helpers/auth.ts: export signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!'), moved from the local signIn in notifications.spec.ts (GET /api/auth/csrf -> POST /api/auth/callback/credentials form, then assert that /api/auth/session has the email). notifications.spec.ts: delete the local signIn and call signInAs(page, ADMIN.email, ADMIN.password); keep its own user upsert and cleanup. dashboard.spec.ts: add a beforeEach that calls signInAs(page, 'admin@schoolhub.test'), because the (app) layout now calls requirePageUser (TASK-6).\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts\",\n        \"tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-6\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 1,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-11\",\n        \"FR-28\",\n        \"FR-34\",\n        \"NFR-13\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-9\",\n      \"description\": \"C9 auth.spec.ts with test.describe.configure({mode:'serial'}). (1) UI sign-in as admin@schoolhub.test / SchoolHub123! lands on /dashboard; the user menu shows 'Alice Admin' and ADMIN; 'Sign out' lands on /login. (2) Wrong password shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' (3) Unauthenticated /dashboard -> /login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard. (4) Forgot -> reset for student2@schoolhub.test: submit /forgot-password, read the newest EmailOutbox row via @prisma/client in the test process (no test-only app route), extract the /reset-password/ link, set a new password, see the /login reset toast, sign in with the new password. Restore the student2 password in afterAll (it is not ADMIN, so parallel specs are not affected). (5) One AxeBuilder scan of /login and /forgot-password: zero serious or critical violations.\",\n      \"files\": [\n        \"tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"TASK-1\",\n        \"TASK-3\",\n        \"TASK-6\",\n        \"TASK-8\"\n      ],\n      \"estimateHours\": 3,\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"FR-2\",\n        \"FR-4\",\n        \"FR-7\",\n        \"FR-11\",\n        \"FR-17\",\n        \"FR-19\",\n        \"FR-26\",\n        \"FR-28\",\n        \"FR-31\",\n        \"FR-34\",\n        \"NFR-5\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"fileStructure\": {\n    \"src/app/(auth)/\": [\n      \"TokenPasswordForm.tsx\",\n      \"forgot-password/\",\n      \"reset-password/[token]/\",\n      \"invite/[token]/\"\n    ],\n    \"src/app/(app)/\": [\n      \"layout.tsx (MOD)\",\n      \"shell.tsx (MOD)\",\n      \"account/security/\"\n    ],\n    \"tests/integration/\": [\n      \"auth.test.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"tests/e2e/\": [\n      \"helpers/\",\n      \"auth.spec.ts\",\n      \"dashboard.spec.ts (MOD)\",\n      \"notifications.spec.ts (MOD)\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"totalEstimateHours\": 17.0,\n  \"nxpPatterns\": [],\n  \"doNotModify\": [\n    \"src/server/**\",\n    \"src/app/api/**\",\n    \"src/middleware.ts\",\n    \"src/app/(auth)/login/**\",\n    \"src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx\",\