{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SmDwHqZmzLbhVw8ebYmHQx","type":"tool_result","content":"export function authLink(kind: AuthEmailKind, rawToken: string): string {\n  return new URL(PATHS[kind] + encodeURIComponent(rawToken), env.APP_URL).toString();\n}\n\n/**\n * PRD-04 FR-16: renders the invite/password-reset template and enqueues one\n * EmailOutbox row (no Notification row, no preference lookup). Unlike\n * notify(), this still throws: a silently lost invite/reset is worse than a\n * 500. The raw link is never logged.\n */\n28:| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |\n29:| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |\n68:| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n69:| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |\n70:| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |\n71:| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n75:| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |\n89:/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)\n91:link ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)\n92:C4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)\n98:/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)\n99:C4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}\n100:C4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')\n128:   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.\n150:| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |\n152:| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |\n153:| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |\n154:| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |\n155:| FR-17 | C1 |\n157:| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |\n171:| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |\n172:| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |\n175:| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |\n178:| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |\n181:| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2906e1d-ad0e-4bbc-bb8a-30196499bfbf","uuid":"90d391ff-cd06-4150-bd06-c361bbee46f2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:34:51.348Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"export function authLink(kind: AuthEmailKind, rawToken: string): string {\n  return new URL(PATHS[kind] + encodeURIComponent(rawToken), env.APP_URL).toString();\n}\n\n/**\n * PRD-04 FR-16: renders the invite/password-reset template and enqueues one\n * EmailOutbox row (no Notification row, no preference lookup). Unlike\n * notify(), this still throws: a silently lost invite/reset is worse than a\n * 500. The raw link is never logged.\n */\n28:| 1 | BROWNFIELD: