{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014FneLLjhMdGpTzQ3CnzAfr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\n4\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n5\t`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n6\t\n7\t> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## 1. Overview\n12\t\n13\tSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5\n14\tand MUI 9.5. Attendance is a **new feature inside a brownfield app**. Nothing attendance-related exists on disk yet\n15\t(`src/server/attendance/` and `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` are both absent, which I verified). The feature is\n16\tbuilt around a single service module and a single shared validator module. A thin set of route handlers and pages\n17\tsits on top, and it plugs into existing extension points: the timetable, notify, access helpers, audit, csv,\n18\tsettings, and the tab and nav configs.\n19\t\n20\t**Shape:** 1 migration · 1 service file + 1 pure rules file · 1 validator file · 10 API routes · 4 page areas\n21\t(take, register, admin, 2 tabs) · 1 shared register client component · config entries · seed extension · tests.\n22\t**No new dependencies, no job queue, no cron, no new auth abstraction** (ADR-1, ADR-4, ADR-5, ADR-8).\n23\t\n24\t### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n25\t\n26\t| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n27\t|---|---|---|\n28\t| 1 | Greenfield within brownfield: models, migration, service, validators, 10 routes, pages, tabs, nav, seed, tests. | Components C1 to C12 below. |\n29\t| 2 | Reuse getScheduleForDate, notify, the access asserts, audit, toCsv, settings and `src/components/<Name>/` (not `shared/`). | §2.1 lists the reused modules. C2 adds **one** additive export to the timetable service (school-wide schedule); everything else is consumed unchanged. |\n30\t| 3 | **FR-5 (MEDIUM)**: there is no school settings page or route. | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN) plus an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` (C9). The user can override this. |\n31\t| 4 | **FR-16 (LOW)**: the daily register route is unspecified. | `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` (C7). The user can override this. |\n32\t| 5 | **FR-23 (LOW)**: metadata for corrected and register_missing is unspecified. | `attendance.corrected`: ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false. `attendance.register_missing`: ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false (C5). |\n33\t| 6 | **NFR-6**: mui-mcp must be reachable before UI work, or it is a hard blocker. | Carried forward to dev. Every MUI component in C7 to C10 must be looked up via `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0 first. |\n34\t\n35\t---\n36\t\n37\t## 2. Component Breakdown\n38\t\n39\t### 2.1 Existing modules reused (consumed only; not modified unless noted)\n40\t\n41\t| Module | Used for |\n42\t|---|---|\n43\t| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`: `getScheduleForDate`, `getCurrentSlot`, `slotInclude` | FR-6/7 teacher landing, current-period highlight. **Additive change:** a new export, `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` (C2). |\n44\t| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`: `notifyStudentAndParents`, `notify` | FR-21/22/31. Both never throw. |\n45\t| `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | **Additive:** 4 new keys (C5). |\n46\t| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | NFR-7 in every handler and server page. |\n47\t| `src/server/audit.ts`: `audit()` | FR-18. Uses the global `prisma` (no `tx` param) and never throws, so it is called **after commit**. |\n48\t| `src/server/http.ts`: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` | Every route (NFR-8). |\n49\t| `src/server/csv.ts`: `toCsv` | FR-32 CSV export. |\n50\t| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | **Additive:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` gains `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?` (FR-4/5). |\n51\t| `src/lib/dates.ts`: `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | Every school-timezone computation (ADR-5). |\n52\t| `src/components/{DataTable,StatCard,UserAvatar,PageHeader,EmptyState,DateDisplay,LoadingSkeleton,Toast}` | UI. Reuse in place; do not move or copy. |\n53\t| `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | **Additive:** entries for FR-24/29/34. |\n54\t\n55\t### 2.2 New components\n56\t\n57\t#### C1 Data model and migration (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, NFR-8)\n58\t\n59\t`prisma/schema.prisma` (additive):\n60\t\n61\t```prisma\n62\tenum AttendanceStatus { PRESENT ABSENT LATE EXCUSED }\n63\tenum AttendanceMode   { PER_PERIOD DAILY_HOMEROOM BOTH }\n64\t\n65\tmodel AttendanceSession {\n66\t  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n67\t  courseId    String?                     // exactly one of courseId / sectionId (CHECK)\n68\t  course      Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n69\t  sectionId   String?\n70\t  section     Section? @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n71\t  periodId    String?                     // set for course sessions, null for daily\n72\t  period      Period?  @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])\n73\t  date        DateTime @db.Date\n74\t  takenById   String                      // FR-6 \"Taken HH:mm by <name>\"\n75\t  takenBy     User     @relation(\"AttendanceTakenBy\", fields: [takenById], references: [id])\n76\t  updatedById String                      // FR-14 \"last changed by\"\n77\t  updatedBy   User     @relation(\"AttendanceUpdatedBy\", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])\n78\t  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n79\t  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n80\t  records     AttendanceRecord[]\n81\t\n82\t  @@index([date])\n83\t}\n84\t\n85\tmodel AttendanceRecord {\n86\t  id          String            @id @default(cuid())\n87\t  sessionId   String\n88\t  session     AttendanceSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n89\t  studentId   String\n90\t  student     User              @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n91\t  status      AttendanceStatus\n92\t  minutesLate Int?              // 1..240, required iff LATE\n93\t  note        String?           // ≤ 500\n94\t  createdAt   DateTime          @default(now())\n95\t  updatedAt   DateTime          @updatedAt\n96\t\n97\t  @@unique([sessionId, studentId])\n98\t  @@index([studentId, createdAt])\n99\t}\n100\t// SchoolSettings += attendanceMode AttendanceMode @default(PER_PERIOD), attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\tBack-relations are added on `Course`, `Section`, `Period` and `User`. These are additive fields only, with no renames (NFR-10).\n104\t\n105\tThe migration is `prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/`. Generate it with `--create-only`, then append the following by hand (ADR-2):\n106\t- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)` (FR-2)\n107\t- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_course_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n108\t- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_section_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n109\t\n110\tThe test database is built with `migrate reset`/`deploy`, never `db push`.\n111\t\n112\t#### C2 School-wide schedule helper (FR-30, FR-31)\n113\t\n114\tAdd one exported function to `timetable-service.ts`: `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date): Promise<ScheduleEntry[]>`. It\n115\tfollows the same steps as `getScheduleForDate`: school-day check, **the PRD-14 holiday hook comment**, the current\n116\tyear, and `slotInclude`, but with no target filter. `slotInclude.course` already carries `teacher` and `section`, which\n117\tthe overview and remind features need. Existing functions are not changed.\n118\t\n119\t#### C3 Pure rules: `src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts` (FR-8, FR-19, FR-22, FR-28, FR-39)\n120\t\n121\tThis file has no DB imports, so unit tests need no database.\n122\t- `schoolToday(now, tz): string`: `yyyy-MM-dd` in the school timezone.\n123\t- `canOpen(role, date, today)`: refuses future dates. ADMIN can open any past date; TEACHER only dates where `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-8).\n124\t- `canEdit(role, date, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-19). Returns `{ ok, reason? }`; `reason` drives the read-only explanation.\n125\t- `diffRecords(prev: Map<studentId, Rec>, next: Rec[])` → `{ created[], changed[{studentId, prev, next}] }`. This drives the writes, FR-18 audit and notifications.\n126\t- `notificationsFor(diff)` → `{ absent[], late[], corrected[] }`: notifies on a transition *into* ABSENT, a transition *into* LATE, and ABSENT→PRESENT (corrected). Unchanged statuses produce nothing, which is the FR-22 dedupe.\n127\t- `attendanceRate(counts)`: `(P+L+E)/total×100`, rounded to 1 dp, or `null` when total is 0 (FR-28).\n128\t- `dayColour(statuses[])`: error if any ABSENT, else warning if any LATE, else success, or default when there is no data (FR-26).\n129\t\n130\t#### C4 Service: `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (FR-37)\n131\t\n132\t| Function | Reqs | Notes |\n133\t|---|---|---|\n134\t| `getToday(user)` | FR-6, FR-7 | `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` for today, joined with today's sessions (`takenBy`, `createdAt`). `getCurrentSlot` gives the highlighted entry. If the mode is DAILY_HOMEROOM or BOTH, it appends sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. |\n135\t| `getRegister(user, key)` | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19, NFR-3 | `key` is `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`. Access: `assertCanManageCourse` (course) or `assertCanManageSection` (section). Runs `canOpen`. The roster is students active on the date (rule below), sorted by last name. Returns the existing records, `updatedBy`/`updatedAt`, `readOnly` and `readOnlyReason`, plus header labels (course, section, period, date). |\n136\t| `saveRegister(user, key, records)` | FR-2, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3 | See §3.2. |\n137\t| `assertCanManageSection(user, sectionId)` | FR-15, NFR-7 | ADMIN, or `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Otherwise it throws `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`. This is the only new access helper and stays private to this module. |\n138\t| `getStudentAttendance(user, studentId, {from,to})` | FR-25 to FR-28, NFR-1 | `assertCanViewStudent`. Runs one `findMany` filtered by `session.date` and by the session kind for the mode (course sessions for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, section sessions for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure folds then produce the term and year summaries, the per-day calendar map and the table rows. **`note` is stripped when the role is STUDENT or PARENT** (FR-27). |\n139\t| `getCourseMatrix(user, courseId)` | FR-29 | `assertCanManageCourse`. Loads the last 20 sessions by date and the students enrolled (ACTIVE plus DROPPED students who have records) with a P/A/L/E cell map and a per-student `attendanceRate`. |\n140\t| `getOverview(date)` | FR-30, FR-31 | Expected = `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` plus sections, if the mode includes daily. Taken = sessions on that date. Missing = expected meetings with no session where `period.startTime + 15 min ≤ now` (school tz, only when `date` is today). Also returns the school-wide rate for the day. |\n141\t| `remindTeacher(admin, {courseId, periodId, date})` | FR-31 | `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[course.teacherId], link:/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=})`, then `audit`. |\n142\t| `getReport(filters)` | FR-32, NFR-8 | `groupBy(['studentId','status'])` over records filtered by session date range (≤ 366 days), grade, section, course and status, folded into per-student rows. The JSON response is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100); `?format=csv` returns all rows through `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n143\t| `getBelowThreshold()` | FR-33 | The same aggregate over the current academic year (start to today), filtered to `rate < settings.attendanceAlertThreshold` and sorted ascending. |\n144\t\n145\t**Active-on-date rule (NFR-3, FR-9):**\n146\t- Course: `Enrollment.courseId = X AND enrolledAt::date ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt::date > date)`.\n147\t- Section: `SectionMember.sectionId = X` for the section's academic year.\n148\t\n149\t**Current term (FR-25):** the `Term` of the current year whose date range contains today; otherwise the latest ended term (intake default).\n150\t\n151\t#### C5 Notification types (FR-20, FR-23): `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (additive)\n152\t\n153\t| Key | category | defaultEmail | mandatoryInApp | roles |\n154\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n155\t| `attendance.absent` | ATTENDANCE | true | true | PARENT, STUDENT |\n156\t| `attendance.late` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n157\t| `attendance.corrected` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n158\t| `attendance.register_missing` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | TEACHER |\n159\t\n160\t#### C6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` (FR-36)\n161\t\n162\tThese schemas are shared by `RegisterForm` and every handler:\n163\t- `registerQuery`: either `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`, as a Zod union. `date` uses `yyyy-MM-dd`.\n164\t- `registerRecord`: `{studentId, status, minutesLate?, note?}`. A `superRefine` requires `minutesLate` 1–240 when the status is LATE and forbids it otherwise. `note` is at most 500 characters (FR-12).\n165\t- `registerPutBody`: `registerQuery & { records: registerRecord[] }`. It has at least one record, and `studentId`s must be unique.\n166\t- `studentAttendanceQuery {from?, to?}`, `courseMatrixQuery`, `overviewQuery {date?}`.\n167\t- `reportFilters {from, to, gradeLevelId?, sectionId?, courseId?, status?, format?: 'csv'}`: a refine rejects ranges over 366 days or with `to < from`.\n168\t- `remindBody {courseId, periodId, date}`.\n169\t- `attendanceSettingsPatch {attendanceMode?, attendanceAlertThreshold?: int 0–100}`.\n170\t\n171\tRole-dependent rules (EXCUSED only for ADMIN, the 14-day window, future dates) are checked in the service against the\n172\tuser, not in Zod. The client imports the same pure `canOpen` rule from C3 for the date picker's `minDate`/`disableFuture`.\n173\t\n174\t#### C7 Register UI (FR-6 to FR-17, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-9)\n175\t\n176\t- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/page.tsx` (server): calls `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` and `getToday`. Lists the meetings with their status, gives the current one a primary \"Take attendance\" button, shows \"Daily register – <section>\" entries, and has a `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate` = today − 14 days for teachers) that navigates to the chosen date.\n177\t- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/[courseId]/page.tsx` and `.../take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx` (server): run `getRegister`, then render the same client component.\n178\t- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` (client, the only register component):\n179\t  - One row per student at least 48 px tall: `UserAvatar`, the name, and an exclusive `ToggleButtonGroup` P/A/L/E with targets at least 44×44 px, palette colours and an `aria-label` such as \"Mark <name> absent\". E is disabled unless the user is an ADMIN.\n180\t  - Choosing L reveals a minutes input that defaults to 5. A note icon opens an optional note field.\n181\t  - The header shows counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked) and \"Mark all present\", which fills only unset rows.\n182\t  - A sticky `Paper` save bar has Save, disabled while any row is unmarked or the register is `readOnly`. When read-only, the form shows the reason and \"last changed by X at Y\".\n183\t  - It PUTs to `/api/attendance/register`. On a network failure it writes a draft to `localStorage` under `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>`. On mount it offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" when a draft exists, and it clears the draft on success (NFR-2, ADR-7).\n184\t  - Validation uses the C6 schemas.\n185\t\n186\t#### C8 Student Attendance tab (FR-24 to FR-28)\n187\t\n188\t`src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/attendance/page.tsx` shows:\n189\t- 2×4 `StatCard`s: term and year rate %, absent, late and excused counts.\n190\t- A read-only `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot coloured by `dayColour`, a `Tooltip` per-day summary, and month navigation that refetches `?from=&to=`.\n191\t- A `DataTable` with filters showing date, period, course, status, minutes late and note. Notes are already stripped server-side for STUDENT/PARENT.\n192\t\n193\t#### C9 Admin pages (FR-5, FR-30 to FR-33)\n194\t\n195\t`src/app/(app)/admin/attendance/page.tsx`, protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. It is a single page with MUI `Tabs`:\n196\t- **Today**: expected vs taken, today's rate, and a \"Missing registers\" list with a \"Remind teacher\" button (POSTs to remind, then a toast).\n197\t- **Report**: a filter form, a `DataGrid` with per-student rows, and an \"Export CSV\" link to `?format=csv`.\n198\t- **Below threshold**: a list sorted ascending, each row linked to `/students/<id>/attendance`.\n199\t- **Settings**: a card editing `attendanceMode` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` via `PATCH /api/settings/school` (FR-5).\n200\t\n201\tOne page with tabs instead of four routes keeps the file count down.\n202\t\n203\t#### C10 Course Attendance tab (FR-29)\n204\t\n205\t`src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/attendance/page.tsx` is a `DataGrid` with one row per student. It has up to 20\n206\tdynamic date columns that scroll horizontally, with coloured cells, plus a rate column. Each column header links to\n207\t`/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=`.\n208\t\n209\t#### C11 Config and nav (FR-24, FR-29, FR-34)\n210\t\n211\t- `student-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', label:'Attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. Page access still goes through `assertCanViewStudent`.\n212\t- `course-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', …, roles:['TEACHER','ADMIN']}`.\n213\t- `navigation.ts`: add \"Attendance\" for TEACHER → `/attendance/take` and \"Attendance\" for ADMIN in the main group → `/admin/attendance`.\n214\t\n215\t#### C12 Seed and tests (FR-38 to FR-41)\n216\t\n217\t- **Seed:** extend the existing seed with a mulberry32 RNG using a fixed seed. Generate 7A/7B course sessions for each timetable slot over the 15 teaching days before the run date, using `SchoolDay`. Records are about 94% P, 3% L (minutes 5–20) and 3% A. Force two named Grade 7 students below 85%. Make the seed idempotent: delete the attendance rows for that window first.\n218\t- **Unit:** `attendance-rules.test.ts` covers `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`/`canOpen` at the 14/15-day edges, and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`, including re-saving with no changes and ABSENT→PRESENT.\n219\t- **Integration:** `attendance-service.int.test.ts` covers atomic save (a failing record means no session row), NFR-3 rejection, the CHECK constraint, both partial unique indexes, EXCUSED rejected for a teacher, and the edit window returning 403.\n220\t- **E2E:** `attendance.spec.ts` at 375×667 takes a register (mark all present, one absent, one late, save), then logs in as the parent and sees the notification and a red day on the calendar.\n221\t\n222\t---\n223\t\n224\t## 3. Data Flow\n225\t\n226\t### 3.1 Request pipeline (every route, NFR-7, NFR-8)\n227\t\n228\t`withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (C6) → resource assert → service (C4) → `ok`/`paginated` or `AppError` → response.\n229\t\n230\t### 3.2 Save register: `PUT /api/attendance/register` (FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-5)\n231\t\n232\t```\n233\tRegisterForm ──PUT {key, records[]}──► route ─► saveRegister(user, key, records)\n234\t  1. Access: assertCanManageCourse | assertCanManageSection\n235\t  2. canOpen(date) else 400. canEdit(role, date, today) else 403 FORBIDDEN (FR-19).\n236\t  3. Any EXCUSED and role ≠ ADMIN → 403 (FR-10).\n237\t  4. prisma.$transaction(async tx => {\n238\t       roster = active-on-date ids (one query). Any record.studentId ∉ roster → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (NFR-3).\n239\t       Records must cover the whole roster → else 400 (FR-13 server-side mirror).\n240\t       session = findFirst(key) ?? create(...). On P2002, re-read (ADR-3, partial idx race).\n241\t       prev = findMany({sessionId}) → Map.\n242\t       diff = diffRecords(prev, records).\n243\t       createMany(diff.created). update each diff.changed row (≤ roster size).\n244\t       session.update({updatedById: user.id}).\n245\t     })\n246\t  5. After commit:\n247\t       for c of diff.changed where status changed → audit('attendance.record.update', {old, new, note}, actor)  (FR-18)\n248\t       for n of notificationsFor(diff) → notifyStudentAndParents (one call per student)  (FR-21/22)\n249\t         title \"X was marked absent\" | \"X was marked late (N min)\" | \"Attendance corrected: X was present\"\n250\t         body  \"<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <EEEE d MMM yyyy>\" | \"<Section> daily register, <date>\"\n251\t         link  /students/<id>/attendance\n252\t  6. Return the fresh register (same shape as GET).\n253\t```\n254\t\n255\tBrand-new records count as transitions from \"nothing\", so the first save that marks a student ABSENT notifies\n256\tonce. A re-save with the same status produces no diff and sends nothing (FR-22).\n257\t\n258\t### 3.3 Read flows\n259\t\n260\t- **Teacher landing:** `/attendance/take` → `getToday` → timetable + sessions (+ homeroom sections).\n261\t- **Student tab:** `GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=` → one indexed query → pure folds (rate, calendar, rows), with notes stripped by role.\n262\t- **Admin overview:** `getSchoolScheduleForDate(today)` minus today's sessions, filtered by the `startTime + 15 min` rule in the school timezone.\n263\t- **Report / below threshold:** `groupBy` on (studentId, status) → per-student rows → JSON page or CSV.\n264\t\n265\t### 3.4 Time handling (ADR-5)\n266\t\n267\tAll \"today\", future-date and 14-day comparisons use `schoolToday(now, settings.timezone)` against `@db.Date`\n268\tvalues. Times are shown with `formatInSchoolTz`. Server-local `new Date()` is never used for date-only logic.\n269\t\n270\t---\n271\t\n272\t## 4. API surface (detailed in `api-contracts.json` by arch-api-contracts)\n273\t\n274\t| Method | Path | Guard | Reqs |\n275\t|---|---|---|---|\n276\t| GET | `/api/attendance/today` | TEACHER, ADMIN | FR-6, FR-7 |\n277\t| GET | `/api/attendance/register?courseId&date&periodId` or `?sectionId&date` | manage course / homeroom or ADMIN | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19 |\n278\t| PUT | `/api/attendance/register` | same, plus edit window and EXCUSED rule | FR-10, FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-3 |\n279\t| GET | `/api/students/:id/attendance?from&to` | `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-25 to FR-28 |\n280\t| GET | `/api/courses/:id/attendance` | `assertCanManageCourse` | FR-29 |\n281\t| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/overview?date` | ADMIN | FR-30, FR-31 |\n282\t| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/report?…&format=csv` | ADMIN | FR-32 |\n283\t| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/below-threshold` | ADMIN | FR-33 |\n284\t| POST | `/api/admin/attendance/remind` | ADMIN | FR-31 |\n285\t| PATCH | `/api/settings/school` | ADMIN, with audit | FR-4, FR-5 |\n286\t\n287\tAll 10 are listed under FR-35. Error codes come from `http.ts` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` 400, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `NOT_FOUND` 404).\n288\t\n289\t---\n290\t\n291\t## 5. Requirements Traceability\n292\t\n293\t| Req | Design element |\n294\t|---|---|\n295\t| FR-1 | C1 models and enum |\n296\t| FR-2 | C1 CHECK; C4 `saveRegister` key shape (C6 union) |\n297\t| FR-3 | C1 partial unique indexes; §3.2 P2002 re-read |\n298\t| FR-4 | C1 SchoolSettings columns; settings service input |\n299\t| FR-5 | C9 Settings tab; `PATCH /api/settings/school` |\n300\t| FR-6 | C4 `getToday`; C7 landing |\n301\t| FR-7 | C4 `getToday` homeroom entries; C7 |\n302\t| FR-8 | C3 `canOpen`; C7 DatePicker |\n303\t| FR-9 | C4 roster rule; C7 `RegisterForm` |\n304\t| FR-10 | §3.2 step 3; C7 E disabled |\n305\t| FR-11 | C7 \"Mark all present\" |\n306\t| FR-12 | C6 `registerRecord`; C7 minutes and note inputs |\n307\t| FR-13 | C7 counters and Save disabled; §3.2 full-roster check |\n308\t| FR-14 | §3.2 transaction; `updatedBy`/`updatedAt` |\n309\t| FR-15 | C4 `assertCanManageSection`; section roster |\n310\t| FR-16 | C7 section route reusing `RegisterForm` |\n311\t| FR-17 | C7 48 px rows, 44 px toggles, sticky Paper |\n312\t| FR-18 | §3.2 step 5 audit |\n313\t| FR-19 | C3 `canEdit`; §3.2 step 2; C7 read-only mode |\n314\t| FR-20 | C5 absent and late types |\n315\t| FR-21 | §3.2 step 5 notify; C3 `notificationsFor` |\n316\t| FR-22 | C3 `notificationsFor` (transition-only, corrected) |\n317\t| FR-23 | C5 corrected and register_missing types |\n318\t| FR-24 | C11 student tab; C8 page |\n319\t| FR-25 | C4 `getStudentAttendance`; C8 StatCards |\n320\t| FR-26 | C3 `dayColour`; C8 DateCalendar day slot |\n321\t| FR-27 | C4 note stripping; C8 DataTable |\n322\t| FR-28 | C3 `attendanceRate`; C4 mode-based session kind |\n323\t| FR-29 | C4 `getCourseMatrix`; C10; C11 course tab |\n324\t| FR-30 | C2 `getSchoolScheduleForDate`; C4 `getOverview`; C9 Today |\n325\t| FR-31 | C4 missing rule and `remindTeacher`; C9 Remind button |\n326\t| FR-32 | C4 `getReport`; C6 `reportFilters`; C9 Report and CSV |\n327\t| FR-33 | C4 `getBelowThreshold`; C9 Below threshold |\n328\t| FR-34 | C11 navigation entries |\n329\t| FR-35 | §4 route table |\n330\t| FR-36 | C6 validators |\n331\t| FR-37 | C4 service path (+ C3 sibling rules file) |\n332\t| FR-38 | C12 seed |\n333\t| FR-39 | C12 unit tests on C3 |\n334\t| FR-40 | C12 integration tests |\n335\t| FR-41 | C12 Playwright |\n336\t| NFR-1 | §3.2 single tx with batched writes; C4 single-query student tab |\n337\t| NFR-2 | C7 localStorage draft and restore |\n338\t| NFR-3 | C4 active-on-date rule; §3.2 roster check |\n339\t| NFR-4 | C7 mark-all-present plus mobile layout |\n340\t| NFR-5 | §3.2 post-commit `notifyStudentAndParents` (in-app immediate, EmailOutbox) |\n341\t| NFR-6 | C7 to C10 MUI only, with mui-mcp lookups (Overview blocker 6) |\n342\t| NFR-7 | §3.1 pipeline; C4 asserts; note stripping |\n343\t| NFR-8 | C1 cuid and `@db.Date`; §3.4 timezone; §4 http helpers; pagination ≤ 100 |\n344\t| NFR-9 | C7 `aria-label`s and 44 px targets |\n345\t| NFR-10 | §2.1 reuse in place, only additive changes, no new deps, holidays (PRD-14) and EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) excluded |\n346\t\n347\t---\n348\t\n349\t## 6. Out of scope\n350\t\n351\tHoliday handling (PRD-14, which stays at the existing hook comment), the absence-note/EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15),\n352\tautomatic missing-register reminders (no scheduler; ADR-5), a general school settings page, and offline-first\n353\tservice workers (ADR-7).\n354\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fe1befa-2c95-4276-8d14-955b8d55df5c","uuid":"22848044-c3f9-4e60-8184-d43b16bbd091","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:39:54.319Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n\nTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5\nand MUI 9.5. Attendance is a **new feature inside a brownfield app**. Nothing attendance-related exists on disk yet\n(`src/server/attendance/` and `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` are both absent, which I verified). The feature is\nbuilt around a single service module and a single shared validator module. A thin set of route handlers and pages\nsits on top, and it plugs into existing extension points: the timetable, notify, access helpers, audit, csv,\nsettings, and the tab and nav configs.\n\n**Shape:** 1 migration · 1 service file + 1 pure rules file · 1 validator file · 10 API routes · 4 page areas\n(take, register, admin, 2 tabs) · 1 shared register client component · config entries · seed extension · tests.\n**No new dependencies, no job queue, no cron, no new auth abstraction** (ADR-1, ADR-4, ADR-5, ADR-8).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield within brownfield: models, migration, service, validators, 10 routes, pages, tabs, nav, seed, tests. | Components C1 to C12 below. |\n| 2 | Reuse getScheduleForDate, notify, the access asserts, audit, toCsv, settings and `src/components/<Name>/` (not `shared/`). | §2.1 lists the reused modules. C2 adds **one** additive export to the timetable service (school-wide schedule); everything else is consumed unchanged. |\n| 3 | **FR-5 (MEDIUM)**: there is no school settings page or route. | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN) plus an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` (C9). The user can override this. |\n| 4 | **FR-16 (LOW)**: the daily register route is unspecified. | `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` (C7). The user can override this. |\n| 5 | **FR-23 (LOW)**: metadata for corrected and register_missing is unspecified. | `attendance.corrected`: ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false. `attendance.register_missing`: ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false (C5). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6**: mui-mcp must be reachable before UI work, or it is a hard blocker. | Carried forward to dev. Every MUI component in C7 to C10 must be looked up via `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0 first. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules reused (consumed only; not modified unless noted)\n\n| Module | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`: `getScheduleForDate`, `getCurrentSlot`, `slotInclude` | FR-6/7 teacher landing, current-period highlight. **Additive change:** a new export, `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` (C2). |\n| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`: `notifyStudentAndParents`, `notify` | FR-21/22/31. Both never throw. |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | **Additive:** 4 new keys (C5). |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | NFR-7 in every handler and server page. |\n| `src/server/audit.ts`: `audit()` | FR-18. Uses the global `prisma` (no `tx` param) and never throws, so it is called **after commit**. |\n| `src/server/http.ts`: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` | Every route (NFR-8). |\n| `src/server/csv.ts`: `toCsv` | FR-32 CSV export. |\n| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | **Additive:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` gains `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?` (FR-4/5). |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts`: `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | Every school-timezone computation (ADR-5). |\n| `src/components/{DataTable,StatCard,UserAvatar,PageHeader,EmptyState,DateDisplay,LoadingSkeleton,Toast}` | UI. Reuse in place; do not move or copy. |\n| `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | **Additive:** entries for FR-24/29/34. |\n\n### 2.2 New components\n\n#### C1 Data model and migration (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, NFR-8)\n\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (additive):\n\n```prisma\nenum AttendanceStatus { PRESENT ABSENT LATE EXCUSED }\nenum AttendanceMode   { PER_PERIOD DAILY_HOMEROOM BOTH }\n\nmodel AttendanceSession {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String?                     // exactly one of courseId / sectionId (CHECK)\n  course      Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  sectionId   String?\n  section     Section? @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  periodId    String?                     // set for course sessions, null for daily\n  period      Period?  @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])\n  date        DateTime @db.Date\n  takenById   String                      // FR-6 \"Taken HH:mm by <name>\"\n  takenBy     User     @relation(\"AttendanceTakenBy\", fields: [takenById], references: [id])\n  updatedById String                      // FR-14 \"last changed by\"\n  updatedBy   User     @relation(\"AttendanceUpdatedBy\", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n  records     AttendanceRecord[]\n\n  @@index([date])\n}\n\nmodel AttendanceRecord {\n  id          String            @id @default(cuid())\n  sessionId   String\n  session     AttendanceSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  student     User              @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  status      AttendanceStatus\n  minutesLate Int?              // 1..240, required iff LATE\n  note        String?           // ≤ 500\n  createdAt   DateTime          @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime          @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([sessionId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId, createdAt])\n}\n// SchoolSettings += attendanceMode AttendanceMode @default(PER_PERIOD), attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)\n```\n\nBack-relations are added on `Course`, `Section`, `Period` and `User`. These are additive fields only, with no renames (NFR-10).\n\nThe migration is `prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/`. Generate it with `--create-only`, then append the following by hand (ADR-2):\n- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)` (FR-2)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_course_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_section_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n\nThe test database is built with `migrate reset`/`deploy`, never `db push`.\n\n#### C2 School-wide schedule helper (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nAdd one exported function to `timetable-service.ts`: `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date): Promise<ScheduleEntry[]>`. It\nfollows the same steps as `getScheduleForDate`: school-day check, **the PRD-14 holiday hook comment**, the current\nyear, and `slotInclude`, but with no target filter. `slotInclude.course` already carries `teacher` and `section`, which\nthe overview and remind features need. Existing functions are not changed.\n\n#### C3 Pure rules: `src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts` (FR-8, FR-19, FR-22, FR-28, FR-39)\n\nThis file has no DB imports, so unit tests need no database.\n- `schoolToday(now, tz): string`: `yyyy-MM-dd` in the school timezone.\n- `canOpen(role, date, today)`: refuses future dates. ADMIN can open any past date; TEACHER only dates where `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-8).\n- `canEdit(role, date, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-19). Returns `{ ok, reason? }`; `reason` drives the read-only explanation.\n- `diffRecords(prev: Map<studentId, Rec>, next: Rec[])` → `{ created[], changed[{studentId, prev, next}] }`. This drives the writes, FR-18 audit and notifications.\n- `notificationsFor(diff)` → `{ absent[], late[], corrected[] }`: notifies on a transition *into* ABSENT, a transition *into* LATE, and ABSENT→PRESENT (corrected). Unchanged statuses produce nothing, which is the FR-22 dedupe.\n- `attendanceRate(counts)`: `(P+L+E)/total×100`, rounded to 1 dp, or `null` when total is 0 (FR-28).\n- `dayColour(statuses[])`: error if any ABSENT, else warning if any LATE, else success, or default when there is no data (FR-26).\n\n#### C4 Service: `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (FR-37)\n\n| Function | Reqs | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `getToday(user)` | FR-6, FR-7 | `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` for today, joined with today's sessions (`takenBy`, `createdAt`). `getCurrentSlot` gives the highlighted entry. If the mode is DAILY_HOMEROOM or BOTH, it appends sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. |\n| `getRegister(user, key)` | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19, NFR-3 | `key` is `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`. Access: `assertCanManageCourse` (course) or `assertCanManageSection` (section). Runs `canOpen`. The roster is students active on the date (rule below), sorted by last name. Returns the existing records, `updatedBy`/`updatedAt`, `readOnly` and `readOnlyReason`, plus header labels (course, section, period, date). |\n| `saveRegister(user, key, records)` | FR-2, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3 | See §3.2. |\n| `assertCanManageSection(user, sectionId)` | FR-15, NFR-7 | ADMIN, or `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Otherwise it throws `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`. This is the only new access helper and stays private to this module. |\n| `getStudentAttendance(user, studentId, {from,to})` | FR-25 to FR-28, NFR-1 | `assertCanViewStudent`. Runs one `findMany` filtered by `session.date` and by the session kind for the mode (course sessions for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, section sessions for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure folds then produce the term and year summaries, the per-day calendar map and the table rows. **`note` is stripped when the role is STUDENT or PARENT** (FR-27). |\n| `getCourseMatrix(user, courseId)` | FR-29 | `assertCanManageCourse`. Loads the last 20 sessions by date and the students enrolled (ACTIVE plus DROPPED students who have records) with a P/A/L/E cell map and a per-student `attendanceRate`. |\n| `getOverview(date)` | FR-30, FR-31 | Expected = `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` plus sections, if the mode includes daily. Taken = sessions on that date. Missing = expected meetings with no session where `period.startTime + 15 min ≤ now` (school tz, only when `date` is today). Also returns the school-wide rate for the day. |\n| `remindTeacher(admin, {courseId, periodId, date})` | FR-31 | `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[course.teacherId], link:/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=})`, then `audit`. |\n| `getReport(filters)` | FR-32, NFR-8 | `groupBy(['studentId','status'])` over records filtered by session date range (≤ 366 days), grade, section, course and status, folded into per-student rows. The JSON response is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100); `?format=csv` returns all rows through `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| `getBelowThreshold()` | FR-33 | The same aggregate over the current academic year (start to today), filtered to `rate < settings.attendanceAlertThreshold` and sorted ascending. |\n\n**Active-on-date rule (NFR-3, FR-9):**\n- Course: `Enrollment.courseId = X AND enrolledAt::date ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt::date > date)`.\n- Section: `SectionMember.sectionId = X` for the section's academic year.\n\n**Current term (FR-25):** the `Term` of the current year whose date range contains today; otherwise the latest ended term (intake default).\n\n#### C5 Notification types (FR-20, FR-23): `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (additive)\n\n| Key | category | defaultEmail | mandatoryInApp | roles |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `attendance.absent` | ATTENDANCE | true | true | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.late` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.corrected` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.register_missing` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | TEACHER |\n\n#### C6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` (FR-36)\n\nThese schemas are shared by `RegisterForm` and every handler:\n- `registerQuery`: either `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`, as a Zod union. `date` uses `yyyy-MM-dd`.\n- `registerRecord`: `{studentId, status, minutesLate?, note?}`. A `superRefine` requires `minutesLate` 1–240 when the status is LATE and forbids it otherwise. `note` is at most 500 characters (FR-12).\n- `registerPutBody`: `registerQuery & { records: registerRecord[] }`. It has at least one record, and `studentId`s must be unique.\n- `studentAttendanceQuery {from?, to?}`, `courseMatrixQuery`, `overviewQuery {date?}`.\n- `reportFilters {from, to, gradeLevelId?, sectionId?, courseId?, status?, format?: 'csv'}`: a refine rejects ranges over 366 days or with `to < from`.\n- `remindBody {courseId, periodId, date}`.\n- `attendanceSettingsPatch {attendanceMode?, attendanceAlertThreshold?: int 0–100}`.\n\nRole-dependent rules (EXCUSED only for ADMIN, the 14-day window, future dates) are checked in the service against the\nuser, not in Zod. The client imports the same pure `canOpen` rule from C3 for the date picker's `minDate`/`disableFuture`.\n\n#### C7 Register UI (FR-6 to FR-17, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-9)\n\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/page.tsx` (server): calls `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` and `getToday`. Lists the meetings with their status, gives the current one a primary \"Take attendance\" button, shows \"Daily register – <section>\" entries, and has a `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate` = today − 14 days for teachers) that navigates to the chosen date.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/[courseId]/page.tsx` and `.../take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx` (server): run `getRegister`, then render the same client component.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` (client, the only register component):\n  - One row per student at least 48 px tall: `UserAvatar`, the name, and an exclusive `ToggleButtonGroup` P/A/L/E with targets at least 44×44 px, palette colours and an `aria-label` such as \"Mark <name> absent\". E is disabled unless the user is an ADMIN.\n  - Choosing L reveals a minutes input that defaults to 5. A note icon opens an optional note field.\n  - The header shows counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked) and \"Mark all present\", which fills only unset rows.\n  - A sticky `Paper` save bar has Save, disabled while any row is unmarked or the register is `readOnly`. When read-only, the form shows the reason and \"last changed by X at Y\".\n  - It PUTs to `/api/attendance/register`. On a network failure it writes a draft to `localStorage` under `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>`. On mount it offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" when a draft exists, and it clears the draft on success (NFR-2, ADR-7).\n  - Validation uses the C6 schemas.\n\n#### C8 Student Attendance tab (FR-24 to FR-28)\n\n`src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/attendance/page.tsx` shows:\n- 2×4 `StatCard`s: term and year rate %, absent, late and excused counts.\n- A read-only `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot coloured by `dayColour`, a `Tooltip` per-day summary, and month navigation that refetches `?from=&to=`.\n- A `DataTable` with filters showing date, period, course, status, minutes late and note. Notes are already stripped server-side for STUDENT/PARENT.\n\n#### C9 Admin pages (FR-5, FR-30 to FR-33)\n\n`src/app/(app)/admin/attendance/page.tsx`, protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. It is a single page with MUI `Tabs`:\n- **Today**: expected vs taken, today's rate, and a \"Missing registers\" list with a \"Remind teacher\" button (POSTs to remind, then a toast).\n- **Report**: a filter form, a `DataGrid` with per-student rows, and an \"Export CSV\" link to `?format=csv`.\n- **Below threshold**: a list sorted ascending, each row linked to `/students/<id>/attendance`.\n- **Settings**: a card editing `attendanceMode` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` via `PATCH /api/settings/school` (FR-5).\n\nOne page with tabs instead of four routes keeps the file count down.\n\n#### C10 Course Attendance tab (FR-29)\n\n`src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/attendance/page.tsx` is a `DataGrid` with one row per student. It has up to 20\ndynamic date columns that scroll horizontally, with coloured cells, plus a rate column. Each column header links to\n`/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=`.\n\n#### C11 Config and nav (FR-24, FR-29, FR-34)\n\n- `student-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', label:'Attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. Page access still goes through `assertCanViewStudent`.\n- `course-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', …, roles:['TEACHER','ADMIN']}`.\n- `navigation.ts`: add \"Attendance\" for TEACHER → `/attendance/take` and \"Attendance\" for ADMIN in the main group → `/admin/attendance`.\n\n#### C12 Seed and tests (FR-38 to FR-41)\n\n- **Seed:** extend the existing seed with a mulberry32 RNG using a fixed seed. Generate 7A/7B course sessions for each timetable slot over the 15 teaching days before the run date, using `SchoolDay`. Records are about 94% P, 3% L (minutes 5–20) and 3% A. Force two named Grade 7 students below 85%. Make the seed idempotent: delete the attendance rows for that window first.\n- **Unit:** `attendance-rules.test.ts` covers `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`/`canOpen` at the 14/15-day edges, and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`, including re-saving with no changes and ABSENT→PRESENT.\n- **Integration:** `attendance-service.int.test.ts` covers atomic save (a failing record means no session row), NFR-3 rejection, the CHECK constraint, both partial unique indexes, EXCUSED rejected for a teacher, and the edit window returning 403.\n- **E2E:** `attendance.spec.ts` at 375×667 takes a register (mark all present, one absent, one late, save), then logs in as the parent and sees the notification and a red day on the calendar.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Request pipeline (every route, NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n`withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (C6) → resource assert → service (C4) → `ok`/`paginated` or `AppError` → response.\n\n### 3.2 Save register: `PUT /api/attendance/register` (FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-5)\n\n```\nRegisterForm ──PUT {key, records[]}──► route ─► saveRegister(user, key, records)\n  1. Access: assertCanManageCourse | assertCanManageSection\n  2. canOpen(date) else 400. canEdit(role, date, today) else 403 FORBIDDEN (FR-19).\n  3. Any EXCUSED and role ≠ ADMIN → 403 (FR-10).\n  4. prisma.$transaction(async tx => {\n       roster = active-on-date ids (one query). Any record.studentId ∉ roster → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (NFR-3).\n       Records must cover the whole roster → else 400 (FR-13 server-side mirror).\n       session = findFirst(key) ?? create(...). On P2002, re-read (ADR-3, partial idx race).\n       prev = findMany({sessionId}) → Map.\n       diff = diffRecords(prev, records).\n       createMany(diff.created). update each diff.changed row (≤ roster size).\n       session.update({updatedById: user.id}).\n     })\n  5. After commit:\n       for c of diff.changed where status changed → audit('attendance.record.update', {old, new, note}, actor)  (FR-18)\n       for n of notificationsFor(diff) → notifyStudentAndParents (one call per student)  (FR-21/22)\n         title \"X was marked absent\" | \"X was marked late (N min)\" | \"Attendance corrected: X was present\"\n         body  \"<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <EEEE d MMM yyyy>\" | \"<Section> daily register, <date>\"\n         link  /students/<id>/attendance\n  6. Return the fresh register (same shape as GET).\n```\n\nBrand-new records count as transitions from \"nothing\", so the first save that marks a student ABSENT notifies\nonce. A re-save with the same status produces no diff and sends nothing (FR-22).\n\n### 3.3 Read flows\n\n- **Teacher landing:** `/attendance/take` → `getToday` → timetable + sessions (+ homeroom sections).\n- **Student tab:** `GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=` → one indexed query → pure folds (rate, calendar, rows), with notes stripped by role.\n- **Admin overview:** `getSchoolScheduleForDate(today)` minus today's sessions, filtered by the `startTime + 15 min` rule in the school timezone.\n- **Report / below threshold:** `groupBy` on (studentId, status) → per-student rows → JSON page or CSV.\n\n### 3.4 Time handling (ADR-5)\n\nAll \"today\", future-date and 14-day comparisons use `schoolToday(now, settings.timezone)` against `@db.Date`\nvalues. Times are shown with `formatInSchoolTz`. Server-local `new Date()` is never used for date-only logic.\n\n---\n\n## 4. API surface (detailed in `api-contracts.json` by arch-api-contracts)\n\n| Method | Path | Guard | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GET | `/api/attendance/today` | TEACHER, ADMIN | FR-6, FR-7 |\n| GET | `/api/attendance/register?courseId&date&periodId` or `?sectionId&date` | manage course / homeroom or ADMIN | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19 |\n| PUT | `/api/attendance/register` | same, plus edit window and EXCUSED rule | FR-10, FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-3 |\n| GET | `/api/students/:id/attendance?from&to` | `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-25 to FR-28 |\n| GET | `/api/courses/:id/attendance` | `assertCanManageCourse` | FR-29 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/overview?date` | ADMIN | FR-30, FR-31 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/report?…&format=csv` | ADMIN | FR-32 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/below-threshold` | ADMIN | FR-33 |\n| POST | `/api/admin/attendance/remind` | ADMIN | FR-31 |\n| PATCH | `/api/settings/school` | ADMIN, with audit | FR-4, FR-5 |\n\nAll 10 are listed under FR-35. Error codes come from `http.ts` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` 400, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `NOT_FOUND` 404).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1 models and enum |\n| FR-2 | C1 CHECK; C4 `saveRegister` key shape (C6 union) |\n| FR-3 | C1 partial unique indexes; §3.2 P2002 re-read |\n| FR-4 | C1 SchoolSettings columns; settings service input |\n| FR-5 | C9 Settings tab; `PATCH /api/settings/school` |\n| FR-6 | C4 `getToday`; C7 landing |\n| FR-7 | C4 `getToday` homeroom entries; C7 |\n| FR-8 | C3 `canOpen`; C7 DatePicker |\n| FR-9 | C4 roster rule; C7 `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-10 | §3.2 step 3; C7 E disabled |\n| FR-11 | C7 \"Mark all present\" |\n| FR-12 | C6 `registerRecord`; C7 minutes and note inputs |\n| FR-13 | C7 counters and Save disabled; §3.2 full-roster check |\n| FR-14 | §3.2 transaction; `updatedBy`/`updatedAt` |\n| FR-15 | C4 `assertCanManageSection`; section roster |\n| FR-16 | C7 section route reusing `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-17 | C7 48 px rows, 44 px toggles, sticky Paper |\n| FR-18 | §3.2 step 5 audit |\n| FR-19 | C3 `canEdit`; §3.2 step 2; C7 read-only mode |\n| FR-20 | C5 absent and late types |\n| FR-21 | §3.2 step 5 notify; C3 `notificationsFor` |\n| FR-22 | C3 `notificationsFor` (transition-only, corrected) |\n| FR-23 | C5 corrected and register_missing types |\n| FR-24 | C11 student tab; C8 page |\n| FR-25 | C4 `getStudentAttendance`; C8 StatCards |\n| FR-26 | C3 `dayColour`; C8 DateCalendar day slot |\n| FR-27 | C4 note stripping; C8 DataTable |\n| FR-28 | C3 `attendanceRate`; C4 mode-based session kind |\n| FR-29 | C4 `getCourseMatrix`; C10; C11 course tab |\n| FR-30 | C2 `getSchoolScheduleForDate`; C4 `getOverview`; C9 Today |\n| FR-31 | C4 missing rule and `remindTeacher`; C9 Remind button |\n| FR-32 | C4 `getReport`; C6 `reportFilters`; C9 Report and CSV |\n| FR-33 | C4 `getBelowThreshold`; C9 Below threshold |\n| FR-34 | C11 navigation entries |\n| FR-35 | §4 route table |\n| FR-36 | C6 validators |\n| FR-37 | C4 service path (+ C3 sibling rules file) |\n| FR-38 | C12 seed |\n| FR-39 | C12 unit tests on C3 |\n| FR-40 | C12 integration tests |\n| FR-41 | C12 Playwright |\n| NFR-1 | §3.2 single tx with batched writes; C4 single-query student tab |\n| NFR-2 | C7 localStorage draft and restore |\n| NFR-3 | C4 active-on-date rule; §3.2 roster check |\n| NFR-4 | C7 mark-all-present plus mobile layout |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 post-commit `notifyStudentAndParents` (in-app immediate, EmailOutbox) |\n| NFR-6 | C7 to C10 MUI only, with mui-mcp lookups (Overview blocker 6) |\n| NFR-7 | §3.1 pipeline; C4 asserts; note stripping |\n| NFR-8 | C1 cuid and `@db.Date`; §3.4 timezone; §4 http helpers; pagination ≤ 100 |\n| NFR-9 | C7 `aria-label`s and 44 px targets |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 reuse in place, only additive changes, no new deps, holidays (PRD-14) and EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) excluded |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Out of scope\n\nHoliday handling (PRD-14, which stays at the existing hook comment), the absence-note/EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15),\nautomatic missing-register reminders (no scheduler; ADR-5), a general school settings page, and offline-first\nservice workers (ADR-7).\n","numLines":354,"startLine":1,"totalLines":354}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014FneLLjhMdGpTzQ3CnzAfr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
