{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E9q22KXcHP9HPYrmumdcyd","type":"tool_result","content":"### [List](#list)\n\nThe `ListItemIcon` default min-width has changed to `36px` (previously `56px`) to be consistent with the menu item, and now uses `theme.spacing` instead of a hardcoded number.\n\n### [Material Icons](#material-icons)\n### [Tabs](#tabs)\n\nThe `tabindex` attribute for each tab will be changed on Arrow Key or Home / End navigation. Previously, keyboard navigation moved DOM focus without updating `tabindex` on the focused `Tab`. Now, we move DOM focus and also add the `tabindex=\"0\"` to the focused `Tab`. Other tabs will have `tabindex=\"-1\"` to keep only one focusable `Tab` at a time.\n\nSelecting a `Tab` will update the focus and `tabindex` as before.\n\n`Tab`s not placed inside `Tabs` will now throw an error.\n\n### [TextField](#textfield)\n\nWhen specifying `<TextField select />` to render a `<Select>`, the underlying `<InputLabel>` renders a `<div>` instead of a native `<label>` element. This does not affect `<InputLabel>` on its own.\n\n### [Theme](#theme)\n\n`MuiTouchRipple` has been removed from the theme `components` types (`ComponentsProps`, `ComponentsOverrides`, and `ComponentsVariants`). TouchRipple has been an internal component since v5 and never consumed theme overrides or default props, so the types were misleading.\n\nIf you were using `MuiTouchRipple` in your theme, remove it and use global CSS with the `MuiTouchRipple-*` class names instead:\n\n```diff\n const theme = createTheme({\n   components: {\n-    MuiTouchRipple: {\n-      styleOverrides: {\n-        root: { color: 'red' },\n-      },\n-    },\n+    MuiButtonBase: {\n+      styleOverrides: {\n+        root: {\n+          '& .MuiTouchRipple-root': { color: 'red' },\n+        },\n+      },\n+    },\n   },\n });\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\n### [jsdom support](#jsdom-support)\n986:- `inputProps` — use `slotProps.input` instead\n991:-  inputProps={{ 'aria-label': 'Checkbox' }}\n1918:- `inputProps` — use `slotProps.input` instead\n1923:-  inputProps={{ 'aria-label': 'Radio' }}\n2244:-  tooltipTitle=\"Add\"\n2245:-  tooltipPlacement=\"right\"\n2246:-  tooltipOpen\n2247:-  TooltipClasses={{ tooltip: 'custom' }}\n2250:+    tooltip: {\n2254:+      classes: { tooltip: 'custom' },\n2274:- `inputProps` — use `slotProps.input` instead\n2279:-  inputProps={{ 'aria-label': 'Switch' }}\n2543:- `InputProps` → use `slotProps.input`\n2544:- `inputProps` → use `slotProps.htmlInput`\n2551:-  InputProps={CustomInputProps}\n2552:-  inputProps={CustomHtmlInputProps}\n2557:+    input: CustomInputProps,\n2558:+    htmlInput: CustomHtmlInputProps,\n2585:-      inputProps={{\n2586:-        ...params.inputProps,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fe1befa-2c95-4276-8d14-955b8d55df5c","uuid":"4c914ce2-200d-45da-8843-44cc4f12ee2a","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:47:32.864Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### [List](#list)\n\nThe `ListItemIcon` default min-width has changed to `36px` (previously `56px`) to be consistent with the menu item, and now uses `theme.spacing` instead of a hardcoded number.\n\n### [Material Icons](#material-icons)\n### [Tabs](#tabs)\n\nThe `tabindex` attribute for each tab will be changed on Arrow Key or Home / End navigation. Previously, keyboard navigation moved DOM focus without updating `tabindex` on the focused `Tab`. Now, we move DOM focus and also add the `tabindex=\"0\"` to the focused `Tab`. Other tabs will have `tabindex=\"-1\"` to keep only one focusable `Tab` at a time.\n\nSelecting a `Tab` will update the focus and `tabindex` as before.\n\n`Tab`s not placed inside `Tabs` will now throw an error.\n\n### [TextField](#textfield)\n\nWhen specifying `<TextField select />` to render a `<Select>`, the underlying `<InputLabel>` renders a `<div>` instead of a native `<label>` element. This does not affect `<InputLabel>` on its own.\n\n### [Theme](#theme)\n\n`MuiTouchRipple` has been removed from the theme `components` types (`ComponentsProps`, `ComponentsOverrides`, and `ComponentsVariants`). TouchRipple has been an internal component since v5 and never consumed theme overrides or default props, so the types were misleading.\n\nIf you were using `MuiTouchRipple` in your theme, remove it and use global CSS with the `MuiTouchRipple-*` class names instead:\n\n```diff\n const theme = createTheme({\n   components: {\n-    MuiTouchRipple: {\n-      styleOverrides: {\n-        root: { color: 'red' },\n-      },\n-    },\n+    MuiButtonBase: {\n+      styleOverrides: {\n+        root: {\n+          '& .MuiTouchRipple-root': { color: 'red' },\n+        },\n+      },\n+    },\n   },\n });\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\n### [jsdom support](#jsdom-support)\n986:- `inputProps` — use `slotProps.input` instead\n991:-  inputProps={{ 'aria-label': 'Checkbox' }}\n1918:- `inputProps` — use `slotProps.input` instead\n1923:-  inputProps={{ 'aria-label': 'Radio' }}\n2244:-  tooltipTitle=\"Add\"\n2245:-  tooltipPlacement=\"right\"\n2246:-  tooltipOpen\n2247:-  TooltipClasses={{ tooltip: 'custom' }}\n2250:+    tooltip: {\n2254:+      classes: { tooltip: 'custom' },\n2274:- `inputProps` — use `slotProps.input` instead\n2279:-  inputProps={{ 'aria-label': 'Switch' }}\n2543:- `InputProps` → use `slotProps.input`\n2544:- `inputProps` → use `slotProps.htmlInput`\n2551:-  InputProps={CustomInputProps}\n2552:-  inputProps={CustomHtmlInputProps}\n2557:+    input: CustomInputProps,\n2558:+    htmlInput: CustomHtmlInputProps,\n2585:-      inputProps={{\n2586:-        ...params.inputProps,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E9q22KXcHP9HPYrmumdcyd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
