{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DuqLQpoK6D3ubDKQzxZsGi","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/qa/qa-report.md:14:1. **BLOCKER (existed before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on it): the app's CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser.**\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:15:   - `next.config.js` (dated Oct 16) sends `Content-Security-Policy: … script-src 'self'`.\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:16:   - That policy blocks Next's inline `self.__next_f` scripts, plus `eval` in dev. In Chromium, `/login` was still not hydrated after 60s.\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:20:   - Every UI verdict below was proven with Playwright `bypassCSP: true`. That proves the SH-1 code is correct; it does **not** prove the shipped app works.\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:22:     - Use a nonce-based CSP in middleware, or allow `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts (plus `'unsafe-eval'` in dev only).\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:23:     - Also add `method=\"post\"` to the auth `<form>`s so a hydration failure can never leak passwords into URLs, logs or history.\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:26:   - Reproduced in jsdom (`tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx`) and in real Chromium (`tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts` › NFR-5).\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:49:     - Dev e2e `auth.spec.ts`: 5/5.\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:53:Also seen, outside SH-1's scope: the sidebar `<ul>` has `<a>` children (`ListItemButton component={Link}`), which is an axe `list` serious violation on signed-in pages. It only shows once the page hydrates. This is pre-existing shell nav code.\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:60:| FR-2 | PASS | src/app/(auth)/login/*; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"admin signs in…\" (with CSP bypass; see blocker 1) |\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:62:| FR-4 | PASS | LoginForm.tsx `loginErrorMessage`; tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"a wrong password shows the generic error\" |\nartifacts/qa/qa-report.md:65:| FR-7 | PASS | tests/unit/auth-valid