urse Attendance tab (matrix) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: Admin attendance page (Today / Report / Below threshold / Settings) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: Tab + navigation config entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: Seed attendance (mulberry32, idempotent) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Playwright e2e at 375×667 — ✓ complete (file written and run; see verification for which assertions were proven)\n\n### Implementation notes\n- **Migration (TASK-1).** Generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel`, the equivalent of `--create-only` with no shadow DB. The diff is additive only. The CHECK constraint and the two partial unique indexes were then appended by hand. Applied to the local DB with `migrate deploy`.\n- **Service, outside Next (TASK-7).** The service does not import `services/settings.ts`, because its `react.cache` is undefined outside Next (the same pattern as the timetable service). It reads the settings row directly instead.\n- **Service, saving a register.** `saveRegister` runs one interactive transaction:\n  - It checks the active-on-date roster (`invalidStudentIds`) and requires the full roster (`missingStudentIds`).\n  - It does find-or-create of the session, then the diff writes.\n  - A P2002 error aborts a Postgres transaction, so a re-read inside the same transaction is impossible. The P2002 race (ADR-3) is therefore handled by re-running the transaction once; the retry's `findFirst` sees the winning session.\n  - Audit and notifications run after commit.\n- **Service, enrollment dates.** Enrollment dates for the active-on-date rule are compared at the start of the next day in the school timezone (`fromZonedTime`).\n- **`getToday` date parameter.** `getToday` takes an optional `date` so the landing page's DatePicker works. `/api/attendance/today` still uses today, matching the contract.\n- **Report and below-threshold pagination.** Both group the rows in SQL (`groupBy`), then paginate in memory. This is marked with a `ponytail:` comment; its ceiling is the student count.\n- **Tooltip accessibility.** The calendar day Tooltip uses `describeChild`. Without it, MUI sets the tooltip text as the day button's aria-label, which hides the day number from assistive tech.\n- **NFR-6.** Before the UI work (TASK-12 to TASK-16), mui-mcp was reached:\n  - `useMuiDocs` for `@mui/material@9.5.0` and `@mui/x-date-pickers`.\n  - `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup, ToggleButton, Tabs and DateCalendar (the custom `day` slot).\n  - The v9 upgrade guide was also read.\n  - The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props, `slotProps.htmlInput`/`inputLabel`, `Tab` only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.\n- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).\n  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.\n  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.\n  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%.\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:\n  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.\n  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.\n  - Rate, day colour and validators.\n- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:\n  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).\n  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.\n  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.\n  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.\n  - Homeroom-only daily register.\n  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.\n  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.\n- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).\n  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.\n- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:\n  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".\n  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.\n  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2).\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)\n1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.\n2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:\n   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.\n   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.\n   - I tried `x-internals@9.14.0` (`--no-save`). That only moves the error to `@mui/x-virtualizer` 9.0.0-alpha.8, which wants `isFirefox` from `x-internals/platform`.\n   - I restored 9.15.0; `package-lock.json` is unchanged. A proper fix is to align the MUI X versions in package.json/lockfile, which is a dependency change outside this ticket.\n3. **vitest config.** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve, so `npm test` fails to start. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (same config, `vitest/config`) works.\n4. **No 7A/7B data.** There is no seed or dev data for sections, courses or the timetable, so the attendance seed is a no-op on this DB until PRD-05/06 data exists. The e2e creates its own fixtures, so it doesn't depend on that data.\n5. **Student tabs are never rendered.** `studentTabs` is not rendered by any page; it is an extension point only. The Attendance entry is registered, but the student pages have no tab bar to show it. Not in this ticket's scope.\n6. **Unrelated server on :3000.** A stale `next dev` from 2026-10-27 is running on :3000. I did not touch it. All runs used :3100.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":96,"newStart":1,"newLines":86,"lines":["-# Dev Log — SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure)","+# Dev Log — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)"," ","-## Iteration (continuation run, 2026-11-04)","+> The previous content of this file was a stale SH-4 log. Per the dev-planning note","+> (\"Stale SH-1 artifacts under artifacts/dev/ must be regenerated, not reused\") it was","+> replaced. This is SH-7's first dev iteration."," ","-Earlier iterations left no source files and no dev-log, so this run started from TASK-1.","-Every artifact uses ticketId `SH-4`, the id on all upstream artifacts. The prompt also said \"UNKNOWN\".","+## Iteration 1 (2026-11-06)"," ","-### Progress so far","-- Generated the migration with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` (equivalent to `migrate dev --create-only`, with no shadow DB). It is additive only: EmailStatus enum, 3 tables, 2 indexes, 2 FKs. Applied to the local dev DB with `migrate deploy`.","-- `react.cache` is undefined outside Next, so the email/notify code does not import `services/settings.ts`. `render.ts` exports `getEmailSchool()`, which reads the singleton directly.","-- The dispatcher's raw SQL uses `now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC'` because the columns are `timestamp(3)` without a time zone and hold UTC.","-- Pre-existing `tsc` errors (MUI v9 system props in Enrollment/SectionDetail clients, and users.ts:189-199) are outside this ticket. They are not touched.","+All 19 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 36 owned files exist."," "," ### Checklist","-- TASK-1: Notifications/email migration — ✓ complete","-- TASK-2: Notification type registry — ✓ complete","-- TASK-3: Shared notification validators — ✓ complete","-- TASK-4: Email templates + render — ✓ complete","-- TASK-5: Backoff + transport — ✓ complete","-- TASK-6: Outbox + auth email seam + INVITE_TTL — ✓ complete","-- TASK-7: Preferences + notify service — ✓ complete","-- TASK-8: Dispatcher + purge — ✓ complete","-- TASK-9: User notification service + 5 routes — ✓ complete","-- TASK-10: Preferences API route — ✓ complete","-- TASK-11: Admin email service + admin routes — ✓ complete","-- TASK-12: Internal dispatch route + '/api/internal/' public path — ✓ complete","-- TASK-13: Email worker script — ✓ complete","+- TASK-1: Prisma schema + attendance migration (CHECK + 2 partial unique indexes) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-2: Zod validators (src/lib/validators/attendance.ts) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-3: 4 attendance notification types — ✓ complete","+- TASK-4: Settings input + PATCH /api/settings/school — ✓ complete","+- TASK-5: Pure rules module + unit tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-6: getSchoolScheduleForDate in the timetable service — ✓ complete","+- TASK-7: Attendance service — ✓ complete","+- TASK-8: Integration tests (attendance-service) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-9: Teacher API routes (today, register GET/PUT) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-10: Student/course attendance API routes — ✓ complete","+- TASK-11: Admin API routes (overview, report+CSV, below-threshold, remind) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-12: RegisterForm client component — ✓ complete","+- TASK-13: Take pages + DateNav — ✓ complete","+- TASK-14: Student Attendance tab — ✓ complete","+- TASK-15: Course Attendance tab (matrix) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-16: Admin attendance page (Today / Report / Below threshold / Settings) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-17: Tab + navigation config entries — ✓ complete","+- TASK-18: Seed attendance (mulberry32, idempotent) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-19: Playwright e2e at 375×667 — ✓ complete (file written and run; see verification for which assertions were proven)"," ","-Verification for TASK-1 to TASK-13: a tsx smoke script (in /tmp, not committed) ran against the dev DB with a temporary user, which was deleted afterwards. It checked the following:","-- notify() dedupes ids and drops `//evil.com`.","-- The rendered HTML escapes `<b>`.","-- sendAuthEmail enqueues the invite with \"expires on November 11, 2026\".","-- dispatchEmails returned `{sent:2}` and both rows ended SENT.","-- `scripts/worker-email.ts` starts and stops cleanly on SIGTERM.","+### Implementation notes","+- **Migration (TASK-1).** Generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel`, the equivalent of `--create-only` with no shadow DB. The diff is additive only. The CHECK constraint and the two partial unique indexes were then appended by hand. Applied to the local DB with `migrate deploy`.","+- **Service, outside Next (TASK-7).** The service does not import `services/settings.ts`, because its `react.cache` is undefined outside Next (the same pattern as the timetable service). It reads the settings row directly instead.","+- **Service, saving a register.** `saveRegister` runs one interactive transaction:","+  - It checks the active-on-date roster (`invalidStudentIds`) and requires the full roster (`missingStudentIds`).","+  - It does find-or-create of the session, then the diff writes.","+  - A P2002 error aborts a Postgres transaction, so a re-read inside the same transaction is impossible. The P2002 race (ADR-3) is therefore handled by re-running the transaction once; the retry's `findFirst` sees the winning session.","+  - Audit and notifications run after commit.","+- **Service, enrollment dates.** Enrollment dates for the active-on-date rule are compared at the start of the next day in the school timezone (`fromZonedTime`).","+- **`getToday` date parameter.** `getToday` takes an optional `date` so the landing page's DatePicker works. `/api/attendance/today` still uses today, matching the contract.","+- **Report and below-threshold pagination.** Both group the rows in SQL (`groupBy`), then paginate in memory. This is marked with a `ponytail:` comment; its ceiling is the student count.","+- **Tooltip accessibility.** The calendar day Tooltip uses `describeChild`. Without it, MUI sets the tooltip text as the day button's aria-label, which hides the day number from assistive tech.","+- **NFR-6.** Before the UI work (TASK-12 to TASK-16), mui-mcp was reached:","+  - `useMuiDocs` for `@mui/material@9.5.0` and `@mui/x-date-pickers`.","+  - `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup, ToggleButton, Tabs and DateCalendar (the custom `day` slot).","+  - The v9 upgrade guide was also read.","+  - The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props, `slotProps.htmlInput`/`inputLabel`, `Tab` only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.","+- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).","+  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.","+  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.","+  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%."," ","-Fix found while testing: the templates now `import * as React`, because tsx and vitest use the classic JSX runtime (tsconfig `jsx: preserve`). Next was unaffected.","-- TASK-14: NotificationBell + shell wiring — ✓ complete","-- TASK-15: /notifications page + NotificationsList — ✓ complete","-- TASK-16: /account/notifications page + PreferencesTable — ✓ complete","-- TASK-17: /admin/email-log page + EmailLogTable — ✓ complete","+### Verification","+- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.","+- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:","+  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.","+  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.","+  - Rate, day colour and validators.","+- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:","+  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).","+  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.","+  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.","+  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.","+  - Homeroom-only daily register.","+  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.","+  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.","+- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:","+  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).","+  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.","+- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:","+  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".","+  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.","+  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2)."," ","-UI notes (NFR-10):","-- Before writing any UI, I called mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0), then `fetchDocs` for the v9 upgrade guide and the Badge, Popover, Tabs, Pagination, Switch and Chip APIs.","-- The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props (styles go in `sx`), and `slotProps.primary` for ListItemText, `slotProps.paper` for Popover and `slotProps.input` for Switch.","-- The admin email log reuses the shared DataTable as planned. DataTable's built-in search box writes `?q=`, which the email-log API ignores, so search has no effect there. Making it work would need a DataTable or API change outside this ticket's scope.","-- shell.tsx still has two lint errors (`Avatar` and `theme` unused). They were already there before this change and are not touched.","-- TASK-18: Seed demo notifications — ✓ complete","-- TASK-19: Unit tests (notifications) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-20: Integration tests (dispatch) + vitest include — ✓ complete","-","-Verification for TASK-18 to TASK-20:","-- Seed:","-  - With the users missing, it logs a skip for each email.","-  - With temporary student@ and parent@ users, two seed runs leave exactly 3 rows each (1 read). The temporary users were removed afterwards.","-- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: 28 tests pass.","-- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`:","-  - With `TEST_DATABASE_URL` pointing at the local DB, all 3 tests pass: concurrent dispatch sends each row once, a row stuck in SENDING for 11 minutes goes back to PENDING with attempts unchanged, and a freshly claimed SENDING row is left alone.","-  - Without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`, the tests are skipped.","-- Full `vitest run`: 112 tests pass. Three files fail, and none of them import code changed in this ticket:","-  - `lockout.test.ts`: next-auth cannot resolve `next/server` under vitest.","-  - `DataTable.test.tsx`: the `@mui/x-internals` exports map.","-  - `useToast.test.tsx`: the auto-hide timer test.","-- TASK-21: Playwright e2e (bell + preferences) — ✓ complete","-","-### HTTP verification (next dev on :3100, temporary admin, all data removed afterwards)","-- Without a session, `/api/notifications/unread-count` returns 401. Credentials sign-in works.","-- Notification flow:","-  - The admin test button returns `{ok:true}` and the unread count goes from 0 to 1.","-  - The list `category=SYSTEM` filter returns the row; ACADEMIC returns nothing; a bad category returns 400.","-  - read/unread toggles the count. Another user's id returns 404. read-all returns `{count:1}`, then the count is 0.","-- Preferences:","-  - GET returns only `system.test`; the emailOnly types are hidden.","-  - PUT persists the change.","-  - PUT returns VALIDATION_ERROR for `account.invite`, for `__proto__`, and for an extra key.","-- Email log:","-  - The `status` filter works and the response has no html or text.","-  - Retry on a non-FAILED row returns 404; retry on a FAILED row resets it to PENDING.","-- Dispatch:","-  - No token or a wrong token returns 401.","-  - The correct bearer token returns `{sent:1}`.","-- Pages:","-  - `/notifications` and `/account/notifications` render (200).","-  - The SSR markup has `role=\"switch\"` with the label \"Test notification email\" and the bell's \"Notifications\" label, matching the e2e selectors.","-","-### Blockers / notes for QA","-1. **Pre-existing dependency mismatch breaks every DataGrid page.**","-   - Cause: `package-lock.json` resolves `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0` against `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0`, so `./useFirstRender` is not exported.","-   - Effect: `/admin/email-log` (TASK-17) returns 500, and so does the existing `/admin/sections`. It is also why `DataTable.test.tsx` fails.","-   - Not fixed here, because the plan keeps `package.json` untouched.","-   - Fix: align the MUI X versions (for example, install `@mui/x-internals` at the version matching data-grid 9.5.0). After that, the first e2e test can pass, since it starts on `/admin/email-log`.","-2. **The e2e spec was not executed.**","-   - Cause: `@playwright/test@1.47.2` needs chromium revision 1248, but only 1200 is installed locally.","-   - It is listed by `playwright test --list` and its flow was exercised over HTTP as described above.","-   - To run it: `npx playwright install chromium`, then `npm run test:e2e`.","-3. The integration tests need `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. They pass against the local DB on :5433.","-4. The worker and cron route require env to be loaded. tsx does not read `.env` for `env.ts`. The worker happened to work locally because PrismaClient loads `.env` first. In production, set the variables in the process environment.","+### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)","+1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.","+2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:","+   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.","+   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.","+   - I tried `x-internals@9.14.0` (`--no-save`). That only moves the error to `@mui/x-virtualizer` 9.0.0-alpha.8, which wants `isFirefox` from `x-internals/platform`.","+   - I restored 9.15.0; `package-lock.json` is unchanged. A proper fix is to align the MUI X versions in package.json/lockfile, which is a dependency change outside this ticket.","+3. **vitest config.** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve, so `npm test` fails to start. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (same config, `vitest/config`) works.","+4. **No 7A/7B data.** There is no seed or dev data for sections, courses or the timetable, so the attendance seed is a no-op on this DB until PRD-05/06 data exists. The e2e creates its own fixtures, so it doesn't depend on that data.","+5. **Student tabs are never rendered.** `studentTabs` is not rendered by any page; it is an extension point only. The Attendance entry is registered, but the student pages have no tab bar to show it. Not in this ticket's scope.","+6. **Unrelated server on :3000.** A stale `next dev` from 2026-10-27 is running on :3000. I did not touch it. All runs used :3100."]}],"originalFile":"# Dev Log — SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure)\n\n## Iteration (continuation run, 2026-11-04)\n\nEarlier iterations left no source files and no dev-log, so this run started from TASK-1.\nEvery artifact uses ticketId `SH-4`, the id on all upstream artifacts. The prompt also said \"UNKNOWN\".\n\n### Progress so far\n- Generated the migration with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` (equivalent to `migrate dev --create-only`, with no shadow DB). It is additive only: EmailStatus enum, 3 tables, 2 indexes, 2 FKs. Applied to the local dev DB with `migrate deploy`.\n- `react.cache` is undefined outside Next, so the email/notify code does not import `services/settings.ts`. `render.ts` exports `getEmailSchool()`, which reads the singleton directly.\n- The dispatcher's raw SQL uses `now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC'` because the columns are `timestamp(3)` without a time zone and hold UTC.\n- Pre-existing `tsc` errors (MUI v9 system props in Enrollment/SectionDetail clients, and users.ts:189-199) are outside this ticket. They are not touched.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Notifications/email migration — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Notification type registry — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: Shared notification validators — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Email templates + render — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Backoff + transport — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: Outbox + auth email seam + INVITE_TTL — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: Preferences + notify service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: Dispatcher + purge — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: User notification service + 5 routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: Preferences API route — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Admin email service + admin routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: Internal dispatch route + '/api/internal/' public path — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Email worker script — ✓ complete\n\nVerification for TASK-1 to TASK-13: a tsx smoke script (in /tmp, not committed) ran against the dev DB with a temporary user, which was deleted afterwards. It checked the following:\n- notify() dedupes ids and drops `//evil.com`.\n- The rendered HTML escapes `<b>`.\n- sendAuthEmail enqueues the invite with \"expires on November 11, 2026\".\n- dispatchEmails returned `{sent:2}` and both rows ended SENT.\n- `scripts/worker-email.ts` starts and stops cleanly on SIGTERM.\n\nFix found while testing: the templates now `import * as React`, because tsx and vitest use the classic JSX runtime (tsconfig `jsx: preserve`). Next was unaffected.\n- TASK-14: NotificationBell + shell wiring — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: /notifications page + NotificationsList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: /account/notifications page + PreferencesTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: /admin/email-log page + EmailLogTable — ✓ complete\n\nUI notes (NFR-10):\n- Before writing any UI, I called mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0), then `fetchDocs` for the v9 upgrade guide and the Badge, Popover, Tabs, Pagination, Switch and Chip APIs.\n- The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props (styles go in `sx`), and `slotProps.primary` for ListItemText, `slotProps.paper` for Popover and `slotProps.input` for Switch.\n- The admin email log reuses the shared DataTable as planned. DataTable's built-in search box writes `?q=`, which the email-log API ignores, so search has no effect there. Making it work would need a DataTable or API change outside this ticket's scope.\n- shell.tsx still has two lint errors (`Avatar` and `theme` unused). They were already there before this change and are not touched.\n- TASK-18: Seed demo notifications — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Unit tests (notifications) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Integration tests (dispatch) + vitest include — ✓ complete\n\nVerification for TASK-18 to TASK-20:\n- Seed:\n  - With the users missing, it logs a skip for each email.\n  - With temporary student@ and parent@ users, two seed runs leave exactly 3 rows each (1 read). The temporary users were removed afterwards.\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: 28 tests pass.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`:\n  - With `TEST_DATABASE_URL` pointing at the local DB, all 3 tests pass: concurrent dispatch sends each row once, a row stuck in SENDING for 11 minutes goes back to PENDING with attempts unchanged, and a freshly claimed SENDING row is left alone.\n  - Without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`, the tests are skipped.\n- Full `vitest run`: 112 tests pass. Three files fail, and none of them import code changed in this ticket:\n  - `lockout.test.ts`: next-auth cannot resolve `next/server` under vitest.\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx`: the `@mui/x-internals` exports map.\n  - `useToast.test.tsx`: the auto-hide timer test.\n- TASK-21: Playwright e2e (bell + preferences) — ✓ complete\n\n### HTTP verification (next dev on :3100, temporary admin, all data removed afterwards)\n- Without a session, `/api/notifications/unread-count` returns 401. Credentials sign-in works.\n- Notification flow:\n  - The admin test button returns `{ok:true}` and the unread count goes from 0 to 1.\n  - The list `category=SYSTEM` filter returns the row; ACADEMIC returns nothing; a bad category returns 400.\n  - read/unread toggles the count. Another user's id returns 404. read-all returns `{count:1}`, then the count is 0.\n- Preferences:\n  - GET returns only `system.test`; the emailOnly types are hidden.\n  - PUT persists the change.\n  - PUT returns VALIDATION_ERROR for `account.invite`, for `__proto__`, and for an extra key.\n- Email log:\n  - The `status` filter works and the response has no html or text.\n  - Retry on a non-FAILED row returns 404; retry on a FAILED row resets it to PENDING.\n- Dispatch:\n  - No token or a wrong token returns 401.\n  - The correct bearer token returns `{sent:1}`.\n- Pages:\n  - `/notifications` and `/account/notifications` render (200).\n  - The SSR markup has `role=\"switch\"` with the label \"Test notification email\" and the bell's \"Notifications\" label, matching the e2e selectors.\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA\n1. **Pre-existing dependency mismatch breaks every DataGrid page.**\n   - Cause: `package-lock.json` resolves `@mui/x-internals@9.15.0` against `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0`, so `./useFirstRender` is not exported.\n   - Effect: `/admin/email-log` (TASK-17) returns 500, and so does the existing `/admin/sections`. It is also why `DataTable.test.tsx` fails.\n   - Not fixed here, because the plan keeps `package.json` untouched.\n   - Fix: align the MUI X versions (for example, install `@mui/x-internals` at the version matching data-grid 9.5.0). After that, the first e2e test can pass, since it starts on `/admin/email-log`.\n2. **The e2e spec was not executed.**\n   - Cause: `@playwright/test@1.47.2` needs chromium revision 1248, but only 1200 is installed locally.\n   - It is listed by `playwright test --list` and its flow was exercised over HTTP as described above.\n   - To run it: `npx playwright install chromium`, then `npm run test:e2e`.\n3. The integration tests need `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. They pass against the local DB on :5433.\n4. The worker and cron route require env to be loaded. tsx does not read `.env` for `env.ts`. The worker happened to work locally because PrismaClient loads `.env` first. In production, set the variables in the process environment.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016k4N9pvu9WFPVDW7cbtjKZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
