{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C3CxTNgQ55zqPMdVHFCkq9","type":"tool_result","content":"FR-1 | Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId→User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration. | \nFR-2 | Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/. | \nFR-3 | POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null. | \nFR-4 | Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.' | \nFR-5 | Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.' | \nFR-6 | Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected. | \nFR-7 | Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName. | \nFR-8 | GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1. | \nFR-9 | Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes. | \nFR-10 | Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users). | \nFR-11 | DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes. | \nFR-12 | purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run. | \nFR-13 | Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button. | \nFR-14 | Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id. | \nFR-15 | Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress. | \nFR-16 | Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title ≤120, lesson title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1–600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only. | \nFR-17 | Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached. | \nFR-18 | Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job. | \nFR-19 | TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green. | \nFR-20 | Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check. | \nFR-21 | Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson. | \nFR-22 | Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module. | \nFR-23 | Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }. | \nFR-24 | Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog. | \nFR-25 | Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image. | \nFR-26 | Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing. | \nFR-27 | The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays. | \nFR-28 | Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future. | \nFR-29 | Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved. | \nFR-30 | Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute. | \nFR-31 | Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'. | \nFR-32 | Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller. | \nFR-33 | For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this. | \nFR-34 | Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage). | \nFR-35 | Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent). | \nFR-36 | Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button. | \nFR-37 | Parents can view a course's Content tab only when a linked student is ACTIVE-enrolled. The existing assertCanViewCourse already enforces this (verified in src/server/auth/course-access.ts PARENT branch), so reuse it as is. | \nFR-38 | Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students. | \nFR-39 | Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.' | \nFR-40 | Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl. | \nFR-41 | SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'. | \nFR-42 | /admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists. | \nFR-43 | Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table. | \nFR-44 | GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules. | \nFR-45 | Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON). | \nFR-46 | Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit(). | \nFR-47 | Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules × 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons. | \nFR-48 | Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload → attach → download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it. | \nNFR-1 | Stored files are never served from a static path, and every download goes through the access registry. | \nNFR-2 | Markdown output is sanitised (rehype-sanitize) and javascript: URLs are stripped, so no script executes from lesson content. | \nNFR-3 | POST /api/files is rate limited to 60 uploads per user per hour (RATE_LIMITED 429), reusing rateLimit() from src/server/rate-limit.ts. | \nNFR-4 | The Content tab for a course with 20 modules × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms. This means no N+1 queries: modules, lessons, attachment counts and progress are loaded in a bounded number of queries. | \nNFR-5 | Uploads stream to disk and the sha256 is computed while streaming, without buffering whole files in memory. The size limit is enforced during the stream. | \nNFR-6 | Accessibility: embedded video iframes have a title, the editor warns when an image has no alt text, and drag reordering has keyboard up/down IconButton alternatives. | \nNFR-7 | UI component rule: only @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the listed MUI X packages are used. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for the installed 9.5.0) before use. Banned libraries are never imported, and Markdown elements map to MUI via the components prop. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented. | \nNFR-8 | Every content and file handler and every server page enforces access server-side (assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent/access registry). Hiding a button is never the only protection. | \nNFR-9 | Brownfield constraint: do not re-scaffold, rename existing routes/models or duplicate helpers. Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. New dependencies are limited to the PRD-allowed set (file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable). | \nNFR-10 | Dates (publishAt, progress dates, 'Saved' indicator) are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The schedule picker interprets input in the school timezone. | \nNFR-11 | Out of scope: S3/cloud storage (the storage module has a single local-disk implementation), SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses. | \nNFR-12 | No console.log in committed code. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. .env.example documents UPLOAD_DIR and MAX_UPLOAD_MB. | \nNone | None |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34574e28-0591-42df-96fb-64403ec6dad4","uuid":"ffd36a5f-a089-4f45-baf0-2d7a0561c2e3","timestamp":"2026-11-06T21:32:26.615Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FR-1 | Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId→User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration. | \nFR-2 | Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/. | \nFR-3 | POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null. | \nFR-4 | Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.' | \nFR-5 | Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.' | \nFR-6 | Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected. | \nFR-7 | Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName. | \nFR-8 | GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1. | \nFR-9 | Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes. | \nFR-10 | Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users). | \nFR-11 | DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes. | \nFR-12 | purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run. | \nFR-13 | Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button. | \nFR-14 | Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id. | \nFR-15 | Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress. | \nFR-16 | Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title ≤120, lesson title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1–600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only. | \nFR-17 | Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached. | \nFR-18 | Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job. | \nFR-19 | TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green. | \nFR-20 | Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check. | \nFR-21 | Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson. | \nFR-22 | Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module. | \nFR-23 | Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }. | \nFR-24 | Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog. | \nFR-25 | Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image. | \nFR-26 | Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing. | \nFR-27 | The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays. | \nFR-28 | Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future. | \nFR-29 | Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved. | \nFR-30 | Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute. | \nFR-31 | Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'. | \nFR-32 | Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller. | \nFR-33 | For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this. | \nFR-34 | Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage). | \nFR-35 | Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent). | \nFR-36 | Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button. | \nFR-37 | Parents can view a course's Content tab only when a linked student is ACTIVE-enrolled. The existing assertCanViewCourse already enforces this (verified in src/server/auth/course-access.ts PARENT branch), so reuse it as is. | \nFR-38 | Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students. | \nFR-39 | Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.' | \nFR-40 | Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl. | \nFR-41 | SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'. | \nFR-42 | /admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists. | \nFR-43 | Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table. | \nFR-44 | GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules. | \nFR-45 | Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON). | \nFR-46 | Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit(). | \nFR-47 | Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules × 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons. | \nFR-48 | Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload → attach → download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it. | \nNFR-1 | Stored files are never served from a static path, and every download goes through the access registry. | \nNFR-2 | Markdown output is sanitised (rehype-sanitize) and javascript: URLs are stripped, so no script executes from lesson content. | \nNFR-3 | POST /api/files is rate limited to 60 uploads per user per hour (RATE_LIMITED 429), reusing rateLimit() from src/server/rate-limit.ts. | \nNFR-4 | The Content tab for a course with 20 modules × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms. This means no N+1 queries: modules, lessons, attachment counts and progress are loaded in a bounded number of queries. | \nNFR-5 | Uploads stream to disk and the sha256 is computed while streaming, without buffering whole files in memory. The size limit is enforced during the stream. | \nNFR-6 | Accessibility: embedded video iframes have a title, the editor warns when an image has no alt text, and drag reordering has keyboard up/down IconButton alternatives. | \nNFR-7 | UI component rule: only @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the listed MUI X packages are used. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for the installed 9.5.0) before use. Banned libraries are never imported, and Markdown elements map to MUI via the components prop. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented. | \nNFR-8 | Every content and file handler and every server page enforces access server-side (assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent/access registry). Hiding a button is never the only protection. | \nNFR-9 | Brownfield constraint: do not re-scaffold, rename existing routes/models or duplicate helpers. Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. New dependencies are limited to the PRD-allowed set (file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable). | \nNFR-10 | Dates (publishAt, progress dates, 'Saved' indicator) are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The schedule picker interprets input in the school timezone. | \nNFR-11 | Out of scope: S3/cloud storage (the storage module has a single local-disk implementation), SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses. | \nNFR-12 | No console.log in committed code. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. .env.example documents UPLOAD_DIR and MAX_UPLOAD_MB. | \nNone | None |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01C3CxTNgQ55zqPMdVHFCkq9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
