{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BbWNzaCKYmRf5dnJjzncm3","type":"tool_result","content":"95:```prisma\n96-model FileObject {\n97-  id            String   @id @default(cuid())\n98-  ownerId       String                     // uploader\n99-  owner         User     @relation(fields: [ownerId], references: [id])\n100-  originalName  String                     // sanitised\n101-  mimeType      String\n102-  sizeBytes     Int\n103-  storageKey    String   @unique           // \"<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>\"\n104-  sha256        String\n105-  context       String                     // \"lesson\", \"assignment\", \"submission\", \"message\", \"logo\", \"admission\"…\n106-  contextId     String?                    // id of the owning record once attached\n107-  createdAt     DateTime @default(now())\n108-  @@index([context, contextId])\n109-}\n110-```\n111-\n112-1. `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile(stream, meta)`, `readFile(storageKey)`, `deleteFile(storageKey)`. Files are written to `UPLOAD_DIR` (new env var, default `./uploads`, git-ignored), never inside `public/`.\n113-2. `POST /api/files` (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus `context`. Limits: 25 MB per file (`MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env, default 25); allowed types by extension **and** magic-number sniffing (`file-type` package): pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4, zip. Rejections return `VALIDATION_ERROR` \"File type .exe is not allowed.\" or \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"\n114-3. Filenames are sanitised (strip path separators and control characters, max 150 characters).\n115-4. `GET /api/files/:id` streams the file with `Content-Disposition: attachment` (inline for images and PDFs when `?inline=1`), `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and the stored MIME type. Access is decided by a resolver registry `src/server/files/access.ts`: `registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>)`. This PRD registers `lesson` (can view the lesson), `logo` (public). Unknown context → only the owner and admins. Later PRDs register their contexts.\n116-5. Unattached files (`contextId` null) older than 24 hours are deleted by `purgeOrphanFiles()`, called from the daily maintenance run started in PRD-04's dispatcher.\n117-6. A reusable `FileUpload` component built from MUI (`Paper` drop zone with dashed border, `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden file input as shown in the MUI MCP \"Button\" file-upload demo, `LinearProgress` per file, `List` of files): drag-and-drop zone + button, multiple files, per-file progress bar (XHR upload progress), remove button, displays name, size and type icon. A `FileList` component shows attached files with download links.\n118-\n119-### FR-2 Content data model\n120-\n121:```prisma\n122-enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }\n123-\n124-model Module {\n125-  id          String        @id @default(cuid())\n126-  courseId    String\n127-  course      Course        @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n128-  title       String                       // max 120\n129-  description String?\n130-  order       Int\n131-  status      ContentStatus @default(DRAFT)\n132-  publishAt   DateTime?\n133-  createdAt   DateTime      @default(now())\n134-  updatedAt   DateTime      @updatedAt\n135-  lessons     Lesson[]\n136-}\n137-\n138-model Lesson {\n139-  id              String        @id @default(cuid())\n140-  moduleId        String\n141-  module          Module        @relation(fields: [moduleId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n142-  title           String                    // max 150\n143-  contentMarkdown String        @default(\"\") // max 100,000 chars\n144-  videoUrl        String?                   // YouTube or Vimeo only\n145-  estimatedMinutes Int?                     // 1–600\n146-  order           Int\n147-  status          ContentStatus @default(DRAFT)\n148-  publishAt       DateTime?\n149-  createdAt       DateTime      @default(now())\n150-  updatedAt       DateTime      @updatedAt\n151-  attachments     LessonAttachment[]\n152-  links           LessonLink[]\n153-  progress        LessonProgress[]\n154-}\n155-\n156-model LessonAttachment {\n157-  id        String     @id @default(cuid())\n158-  lessonId  String\n159-  lesson    Lesson     @relation(fields: [lessonId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n160-  fileId    String\n161-  file      FileObject @relation(fields: [fileId], references: [id])\n162-  order     Int\n163-}\n164-\n165-model LessonLink {\n166-  id        String @id @default(cuid())\n167-  lessonId  String\n168-  lesson    Lesson @relation(fields: [lessonId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n169-  title     String\n170-  url       String                          // http(s) only\n171-  order     Int\n172-}\n173-\n174-model LessonProgress {\n175-  lessonId     String\n176-  lesson       Lesson   @relation(fields: [lessonId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n177-  studentId    String\n178-  firstViewedAt DateTime @default(now())\n179-  completedAt  DateTime?\n180-  @@id([lessonId, studentId])\n181-}\n182-```\n183-\n184-### FR-3 Visibility rules\n185-1. A lesson is visible to students and parents when the lesson **and** its module are `PUBLISHED`, or `SCHEDULED` with `publishAt <= now` (evaluated at read time — no job needed).\n186-2. Teachers and admins see everything, with a status badge (Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green).\n187-\n188-### FR-4 Content tab (course page)\n189-1. Register course tab \"Content\" (all roles that can view the course). Shows modules as collapsible MUI `Accordion` sections in order, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and (for students) a completion check.\n190-2. Students see a per-module progress bar (\"3 of 5 complete\") and a course-level progress bar plus a \"Continue\" button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson.\n191-3. Teacher controls: