rt, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus `context`. Limits: 25 MB per file (`MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env, default 25); allowed types by extension **and** magic-number sniffing (`file-type` package): pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4, zip. Rejections return `VALIDATION_ERROR` \"File type .exe is not allowed.\" or \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"\n114-3. Filenames are sanitised (strip path separators and control characters, max 150 characters).\n115-4. `GET /api/files/:id` streams the file with `Content-Disposition: attachment` (inline for images and PDFs when `?inline=1`), `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and the stored MIME type. Access is decided by a resolver registry `src/server/files/access.ts`: `registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>)`. This PRD registers `lesson` (can view the lesson), `logo` (public). Unknown context → only the owner and admins. Later PRDs register their contexts.\n116-5. Unattached files (`contextId` null) older than 24 hours are deleted by `purgeOrphanFiles()`, called from the daily maintenance run started in PRD-04's dispatcher.\n117-6. A reusable `FileUpload` component built from MUI (`Paper` drop zone with dashed border, `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden file input as shown in the MUI MCP \"Button\" file-upload demo, `LinearProgress` per file, `List` of files): drag-and-drop zone + button, multiple files, per-file progress bar (XHR upload progress), remove button, displays name, size and type icon. A `FileList` component shows attached files with download links.\n118-\n119-### FR-2 Content data model\n120-\n121:```prisma\n122-enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }\n123-\n124-model Module {\n125-  id          String        @id @default(cuid())\n126-  courseId    String\n127-  course      Course        @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n128-  title       String                       // max 120\n129-  descriptio