only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.\n- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).\n  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.\n  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.\n  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%.\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:\n  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.\n  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.\n  - Rate, day colour and validators.\n- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:\n  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).\n  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.\n  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.\n  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.\n  - Homeroom-only daily register.\n  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.\n  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.\n- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).\n  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.\n- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:\n  - **Teacher test passes.** It