{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DXYVj74ukdZBRzR5jw9ZLL","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (33.1KB). Full output saved to: /Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub/1ed4e388-5ff3-479e-ba38-660b1be74fc5/tool-results/bvpyo3xn9.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n     281 artifacts/architect/system-design.md\n      97 artifacts/dev-planning/file-structure.md\n     317 artifacts/dev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json\n     695 total\n# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ed4e388-5ff3-479e-ba38-660b1be74fc5","uuid":"0ca9bc46-2d6b-4048-b557-c28b4d523af4","timestamp":"2026-11-06T23:54:52.144Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     281 artifacts/architect/system-design.md\n      97 artifacts/dev-planning/file-structure.md\n     317 artifacts/dev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json\n     695 total\n# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\n| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |\n| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |\n\n### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |\n| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |\n| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |\n| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |\n| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |\n| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |\n\n### 1.3 Schema note\n\nThe PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)\n\n- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.\n- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.\n- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.\n- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey.\n\n### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |\n| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |\n\n**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory.\n\n**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`.\n\n### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |\n| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |\n| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |\n\n`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):\n\n- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.\n- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).\n- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.\n- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.\n- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.\n- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).\n- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).\n- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).\n- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).\n- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).\n- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).\n- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).\n- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46).\n\n### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)\n\n| Existing | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |\n| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |\n| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |\n| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |\n| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |\n| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |\n| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |\n| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |\n| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |\n| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |\n| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |\n\n### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)\n\n| File | Methods | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |\n| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |\n\nThat is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)\n\n| File | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |\n| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |\n| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |\n| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |\n\n### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits\n\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).\n- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).\n- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).\n- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.\n- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).\n- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)\n```\nFileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy\n   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)\n   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}\nLessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse\n   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach\nViewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile\n   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)\n   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN\n   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)\n```\n\n### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)\n```\nrequest ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?\n   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now\n```\nNo job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39).\n\n### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)\n`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`.\n\n### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)\nViewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course.\n\n### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)\ndnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast.\n\n### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)\nThe email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos.\n\n### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)\nThe admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)\n\n- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.\n- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).\n- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).\n- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.\n- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.\n- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.\n- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts.\n\n## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)\n\n- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).\n- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.\n- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.\n- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub/1ed4e388-5ff3-479e-ba38-660b1be74fc5/tool-results/bvpyo3xn9.txt","persistedOutputSize":33849},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DXYVj74ukdZBRzR5jw9ZLL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnaRMFwGjnDFAQueKJzJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015p77dsq9NRP2Dzj8QWJCkB","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub/1ed4e388-5ff3-479e-ba38-660b1be74fc5/tool-results/bvpyo3xn9.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1200,"cache_read_input_tokens":49193,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1200},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ed4e388-5ff3-479e-ba38-660b1be74fc5","uuid":"19d06b00-6c2b-41b7-b97d-efbb7eb0af9a","timestamp":"2026-11-06T23:54:55.158Z","request_id":"req_011CgnaRM3nVHHuHjCP2XwXD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015p77dsq9NRP2Dzj8QWJCkB":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub/1ed4e388-5ff3-479e-ba38-660b1be74fc5/tool-results/bvpyo3xn9.txt"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015p77dsq9NRP2Dzj8QWJCkB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t     281 artifacts/architect/system-design.md\n2\t      97 artifacts/dev-planning/file-structure.md\n3\t     317 artifacts/dev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json\n4\t     695 total\n5\t# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n6\t\n7\tTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\n8\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n9\t`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n10\t\n11\t> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n12\t\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t## 1. Overview\n16\t\n17\tSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\n18\tSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n19\t\n20\t1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n21\t2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n22\t\n23\tThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n24\t\n25\t### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n26\t\n27\t| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n28\t|---|---|---|\n29\t| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n30\t| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n31\t| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n32\t| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n33\t| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n34\t| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\n35\t| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |\n36\t| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |\n37\t\n38\t### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)\n39\t\n40\t| # | Decision |\n41\t|---|---|\n42\t| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n43\t| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |\n44\t| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |\n45\t| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |\n46\t| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |\n47\t| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |\n48\t| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |\n49\t\n50\t### 1.3 Schema note\n51\t\n52\tThe PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students.\n53\t\n54\t---\n55\t\n56\t## 2. Component Breakdown\n57\t\n58\t### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)\n59\t\n60\t- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.\n61\t- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.\n62\t- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.\n63\t- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey.\n64\t\n65\t### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`\n66\t\n67\t| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n68\t|---|---|---|\n69\t| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n70\t| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |\n71\t| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |\n72\t| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |\n73\t| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |\n74\t| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |\n75\t| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |\n76\t\n77\t**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory.\n78\t\n79\t**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`.\n80\t\n81\t### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`\n82\t\n83\t| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n84\t|---|---|---|\n85\t| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |\n86\t| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |\n87\t| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |\n88\t| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |\n89\t\n90\t`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):\n91\t\n92\t- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.\n93\t- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).\n94\t- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.\n95\t- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.\n96\t- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.\n97\t- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).\n98\t- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).\n99\t- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).\n100\t- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).\n101\t- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).\n102\t- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).\n103\t- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).\n104\t- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46).\n105\t\n106\t### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)\n107\t\n108\t| Existing | Used for |\n109\t|---|---|\n110\t| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |\n111\t| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |\n112\t| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |\n113\t| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |\n114\t| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |\n115\t| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |\n116\t| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |\n117\t| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |\n118\t| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |\n119\t| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |\n120\t| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |\n121\t\n122\t### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)\n123\t\n124\t| File | Methods | Reqs |\n125\t|---|---|---|\n126\t| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |\n127\t| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n128\t| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |\n129\t| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |\n130\t| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |\n131\t| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |\n132\t| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |\n133\t| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |\n134\t| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |\n135\t\n136\tThat is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n137\t\n138\t### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)\n139\t\n140\t| File | Notes | Reqs |\n141\t|---|---|---|\n142\t| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n143\t| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |\n144\t| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |\n145\t| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |\n146\t| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |\n147\t| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |\n148\t| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |\n149\t| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |\n150\t| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |\n151\t| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |\n152\t\n153\t### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits\n154\t\n155\t- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).\n156\t- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).\n157\t- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).\n158\t- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.\n159\t- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).\n160\t- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12).\n161\t\n162\t---\n163\t\n164\t## 3. Data Flow\n165\t\n166\t### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)\n167\t```\n168\tFileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy\n169\t   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)\n170\t   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}\n171\tLessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse\n172\t   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach\n173\tViewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile\n174\t   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)\n175\t   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN\n176\t   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)\n177\t```\n178\t\n179\t### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)\n180\t```\n181\trequest ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?\n182\t   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now\n183\t```\n184\tNo job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39).\n185\t\n186\t### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)\n187\t`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`.\n188\t\n189\t### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)\n190\tViewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course.\n191\t\n192\t### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)\n193\tdnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast.\n194\t\n195\t### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)\n196\tThe email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos.\n197\t\n198\t### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)\n199\tThe admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver.\n200\t\n201\t---\n202\t\n203\t## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)\n204\t\n205\t- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.\n206\t- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).\n207\t- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).\n208\t- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.\n209\t- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.\n210\t- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.\n211\t- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts.\n212\t\n213\t## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)\n214\t\n215\t- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).\n216\t- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.\n217\t- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.\n218\t- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-7).\n219\t\n220\t---\n221\t\n222\t## 6. Requirements Traceability\n223\t\n224\t| Req | Design element |\n225\t|---|---|\n226\t| FR-1 | §2.1 `FileObject` model, migration `add_files_and_content` |\n227\t| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/server/storage.ts`, `env.ts` UPLOAD_DIR |\n228\t| FR-3 | §2.2 `files-service.uploadFile`, §2.5 `POST /api/files`, §3.1 |\n229\t| FR-4 | §2.2 `maxBytesFor`, busboy `fileSize` limit, Content-Length pre-check |\n230\t| FR-5 | §2.2 `validate.ts` ALLOWED table + `fileTypeFromBuffer` |\n231\t| FR-6 | §2.2 `checkType` sniff modes (none / zip-or-ooxml / required) |\n232\t| FR-7 | §2.2 `sanitizeFilename` |\n233\t| FR-8 | §2.2 download headers, §2.5 `GET /api/files/:id` |\n234\t| FR-9 | §2.2 `files/access.ts` registry + dispatch order |\n235\t| FR-10 | §2.2 `files/contexts.ts` lesson + logo resolvers |\n236\t| FR-11 | §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile`, §2.1 Restrict FK |\n237\t| FR-12 | §2.2 `files/purge.ts`, §2.7 dispatcher hook, §3.6 |\n238\t| FR-13 | §2.6 `FileUpload` |\n239\t| FR-14 | §2.6 `FileList` |\n240\t| FR-15 | §2.1 ContentStatus + Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress, §1.3 |\n241\t| FR-16 | §2.3 `validators/content.ts` |\n242\t| FR-17 | §2.2 `attachFiles` eligibility, §2.3 `updateLesson` |\n243\t| FR-18 | §2.3 `visibility.ts`, §3.2 |\n244\t| FR-19 | §2.3 `canSeeDrafts`, §2.6 `StatusChip` |\n245\t| FR-20 | §2.6 `content` course tab, §2.3 `listCourseContent` |\n246\t| FR-21 | §2.3 `listCourseContent` counts + `continueLessonId`, §2.6 progress bars |\n247\t| FR-22 | §2.3 `createModule`/`updateModule`/`createLesson`, §2.6 module Menu |\n248\t| FR-23 | §2.3 `reorderContent`, §2.6 dnd-kit, §3.5 |\n249\t| FR-24 | §2.4 ConfirmDialog `confirmText`, §2.3 `deleteModule` |\n250\t| FR-25 | §2.6 lesson editor page + Markdown editor |\n251\t| FR-26 | §2.6 image insert, §1.2 D3 inline-image attach |\n252\t| FR-27 | §2.6 attachments/links sections, §2.3 `updateLesson` replace-all |\n253\t| FR-28 | §2.6 Schedule DateTimePicker, §2.3 Zod future check |\n254\t| FR-29 | §2.6 autosave + unsaved-changes guard |\n255\t| FR-30 | §2.3 `src/lib/video.ts`, §2.6 `VideoEmbed`, §2.7 CSP frame-src |\n256\t| FR-31 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` |\n257\t| FR-32 | §2.6 lesson viewer, §2.3 `getLesson` prev/next |\n258\t| FR-33 | §2.3 `getLesson` first-view upsert + `setLessonProgress` |\n259\t| FR-34 | §2.3 `listLessonProgress`, §2.6 Progress Drawer |\n260\t| FR-35 | §2.3 `getStudentLearning`, §2.6 `learning` student tab |\n261\t| FR-36 | §2.3 `setLessonProgress` STUDENT-only, §2.6 viewer hides the button |\n262\t| FR-37 | §2.4 `assertCanViewCourse` reused unchanged |\n263\t| FR-38 | §2.3 `notifyLessonPublished`, §2.7 NOTIFICATION_TYPES, §3.3 |\n264\t| FR-39 | §3.2 no job, §2.6 Schedule tooltip |\n265\t| FR-40 | §2.6 admin settings logo FileUpload, §2.4 `updateSchoolSettings` + logoFileId, §3.7 |\n266\t| FR-41 | §2.2 SVG logo-only + CSP header, §1.2 D7 |\n267\t| FR-42 | §2.6 `/admin/settings/school` page + nav entry |\n268\t| FR-43 | §2.5 route table (15 endpoints), §2.3 service functions |\n269\t| FR-44 | §2.3 `getLesson` NOT_FOUND for hidden lessons |\n270\t| FR-45 | §2.3 `content-service.ts`, §2.2 `src/server/files/`, thin handlers §2.5 |\n271\t| FR-46 | §1.2 D6, §2.3 audit rule, §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile` audit |\n272\t| FR-47 | §2.1 seed + `prisma/seed-assets/` |\n273\t| FR-48 | §5 Testing Strategy |\n274\t| NFR-1 | §2.2 storage outside public + registry, §4 |\n275\t| NFR-2 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` sanitize + `a` mapper, §4 |\n276\t| NFR-3 | §2.2 upload pipeline `rateLimit` |\n277\t| NFR-4 | §2.3 2-query `listCourseContent`, §1.3 order indexes |\n278\t| NFR-5 | §2.2 busboy streaming + hash/count tap + tmp→rename |\n279\t| NFR-6 | §2.6 iframe title, alt-text Alert, up/down IconButtons |\n280\t| NFR-7 | §1.1 blocker 8, §2.6 MUI-only + mui-mcp lookup |\n281\t| NFR-8 | §2.3 per-function access checks, §1.2 D1, §4 |\n282\t| NFR-9 | §2.4 reuse table, ADR-1 deps, §5 gate |\n283\t| NFR-10 | §2.6 StatusChip/Schedule school timezone, `formatInSchoolTz`, `fromZonedTime` |\n284\t| NFR-11 | §1 single local-disk storage, no abstraction |\n285\t| NFR-12 | §2.2 `logger`, §2.7 `.env.example` |\n286\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ed4e388-5ff3-479e-ba38-660b1be74fc5","uuid":"5377086f-cf0d-4927-889f-e6a318e221bb","timestamp":"2026-11-06T23:54:55.506Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub/1ed4e388-5ff3-479e-ba38-660b1be74fc5/tool-results/bvpyo3xn9.txt","content":"     281 artifacts/architect/system-design.md\n      97 artifacts/dev-planning/file-structure.md\n     317 artifacts/dev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json\n     695 total\n# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\n| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |\n| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |\n\n### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |\n| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |\n| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |\n| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |\n| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |\n| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |\n\n### 1.3 Schema note\n\nThe PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)\n\n- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.\n- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.\n- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.\n- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey.\n\n### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |\n| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |\n\n**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory.\n\n**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`.\n\n### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |\n| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |\n| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |\n\n`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):\n\n- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.\n- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).\n- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.\n- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.\n- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.\n- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).\n- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).\n- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).\n- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).\n- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).\n- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).\n- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).\n- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46).\n\n### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)\n\n| Existing | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |\n| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |\n| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |\n| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |\n| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |\n| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |\n| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |\n| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |\n| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |\n| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |\n| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |\n\n### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)\n\n| File | Methods | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |\n| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |\n\nThat is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)\n\n| File | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |\n| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |\n| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |\n| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |\n\n### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits\n\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).\n- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).\n- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).\n- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.\n- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).\n- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)\n```\nFileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy\n   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)\n   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}\nLessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse\n   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach\nViewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile\n   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)\n   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN\n   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)\n```\n\n### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)\n```\nrequest ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?\n   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now\n```\nNo job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39).\n\n### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)\n`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`.\n\n### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)\nViewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course.\n\n### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)\ndnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast.\n\n### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)\nThe email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos.\n\n### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)\nThe admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)\n\n- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.\n- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).\n- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).\n- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.\n- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.\n- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.\n- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts.\n\n## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)\n\n- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).\n- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.\n- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.\n- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 `FileObject` model, migration `add_files_and_content` |\n| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/server/storage.ts`, `env.ts` UPLOAD_DIR |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `files-service.uploadFile`, §2.5 `POST /api/files`, §3.1 |\n| FR-4 | §2.2 `maxBytesFor`, busboy `fileSize` limit, Content-Length pre-check |\n| FR-5 | §2.2 `validate.ts` ALLOWED table + `fileTypeFromBuffer` |\n| FR-6 | §2.2 `checkType` sniff modes (none / zip-or-ooxml / required) |\n| FR-7 | §2.2 `sanitizeFilename` |\n| FR-8 | §2.2 download headers, §2.5 `GET /api/files/:id` |\n| FR-9 | §2.2 `files/access.ts` registry + dispatch order |\n| FR-10 | §2.2 `files/contexts.ts` lesson + logo resolvers |\n| FR-11 | §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile`, §2.1 Restrict FK |\n| FR-12 | §2.2 `files/purge.ts`, §2.7 dispatcher hook, §3.6 |\n| FR-13 | §2.6 `FileUpload` |\n| FR-14 | §2.6 `FileList` |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 ContentStatus + Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress, §1.3 |\n| FR-16 | §2.3 `validators/content.ts` |\n| FR-17 | §2.2 `attachFiles` eligibility, §2.3 `updateLesson` |\n| FR-18 | §2.3 `visibility.ts`, §3.2 |\n| FR-19 | §2.3 `canSeeDrafts`, §2.6 `StatusChip` |\n| FR-20 | §2.6 `content` course tab, §2.3 `listCourseContent` |\n| FR-21 | §2.3 `listCourseContent` counts + `continueLessonId`, §2.6 progress bars |\n| FR-22 | §2.3 `createModule`/`updateModule`/`createLesson`, §2.6 module Menu |\n| FR-23 | §2.3 `reorderContent`, §2.6 dnd-kit, §3.5 |\n| FR-24 | §2.4 ConfirmDialog `confirmText`, §2.3 `deleteModule` |\n| FR-25 | §2.6 lesson editor page + Markdown editor |\n| FR-26 | §2.6 image insert, §1.2 D3 inline-image attach |\n| FR-27 | §2.6 attachments/links sections, §2.3 `updateLesson` replace-all |\n| FR-28 | §2.6 Schedule DateTimePicker, §2.3 Zod future check |\n| FR-29 | §2.6 autosave + unsaved-changes guard |\n| FR-30 | §2.3 `src/lib/video.ts`, §2.6 `VideoEmbed`, §2.7 CSP frame-src |\n| FR-31 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` |\n| FR-32 | §2.6 lesson viewer, §2.3 `getLesson` prev/next |\n| FR-33 | §2.3 `getLesson` first-view upsert + `setLessonProgress` |\n| FR-34 | §2.3 `listLessonProgress`, §2.6 Progress Drawer |\n| FR-35 | §2.3 `getStudentLearning`, §2.6 `learning` student tab |\n| FR-36 | §2.3 `setLessonProgress` STUDENT-only, §2.6 viewer hides the button |\n| FR-37 | §2.4 `assertCanViewCourse` reused unchanged |\n| FR-38 | §2.3 `notifyLessonPublished`, §2.7 NOTIFICATION_TYPES, §3.3 |\n| FR-39 | §3.2 no job, §2.6 Schedule tooltip |\n| FR-40 | §2.6 admin settings logo FileUpload, §2.4 `updateSchoolSettings` + logoFileId, §3.7 |\n| FR-41 | §2.2 SVG logo-only + CSP header, §1.2 D7 |\n| FR-42 | §2.6 `/admin/settings/school` page + nav entry |\n| FR-43 | §2.5 route table (15 endpoints), §2.3 service functions |\n| FR-44 | §2.3 `getLesson` NOT_FOUND for hidden lessons |\n| FR-45 | §2.3 `content-service.ts`, §2.2 `src/server/files/`, thin handlers §2.5 |\n| FR-46 | §1.2 D6, §2.3 audit rule, §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile` audit |\n| FR-47 | §2.1 seed + `prisma/seed-assets/` |\n| FR-48 | §5 Testing Strategy |\n| NFR-1 | §2.2 storage outside public + registry, §4 |\n| NFR-2 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` sanitize + `a` mapper, §4 |\n| NFR-3 | §2.2 upload pipeline `rateLimit` |\n| NFR-4 | §2.3 2-query `listCourseContent`, §1.3 order indexes |\n| NFR-5 | §2.2 busboy streaming + hash/count tap + tmp→rename |\n| NFR-6 | §2.6 iframe title, alt-text Alert, up/down IconButtons |\n| NFR-7 | §1.1 blocker 8, §2.6 MUI-only + mui-mcp lookup |\n| NFR-8 | §2.3 per-function access checks, §1.2 D1, §4 |\n| NFR-9 | §2.4 reuse table, ADR-1 deps, §5 gate |\n| NFR-10 | §2.6 StatusChip/Schedule school timezone, `formatInSchoolTz`, `fromZonedTime` |\n| NFR-11 | §1 single local-disk storage, no abstraction |\n| NFR-12 | §2.2 `logger`, §2.7 `.env.example` |\n","numLines":286,"startLine":1,"totalLines":286}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015p77dsq9NRP2Dzj8QWJCkB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
