 GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions (manage) lists every enrolled student, including those who have not submitted, with their status, exemption and submission summary. | \nFR-55 | GET /api/submissions/:id is open to the submitting student, their parents and course managers. SubmissionHistory is included only for managers. | \nFR-56 | PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade (manage) {rawScore, penaltyPercent, feedback, rubricScores} sets gradedById/gradedAt and the computed finalScore. | \nFR-57 | GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab= (any role) returns the role-shaped data for /assignments. studentId is accepted for parents (it must be a linked child). | \nFR-58 | GET /api/students/:id/assignments (view student; uses the existing assertCanViewStudent) returns the per-student assignment list. | \nFR-59 | Grading, returning, exempting and offline grading change records owned by a student, so each writes an AuditLog row through the existing audit(). | \nFR-60 | Assignments with submissionType NO_SUBMISSION are not counted as Missing and trigger no due_soon or missing reminders. They are graded offline only. | \nFR-61 | Seed data: MATH-7A gets 4 assignments (one returned with all students graded at 55–100 %; one submitted and awaiting grading with 60 % submitted and 2 late; one due in 2 days; one draft). ENG-7A gets 2 (one with a 3-criterion rubric, returned). SCI-7A gets 1 NO_SUBMISSION assignment graded offline. The seed is idempotent and skips when those courses do not exist. | \nNFR-1 | Correctness: all score arithmetic uses Decimal end to end (Prisma.Decimal / decimal.js, which ships with Prisma), never JS floating point. Final scores round half-up to 2 dp. | \nNFR-2 | Integrity: submission, deadline, late-day, visibility and reminder checks use server time only. Client timestamps are never trusted. | \nNFR-3 | Performance: the grading screen switches between students in under 300 ms by prefetching the next and previous submissions. | \nNFR-4 | Privacy: students never see other students' submissions, scores or files, in the API or through the file URLs. | \nNFR-5 | Access control is enforced server-side on every handler and server page through requireUser/requireRole and the existing assertCanViewCourse, assertCanManageCourse and assertCanViewStudent. Hiding UI is never the only protection. | \nNFR-6 | UI component rule: Material UI v9.5.0 and MUI X only, styled through the theme, sx and styled(). No banned libraries, enforced by the ESLint no-restricted-imports rule. Every component (List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataTable/DataGrid, DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar via useToast) is looked up through mui-mcp (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented. | \nNFR-7 | API conventions: route handlers are thin (Zod → service → JSON). They use the {data} / list {data,page,pageSize,total} / {error:{code,message,details}} envelopes and the standard error codes. Pagination defaults to 20 (max 100), with ?sort=&order= and ?q=. | \nNFR-8 | Code layout: business logic goes in src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts (the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent). Zod schemas go in src/lib/validators/assignments.ts. Routes go under src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…. Pages go under src/app/(app)/…. | \nNFR-9 | Time handling: timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The late-day calculation is correct across a DST change in the school timezone and on the exact 24 h boundary (exactly 24 h late = 1 day). | \nNFR-10 | Markdown (instructions, submission text, feedback) is rendered with react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with every element mapped to an MUI component. | \nNFR-11 | Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold, rename existing routes or models, or duplicate existing helpers. Reuse notify(), notifyStudentAndParents(), audit(), registerFileAccess/contexts, the files service and /api/files, the DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, PageHeader and useToast components, formatInSchoolTz, and the courseTabs/studentTabs registries. | \nNFR-12 | Committed code has no console.log. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. | \nNFR-13 | Quality gate: npm run lint, npm run typecheck and npm run test keep passing. | \nNFR-14 | Unit tests cover: the late-days calculation (exact 24 h boundary, DST change), the penalty cap, final-score rounding and rubric-sum validation. Integration tests cover: resubmission history, the return flow, reminder idempotency and the effect of exemptions on the missing list. A Playwright e2e covers: teacher creates → student submits a file → teacher grades with a rubric and returns → student sees feedback; parent sees the missing list. | \nNFR-15 | Scope guard: no plagiarism detection, peer review, group assignments, inline document annotation, or gradebook weighting / term grades (PRD-11 consumes these scores). Do not change behaviour owned by later PRDs. | \nNFR-16 | Usability goals: a teacher can create and publish an assignment in under 2 minutes, and can grade 30 submissions with the keyboard without leaving the grading screen. | \nNFR-17 | English-only UI, single school, support for evergreen browsers (last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari), and basic accessibility (labelled inputs, keyboard-operable controls). | \nNone | None | \nNone | None |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FZjfXTk2QJ4bR5tnLBZf7A","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
