wait getAccessibleStudentIds(user);\n\n  if (accessible === 'ALL') return;\n\n  if (accessible.includes(studentId)) return;\n\n  if (user.role === 'STUDENT' || user.role === 'PARENT') {\n    throw new AppError('NOT_FOUND', 'Resource not found');\n  }\n\n  throw new AppError('FORBIDDEN', 'You do not have permission to view this student.');\n}\nimport type { ContentStatus } from '@prisma/client';\n\n/**\n * Single source of truth for content visibility (PRD-08 FR-18, FR-19, FR-44).\n * Pure: evaluated at read time, no background job. Used by list, get,\n * prev/next, file access, progress and the Learning tab.\n */\n\nexport interface Publishable {\n  status: ContentStatus;\n  publishAt: Date | null;\n}\n\nexport function isVisible(item: Publishable, now: Date): boolean {\n  if (item.status === 'PUBLISHED') return true;\n  return item.status === 'SCHEDULED' && item.publishAt !== null && item.publishAt.getTime() <= now.getTime();\n}\n\n/** A lesson is visible to students/parents only when it AND its module are visible. */\nexport function isLessonVisible(lesson: Publishable, module: Publishable, now: Date): boolean {\n  return isVisible(module, now) && isVisible(lesson, now);\n}\n\n/** ADMIN, or the course's teacher/co-teacher, see drafts and scheduled items. */\nexport function canSeeDrafts(\n  user: { id: string; role: string },\n  course: { teacherId: string; coTeacherIds: string[] },\n): boolean {\n  if (user.role === 'ADMIN') return true;\n  return user.role === 'TEACHER' && (course.teacherId === user.id || course.coTeacherIds.includes(user.id));\n}\nimport type { Prisma } from '@prisma/client';\nimport { prisma } from '@/server/db';\nimport { getClientIp } from '@/server/http';\nimport { logger } from '@/lib/logger';\n\nexport interface AuditInput {\n  actorId?: string | null;\n  action: string;\n  entityType?: string;\n  entityId?: string;\n  metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;\n  /** When given, the client IP (x-forwarded-for) is stored in AuditLog.ip (FR-30). */\n  request?: Request;\n}\n\n// FR-31 defence in depth: callers pass explicit metadata, this strips secrets anyway.\nconst SECRET_KEYS = ['password', 'passwordHash', 'newPassword', 'currentPassword', 'token', 'rawToken'];\n\n/**\n * Insert-only audit trail, the single writer of AuditLog rows. Every write\n * endpoint calls this after a successful mutation with action\n * `<entity>.create|update|archive|delete`. Never throws -- a failed audit\n * write must not fail the request it's recording, so errors are logged\n * and swallowed.\n */\nexport async function audit(input: AuditInput): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const metadata = input.metadata\n      ? Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(input.metadata).filter(([key]) => !SECRET_KEYS.includes(key)))\n      : undefined;\n    await prisma.auditLog.create({\n      data: {\n        actorId: input.actorId ?? null,\n        action: input.action,\n        entityType: input.entityType,\n        entityId: input.entityId,\n        metadata: metadata as Prisma.InputJsonValue | undefined,\n        ip: input.request ? getClientIp(input.request) : null,\n      },\n    });\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error('Failed to write audit log', {\n      action: input.action,\n      error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n    });\n  }\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kaw8J3vDiRbv9ZdZcjphKp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgrp2JHbFcNsopsQubtsj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MaKfmc543BFhpZEipxQGRb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat src/server/notifications/types.ts src/server/notifications/notify.ts src/server/files/contexts.ts src/server/files/access.ts && sed -n 1,400p src/server/files/files-service.ts","description":"Read notifications and files code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3679,"cache_read_input_tokens":80275,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3679},"output_tokens":32,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a968fd-48d7-4da9-a01e-aaa2035d3ca9","uuid":"96f1ec2d-7baa-4a50-9f9b-719510fed3e2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:35:42.252Z","request_id":"req_011Cgrp2J4wzUacV4DR3nioH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MaKfmc543BFhpZEipxQGRb":{"command":"cd /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub && cat src/server/notifications/types.ts src/server/notifications/notify.ts src/server/files/contexts.ts src/server/files/access.ts && sed -n 1,400p src/server/files/files-service.ts","description":"Read notifications and files code"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01MaKfmc543BFhpZEipxQGRb":{"cwd":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MaKfmc543BFhpZEipxQGRb","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * Notification type registry (PRD-04 FR-2..5). Client-safe: no prisma/env\n * imports, so validators and client pages can import it. Later PRDs add keys\n * to NOTIFICATION_TYPES; there is no runtime registration API.\n */\nexport type Role = 'ADMIN' | 'TEACHER' | 'STUDENT' | 'PARENT';\n\nconst ALL: readonly Role[] = ['ADMIN', 'TEACHER', 'STUDENT', 'PARENT'];\n\nexport const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT', 'ACADEMIC', 'ATTENDANCE', 'COMMUNICATION', 'FINANCE', 'SYSTEM'] as const;\nexport type NotificationCategory = (typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)[number];\n\nexport const CATEGORY_LABELS: Record<NotificationCategory, string> = {\n  ACCOUNT: 'Account',\n  ACADEMIC: 'Academic',\n  ATTENDANCE: 'Attendance',\n  COMMUNICATION: 'Communication',\n  FINANCE: 'Finance',\n  SYSTEM: 'System',\n};\n\nexport type NotificationTypeDef = {\n  label: string;\n  description: string;\n  category: NotificationCategory;\n  defaultEmail: boolean;\n  mandatoryInApp: boolean;\n  roles: readonly Role[];\n  /** Sent straight to the outbox (sendAuthEmail); hidden from preferences. */\n  emailOnly?: true;\n};\n\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {\n  'account.invite': {\n    label: 'Account invitation',\n    description: 'Invitation to set up your SchoolHub account.',\n    category: 'ACCOUNT',\n    defaultEmail: true,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    emailOnly: true,\n    roles: ALL,\n  },\n  'account.password_reset': {\n    label: 'Password reset',\n    description: 'Link to reset your password.',\n    category: 'ACCOUNT',\n    defaultEmail: true,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    emailOnly: true,\n    roles: ALL,\n  },\n  'system.test': {\n    label: 'Test notification',\n    description: 'Test messages sent by an administrator.',\n    category: 'SYSTEM',\n    defaultEmail: true,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ALL,\n  },\n  // PRD-07 attendance (FR-20, FR-23).\n  'attendance.absent': {\n    label: 'Marked absent',\n    description: 'A student was marked absent from a class or the daily register.',\n    category: 'ATTENDANCE',\n    defaultEmail: true,\n    mandatoryInApp: true,\n    roles: ['PARENT', 'STUDENT'],\n  },\n  'attendance.late': {\n    label: 'Marked late',\n    description: 'A student was marked late.',\n    category: 'ATTENDANCE',\n    defaultEmail: false,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ['PARENT', 'STUDENT'],\n  },\n  'attendance.corrected': {\n    label: 'Attendance corrected',\n    description: 'An absence was corrected to present.',\n    category: 'ATTENDANCE',\n    defaultEmail: false,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ['PARENT', 'STUDENT'],\n  },\n  'attendance.register_missing': {\n    label: 'Register not taken',\n    description: 'An administrator reminded you to take a register.',\n    category: 'ATTENDANCE',\n    defaultEmail: false,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ['TEACHER'],\n  },\n  // PRD-08 course content (FR-38). Scheduled lessons never notify (FR-39).\n  'content.lesson_published': {\n    label: 'New lesson published',\n    description: 'A teacher published a new lesson in one of your courses.',\n    category: 'ACADEMIC',\n    defaultEmail: false,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ['STUDENT'],\n  },\n} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;\n\nexport type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;\n\nconst entries = Object.entries(NOTIFICATION_TYPES) as [NotificationType, NotificationTypeDef][];\n\nexport function getTypeDef(type: string): NotificationTypeDef | undefined {\n  return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(NOTIFICATION_TYPES, type)\n    ? (NOTIFICATION_TYPES as Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>)[type]\n    : undefined;\n}\n\n/** Types a role may see and configure (FR-28, FR-37): role match, not emailOnly. */\nexport function visibleTypesFor(role: Role): NotificationType[] {\n  return entries.filter(([, def]) => def.roles.includes(role) && !def.emailOnly).map(([key]) => key);\n}\n\n/** Type keys in a category, for the FR-34 list filter. */\nexport function typesInCategory(category: NotificationCategory): NotificationType[] {\n  return entries.filter(([, def]) => def.category === category).map(([key]) => key);\n}\n\nexport function categoryOf(type: string): NotificationCategory | null {\n  return getTypeDef(type)?.category ?? null;\n}\nimport { prisma } from '@/server/db';\nimport { logger } from '@/lib/logger';\nimport { BODY_MAX, isSafeRelativeLink, TITLE_MAX } from '@/lib/validators/notifications';\nimport { getEmailSchool, renderEmail } from '@/server/email/render';\nimport { resolvePrefs } from './preferences';\nimport { NOTIFICATION_TYPES, type NotificationType } from './types';\n\nexport interface NotifyInput {\n  type: NotificationType;\n  userIds: string[];\n  title: string;\n  body?: string;\n  link?: string;\n  email?: { subject?: string; template: 'generic-notification'; data?: Record<string, unknown> };\n}\n\nfunction truncate(value: string, max: number, field: string, type: string): string {\n  if (value.length <= max) return value;\n  logger.warn('Notification field truncated', { field, type, length: value.length, max });\n  return value.slice(0, max);\n}\n\n/**\n * Single producer entry point (FR-6..11). Writes in-app rows and enqueues\n * emails per resolved preferences. NEVER throws — failures are logged.\n * Call after your transaction commits.\n */\nexport async function notify(input: NotifyInput): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const def = NOTIFICATION_TYPES[input.type];\n    const userIds = [...new Set(input.userIds)];\n    if (!def || userIds.length === 0) return;\n\n    const title = truncate(input.title, TITLE_MAX, 'title', input.type);\n    const body = input.body == null ? null : truncate(input.body, BODY_MAX, 'body', input.type);\n    let link: string | null = input.link ?? null;\n    if (link !== null && !isSafeRelativeLink(link)) {\n      logger.warn('Notification link dropped (not a safe relative path)', { type: input.type });\n      link = null;\n    }\n\n    const [users, prefRows] = await Promise.all([\n      prisma.user.findMany({\n        where: { id: { in: userIds }, status: { notIn: ['DISABLED', 'ARCHIVED'] }, archivedAt: null },\n        select: { id: true, email: true, firstName: true },\n      }),\n      prisma.notificationPreference.findMany({ where: { userId: { in: userIds }, type: input.type } }),\n    ]);\n    const prefByUser = new Map(prefRows.map((r) => [r.userId, r]));\n\n    const inAppIds: string[] = [];\n    const emailTo: { email: string; firstName: string }[] = [];\n    for (const user of users) {\n      const prefs = resolvePrefs(def, prefByUser.get(user.id));\n      if (prefs.inApp) inAppIds.push(user.id);\n      if (prefs.email && input.email && user.email) emailTo.push(user);\n    }\n\n    if (inAppIds.length) {\n      await prisma.notification.createMany({\n        data: inAppIds.map((userId) => ({ userId, type: input.type, title, body, link })),\n      });\n    }\n\n    if (emailTo.length && input.email) {\n      // Rendered once per call (ADR-6): generic emails carry no per-recipient greeting.\n      const school = await getEmailSchool();\n      const { html, text } = await renderEmail(\n        input.email.template,\n        { title, body, link, ...(input.email.data ?? {}) },\n        school,\n      );\n      const subject = input.email.subject ?? title;\n      await prisma.emailOutbox.createMany({\n        data: emailTo.map((u) => ({ toEmail: u.email, toName: u.firstName, subject, html, text })),\n      });\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error('notify() failed', {\n      type: input.type,\n      message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n    });\n  }\n}\n\n/** Students ∪ their linked parents, deduped (FR-12). Pure. */\nexport function expandStudentRecipients(\n  studentIds: string[],\n  links: { studentId: string; parentId: string }[],\n): string[] {\n  const students = new Set(studentIds);\n  const ids = new Set(studentIds);\n  for (const link of links) if (students.has(link.studentId)) ids.add(link.parentId);\n  return [...ids];\n}\n\n/** notify() for students and every parent linked to them (FR-12). Never throws. */\nexport async function notifyStudentAndParents(\n  input: Omit<NotifyInput, 'userIds'> & { studentIds: string[] },\n): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const { studentIds, ...rest } = input;\n    const links = await prisma.parentStudentLink.findMany({\n      where: { studentId: { in: studentIds } },\n      select: { studentId: true, parentId: true },\n    });\n    await notify({ ...rest, userIds: expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links) });\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error('notifyStudentAndParents() failed', {\n      type: input.type,\n      message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n    });\n  }\n}\nimport { prisma } from '@/server/db';\nimport { assertCanViewCourse } from '@/server/auth/course-access';\nimport { canSeeDrafts, isLessonVisible } from '@/server/content/visibility';\nimport type { FileAccessResolver } from './access';\n\n/**\n * Built-in file contexts (PRD-08 FR-10). Registered lazily by access.ts on\n * first canAccessFile call, so every caller gets them.\n */\n\n/** 'lesson': the caller can view the course and (unless they manage it) the lesson is visible. */\nexport const lessonResolver: FileAccessResolver = async (user, file) => {\n  if (!user || !file.contextId) return false;\n  const lesson = await prisma.lesson.findUnique({\n    where: { id: file.contextId },\n    select: {\n      status: true,\n      publishAt: true,\n      module: {\n        select: { status: true, publishAt: true, course: { select: { id: true, teacherId: true, coTeacherIds: true } } },\n      },\n    },\n  });\n  if (!lesson) return false;\n  try {\n    await assertCanViewCourse(user as Parameters<typeof assertCanViewCourse>[0], lesson.module.course.id);\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n  return canSeeDrafts(user, lesson.module.course) || isLessonVisible(lesson, lesson.module, new Date());\n};\n\n/** 'logo': public, including anonymous (app shell, login page, emails). */\nexport const logoResolver: FileAccessResolver = () => true;\n\nexport function registerBuiltInContexts(register: (context: string, resolver: FileAccessResolver) => void): void {\n  register('lesson', lessonResolver);\n  register('logo', logoResolver);\n}\nimport type { FileObject } from '@prisma/client';\nimport { registerBuiltInContexts } from './contexts';\n\n/**\n * File access registry (PRD-08 FR-9, NFR-1). Every download goes through\n * canAccessFile. Later PRDs call registerFileAccess for their own contexts.\n */\n\nexport interface FileAccessUser {\n  id: string;\n  role: string;\n}\n\nexport type FileAccessFile = Pick<FileObject, 'id' | 'ownerId' | 'context' | 'contextId'>;\n\n/** Resolvers receive null for anonymous callers; only return true for null if the context is public. */\nexport type FileAccessResolver = (user: FileAccessUser | null, file: FileAccessFile) => boolean | Promise<boolean>;\n\nconst registry = new Map<string, FileAccessResolver>();\n\nexport function registerFileAccess(context: string, resolver: FileAccessResolver): void {\n  registry.set(context, resolver);\n}\n\nconst ownerOrAdmin = (user: FileAccessUser | null, file: FileAccessFile) =>\n  user !== null && (user.role === 'ADMIN' || user.id === file.ownerId);\n\nlet builtInsRegistered = false;\n\n/**\n * Dispatch order: (1) unattached -> owner/ADMIN; (2) registered resolver;\n * (3) unknown context -> owner/ADMIN. Anonymous is denied except where a\n * resolver explicitly accepts null. Resolver errors deny.\n */\nexport async function canAccessFile(user: FileAccessUser | null, file: FileAccessFile): Promise<boolean> {\n  // Lazy so the circular import with contexts.ts never hits an uninitialised registry,\n  // and no caller can forget to load the built-in contexts.\n  if (!builtInsRegistered) {\n    builtInsRegistered = true;\n    registerBuiltInContexts(registerFileAccess);\n  }\n  if (file.contextId === null) return ownerOrAdmin(user, file);\n  const resolver = registry.get(file.context);\n  if (!resolver) return ownerOrAdmin(user, file);\n  try {\n    return (await resolver(user, file)) === true;\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\nimport { Readable } from 'node:stream';\nimport type { ReadableStream as NodeWebReadableStream } from 'node:stream/web';\nimport type { FileObject, Prisma } from '@prisma/client';\n// @ts-expect-error -- ponytail: busboy ships without types and comes transitively via next (ADR-2); add @types/busboy if it becomes a direct dep.\nimport busboy from 'busboy';\nimport { fileTypeFromBuffer } from 'file-type';\nimport { prisma } from '@/server/db';\nimport { AppError } from '@/server/http';\nimport { audit } from '@/server/audit';\nimport { rateLimit } from '@/server/rate-limit';\nimport { env } from '@/lib/env';\nimport { deleteFile, readFile, saveFile } from '@/server/storage';\nimport { canAccessFile, type FileAccessUser } from './access';\nimport { checkType, extOf, maxBytesFor, sanitizeFilename } from './validate';\n\n/**\n * File business logic (PRD-08 FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46, NFR-3, NFR-5).\n * Route handlers in src/app/api/files stay thin.\n */\n\nconst HEAD_BYTES = 4100;\nconst MULTIPART_SLACK = 64 * 1024;\nconst CONTEXT_RE = /^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,39}$/;\nconst UPLOADS_PER_HOUR = 60;\n\nexport interface FileSummary {\n  id: string;\n  originalName: string;\n  mimeType: string;\n  sizeBytes: number;\n}\n\nexport const toSummary = (f: Pick<FileObject, 'id' | 'originalName' | 'mimeType' | 'sizeBytes'>): FileSummary => ({\n  id: f.id,\n  originalName: f.originalName,\n  mimeType: f.mimeType,\n  sizeBytes: f.sizeBytes,\n});\n\nfunction maxUploadMb(): number {\n  const fromProcess = Number(process.env.MAX_UPLOAD_MB);\n  return Number.isInteger(fromProcess) && fromProcess > 0 ? fromProcess : env.MAX_UPLOAD_MB;\n}\n\n/** Lets busboy reach 'close' after we stop reading a part (the async iterator's 'readable' listener blocks resume()). */\nfunction drain(stream: Readable): void {\n  stream.removeAllListeners('readable');\n  stream.resume();\n}\n\nconst tooBig = (maxBytes: number) =>\n  new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', `File exceeds ${Math.round(maxBytes / (1024 * 1024))} MB.`);\n\n/** Streams one file part to disk: sniff the head, then hash+count while writing (NFR-5). */\nasync function storePart(\n  user: FileAccessUser,\n  context: string,\n  filename: string,\n  stream: Readable & { truncated?: boolean },\n  maxBytes: number,\n): Promise<FileSummary> {\n  const originalName = sanitizeFilename(filename);\n  const ext = extOf(originalName);\n\n  // Peek the first HEAD_BYTES without buffering the rest.\n  const iterator = stream[Symbol.asyncIterator]() as AsyncIterator<Buffer>;\n  const headChunks: Buffer[] = [];\n  let headLength = 0;\n  let done = false;\n  while (headLength < HEAD_BYTES) {\n    const next = await iterator.next();\n    if (next.done) {\n      done = true;\n      break;\n    }\n    headChunks.push(next.value);\n    headLength += next.value.length;\n  }\n  const head = Buffer.concat(headChunks);\n  const sniffed = head.length ? (await fileTypeFromBuffer(head))?.mime : undefined;\n  const check = checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head);\n  if (!check.ok) {\n    drain(stream);\n    throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', check.error);\n  }\n  if (head.length === 0) {\n    throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'File is empty.');\n  }\n\n  async function* body() {\n    let total = head.length;\n    if (total > maxBytes) throw tooBig(maxBytes);\n    yield head;\n    if (!done) {\n      for (let next = await iterator.next(); !next.done; next = await iterator.next()) {\n        total += next.value.length;\n        // Per-context cap (logo 2 MB) is enforced here mid-stream; saveFile unlinks the tmp file.\n        if (total > maxBytes) throw tooBig(maxBytes);\n        yield next.value;\n      }\n    }\n    // busboy stops emitting at limits.fileSize and marks the stream truncated.\n    if (stream.truncated) throw tooBig(maxBytes);\n  }\n\n  const saved = await saveFile(Readable.from(body()), { ext });\n  const row = await prisma.fileObject.create({\n    data: {\n      ownerId: user.id,\n      originalName,\n      mimeType: check.mime,\n      sizeBytes: saved.sizeBytes,\n      storageKey: saved.storageKey,\n      sha256: saved.sha256,\n      context,\n      contextId: null,\n    },\n  });\n  return toSummary(row);\n}\n\n/** POST /api/files: multipart with a `context` field BEFORE the `file` part (ADR-2). */\nexport async function uploadFile(user: FileAccessUser, request: Request): Promise<FileSummary> {\n  const limit = rateLimit(`upload:${user.id}`, UPLOADS_PER_HOUR, 3_600_000);\n  if (!limit.ok) {\n    throw new AppError('RATE_LIMITED', 'Too many uploads. Try again later.', {\n      retryAfterSeconds: Math.ceil(limit.retryAfterMs / 1000),\n    });\n  }\n\n  const contentType = request.headers.get('content-type') ?? '';\n  if (!contentType.startsWith('multipart/form-data') || !request.body) {\n    throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'Expected multipart/form-data.');\n  }\n  const globalMax = maxBytesFor('lesson', maxUploadMb());\n  const declared = Number(request.headers.get('content-length'));\n  if (Number.isFinite(declared) && declared > globalMax + MULTIPART_SLACK) throw tooBig(globalMax);\n\n  return new Promise<FileSummary>((resolve, reject) => {\n    let context: string | null = null;\n    let work: Promise<FileSummary> | null = null;\n    let parser: ReturnType<typeof busboy>;\n    try {\n      parser = busboy({\n        headers: { 'content-type': contentType },\n        limits: { files: 1, fields: 5, fileSize: globalMax },\n      });\n    } catch {\n      reject(new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'Malformed multipart body.'));\n      return;\n    }\n\n    parser.on('field', (name: string, value: string) => {\n      if (name === 'context') context = value;\n    });\n\n    parser.on('file', (_name: string, stream: Readable & { truncated?: boolean }, info: { filename?: string }) => {\n      if (work) {\n        drain(stream);\n        return;\n      }\n      if (!context || !CONTEXT_RE.test(context)) {\n        drain(stream);\n        work = Promise.reject(new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'A valid context field must precede the file.'));\n        work.catch(() => undefined);\n        return;\n      }\n      work = storePart(user, context, info.filename ?? 'file', stream, maxBytesFor(context, maxUploadMb()));\n      // On failure keep draining so busboy reaches 'close' and the promise settles.\n      work.catch(() => drain(stream));\n    });\n\n    parser.on('error', () => reject(new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'Malformed multipart body.')));\n    parser.on('close', () => {\n      if (!work) reject(new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'No file was uploaded.'));\n      else work.then(resolve, reject);\n    });\n\n    Readable.fromWeb(request.body as unknown as NodeWebReadableStream).on('error', reject).pipe(parser);\n  });\n}\n\n/** Loads the row and runs the registry; denial is NOT_FOUND before any bytes are read (FR-9, NFR-1). */\nexport async function getFileForDownload(user: FileAccessUser | null, id: string) {\n  const file = await prisma.fileObject.findUnique({ where: { id } });\n  if (!file || !(await canAccessFile(user, file))) throw new AppError('NOT_FOUND', 'File not found');\n  return { file, stream: readFile(file.storageKey) };\n}\n\n/** FR-11: owner or ADMIN, only while unattached. Row first, then bytes. */\nexport async function deleteUnattachedFile(user: FileAccessUser, id: string, request?: Request): Promise<void> {\n  const file = await prisma.fileObject.findUnique({ where: { id } });\n  if (!file || (user.role !== 'ADMIN' && file.ownerId !== user.id)) throw new AppError('NOT_FOUND', 'File not found');\n  if (file.contextId !== null) throw new AppError('CONFLICT', 'File is attached and cannot be deleted.');\n  await prisma.fileObject.delete({ where: { id } });\n  await deleteFile(file.storageKey);\n  if (file.ownerId !== user.id) {\n    await audit({\n      actorId: user.id,\n      action: 'file.delete',\n      entityType: 'FileObject',\n      entityId: id,\n      metadata: { ownerId: file.ownerId, originalName: file.originalName },\n      request,\n    });\n  }\n}\n\ntype Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient;\n\n/**\n * FR-17: attach files to (context, contextId). Each must be the caller's\n * (any for ADMIN) and either unattached or already on this same record.\n */\nexport async function attachFiles(\n  tx: Tx,\n  user: FileAccessUser,\n  fileIds: string[],\n  context: string,\n  contextId: string,\n): Promise<void> {\n  const ids = [...new Set(fileIds)];\n  if (ids.length === 0) return;\n  const files = await tx.fileObject.findMany({\n    where: { id: { in: ids } },\n    select: { id: true, ownerId: true, context: true, contextId: true },\n  });\n  const eligible = files.filter(\n    (f) =>\n      (user.role === 'ADMIN' || f.ownerId === user.id) &&\n      (f.contextId === null || (f.contextId === contextId && f.context === context)),\n  );\n  if (eligible.length !== ids.length) {\n    throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'One or more files cannot be attached.', {\n      fileIds: ids.filter((id) => !eligible.some((f) => f.id === id)),\n    });\n  }\n  await tx.fileObject.updateMany({ where: { id: { in: ids } }, data: { context, contextId } });\n}\n\n/** D5: detached files get contextId null and are purged 24 h later. */\nexport async function detachFiles(tx: Tx, fileIds: string[]): Promise<void> {\n  if (fileIds.length === 0) return;\n  await tx.fileObject.updateMany({ where: { id: { in: fileIds } }, data: { contextId: null } });\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a968fd-48d7-4da9-a01e-aaa2035d3ca9","uuid":"f78ef07b-181f-48c6-a01d-c5fd70a5608c","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:35:42.413Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * Notification type registry (PRD-04 FR-2..5). Client-safe: no prisma/env\n * imports, so validators and client pages can import it. Later PRDs add keys\n * to NOTIFICATION_TYPES; there is no runtime registration API.\n */\nexport type Role = 'ADMIN' | 'TEACHER' | 'STUDENT' | 'PARENT';\n\nconst ALL: readonly Role[] = ['ADMIN', 'TEACHER', 'STUDENT', 'PARENT'];\n\nexport const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT', 'ACADEMIC', 'ATTENDANCE', 'COMMUNICATION', 'FINANCE', 'SYSTEM'] as const;\nexport type NotificationCategory = (typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)[number];\n\nexport const CATEGORY_LABELS: Record<NotificationCategory, string> = {\n  ACCOUNT: 'Account',\n  ACADEMIC: 'Academic',\n  ATTENDANCE: 'Attendance',\n  COMMUNICATION: 'Communication',\n  FINANCE: 'Finance',\n  SYSTEM: 'System',\n};\n\nexport type NotificationTypeDef = {\n  label: string;\n  description: string;\n  category: NotificationCategory;\n  defaultEmail: boolean;\n  mandatoryInApp: boolean;\n  roles: readonly Role[];\n  /** Sent straight to the outbox (sendAuthEmail); hidden from preferences. */\n  emailOnly?: true;\n};\n\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {\n  'account.invite': {\n    label: 'Account invitation',\n    description: 'Invitation to set up your SchoolHub account.',\n    category: 'ACCOUNT',\n    defaultEmail: true,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    emailOnly: true,\n    roles: ALL,\n  },\n  'account.password_reset': {\n    label: 'Password reset',\n    description: 'Link to reset your password.',\n    category: 'ACCOUNT',\n    defaultEmail: true,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    emailOnly: true,\n    roles: ALL,\n  },\n  'system.test': {\n    label: 'Test notification',\n    description: 'Test messages sent by an administrator.',\n    category: 'SYSTEM',\n    defaultEmail: true,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ALL,\n  },\n  // PRD-07 attendance (FR-20, FR-23).\n  'attendance.absent': {\n    label: 'Marked absent',\n    description: 'A student was marked absent from a class or the daily register.',\n    category: 'ATTENDANCE',\n    defaultEmail: true,\n    mandatoryInApp: true,\n    roles: ['PARENT', 'STUDENT'],\n  },\n  'attendance.late': {\n    label: 'Marked late',\n    description: 'A student was marked late.',\n    category: 'ATTENDANCE',\n    defaultEmail: false,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ['PARENT', 'STUDENT'],\n  },\n  'attendance.corrected': {\n    label: 'Attendance corrected',\n    description: 'An absence was corrected to present.',\n    category: 'ATTENDANCE',\n    defaultEmail: false,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ['PARENT', 'STUDENT'],\n  },\n  'attendance.register_missing': {\n    label: 'Register not taken',\n    description: 'An administrator reminded you to take a register.',\n    category: 'ATTENDANCE',\n    defaultEmail: false,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ['TEACHER'],\n  },\n  // PRD-08 course content (FR-38). Scheduled lessons never notify (FR-39).\n  'content.lesson_published': {\n    label: 'New lesson published',\n    description: 'A teacher published a new lesson in one of your courses.',\n    category: 'ACADEMIC',\n    defaultEmail: false,\n    mandatoryInApp: false,\n    roles: ['STUDENT'],\n  },\n} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;\n\nexport type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;\n\nconst entries = Object.entries(NOTIFICATION_TYPES) as [NotificationType, NotificationTypeDef][];\n\nexport function getTypeDef(type: string): NotificationTypeDef | undefined {\n  return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(NOTIFICATION_TYPES, type)\n    ? (NOTIFICATION_TYPES as Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>)[type]\n    : undefined;\n}\n\n/** Types a role may see and configure (FR-28, FR-37): role match, not emailOnly. */\nexport function visibleTypesFor(role: Role): NotificationType[] {\n  return entries.filter(([, def]) => def.roles.includes(role) && !def.emailOnly).map(([key]) => key);\n}\n\n/** Type keys in a category, for the FR-34 list filter. */\nexport function typesInCategory(category: NotificationCategory): NotificationType[] {\n  return entries.filter(([, def]) => def.category === category).map(([key]) => key);\n}\n\nexport function categoryOf(type: string): NotificationCategory | null {\n  return getTypeDef(type)?.category ?? null;\n}\nimport { prisma } from '@/server/db';\nimport { logger } from '@/lib/logger';\nimport { BODY_MAX, isSafeRelativeLink, TITLE_MAX } from '@/lib/validators/notifications';\nimport { getEmailSchool, renderEmail } from '@/server/email/render';\nimport { resolvePrefs } from './preferences';\nimport { NOTIFICATION_TYPES, type NotificationType } from './types';\n\nexport interface NotifyInput {\n  type: NotificationType;\n  userIds: string[];\n  title: string;\n  body?: string;\n  link?: string;\n  email?: { subject?: string; template: 'generic-notification'; data?: Record<string, unknown> };\n}\n\nfunction truncate(value: string, max: number, field: string, type: string): string {\n  if (value.length <= max) return value;\n  logger.warn('Notification field truncated', { field, type, length: value.length, max });\n  return value.slice(0, max);\n}\n\n/**\n * Single producer entry point (FR-6..11). Writes in-app rows and enqueues\n * emails per resolved preferences. NEVER throws — failures are logged.\n * Call after your transaction commits.\n */\nexport async function notify(input: NotifyInput): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const def = NOTIFICATION_TYPES[input.type];\n    const userIds = [...new Set(input.userIds)];\n    if (!def || userIds.length === 0) return;\n\n    const title = truncate(input.title, TITLE_MAX, 'title', input.type);\n    const body = input.body == null ? null : truncate(input.body, BODY_MAX, 'body', input.type);\n    let link: string | null = input.link ?? null;\n    if (link !== null && !isSafeRelativeLink(link)) {\n      logger.warn('Notification link dropped (not a safe relative path)', { type: input.type });\n      link = null;\n    }\n\n    const [users, prefRows] = await Promise.all([\n      prisma.user.findMany({\n        where: { id: { in: userIds }, status: { notIn: ['DISABLED', 'ARCHIVED'] }, archivedAt: null },\n        select: { id: true, email: true, firstName: true },\n      }),\n      prisma.notificationPreference.findMany({ where: { userId: { in: userIds }, type: input.type } }),\n    ]);\n    const prefByUser = new Map(prefRows.map((r) => [r.userId, r]));\n\n    const inAppIds: string[] = [];\n    const emailTo: { email: string; firstName: string }[] = [];\n    for (const user of users) {\n      const prefs = resolvePrefs(def, prefByUser.get(user.id));\n      if (prefs.inApp) inAppIds.push(user.id);\n      if (prefs.email && input.email && user.email) emailTo.push(user);\n    }\n\n    if (inAppIds.length) {\n      await prisma.notification.createMany({\n        data: inAppIds.map((userId) => ({ userId, type: input.type, title, body, link })),\n      });\n    }\n\n    if (emailTo.length && input.email) {\n      // Rendered once per call (ADR-6): generic emails carry no per-recipient greeting.\n      const school = await getEmailSchool();\n      const { html, text } = await renderEmail(\n        input.email.template,\n        { title, body, link, ...(input.email.data ?? {}) },\n        school,\n      );\n      const subject = input.email.subject ?? title;\n      await prisma.emailOutbox.createMany({\n        data: emailTo.map((u) => ({ toEmail: u.email, toName: u.firstName, subject, html, text })),\n      });\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error('notify() failed', {\n      type: input.type,\n      message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n    });\n  }\n}\n\n/** Students ∪ their linked parents, deduped (FR-12). Pure. */\nexport function expandStudentRecipients(\n  studentIds: string[],\n  links: { studentId: string; parentId: string }[],\n): string[] {\n  const students = new Set(studentIds);\n  const ids = new Set(studentIds);\n  for (const link of links) if (students.has(link.studentId)) ids.add(link.parentId);\n  return [...ids];\n}\n\n/** notify() for students and every parent linked to them (FR-12). Never throws. */\nexport async function notifyStudentAndParents(\n  input: Omit<NotifyInput, 'userIds'> & { studentIds: string[] },\n): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    const { studentIds, ...rest } = input;\n    const links = await prisma.parentStudentLink.findMany({\n      where: { studentId: { in: studentIds } },\n      select: { studentId: true, parentId: true },\n    });\n    await notify({ ...rest, userIds: expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links) });\n  } catch (error) {\n    logger.error('notifyStudentAndParents() failed', {\n      type: input.type,\n      message: error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error),\n    });\n  }\n}\nimport { prisma } from '@/server/db';\nimport { assertCanViewCourse } from '@/server/auth/course-access';\nimport { canSeeDrafts, isLessonVisible } from '@/server/content/visibility';\nimport type { FileAccessResolver } from './access';\n\n/**\n * Built-in file contexts (PRD-08 FR-10). Registered lazily by access.ts on\n * first canAccessFile call, so every caller gets them.\n */\n\n/** 'lesson': the caller can view the course and (unless they manage it) the lesson is visible. */\nexport const lessonResolver: FileAccessResolver = async (user, file) => {\n  if (!user || !file.contextId) return false;\n  const lesson = await prisma.lesson.findUnique({\n    where: { id: file.contextId },\n    select: {\n      status: true,\n      publishAt: true,\n      module: {\n        select: { status: true, publishAt: true, course: { select: { id: true, teacherId: true, coTeacherIds: true } } },\n      },\n    },\n  });\n  if (!lesson) return false;\n  try {\n    await assertCanViewCourse(user as Parameters<typeof assertCanViewCourse>[0], lesson.module.course.id);\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n  return canSeeDrafts(user, lesson.module.course) || isLessonVisible(lesson, lesson.module, new Date());\n};\n\n/** 'logo': public, including anonymous (app shell, login page, emails). */\nexport const logoResolver: FileAccessResolver = () => true;\n\nexport function registerBuiltInContexts(register: (context: string, resolver: FileAccessResolver) => void): void {\n  register('lesson', lessonResolver);\n  register('logo', logoResolver);\n}\nimport type { FileObject } from '@prisma/client';\nimport { registerBuiltInContexts } from './contexts';\n\n/**\n * File access registry (PRD-08 FR-9, NFR-1). Every download goes through\n * canAccessFile. Later PRDs call registerFileAccess for their own contexts.\n */\n\nexport interface FileAccessUser {\n  id: string;\n  role: string;\n}\n\nexport type FileAccessFile = Pick<FileObject, 'id' | 'ownerId' | 'context' | 'contextId'>;\n\n/** Resolvers receive null for anonymous callers; only return true for null if the context is public. */\nexport type FileAccessResolver = (user: FileAccessUser | null, file: FileAccessFile) => boolean | Promise<boolean>;\n\nconst registry = new Map<string, FileAccessResolver>();\n\nexport function registerFileAccess(context: string, resolver: FileAccessResolver): void {\n  registry.set(context, resolver);\n}\n\nconst ownerOrAdmin = (user: FileAccessUser | null, file: FileAccessFile) =>\n  user !== null && (user.role === 'ADMIN' || user.id === file.ownerId);\n\nlet builtInsRegistered = false;\n\n/**\n * Dispatch order: (1) unattached -> owner/ADMIN; (2) registered resolver;\n * (3) unknown context -> owner/ADMIN. Anonymous is denied except where a\n * resolver explicitly accepts null. Resolver errors deny.\n */\nexport async function canAccessFile(user: FileAccessUser | null, file: FileAccessFile): Promise<boolean> {\n  // Lazy so the circular import with contexts.ts never hits an uninitialised registry,\n  // and no caller can forget to load the built-in contexts.\n  if (!builtInsRegistered) {\n    builtInsRegistered = true;\n    registerBuiltInContexts(registerFileAccess);\n  }\n  if (file.contextId === null) return ownerOrAdmin(user, file);\n  const resolver = registry.get(file.context);\n  if (!resolver) return ownerOrAdmin(user, file);\n  try {\n    return (await resolver(user, file)) === true;\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n}\nimport { Readable } from 'node:stream';\nimport type { ReadableStream as NodeWebReadableStream } from 'node:stream/web';\nimport type { FileObject, Prisma } from '@prisma/client';\n// @ts-expect-error -- ponytail: busboy ships without types and comes transitively via next (ADR-2); add @types/busboy if it becomes a direct dep.\nimport busboy from 'busboy';\nimport { fileTypeFromBuffer } from 'file-type';\nimport { prisma } from '@/server/db';\nimport { AppError } from '@/server/http';\nimport { audit } from '@/server/audit';\nimport { rateLimit } from '@/server/rate-limit';\nimport { env } from '@/lib/env';\nimport { deleteFile, readFile, saveFile } from '@/server/storage';\nimport { canAccessFile, type FileAccessUser } from './access';\nimport { checkType, extOf, maxBytesFor, sanitizeFilename } from './validate';\n\n/**\n * File business logic (PRD-08 FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46, NFR-3, NFR-5).\n * Route handlers in src/app/api/files stay thin.\n */\n\nconst HEAD_BYTES = 4100;\nconst MULTIPART_SLACK = 64 * 1024;\nconst CONTEXT_RE = /^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,39}$/;\nconst UPLOADS_PER_HOUR = 60;\n\nexport interface FileSummary {\n  id: string;\n  originalName: string;\n  mimeType: string;\n  sizeBytes: number;\n}\n\nexport const toSummary = (f: Pick<FileObject, 'id' | 'originalName' | 'mimeType' | 'sizeBytes'>): FileSummary => ({\n  id: f.id,\n  originalName: f.originalName,\n  mimeType: f.mimeType,\n  sizeBytes: f.sizeBytes,\n});\n\nfunction maxUploadMb(): number {\n  const fromProcess = Number(process.env.MAX_UPLOAD_MB);\n  return Number.isInteger(fromProcess) && fromProcess > 0 ? fromProcess : env.MAX_UPLOAD_MB;\n}\n\n/** Lets busboy reach 'close' after we stop reading a part (the async iterator's 'readable' listener blocks resume()). */\nfunction drain(stream: Readable): void {\n  stream.removeAllListeners('readable');\n  stream.resume();\n}\n\nconst tooBig = (maxBytes: number) =>\n  new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', `File exceeds ${Math.round(maxBytes / (1024 * 1024))} MB.`);\n\n/** Streams one file part to disk: sniff the head, then hash+count while writing (NFR-5). */\nasync function storePart(\n  user: FileAccessUser,\n  context: string,\n  filename: string,\n  stream: Readable & { truncated?: boolean },\n  maxBytes: number,\n): Promise<FileSummary> {\n  const originalName = sanitizeFilename(filename);\n  const ext = extOf(originalName);\n\n  // Peek the first HEAD_BYTES without buffering the rest.\n  const iterator = stream[Symbol.asyncIterator]() as AsyncIterator<Buffer>;\n  const headChunks: Buffer[] = [];\n  let headLength = 0;\n  let done = false;\n  while (headLength < HEAD_BYTES) {\n    const next = await iterator.next();\n    if (next.done) {\n      done = true;\n      break;\n    }\n    headChunks.push(next.value);\n    headLength += next.value.length;\n  }\n  const head = Buffer.concat(headChunks);\n  const sniffed = head.length ? (await fileTypeFromBuffer(head))?.mime : undefined;\n  const check = checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head);\n  if (!check.ok) {\n    drain(stream);\n    throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', check.error);\n  }\n  if (head.length === 0) {\n    throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'File is empty.');\n  }\n\n  async function* body() {\n    let total = head.length;\n    if (total > maxBytes) throw tooBig(maxBytes);\n    yield head;\n    if (!done) {\n      for (let next = await iterator.next(); !next.done; next = await iterator.next()) {\n        total += next.value.length;\n        // Per-context cap (logo 2 MB) is enforced here mid-stream; saveFile unlinks the tmp file.\n        if (total > maxBytes) throw tooBig(maxBytes);\n        yield next.value;\n      }\n    }\n    // busboy stops emitting at limits.fileSize and marks the stream truncated.\n    if (stream.truncated) throw tooBig(maxBytes);\n  }\n\n  const saved = await saveFile(Readable.from(body()), { ext });\n  const row = await prisma.fileObject.create({\n    data: {\n      ownerId: user.id,\n      originalName,\n      mimeType: check.mime,\n      sizeBytes: saved.sizeBytes,\n      storageKey: saved.storageKey,\n      sha256: saved.sha256,\n      context,\n      contextId: null,\n    },\n  });\n  return toSummary(row);\n}\n\n/** POST /api/files: multipart with a `context` field BEFORE the `file` part (ADR-2). */\nexport async function uploadFile(user: FileAccessUser, request: Request): Promise<FileSummary> {\n  const limit = rateLimit(`upload:${user.id}`, UPLOADS_PER_HOUR, 3_600_000);\n  if (!limit.ok) {\n    throw new AppError('RATE_LIMITED', 'Too many uploads. Try again later.', {\n      retryAfterSeconds: Math.ceil(limit.retryAfterMs / 1000),\n    });\n  }\n\n  const contentType = request.headers.get('content-type') ?? '';\n  if (!contentType.startsWith('multipart/form-data') || !request.body) {\n    throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'Expected multipart/form-data.');\n  }\n  const globalMax = maxBytesFor('lesson', maxUploadMb());\n  const declared = Number(request.headers.get('content-length'));\n  if (Number.isFinite(declared) && declared > globalMax + MULTIPART_SLACK) throw tooBig(globalMax);\n\n  return new Promise<FileSummary>((resolve, reject) => {\n    let context: string | null = null;\n    let work: Promise<FileSummary> | null = null;\n    let parser: ReturnType<typeof busboy>;\n    try {\n      parser = busboy({\n        headers: { 'content-type': contentType },\n        limits: { files: 1, fields: 5, fileSize: globalMax },\n      });\n    } catch {\n      reject(new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'Malformed multipart body.'));\n      return;\n    }\n\n    parser.on('field', (name: string, value: string) => {\n      if (name === 'context') context = value;\n    });\n\n    parser.on('file', (_name: string, stream: Readable & { truncated?: boolean }, info: { filename?: string }) => {\n      if (work) {\n        drain(stream);\n        return;\n      }\n      if (!context || !CONTEXT_RE.test(context)) {\n        drain(stream);\n        work = Promise.reject(new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'A valid context field must precede the file.'));\n        work.catch(() => undefined);\n        return;\n      }\n      work = storePart(user, context, info.filename ?? 'file', stream, maxBytesFor(context, maxUploadMb()));\n      // On failure keep draining so busboy reaches 'close' and the promise settles.\n      work.catch(() => drain(stream));\n    });\n\n    parser.on('error', () => reject(new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'Malformed multipart body.')));\n    parser.on('close', () => {\n      if (!work) reject(new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'No file was uploaded.'));\n      else work.then(resolve, reject);\n    });\n\n    Readable.fromWeb(request.body as unknown as NodeWebReadableStream).on('error', reject).pipe(parser);\n  });\n}\n\n/** Loads the row and runs the registry; denial is NOT_FOUND before any bytes are read (FR-9, NFR-1). */\nexport async function getFileForDownload(user: FileAccessUser | null, id: string) {\n  const file = await prisma.fileObject.findUnique({ where: { id } });\n  if (!file || !(await canAccessFile(user, file))) throw new AppError('NOT_FOUND', 'File not found');\n  return { file, stream: readFile(file.storageKey) };\n}\n\n/** FR-11: owner or ADMIN, only while unattached. Row first, then bytes. */\nexport async function deleteUnattachedFile(user: FileAccessUser, id: string, request?: Request): Promise<void> {\n  const file = await prisma.fileObject.findUnique({ where: { id } });\n  if (!file || (user.role !== 'ADMIN' && file.ownerId !== user.id)) throw new AppError('NOT_FOUND', 'File not found');\n  if (file.contextId !== null) throw new AppError('CONFLICT', 'File is attached and cannot be deleted.');\n  await prisma.fileObject.delete({ where: { id } });\n  await deleteFile(file.storageKey);\n  if (file.ownerId !== user.id) {\n    await audit({\n      actorId: user.id,\n      action: 'file.delete',\n      entityType: 'FileObject',\n      entityId: id,\n      metadata: { ownerId: file.ownerId, originalName: file.originalName },\n      request,\n    });\n  }\n}\n\ntype Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient;\n\n/**\n * FR-17: attach files to (context, contextId). Each must be the caller's\n * (any for ADMIN) and either unattached or already on this same record.\n */\nexport async function attachFiles(\n  tx: Tx,\n  user: FileAccessUser,\n  fileIds: string[],\n  context: string,\n  contextId: string,\n): Promise<void> {\n  const ids = [...new Set(fileIds)];\n  if (ids.length === 0) return;\n  const files = await tx.fileObject.findMany({\n    where: { id: { in: ids } },\n    select: { id: true, ownerId: true, context: true, contextId: true },\n  });\n  const eligible = files.filter(\n    (f) =>\n      (user.role === 'ADMIN' || f.ownerId === user.id) &&\n      (f.contextId === null || (f.contextId === contextId && f.context === context)),\n  );\n  if (eligible.length !== ids.length) {\n    throw new AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'One or more files cannot be attached.', {\n      fileIds: ids.filter((id) => !eligible.some((f) => f.id === id)),\n    });\n  }\n  await tx.fileObject.updateMany({ where: { id: { in: ids } }, data: { context, contextId } });\n}\n\n/** D5: detached files get contextId null and are purged 24 h later. */\nexport async function detachFiles(tx: Tx, fileIds: string[]): Promise<void> {\n  if (fileIds.length === 0) return;\n  await tx.fileObject.updateMany({ where: { id: { in: fileIds } }, data: { contextId: null } });\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MaKfmc543BFhpZEipxQGRb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
