{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XpeDXufnpzCKTce1VH5fc5","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md:29:## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\nartifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md:31:**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\nartifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md:33:**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\nartifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md:110:1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\nartifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md:162:| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 **is installed** (package.json L34). It very likely has the same `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 mismatch, so FR-9's DateTimePicker is also at risk. That makes aligning the versions the real fix, rather than a Table workaround. |\nartifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json:11:    \"ENV BREAK: @mui/x-internals 9.15.0 is mismatched with @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0, so DataTable/DataGrid pages fail to compile. FR-17 (the teacher assignments table) needs it. Either align the MUI X versions in package.json or the lockfile, or render the table without DataGrid. This needs a decision.\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a968fd-48d7-4da9-a01e-aaa2035d3ca9","uuid":"3cd7f0d0-d6c6-4925-b40d-5d230f8dc29a","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:57:42.042Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md:29:## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\nartifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md:31:**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\nartifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md:33:**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\nartifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md:110:1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\nartifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md:162:| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 **is installed** (package.json L34). It very likely has the same `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 mismatch, so FR-9's DateTimePicker is also at risk. That makes aligning the versions the real fix, rather than a Table workaround. |\nartifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json:11:    \"ENV BREAK: @mui/x-internals 9.15.0 is mismatched with @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0, so DataTable/DataGrid pages fail to compile. FR-17 (the teacher assignments table) needs it. Either align the MUI X versions in package.json or the lockfile, or render the table without DataGrid. This needs a decision.\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XpeDXufnpzCKTce1VH5fc5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
