{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrrHTeomyNWJLfCqyTvL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GhHDC6tJyJUb47XEBxHcZJ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/dev/dev-log.md","content":"# Dev Log — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)\n\n> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-7 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-7's).\n> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-9. This is SH-9's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)\n\nAll 26 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in\n`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 55 matrix paths were verified on disk (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is deleted as planned).\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Environment fixes (x-internals override, vitest import, delete tmp config) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Prisma schema + migration add_assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: grading-math.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: nextTeachingDayDueAt in src/lib/dates.ts + DST tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: Publishable type widened + 4 notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: assignments-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: reminders.ts + dispatcher hook — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: assignment/submission file resolvers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: course/assignment/duplicate route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: submission/grading route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: /api/me/assignments + /api/students/[id]/assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: next.config.js header split (D11) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: MarkdownView + MarkdownEditor — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: FileUpload + FileList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: course-tabs / navigation / student-tabs entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: RubricBuilder — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: AssignmentForm + new/edit pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: AssignmentList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Course Assignments tab + CourseAssignmentsTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: Assignment page + SubmissionPanel — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: Grading page + GradingWorkspace — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: /assignments + /students/[id]/assignments pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-24: Idempotent FR-61 seed block — ✓ complete\n- TASK-25: Integration tests (submissions, grading, reminders) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-26: Playwright e2e — ✓ complete\n\n### Verification run this iteration\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | No ESLint warnings or errors |\n| Unit: `tests/unit/assignments/*`, `tests/unit/dates.test.ts` | 29 / 29 pass |\n| Integration: `tests/integration/assignments/*` (`TEST_DATABASE_URL` = local Postgres :5433, tagged fixtures, cleaned up) | 14 / 14 pass; 3 consecutive full-folder runs green |\n| `npm run build` | **passes** (needs network access for `next/font` Google Fonts) |\n| e2e `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` against a fresh `next start -p 3100` | 5 / 5 pass |\n| Seed: run twice against temporary MATH-7A/ELA-7A/SCI-7A courses | 7 created, then 0 (idempotent); missing courses skip with a log line. Temp data removed. |\n| Migration `20261109000000_add_assignments` | applied with `prisma migrate deploy`; additive only (no DROP/ALTER of existing tables) |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp gate | reachable. `useMuiDocs` (material-ui 9.5.0 llms.txt) + `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup and LinearProgress. Other components follow existing in-repo v9 usage. |\n\n### Decisions and deviations (for QA / reviewer)\n1. **ADR-2 is not enough on its own — follow-up fix in `next.config.js`.** With `@mui/x-internals` pinned to 9.1.0 (`npm ls` shows 9.1.0 everywhere), `next build` still failed with\n   `'useFirstRender' is not exported`. Root cause: webpack resolves `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender` to its **CJS** build. That build re-exports through `Object.keys`, which webpack can't analyse statically,\n   so x-data-grid's `export *` of it breaks. Fix: one `webpack()` alias that points that specifier at the ESM file (commented, removable on a MUI X upgrade). With the alias,\n   DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9) build, so **no D2 fallbacks were needed**. This touches `next.config.js`, which the plan gives to TASK-13. It's logged here as part of TASK-1's environment fix.\n   The pin is kept, because the alias targets the 9.1.0 file.\n2. **Decimal source:** `grading-math.ts` imports `Decimal` from `@prisma/client/runtime/index-browser.js`, which is Prisma's bundled decimal.js. The plain `decimal.js` package is only a transitive\n   **devDependency** (via jsdom), so it would be missing in a production install. ADR-1 (no new dependencies) holds. Values go to Prisma as 2 dp strings, so the two Decimal classes never mix.\n3. **Decimal serialization:** done in explicit typed mappers (`serializeDecimal` helper → `\"14.40\"`), not a generic walker. Same output as D5.\n4. **`GET /api/me/assignments`:** when `tab` is omitted, all rows come back, each with its server-computed `group`. The `/assignments` page groups them on the client (one fetch for all four tabs). With `tab`, the filter works as contracted.\n   The contract said `default UPCOMING`.\n5. **DateTimePicker + school timezone:** `AdapterDateFns` has no timezone support. The form converts UTC ↔ school wall clock with `toZonedTime`/`fromZonedTime` (NFR-9).\n6. **Reminders robustness:** `claim()` treats P2003 (assignment hard-deleted mid-pass) like P2002. Found because the global pass touched another test's assignment during parallel runs.\n7. **Rubric edits keep criterion ids** (upsert by id), so saved `rubricScores` stay valid after an edit.\n8. **TO_GRADE list** is capped at 200 rows (`ponytail:` note). The manager course table pages client-side (`ponytail:` note).\n9. `GET /api/assignments/:id` also returns `studentId` (the viewed child), so parent links stay on the same child.\n\n### Pre-existing issues seen (not caused by SH-9 and not in scope)\n- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 2 failures (FR-22 notification count, FR-10/FR-19 EXCUSED save). These exercise attendance code that SH-9 doesn't touch. They look time-of-day dependent.\n- `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx` (focus assertion), `tests/unit/useToast.test.tsx` (timer/provider), and `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts` (next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM) fail.\n  None of them import SH-9 code. There is no baseline to compare against, because the old `vitest/config.js` import couldn't load at all (blocker 3, now fixed).\n- `next build` prints \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines for every existing GET route. That's build-time log noise, not a failure. `/api/me/assignments` is marked `force-dynamic` to stay quiet.\n- **A stale `next-server` from 27 Oct (PID 63666) is still listening on :3000 for this project, serving old code.** Playwright's `reuseExistingServer` would reuse it, so e2e was run on :3100.\n  I didn't kill it. Restart it before manual testing or QA.\n- The repo's git root is the home directory and the whole project is untracked, so `git stash`/diff can't serve as a baseline.\n\n### Known gaps carried forward (from the design; not new scope)\n- There's no `studentTabs` renderer, so `/students/[id]/assignments` is reachable by URL only (FR-41, blocker 5).\n- The platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true` (ADR-4).\n- D11 changes a security header narrowly (`X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + `frame-ancestors 'self'` only on `/api/files/:id`). Reviewer sign-off is recommended.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1090,"cache_read_input_tokens":327131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1090},"output_tokens":39,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a968fd-48d7-4da9-a01e-aaa2035d3ca9","uuid":"973d1828-5e2f-48b1-9b17-eff37fcb1d84","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:05:46.272Z","request_id":"req_011CgrrHTPRtXfJ96BfYtK4i","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GhHDC6tJyJUb47XEBxHcZJ":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/dev/dev-log.md","content":"# Dev Log — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)\n\n> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-7 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-7's).\n> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-9. This is SH-9's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)\n\nAll 26 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in\n`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 55 matrix paths were verified on disk (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is deleted as planned).\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Environment fixes (x-internals override, vitest import, delete tmp config) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Prisma schema + migration add_assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: grading-math.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: nextTeachingDayDueAt in src/lib/dates.ts + DST tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: Publishable type widened + 4 notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: assignments-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: reminders.ts + dispatcher hook — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: assignment/submission file resolvers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: course/assignment/duplicate route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: submission/grading route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: /api/me/assignments + /api/students/[id]/assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: next.config.js header split (D11) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: MarkdownView + MarkdownEditor — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: FileUpload + FileList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: course-tabs / navigation / student-tabs entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: RubricBuilder — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: AssignmentForm + new/edit pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: AssignmentList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Course Assignments tab + CourseAssignmentsTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: Assignment page + SubmissionPanel — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: Grading page + GradingWorkspace — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: /assignments + /students/[id]/assignments pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-24: Idempotent FR-61 seed block — ✓ complete\n- TASK-25: Integration tests (submissions, grading, reminders) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-26: Playwright e2e — ✓ complete\n\n### Verification run this iteration\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | No ESLint warnings or errors |\n| Unit: `tests/unit/assignments/*`, `tests/unit/dates.test.ts` | 29 / 29 pass |\n| Integration: `tests/integration/assignments/*` (`TEST_DATABASE_URL` = local Postgres :5433, tagged fixtures, cleaned up) | 14 / 14 pass; 3 consecutive full-folder runs green |\n| `npm run build` | **passes** (needs network access for `next/font` Google Fonts) |\n| e2e `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` against a fresh `next start -p 3100` | 5 / 5 pass |\n| Seed: run twice against temporary MATH-7A/ELA-7A/SCI-7A courses | 7 created, then 0 (idempotent); missing courses skip with a log line. Temp data removed. |\n| Migration `20261109000000_add_assignments` | applied with `prisma migrate deploy`; additive only (no DROP/ALTER of existing tables) |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp gate | reachable. `useMuiDocs` (material-ui 9.5.0 llms.txt) + `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup and LinearProgress. Other components follow existing in-repo v9 usage. |\n\n### Decisions and deviations (for QA / reviewer)\n1. **ADR-2 is not enough on its own — follow-up fix in `next.config.js`.** With `@mui/x-internals` pinned to 9.1.0 (`npm ls` shows 9.1.0 everywhere), `next build` still failed with\n   `'useFirstRender' is not exported`. Root cause: webpack resolves `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender` to its **CJS** build. That build re-exports through `Object.keys`, which webpack can't analyse statically,\n   so x-data-grid's `export *` of it breaks. Fix: one `webpack()` alias that points that specifier at the ESM file (commented, removable on a MUI X upgrade). With the alias,\n   DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9) build, so **no D2 fallbacks were needed**. This touches `next.config.js`, which the plan gives to TASK-13. It's logged here as part of TASK-1's environment fix.\n   The pin is kept, because the alias targets the 9.1.0 file.\n2. **Decimal source:** `grading-math.ts` imports `Decimal` from `@prisma/client/runtime/index-browser.js`, which is Prisma's bundled decimal.js. The plain `decimal.js` package is only a transitive\n   **devDependency** (via jsdom), so it would be missing in a production install. ADR-1 (no new dependencies) holds. Values go to Prisma as 2 dp strings, so the two Decimal classes never mix.\n3. **Decimal serialization:** done in explicit typed mappers (`serializeDecimal` helper → `\"14.40\"`), not a generic walker. Same output as D5.\n4. **`GET /api/me/assignments`:** when `tab` is omitted, all rows come back, each with its server-computed `group`. The `/assignments` page groups them on the client (one fetch for all four tabs). With `tab`, the filter works as contracted.\n   The contract said `default UPCOMING`.\n5. **DateTimePicker + school timezone:** `AdapterDateFns` has no timezone support. The form converts UTC ↔ school wall clock with `toZonedTime`/`fromZonedTime` (NFR-9).\n6. **Reminders robustness:** `claim()` treats P2003 (assignment hard-deleted mid-pass) like P2002. Found because the global pass touched another test's assignment during parallel runs.\n7. **Rubric edits keep criterion ids** (upsert by id), so saved `rubricScores` stay valid after an edit.\n8. **TO_GRADE list** is capped at 200 rows (`ponytail:` note). The manager course table pages client-side (`ponytail:` note).\n9. `GET /api/assignments/:id` also returns `studentId` (the viewed child), so parent links stay on the same child.\n\n### Pre-existing issues seen (not caused by SH-9 and not in scope)\n- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 2 failures (FR-22 notification count, FR-10/FR-19 EXCUSED save). These exercise attendance code that SH-9 doesn't touch. They look time-of-day dependent.\n- `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx` (focus assertion), `tests/unit/useToast.test.tsx` (timer/provider), and `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts` (next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM) fail.\n  None of them import SH-9 code. There is no baseline to compare against, because the old `vitest/config.js` import couldn't load at all (blocker 3, now fixed).\n- `next build` prints \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines for every existing GET route. That's build-time log noise, not a failure. `/api/me/assignments` is marked `force-dynamic` to stay quiet.\n- **A stale `next-server` from 27 Oct (PID 63666) is still listening on :3000 for this project, serving old code.** Playwright's `reuseExistingServer` would reuse it, so e2e was run on :3100.\n  I didn't kill it. Restart it before manual testing or QA.\n- The repo's git root is the home directory and the whole project is untracked, so `git stash`/diff can't serve as a baseline.\n\n### Known gaps carried forward (from the design; not new scope)\n- There's no `studentTabs` renderer, so `/students/[id]/assignments` is reachable by URL only (FR-41, blocker 5).\n- The platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true` (ADR-4).\n- D11 changes a security header narrowly (`X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + `frame-ancestors 'self'` only on `/api/files/:id`). Reviewer sign-off is recommended.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GhHDC6tJyJUb47XEBxHcZJ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/dev/dev-log.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a968fd-48d7-4da9-a01e-aaa2035d3ca9","uuid":"6fac722a-3534-4672-8cce-248a6f876ef2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:05:46.400Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/dev/dev-log.md","content":"# Dev Log — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)\n\n> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-7 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-7's).\n> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-9. This is SH-9's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)\n\nAll 26 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in\n`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 55 matrix paths were verified on disk (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is deleted as planned).\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Environment fixes (x-internals override, vitest import, delete tmp config) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Prisma schema + migration add_assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: grading-math.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: nextTeachingDayDueAt in src/lib/dates.ts + DST tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: Publishable type widened + 4 notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: assignments-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: reminders.ts + dispatcher hook — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: assignment/submission file resolvers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: course/assignment/duplicate route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: submission/grading route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: /api/me/assignments + /api/students/[id]/assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: next.config.js header split (D11) — ✓ compl