O_GRADE list** is capped at 200 rows (`ponytail:` note). The manager course table pages client-side (`ponytail:` note).\n9. `GET /api/assignments/:id` also returns `studentId` (the viewed child), so parent links stay on the same child.\n\n### Pre-existing issues seen (not caused by SH-9 and not in scope)\n- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 2 failures (FR-22 notification count, FR-10/FR-19 EXCUSED save). These exercise attendance code that SH-9 doesn't touch. They look time-of-day dependent.\n- `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx` (focus assertion), `tests/unit/useToast.test.tsx` (timer/provider), and `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts` (next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM) fail.\n  None of them import SH-9 code. There is no baseline to compare against, because the old `vitest/config.js` import couldn't load at all (blocker 3, now fixed).\n- `next build` prints \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines for every existing GET route. That's build-time log noise, not a failure. `/api/me/assignments` is marked `force-dynamic` to stay quiet.\n- **A stale `next-server` from 27 Oct (PID 63666) is still listening on :3000 for this project, serving old code.** Playwright's `reuseExistingServer` would reuse it, so e2e was run on :3100.\n  I didn't kill it. Restart it before manual testing or QA.\n- The repo's git root is the home directory and the whole project is untracked, so `git stash`/diff can't serve as a baseline.\n\n### Known gaps carried forward (from the design; not new scope)\n- There's no `studentTabs` renderer, so `/students/[id]/assignments` is reachable by URL only (FR-41, blocker 5).\n- The platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true` (ADR-4).\n- D11 changes a security header narrowly (`X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + `frame-ancestors 'self'` only on `/api/files/:id`). Reviewer sign-off is recommended.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":86,"newStart":1,"newLines":81,"lines":["-# Dev Log — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)","+# Dev Log — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)"," ","-> The previous content of this file was a stale SH-4 log. Per the dev-planning note","-> (\"Stale SH-1 artifacts under artifacts/dev/ must be regenerated, not reused\") it was","-> replaced. This is SH-7's first dev iteration.","+> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-7 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-7's).","+> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-9. This is SH-9's first dev iteration."," ","-## Iteration 1 (2026-11-06)","+## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)"," ","-All 19 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 36 owned files exist.","+All 26 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in","+`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 55 matrix paths were verified on disk (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is deleted as planned)."," "," ### Checklist","-- TASK-1: Prisma schema + attendance migration (CHECK + 2 partial unique indexes) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-2: Zod validators (src/lib/validators/attendance.ts) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-3: 4 attendance notification types — ✓ complete","-- TASK-4: Settings input + PATCH /api/settings/school — ✓ complete","-- TASK-5: Pure rules module + unit tests — ✓ complete","-- TASK-6: getSchoolScheduleForDate in the timetable service — ✓ complete","-- TASK-7: Attendance service — ✓ complete","-- TASK-8: Integration tests (attendance-service) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-9: Teacher API routes (today, register GET/PUT) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-10: Student/course attendance API routes — ✓ complete","-- TASK-11: Admin API routes (overview, report+CSV, below-threshold, remind) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-12: RegisterForm client component — ✓ complete","-- TASK-13: Take pages + DateNav — ✓ complete","-- TASK-14: Student Attendance tab — ✓ complete","-- TASK-15: Course Attendance tab (matrix) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-16: Admin attendance page (Today / Report / Below threshold / Settings) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-17: Tab + navigation config entries — ✓ complete","-- TASK-18: Seed attendance (mulberry32, idempotent) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-19: Playwright e2e at 375×667 — ✓ complete (file written and run; see verification for which assertions were proven)","+- TASK-1: Environment fixes (x-internals override, vitest import, delete tmp config) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-2: Prisma schema + migration add_assignments — ✓ complete","+- TASK-3: grading-math.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-4: nextTeachingDayDueAt in src/lib/dates.ts + DST tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-5: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-6: Publishable type widened + 4 notification types — ✓ complete","+- TASK-7: assignments-service.ts — ✓ complete","+- TASK-8: reminders.ts + dispatcher hook — ✓ complete","+- TASK-9: assignment/submission file resolvers — ✓ complete","+- TASK-10: course/assignment/duplicate route handlers — ✓ complete","+- TASK-11: submission/grading route handlers — ✓ complete","+- TASK-12: /api/me/assignments + /api/students/[id]/assignments — ✓ complete","+- TASK-13: next.config.js header split (D11) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-14: MarkdownView + MarkdownEditor — ✓ complete","+- TASK-15: FileUpload + FileList — ✓ complete","+- TASK-16: course-tabs / navigation / student-tabs entries — ✓ complete","+- TASK-17: RubricBuilder — ✓ complete","+- TASK-18: AssignmentForm + new/edit pages — ✓ complete","+- TASK-19: AssignmentList — ✓ complete","+- TASK-20: Course Assignments tab + CourseAssignmentsTable — ✓ complete","+- TASK-21: Assignment page + SubmissionPanel — ✓ complete","+- TASK-22: Grading page + GradingWorkspace — ✓ complete","+- TASK-23: /assignments + /students/[id]/assignments pages — ✓ complete","+- TASK-24: Idempotent FR-61 seed block — ✓ complete","+- TASK-25: Integration tests (submissions, grading, reminders) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-26: Playwright e2e — ✓ complete"," ","-### Implementation notes","-- **Migration (TASK-1).** Generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel`, the equivalent of `--create-only` with no shadow DB. The diff is additive only. The CHECK constraint and the two partial unique indexes were then appended by hand. Applied to the local DB with `migrate deploy`.","-- **Service, outside Next (TASK-7).** The service does not import `services/settings.ts`, because its `react.cache` is undefined outside Next (the same pattern as the timetable service). It reads the settings row directly instead.","-- **Service, saving a register.** `saveRegister` runs one interactive transaction:","-  - It checks the active-on-date roster (`invalidStudentIds`) and requires the full roster (`missingStudentIds`).","-  - It does find-or-create of the session, then the diff writes.","-  - A P2002 error aborts a Postgres transaction, so a re-read inside the same transaction is impossible. The P2002 race (ADR-3) is therefore handled by re-running the transaction once; the retry's `findFirst` sees the winning session.","-  - Audit and notifications run after commit.","-- **Service, enrollment dates.** Enrollment dates for the active-on-date rule are compared at the start of the next day in the school timezone (`fromZonedTime`).","-- **`getToday` date parameter.** `getToday` takes an optional `date` so the landing page's DatePicker works. `/api/attendance/today` still uses today, matching the contract.","-- **Report and below-threshold pagination.** Both group the rows in SQL (`groupBy`), then paginate in memory. This is marked with a `ponytail:` comment; its ceiling is the student count.","-- **Tooltip accessibility.** The calendar day Tooltip uses `describeChild`. Without it, MUI sets the tooltip text as the day button's aria-label, which hides the day number from assistive tech.","-- **NFR-6.** Before the UI work (TASK-12 to TASK-16), mui-mcp was reached:","-  - `useMuiDocs` for `@mui/material@9.5.0` and `@mui/x-date-pickers`.","-  - `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup, ToggleButton, Tabs and DateCalendar (the custom `day` slot).","-  - The v9 upgrade guide was also read.","-  - The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props, `slotProps.htmlInput`/`inputLabel`, `Tab` only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.","-- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).","-  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.","-  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.","-  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%.","+### Verification run this iteration","+| Check | Result |","+|---|---|","+| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |","+| `npm run lint` | No ESLint warnings or errors |","+| Unit: `tests/unit/assignments/*`, `tests/unit/dates.test.ts` | 29 / 29 pass |","+| Integration: `tests/integration/assignments/*` (`TEST_DATABASE_URL` = local Postgres :5433, tagged fixtures, cleaned up) | 14 / 14 pass; 3 consecutive full-folder runs green |","+| `npm run build` | **passes** (needs network access for `next/font` Google Fonts) |","+| e2e `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` against a fresh `next start -p 3100` | 5 / 5 pass |","+| Seed: run twice against temporary MATH-7A/ELA-7A/SCI-7A courses | 7 created, then 0 (idempotent); missing courses skip with a log line. Temp data removed. |","+| Migration `20261109000000_add_assignments` | applied with `prisma migrate deploy`; additive only (no DROP/ALTER of existing tables) |","+| NFR-6 mui-mcp gate | reachable. `useMuiDocs` (material-ui 9.5.0 llms.txt) + `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup and LinearProgress. Other components follow existing in-repo v9 usage. |"," ","-### Verification","-- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.","-- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:","-  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.","-  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.","-  - Rate, day colour and validators.","-- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:","-  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).","-  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.","-  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.","-  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.","-  - Homeroom-only daily register.","-  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.","-  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.","-- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:","-  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).","-  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.","-- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:","-  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".","-  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.","-  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2).","+### Decisions and deviations (for QA / reviewer)","+1. **ADR-2 is not enough on its own — follow-up fix in `next.config.js`.** With `@mui/x-internals` pinned to 9.1.0 (`npm ls` shows 9.1.0 everywhere), `next build` still failed with","+   `'useFirstRender' is not exported`. Root cause: webpack resolves `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender` to its **CJS** build. That build re-exports through `Object.keys`, which webpack can't analyse statically,","+   so x-data-grid's `export *` of it breaks. Fix: one `webpack()` alias that points that specifier at the ESM file (commented, removable on a MUI X upgrade). With the alias,","+   DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9) build, so **no D2 fallbacks were needed**. This touches `next.config.js`, which the plan gives to TASK-13. It's logged here as part of TASK-1's environment fix.","+   The pin is kept, because the alias targets the 9.1.0 file.","+2. **Decimal source:** `grading-math.ts` imports `Decimal` from `@prisma/client/runtime/index-browser.js`, which is Prisma's bundled decimal.js. The plain `decimal.js` package is only a transitive","+   **devDependency** (via jsdom), so it would be missing in a production install. ADR-1 (no new dependencies) holds. Values go to Prisma as 2 dp strings, so the two Decimal classes never mix.","+3. **Decimal serialization:** done in explicit typed mappers (`serializeDecimal` helper → `\"14.40\"`), not a generic walker. Same output as D5.","+4. **`GET /api/me/assignments`:** when `tab` is omitted, all rows come back, each with its server-computed `group`. The `/assignments` page groups them on the client (one fetch for all four tabs). With `tab`, the filter works as contracted.","+   The contract said `default UPCOMING`.","+5. **DateTimePicker + school timezone:** `AdapterDateFns` has no timezone support. The form converts UTC ↔ school wall clock with `toZonedTime`/`fromZonedTime` (NFR-9).","+6. **Reminders robustness:** `claim()` treats P2003 (assignment hard-deleted mid-pass) like P2002. Found because the global pass touched another test's assignment during parallel runs.","+7. **Rubric edits keep criterion ids** (upsert by id), so saved `rubricScores` stay valid after an edit.","+8. **TO_GRADE list** is capped at 200 rows (`ponytail:` note). The manager course table pages client-side (`ponytail:` note).","+9. `GET /api/assignments/:id` also returns `studentId` (the viewed child), so parent links stay on the same child."," ","-### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)","-1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.","-2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:","-   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.","-   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.","-   - I tried `x-internals@9.14.0` (`--no-save`). That only moves the error to `@mui/x-virtualizer` 9.0.0-alpha.8, which wants `isFirefox` from `x-internals/platform`.","-   - I restored 9.15.0; `package-lock.json` is unchanged. A proper fix is to align the MUI X versions in package.json/lockfile, which is a dependency change outside this ticket.","-3. **vitest config.** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve, so `npm test` fails to start. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (same config, `vitest/config`) works.","-4. **No 7A/7B data.** There is no seed or dev data for sections, courses or the timetable, so the attendance seed is a no-op on this DB until PRD-05/06 data exists. The e2e creates its own fixtures, so it doesn't depend on that data.","-5. **Student tabs are never rendered.** `studentTabs` is not rendered by any page; it is an extension point only. The Attendance entry is registered, but the student pages have no tab bar to show it. Not in this ticket's scope.","-6. **Unrelated server on :3000.** A stale `next dev` from 2026-10-27 is running on :3000. I did not touch it. All runs used :3100.","+### Pre-existing issues seen (not caused by SH-9 and not in scope)","+- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 2 failures (FR-22 notification count, FR-10/FR-19 EXCUSED save). These exercise attendance code that SH-9 doesn't touch. They look time-of-day dependent.","+- `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx` (focus assertion), `tests/unit/useToast.test.tsx` (timer/provider), and `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts` (next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM) fail.","+  None of them import SH-9 code. There is no baseline to compare against, because the old `vitest/config.js` import couldn't load at all (blocker 3, now fixed).","+- `next build` prints \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines for every existing GET route. That's build-time log noise, not a failure. `/api/me/assignments` is marked `force-dynamic` to stay quiet.","+- **A stale `next-server` from 27 Oct (PID 63666) is still listening on :3000 for this project, serving old code.** Playwright's `reuseExistingServer` would reuse it, so e2e was run on :3100.","+  I didn't kill it. Restart it before manual testing or QA.","+- The repo's git root is the home directory and the whole project is untracked, so `git stash`/diff can't serve as a baseline.","+","+### Known gaps carried forward (from the design; not new scope)","+- There's no `studentTabs` renderer, so `/students/[id]/assignments` is reachable by URL only (FR-41, blocker 5).","+- The platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true` (ADR-4).","+- D11 changes a security header narrowly (`X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + `frame-ancestors 'self'` only on `/api/files/:id`). Reviewer sign-off is recommended."]}],"originalFile":"# Dev Log — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)\n\n> The previous content of this file was a stale SH-4 log. Per the dev-planning note\n> (\"Stale SH-1 artifacts under artifacts/dev/ must be regenerated, not reused\") it was\n> replaced. This is SH-7's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-06)\n\nAll 19 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 36 owned files exist.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma schema + attendance migration (CHECK + 2 partial unique indexes) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Zod validators (src/lib/validators/attendance.ts) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: 4 attendance notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Settings input + PATCH /api/settings/school — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Pure rules module + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: getSchoolScheduleForDate in the timetable service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: Attendance service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: Integration tests (attendance-service) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: Teacher API routes (today, register GET/PUT) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: Student/course attendance API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Admin API routes (overview, report+CSV, below-threshold, remind) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: RegisterForm client component — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Take pages + DateNav — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: Student Attendance tab — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: Course Attendance tab (matrix) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: Admin attendance page (Today / Report / Below threshold / Settings) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: Tab + navigation config entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: Seed attendance (mulberry32, idempotent) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Playwright e2e at 375×667 — ✓ complete (file written and run; see verification for which assertions were proven)\n\n### Implementation notes\n- **Migration (TASK-1).** Generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel`, the equivalent of `--create-only` with no shadow DB. The diff is additive only. The CHECK constraint and the two partial unique indexes were then appended by hand. Applied to the local DB with `migrate deploy`.\n- **Service, outside Next (TASK-7).** The service does not import `services/settings.ts`, because its `react.cache` is undefined outside Next (the same pattern as the timetable service). It reads the settings row directly instead.\n- **Service, saving a register.** `saveRegister` runs one interactive transaction:\n  - It checks the active-on-date roster (`invalidStudentIds`) and requires the full roster (`missingStudentIds`).\n  - It does find-or-create of the session, then the diff writes.\n  - A P2002 error aborts a Postgres transaction, so a re-read inside the same transaction is impossible. The P2002 race (ADR-3) is therefore handled by re-running the transaction once; the retry's `findFirst` sees the winning session.\n  - Audit and notifications run after commit.\n- **Service, enrollment dates.** Enrollment dates for the active-on-date rule are compared at the start of the next day in the school timezone (`fromZonedTime`).\n- **`getToday` date parameter.** `getToday` takes an optional `date` so the landing page's DatePicker works. `/api/attendance/today` still uses today, matching the contract.\n- **Report and below-threshold pagination.** Both group the rows in SQL (`groupBy`), then paginate in memory. This is marked with a `ponytail:` comment; its ceiling is the student count.\n- **Tooltip accessibility.** The calendar day Tooltip uses `describeChild`. Without it, MUI sets the tooltip text as the day button's aria-label, which hides the day number from assistive tech.\n- **NFR-6.** Before the UI work (TASK-12 to TASK-16), mui-mcp was reached:\n  - `useMuiDocs` for `@mui/material@9.5.0` and `@mui/x-date-pickers`.\n  - `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup, ToggleButton, Tabs and DateCalendar (the custom `day` slot).\n  - The v9 upgrade guide was also read.\n  - The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props, `slotProps.htmlInput`/`inputLabel`, `Tab` only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.\n- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).\n  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.\n  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.\n  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%.\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:\n  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.\n  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.\n  - Rate, day colour and validators.\n- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:\n  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).\n  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.\n  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.\n  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.\n  - Homeroom-only daily register.\n  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.\n  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.\n- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).\n  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.\n- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:\n  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".\n  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.\n  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2).\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)\n1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.\n2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:\n   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.\n   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.\n   - I tried `x-internals@9.14.0` (`--no-save`). That only moves the error to `@mui/x-virtualizer` 9.0.0-alpha.8, which wants `isFirefox` from `x-internals/platform`.\n   - I restored 9.15.0; `package-lock.json` is unchanged. A proper fix is to align the MUI X versions in package.json/lockfile, which is a dependency change outside this ticket.\n3. **vitest config.** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve, so `npm test` fails to start. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (same config, `vitest/config`) works.\n4. **No 7A/7B data.** There is no seed or dev data for sections, courses or the timetable, so the attendance seed is a no-op on this DB until PRD-05/06 data exists. The e2e creates its own fixtures, so it doesn't depend on that data.\n5. **Student tabs are never rendered.** `studentTabs` is not rendered by any page; it is an extension point only. The Attendance entry is registered, but the student pages have no tab bar to show it. Not in this ticket's scope.\n6. **Unrelated server on :3000.** A stale `next dev` from 2026-10-27 is running on :3000. I did not touch it. All runs used :3100.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GhHDC6tJyJUb47XEBxHcZJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
