{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrrLmYuv3qAntf7HzAqK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SH-9 dev phase is finished: all 26 tasks are implemented, every file in the ownership matrix is in place, and all 26 are marked complete in `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json`.\n\n**Test and build results:**\n- Typecheck and lint are clean.\n- The 43 new unit and integration tests pass. The integration tests ran against your local Postgres; their test data is removed afterwards.\n- The production build now passes. It needs network access to download Google Fonts.\n- The end-to-end test passes 5/5: teacher creates an assignment with a rubric → student uploads a file → teacher grades with the rubric and returns it → student sees the score and feedback → parent sees the missing assignment.\n- The seed creates the 7 demo assignments and is safe to re-run. It skips cleanly when MATH-7A, ENG-7A or SCI-7A don't exist, which is the case in your current database.\n\n**Things to know:**\n1. **The planned fix for the MUI X break didn't work on its own.** With the version pin, the build still failed. The cause is how webpack loads one MUI X internal file (`useFirstRender`). I added a short, commented alias in `next.config.js` that fixes it, so the data table and date picker both work and no fallback UI was needed. That file belonged to a different task in the plan; the change is noted in the log.\n2. **A two-week-old `next-server` (PID 63666) is still running on port 3000 for this project, serving old code.** The e2e setup would reuse it, so I ran on port 3100 instead and left it alone. Restart it before QA or manual testing.\n3. **Some existing tests fail, but none of them touch SH-9 code:** two in `attendance-qa`, plus `auth-forms`, `useToast` and `lockout`. I couldn't compare against a \"before\" run: the old vitest config couldn't load at all (that was blocker 3, now fixed), and the git repo root is your home directory with the whole project untracked.\n4. **Smaller differences from the design:**\n   - Decimal math uses the copy bundled inside Prisma. The standalone `decimal.js` package is only present through a dev dependency, so it would be missing in production.\n   - `/api/me/assignments` returns every row when no tab is given; the contract said it should default to Upcoming.\n   - The reminder job now skips an assignment deleted mid-run instead of aborting. Parallel test runs exposed this.\n5. **Reviewer sign-off is still recommended** for the narrow header change that lets PDFs preview in an iframe (only on `/api/files/:id`). The student assignments page is still reachable only by URL, because nothing renders student tabs yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":355,"cache_read_input_tokens":332039,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":355},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a968fd-48d7-4da9-a01e-aaa2035d3ca9","uuid":"87551181-6c00-4e65-9dc8-1bcea6a52481","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:06:12.697Z","request_id":"req_011CgrrLmHnxaLa4YESx7Y5F"}
