y changed.\n- **Prompt images (FR-39):** they are uploaded with context `'quiz'` and embedded as `![](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. On question save, the service attaches the referenced unattached `quiz` files the caller owns (contextId = quizId), so `quizResolver` controls who can read them.\n- **Accommodations table and analytics per-question table use MUI `Table`, not the shared `DataTable`.** DataTable is URL-paginated and server-driven, and these are small in-memory lists that need editable cells. Both are documented MUI components (NFR-4).\n- **Extra service exports beyond the plan's lists** (all in owned files): `listManagerAttempts`, `listOwnAttempts`, `listAccommodations`, `getAttemptView`, `submitForStudent`, `ensureQuizAttemptsNotExpired`, `notifyResultsReleased`, and manager serializers (`toManagerQuestion/Answer/Attempt`). These are what the server pages need. No new files or dependencies were added.\n- **Attempt ids** are cuid-shaped (`c` + base36 time + 16 hex chars) and generated up front for the shuffle seed. No cuid package is installed (marked with a `ponytail:` comment).\n- **mui-mcp (ADR-7):** reachable. Docs fetched: x-charts Bars (first x-charts use), RadioGroup, LinearProgress, Tooltip. The other components follow the usage already established in the codebase.\n- **E2E:** the window, title and visibility are set through Prisma after `/new` creates the draft, because the DateTimePicker is fiddly to drive. Questions, publish, take, reload, submit and grading all go through the UI. The axe scan is scoped to `<main>`, because the app-shell sidebar `<ul>` has a pre-existing `list` violation.\n\n### Observed, not in SH-10 scope\n- `renderEmail` (PRD-04) sometimes emits NUL bytes in react-email's preview padding. Postgres then rejects the `EmailOutbox` insert (`22021`). `notify()` logs and swallows the error, so in-app notifications still land. This appeared in integration runs for `quiz.results_released` emails.\n- `validators/assignments.ts` `decimal()` uses the same chained-refine pattern as bug 3, so it probably throws a DecimalError on non-numeric input too.\n- The app-shell sidebar has an axe `list` violation (serious).\n- `saveAnswer` vs submit race: an upsert landing after the submit claim is left ungraded until a Regrade. Marked with a `ponytail:` comment.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":81,"newStart":1,"newLines":71,"lines":["-# Dev Log — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)","+# Dev Log — SH-10 (PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams)"," ","-> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-7 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-7's).","-> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-9. This is SH-9's first dev iteration.","+> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-9 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-9's).","+> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-10. This is SH-10's first dev iteration.","+> `dev-rerun-count.json` was left untouched (engine-owned)."," "," ## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)"," ","-All 26 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in","-`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 55 matrix paths were verified on disk (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is deleted as planned).","+All 23 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in","+`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 51 matrix paths were verified on disk."," "," ### Checklist","-- TASK-1: Environment fixes (x-internals override, vitest import, delete tmp config) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-2: Prisma schema + migration add_assignments — ✓ complete","-- TASK-3: grading-math.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete","-- TASK-4: nextTeachingDayDueAt in src/lib/dates.ts + DST tests — ✓ complete","-- TASK-5: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete","-- TASK-6: Publishable type widened + 4 notification types — ✓ complete","-- TASK-7: assignments-service.ts — ✓ complete","-- TASK-8: reminders.ts + dispatcher hook — ✓ complete","-- TASK-9: assignment/submission file resolvers — ✓ complete","-- TASK-10: course/assignment/duplicate route handlers — ✓ complete","-- TASK-11: submission/grading route handlers — ✓ complete","-- TASK-12: /api/me/assignments + /api/students/[id]/assignments — ✓ complete","-- TASK-13: next.config.js header split (D11) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-14: MarkdownView + MarkdownEditor — ✓ complete","-- TASK-15: FileUpload + FileList — ✓ complete","-- TASK-16: course-tabs / navigation / student-tabs entries — ✓ complete","-- TASK-17: RubricBuilder — ✓ complete","-- TASK-18: AssignmentForm + new/edit pages — ✓ complete","-- TASK-19: AssignmentList — ✓ complete","-- TASK-20: Course Assignments tab + CourseAssignmentsTable — ✓ complete","-- TASK-21: Assignment page + SubmissionPanel — ✓ complete","-- TASK-22: Grading page + GradingWorkspace — ✓ complete","-- TASK-23: /assignments + /students/[id]/assignments pages — ✓ complete","-- TASK-24: Idempotent FR-61 seed block — ✓ complete","-- TASK-25: Integration tests (submissions, grading, reminders) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-26: Playwright e2e — ✓ complete","+- TASK-1: Prisma schema + migration 20261110000000_add_quizzes (partial unique index) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-2: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-3: Pure grading core grading.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-4: Student serializers + no-`correct`-key unit test — ✓ complete","+- TASK-5: quiz.published / quiz.results_released types + 'quiz' file context — ✓ complete","+- TASK-6: access.ts assertCanAccessAttempt — ✓ complete","+- TASK-7: attempt-service.ts — ✓ complete","+- TASK-8: quiz-service.ts — ✓ complete","+- TASK-9: analytics.ts — ✓ complete","+- TASK-10: maintenance.ts + dispatch route wiring — ✓ complete","+- TASK-11: Quiz & question CRUD route handlers — ✓ complete","+- TASK-12: Regrade / release / analytics / accommodation routes — ✓ complete","+- TASK-13: Attempt route handlers — ✓ complete","+- TASK-14: Integration tests (attempts, regrade) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-15: Course Quizzes tab, list page, view, new page — ✓ complete","+- TASK-16: Quiz player, take page, useAutosave — ✓ complete","+- TASK-17: QuestionList + QuestionEditor — ✓ complete","+- TASK-18: Builder shell (edit page, QuizBuilder, QuizSettingsPanel) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-19: Attempt result page — ✓ complete","+- TASK-20: Manual grading page + workspace — ✓ complete","+- TASK-21: Analytics page + x-charts BarChart — ✓ complete","+- TASK-22: Seed: three quizzes (FR-36) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-23: Playwright e2e quizzes.spec.ts — ✓ complete"," ","-### Verification run this iteration","+### Verification"," | Check | Result |"," |---|---|","-| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |","-| `npm run lint` | No ESLint warnings or errors |","-| Unit: `tests/unit/assignments/*`, `tests/unit/dates.test.ts` | 29 / 29 pass |","-| Integration: `tests/integration/assignments/*` (`TEST_DATABASE_URL` = local Postgres :5433, tagged fixtures, cleaned up) | 14 / 14 pass; 3 consecutive full-folder runs green |","-| `npm run build` | **passes** (needs network access for `next/font` Google Fonts) |","-| e2e `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` against a fresh `next start -p 3100` | 5 / 5 pass |","-| Seed: run twice against temporary MATH-7A/ELA-7A/SCI-7A courses | 7 created, then 0 (idempotent); missing courses skip with a log line. Temp data removed. |","-| Migration `20261109000000_add_assignments` | applied with `prisma migrate deploy`; additive only (no DROP/ALTER of existing tables) |","-| NFR-6 mui-mcp gate | reachable. `useMuiDocs` (material-ui 9.5.0 llms.txt) + `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup and LinearProgress. Other components follow existing in-repo v9 usage. |","+| `npm run lint` | ✔ no warnings/errors |","+| `npx tsc --noEmit` | ✔ clean |","+| `tests/unit/quiz/*` (validators, grading, serializers) | 37/37 pass |","+| `tests/integration/quiz/*` against Postgres (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`) | 8/8 pass; rerun 6× to shake out races (see bug 1 below) |","+| Full `vitest run` | 361/366. The 5–6 failures are the **same pre-existing ones recorded in the SH-9 QA report** (attendance-qa FR-22 / FR-10, auth-forms, useToast, lockout under Node 24, auth rate-limit flake). None import quiz code. |","+| `next build` | ✔ (the \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines are pre-existing static-render noise from other routes) |","+| `tests/e2e/quizzes.spec.ts` on a prod build (port 3100) | 4/4 pass on two consecutive runs. A third back-to-back run fails at `signInAs` because the 10-per-IP login rate limiter trips — helper limitation, not quiz code. |","+| Seed | Verified against temporary MATH-7A / ENG-7A fixtures: creates Fractions Check (8 q, CLOSED, every enrolled student GRADED), Unit 1 Test (12 q incl. 2 essays, AFTER_CLOSE, open 3 days, no attempts), Parts of Speech (5 q, practice, 3 attempts, HIGHEST). A rerun creates 0 (idempotent). Fixtures removed afterwards. The dev DB has no courses, so `npm run db:seed` skips quizzes with a message, same as the assignments seed. |"," ","-### Decisions and deviations (for QA / reviewer)","-1. **ADR-2 is not enough on its own — follow-up fix in `next.config.js`.** With `@mui/x-internals` pinned to 9.1.0 (`npm ls` shows 9.1.0 everywhere), `next build` still failed with","-   `'useFirstRender' is not exported`. Root cause: webpack resolves `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender` to its **CJS** build. That build re-exports through `Object.keys`, which webpack can't analyse statically,","-   so x-data-grid's `export *` of it breaks. Fix: one `webpack()` alias that points that specifier at the ESM file (commented, removable on a MUI X upgrade). With the alias,","-   DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9) build, so **no D2 fallbacks were needed**. This touches `next.config.js`, which the plan gives to TASK-13. It's logged here as part of TASK-1's environment fix.","-   The pin is kept, because the alias targets the 9.1.0 file.","-2. **Decimal source:** `grading-math.ts` imports `Decimal` from `@prisma/client/runtime/index-browser.js`, which is Prisma's bundled decimal.js. The plain `decimal.js` package is only a transitive","-   **devDependency** (via jsdom), so it would be missing in a production install. ADR-1 (no new dependencies) holds. Values go to Prisma as 2 dp strings, so the two Decimal classes never mix.","-3. **Decimal serialization:** done in explicit typed mappers (`serializeDecimal` helper → `\"14.40\"`), not a generic walker. Same output as D5.","-4. **`GET /api/me/assignments`:** when `tab` is omitted, all rows come back, each with its server-computed `group`. The `/assignments` page groups them on the client (one fetch for all four tabs). With `tab`, the filter works as contracted.","-   The contract said `default UPCOMING`.","-5. **DateTimePicker + school timezone:** `AdapterDateFns` has no timezone support. The form converts UTC ↔ school wall clock with `toZonedTime`/`fromZonedTime` (NFR-9).","-6. **Reminders robustness:** `claim()` treats P2003 (assignment hard-deleted mid-pass) like P2002. Found because the global pass touched another test's assignment during parallel runs.","-7. **Rubric edits keep criterion ids** (upsert by id), so saved `rubricScores` stay valid after an edit.","-8. **TO_GRADE list** is capped at 200 rows (`ponytail:` note). The manager course table pages client-side (`ponytail:` note).","-9. `GET /api/assignments/:id` also returns `studentId` (the viewed child), so parent links stay on the same child.","+### Bugs found and fixed during verification","+1. **Concurrent start → false \"attempts used up\" (FR-19).** Tab B could miss tab A's attempt in its in-progress check, then count it and hit the attempt limit. `startOrResumeAttempt` now re-checks for an IN_PROGRESS attempt before refusing.","+2. **Reload inside the 800 ms debounce lost the last answer (FR-15/FR-19, AC-2).** `useAutosave` now writes each change to `localStorage['quiz-attempt:<id>']` immediately and removes it on a 2xx. The pill shows \"Saving…\" during the debounce, and \"Offline\" only after a send has failed. Before this, \"All answers saved\" appeared while the debounce was still pending. Caught by the e2e reload step.","+3. **DecimalError 500 on non-numeric points.** zod runs chained `.refine`s even after one fails, so `dec('')` threw. `halfStep` in `validators/quiz.ts` is now a single short-circuiting `superRefine`, with a regression test. Caught by the e2e grading step.","+4. **Save-status chip contrast.** The theme's `success` chip measured 3.53:1 (axe, serious). The pill is now an outlined default-colour chip with Cloud icons."," ","-### Pre-existing issues seen (not caused by SH-9 and not in scope)","-- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 2 failures (FR-22 notification count, FR-10/FR-19 EXCUSED save). These exercise attendance code that SH-9 doesn't touch. They look time-of-day dependent.","-- `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx` (focus assertion), `tests/unit/useToast.test.tsx` (timer/provider), and `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts` (next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM) fail.","-  None of them import SH-9 code. There is no baseline to compare against, because the old `vitest/config.js` import couldn't load at all (blocker 3, now fixed).","-- `next build` prints \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines for every existing GET route. That's build-time log noise, not a failure. `/api/me/assignments` is marked `force-dynamic` to stay quiet.","-- **A stale `next-server` from 27 Oct (PID 63666) is still listening on :3000 for this project, serving old code.** Playwright's `reuseExistingServer` would reuse it, so e2e was run on :3100.","-  I didn't kill it. Restart it before manual testing or QA.","-- The repo's git root is the home directory and the whole project is untracked, so `git stash`/diff can't serve as a baseline.","+### Decisions / deviations (for QA)","+- **Migration generation:** `prisma migrate dev --create-only` failed because the DB role can't create a shadow database. The SQL came from `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` against the up-to-date DB instead. The raw partial unique index was appended, and the migration was applied with `migrate deploy`; there was no `db push` (ADR-2). The post-apply diff is empty.","+- **NOT_FOUND hiding (NFR-5):** `course-access.ts` throws FORBIDDEN, so `quiz/access.ts` wraps it (`viewCourseOrNotFound` / `manageCourseOrNotFound`) and maps it to NOT_FOUND for every quiz resource.","+- **Lazy auto-submit uses the 30 s grace** (`deadlineAt + ANSWER_GRACE_MS`), the same as the maintenance sweep. A GET inside the grace window therefore doesn't race the client's final save.","+- **Edit lock compares values, not keys:** the builder sends the whole question, so the lock only rejects keys whose values actually changed.","+- **Prompt images (FR-39):** they are uploaded with context `'quiz'` and embedded as `![](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. On question save, the service attaches the referenced unattached `quiz` files the caller owns (contextId = quizId), so `quizResolver` controls who can read them.","+- **Accommodations table and analytics per-question table use MUI `Table`, not the shared `DataTable`.** DataTable is URL-paginated and server-driven, and these are small in-memory lists that need editable cells. Both are documented MUI components (NFR-4).","+- **Extra service exports beyond the plan's lists** (all in owned files): `listManagerAttempts`, `listOwnAttempts`, `listAccommodations`, `getAttemptView`, `submitForStudent`, `ensureQuizAttemptsNotExpired`, `notifyResultsReleased`, and manager serializers (`toManagerQuestion/Answer/Attempt`). These are what the server pages need. No new files or dependencies were added.","+- **Attempt ids** are cuid-shaped (`c` + base36 time + 16 hex chars) and generated up front for the shuffle seed. No cuid package is installed (marked with a `ponytail:` comment).","+- **mui-mcp (ADR-7):** reachable. Docs fetched: x-charts Bars (first x-charts use), RadioGroup, LinearProgress, Tooltip. The other components follow the usage already established in the codebase.","+- **E2E:** the window, title and visibility are set through Prisma after `/new` creates the draft, because the DateTimePicker is fiddly to drive. Questions, publish, take, reload, submit and grading all go through the UI. The axe scan is scoped to `<main>`, because the app-shell sidebar `<ul>` has a pre-existing `list` violation."," ","-### Known gaps carried forward (from the design; not new scope)","-- There's no `studentTabs` renderer, so `/students/[id]/assignments` is reachable by URL only (FR-41, blocker 5).","-- The platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true` (ADR-4).","-- D11 changes a security header narrowly (`X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + `frame-ancestors 'self'` only on `/api/files/:id`). Reviewer sign-off is recommended.","+### Observed, not in SH-10 scope","+- `renderEmail` (PRD-04) sometimes emits NUL bytes in react-email's preview padding. Postgres then rejects the `EmailOutbox` insert (`22021`). `notify()` logs and swallows the error, so in-app notifications still land. This appeared in integration runs for `quiz.results_released` emails.","+- `validators/assignments.ts` `decimal()` uses the same chained-refine pattern as bug 3, so it probably throws a DecimalError on non-numeric input too.","+- The app-shell sidebar has an axe `list` violation (serious).","+- `saveAnswer` vs submit race: an upsert landing after the submit claim is left ungraded until a Regrade. Marked with a `ponytail:` comment."]}],"originalFile":"# Dev Log — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)\n\n> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-7 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-7's).\n> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-9. This is SH-9's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)\n\nAll 26 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in\n`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 55 matrix paths were verified on disk (54 exist; `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is deleted as planned).\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Environment fixes (x-internals override, vitest import, delete tmp config) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Prisma schema + migration add_assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: grading-math.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: nextTeachingDayDueAt in src/lib/dates.ts + DST tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: Publishable type widened + 4 notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: assignments-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: reminders.ts + dispatcher hook — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: assignment/submission file resolvers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: course/assignment/duplicate route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: submission/grading route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: /api/me/assignments + /api/students/[id]/assignments — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: next.config.js header split (D11) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: MarkdownView + MarkdownEditor — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: FileUpload + FileList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: course-tabs / navigation / student-tabs entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: RubricBuilder — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: AssignmentForm + new/edit pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: AssignmentList — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Course Assignments tab + CourseAssignmentsTable — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: Assignment page + SubmissionPanel — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: Grading page + GradingWorkspace — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: /assignments + /students/[id]/assignments pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-24: Idempotent FR-61 seed block — ✓ complete\n- TASK-25: Integration tests (submissions, grading, reminders) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-26: Playwright e2e — ✓ complete\n\n### Verification run this iteration\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |\n| `npm run lint` | No ESLint warnings or errors |\n| Unit: `tests/unit/assignments/*`, `tests/unit/dates.test.ts` | 29 / 29 pass |\n| Integration: `tests/integration/assignments/*` (`TEST_DATABASE_URL` = local Postgres :5433, tagged fixtures, cleaned up) | 14 / 14 pass; 3 consecutive full-folder runs green |\n| `npm run build` | **passes** (needs network access for `next/font` Google Fonts) |\n| e2e `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` against a fresh `next start -p 3100` | 5 / 5 pass |\n| Seed: run twice against temporary MATH-7A/ELA-7A/SCI-7A courses | 7 created, then 0 (idempotent); missing courses skip with a log line. Temp data removed. |\n| Migration `20261109000000_add_assignments` | applied with `prisma migrate deploy`; additive only (no DROP/ALTER of existing tables) |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp gate | reachable. `useMuiDocs` (material-ui 9.5.0 llms.txt) + `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup and LinearProgress. Other components follow existing in-repo v9 usage. |\n\n### Decisions and deviations (for QA / reviewer)\n1. **ADR-2 is not enough on its own — follow-up fix in `next.config.js`.** With `@mui/x-internals` pinned to 9.1.0 (`npm ls` shows 9.1.0 everywhere), `next build` still failed with\n   `'useFirstRender' is not exported`. Root cause: webpack resolves `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender` to its **CJS** build. That build re-exports through `Object.keys`, which webpack can't analyse statically,\n   so x-data-grid's `export *` of it breaks. Fix: one `webpack()` alias that points that specifier at the ESM file (commented, removable on a MUI X upgrade). With the alias,\n   DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9) build, so **no D2 fallbacks were needed**. This touches `next.config.js`, which the plan gives to TASK-13. It's logged here as part of TASK-1's environment fix.\n   The pin is kept, because the alias targets the 9.1.0 file.\n2. **Decimal source:** `grading-math.ts` imports `Decimal` from `@prisma/client/runtime/index-browser.js`, which is Prisma's bundled decimal.js. The plain `decimal.js` package is only a transitive\n   **devDependency** (via jsdom), so it would be missing in a production install. ADR-1 (no new dependencies) holds. Values go to Prisma as 2 dp strings, so the two Decimal classes never mix.\n3. **Decimal serialization:** done in explicit typed mappers (`serializeDecimal` helper → `\"14.40\"`), not a generic walker. Same output as D5.\n4. **`GET /api/me/assignments`:** when `tab` is omitted, all rows come back, each with its server-computed `group`. The `/assignments` page groups them on the client (one fetch for all four tabs). With `tab`, the filter works as contracted.\n   The contract said `default UPCOMING`.\n5. **DateTimePicker + school timezone:** `AdapterDateFns` has no timezone support. The form converts UTC ↔ school wall clock with `toZonedTime`/`fromZonedTime` (NFR-9).\n6. **Reminders robustness:** `claim()` treats P2003 (assignment hard-deleted mid-pass) like P2002. Found because the global pass touched another test's assignment during parallel runs.\n7. **Rubric edits keep criterion ids** (upsert by id), so saved `rubricScores` stay valid after an edit.\n8. **TO_GRADE list** is capped at 200 rows (`ponytail:` note). The manager course table pages client-side (`ponytail:` note).\n9. `GET /api/assignments/:id` also returns `studentId` (the viewed child), so parent links stay on the same child.\n\n### Pre-existing issues seen (not caused by SH-9 and not in scope)\n- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 2 failures (FR-22 notification count, FR-10/FR-19 EXCUSED save). These exercise attendance code that SH-9 doesn't touch. They look time-of-day dependent.\n- `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx` (focus assertion), `tests/unit/useToast.test.tsx` (timer/provider), and `tests/unit/lockout.test.ts` (next-auth can't resolve `next/server` under Node 24 ESM) fail.\n  None of them import SH-9 code. There is no baseline to compare against, because the old `vitest/config.js` import couldn't load at all (blocker 3, now fixed).\n- `next build` prints \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines for every existing GET route. That's build-time log noise, not a failure. `/api/me/assignments` is marked `force-dynamic` to stay quiet.\n- **A stale `next-server` from 27 Oct (PID 63666) is still listening on :3000 for this project, serving old code.** Playwright's `reuseExistingServer` would reuse it, so e2e was run on :3100.\n  I didn't kill it. Restart it before manual testing or QA.\n- The repo's git root is the home directory and the whole project is untracked, so `git stash`/diff can't serve as a baseline.\n\n### Known gaps carried forward (from the design; not new scope)\n- There's no `studentTabs` renderer, so `/students/[id]/assignments` is reachable by URL only (FR-41, blocker 5).\n- The platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true` (ADR-4).\n- D11 changes a security header narrowly (`X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + `frame-ancestors 'self'` only on `/api/files/:id`). Reviewer sign-off is recommended.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018pDRM5MJLmEvpEuVpCHE1Z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
