{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrzTJjVQX8yDpazWJEEe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SH-10 dev phase is finished: all 23 tasks are built and marked complete, and every one of the 51 file paths in the ownership matrix exists on disk. Lint and typecheck are clean. The quiz unit tests (37/37) and quiz integration tests against Postgres (8/8) pass. The browser end-to-end test passed 4/4 on two runs in a row against a production build.\n\n**What's in place:**\n- **Database:** a migration for the quiz tables, plus a database rule that allows only one in-progress attempt per student per quiz.\n- **Server:** grading, attempts, quiz management, analytics, and a cron job that auto-submits expired attempts and sends \"results released\" notices after a quiz closes.\n- **API:** 14 endpoints.\n- **Screens:** the course \"Quizzes\" tab, the quiz builder with preview, the timed player with autosave, the result page, the grading screen (by student or by question), and analytics with a score chart and CSV export.\n- **Seed data:** three demo quizzes. The dev database has no courses yet, so `npm run db:seed` skips them, just as it skips assignments. I checked the seed against temporary courses, which I then deleted.\n\n**Bugs I found while testing, now fixed:**\n1. If a student opened the quiz in two tabs at once, one tab could wrongly say all attempts were used up. It now picks up the attempt the other tab started.\n2. Reloading the page within 0.8 s of answering lost that last answer, and \"All answers saved\" was showing before anything was saved. Answers are now stored in the browser immediately and the label is accurate.\n3. Typing a non-number into a points box caused a server error (500) instead of a validation message. Fixed, with a regression test.\n4. The green \"All answers saved\" label failed the accessibility contrast check, so it now uses a neutral colour with an icon.\n\n**Things you should know:**\n- **Full test suite:** 361/366 pass. The 5 failures are the same ones the SH-9 QA report recorded as pre-existing (attendance-qa, auth-forms, useToast, lockout, the auth rate-limit test), and none of them touch quiz code.\n- **End-to-end test limits:** a third back-to-back run failed only because the login rate limit (10 sign-ins per IP) kicked in. The test also sets the quiz's open/close dates directly in the database rather than through the date picker. Its accessibility check covers only the main page area, because the existing sidebar fails the check on its own.\n- **How the migration was made:** the database user isn't allowed to create the temporary database `prisma migrate dev` needs. I generated the SQL by comparing the live database to the schema instead, then applied it with `migrate deploy` (never `db push`). A follow-up comparison shows no differences.\n- **Port 3000:** that's a dev server from your `schoolhub-prds` project. I left it alone and ran this app on port 3100.\n\n**Problems outside this ticket, logged in `dev-log.md` but not fixed:**\n- The shared email renderer sometimes produces invalid characters, so some notification emails fail to save. In-app notifications still arrive.\n- The assignments points validator has the same bug as fix 3 above.\n- The sidebar has the accessibility issue mentioned above.\n\nI replaced the leftover SH-9 `dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` with SH-10 versions and didn't touch `dev-rerun-count.json`. The old SH-9 `security-scan-report.json` is still in `artifacts/dev/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3888,"cache_read_input_tokens":363293,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3888,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3eb50254-5396-4c9e-84e7-da065a5fc108","uuid":"fdb77a3f-2d19-4284-9f50-029d1007d1d3","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:52:38.859Z","request_id":"req_011CgrzTJFyQaZ9y9k7NotZj"}
