{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013DDH65K2raNTSx7KAUptZZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n2\t\n3\t**Ticket:** SCH-011 · **Depends on:** PRD-00 – PRD-10 · **Run mode:** `--brownfield --tech-stack react`\n4\t\n5\t## Summary\n6\t\n7\tA unified gradebook per course that pulls in assignment and quiz scores automatically, supports manual grade items (for example an in-class presentation), weighted categories, term grades with a school-wide letter grading scale, teacher overrides and comments. At term end, admins generate report cards that combine every course grade with attendance and comments, review them, publish them to students and parents, and print them.\n8\t\n9\t## Platform Context (shared by every SchoolHub PRD)\n10\t\n11\tSchoolHub is a single-school web platform for administrators, teachers, students and parents. It is built incrementally by a sequence of PRDs (PRD-00 … PRD-18). **When this PRD runs, every lower-numbered PRD is already implemented in the workspace.** Reuse existing models, services, components and helpers — never re-scaffold the project, never duplicate a helper that already exists, never rename existing routes or models.\n12\t\n13\t### Fixed technology decisions\n14\t\n15\t| Concern | Decision |\n16\t|---|---|\n17\t| Framework | Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript `strict: true` |\n18\t| UI components | **Material UI only** — `@mui/material` v9 (+ `@emotion/react`, `@emotion/styled`), `@mui/material-nextjs` (App Router cache provider), `@mui/icons-material`. Every component is looked up through the MUI MCP server first (see \"UI component rule\" below) |\n19\t| Theming | MUI `createTheme` with `cssVariables: true` and light/dark `colorSchemes`, `InitColorSchemeScript`, `useColorScheme()` for the toggle; styling only through the theme, the `sx` prop and `styled()` — no Tailwind, no CSS modules |\n20\t| Dates & pickers | `@mui/x-date-pickers` v9 (MIT) with `AdapterDateFns`; `date-fns` + `date-fns-tz` for logic |\n21\t| Database | PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma ORM (`prisma/schema.prisma`), migrations with `prisma migrate` |\n22\t| Auth | Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy, bcrypt password hashes |\n23\t| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts`, shared by client forms and API handlers |\n24\t| Forms | React Hook Form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` |\n25\t| Data tables | `@mui/x-data-grid` v9 (MIT `DataGrid`, server-side pagination/sorting/filtering) wrapped by the shared `DataTable` component |\n26\t| Charts | `@mui/x-charts` v9 (MIT) |\n27\t| Email | Nodemailer via the `EmailOutbox` table (from PRD-04); dev transport logs to console |\n28\t| Calendar UI | `@mui/x-scheduler` (MIT Community `EventCalendar`; pin the exact version found via the MUI MCP — it is in beta) |\n29\t| Tests | Vitest + Testing Library (unit/integration), Playwright (e2e in `tests/e2e`) |\n30\t| Local infra | `docker-compose.yml` with Postgres; `.env.example` documents every env var |\n31\t\n32\t### UI component rule (mandatory — applies to every screen in this PRD)\n33\t\n34\t1. **Material UI components only.** Every visible UI element is built from `@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material` or the MUI X packages listed above (`@mui/x-data-grid`, `@mui/x-date-pickers`, `@mui/x-charts`, `@mui/x-scheduler`) — composed with `Box`, `Stack`, `Grid` and the theme. Hand-styled raw HTML (`<div>`/`<button>`/`<table>` with custom CSS) is not allowed where an MUI component exists.\n35\t2. **Look up every component through the MUI MCP server (`mui-mcp`) before using it.** Call `useMuiDocs` with the package (for example `@mui/material@9.5.0`, `@mui/x-data-grid`) to get the docs index, then `fetchDocs` on the component's page, and use only props, slots and imports documented there for the installed version. Never write MUI code from memory, and never invent props. If the MCP server is unreachable, stop and report it as a blocker instead of guessing.\n36\t3. **Banned:** Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Radix UI, Headless UI, Chakra UI, Ant Design, Bootstrap, `lucide-react`, `next-themes`, `@tanstack/react-table`, Recharts, FullCalendar, `react-select`, `react-datepicker`, `sonner`, `notistack` and any other component or styling library. PRD-00 enforces this with an ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule.\n37\t4. **Allowed non-visual libraries** (they render no UI of their own): React Hook Form, Zod, `@dnd-kit/core` and `@dnd-kit/sortable` (drag behaviour only — draggable items are MUI components), `react-markdown` + `remark-gfm` + `rehype-sanitize` (every Markdown element is mapped to an MUI component through the `components` prop), `papaparse`, `date-fns`. Email templates (`@react-email/components`) are exempt because email clients cannot render MUI.\n38\t5. Shared wrappers live in `src/components/shared/` and are themselves built from MUI. Toasts use MUI `Snackbar` + `Alert` through the shared `useToast()` hook from PRD-00; side panels use `Drawer`; confirmations use `Dialog`; pickers and searchable selects use `Autocomplete`.\n39\t6. Intake must record this rule as a non-functional requirement, and QA must check it: no banned imports, and every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\n40\t\n41\t### Code layout and conventions\n42\t\n43\t- `src/app/(public)/…` public pages, `src/app/(auth)/…` sign-in flows, `src/app/(app)/…` authenticated app with the shared sidebar shell.\n44\t- `src/app/api/<feature>/…/route.ts` REST route handlers. Handlers are thin: parse with Zod → call a service → return JSON.\n45\t- `src/server/services/<feature>.ts` business logic and Prisma access. Server components may call services directly; client components call the REST API. New features follow PRD-05's precedent of a feature-named subdirectory instead: `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts` (for example `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`), not this older flat path — which remains accurate only for the already-built PRD-02/03-era services that still live there.\n46\t- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` exposes `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)` and per-entity access checks. Every handler and every server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\n47\t- Response shape: success `{ \"data\": … }`; list `{ \"data\": [...], \"page\": 1, \"pageSize\": 20, \"total\": 134 }`; error `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"…\", \"details\": {…} } }`. Error codes: `VALIDATION_ERROR` (400), `UNAUTHENTICATED` (401), `FORBIDDEN` (403), `NOT_FOUND` (404), `CONFLICT` (409), `RATE_LIMITED` (429), `INTERNAL` (500).\n48\t- Pagination: `?page=` (default 1) and `?pageSize=` (default 20, maximum 100). Sorting: `?sort=field&order=asc|desc`. Search: `?q=`.\n49\t- IDs are `cuid()` strings. Every model has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone from `SchoolSettings.timezone`. Date-only values use `@db.Date`.\n50\t- Sidebar navigation lives in `src/config/navigation.ts` as an array of `{ label, href, icon, roles }`. A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry there.\n51\t- Student detail page `/students/[studentId]` is tab-based; tabs are registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts`. Feature PRDs add a tab there instead of creating a separate student page.\n52\t- Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an `AuditLog` row through `audit()` (from PRD-01).\n53\t- Notifications go through `notify()` (from PRD-04). Notification type keys are registered in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`.\n54\t- No `console.log` in committed code except the dev email transport; use the `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts`.\n55\t\n56\t### Roles\n57\t\n58\t`ADMIN` (school office staff and principal), `TEACHER`, `STUDENT`, `PARENT` (parent or guardian). A user has exactly one role. Parents see data only for students linked to them; students see only their own data; teachers see data for courses they teach and sections they are homeroom teacher of; admins see everything.\n59\t\n60\t### Assumptions and constraints\n61\t\n62\t- **Assumptions:** one school per deployment (no multi-tenancy); English-only UI; the school timezone is the reference for every date rule; users have a modern evergreen browser (last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari).\n63\t- **Constraints:** this PRD is delivered in a single forge run, so its scope must not expand beyond the sections below; do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs; keep all existing tests passing (`npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test`) and add the tests listed in this PRD.\n64\t- **Delivery milestones:** Milestone 1 \"Core platform\" = PRD-00 – PRD-05 · Milestone 2 \"Teaching & learning\" = PRD-06 – PRD-11 · Milestone 3 \"Communication\" = PRD-12 – PRD-15 · Milestone 4 \"Operations & public\" = PRD-16 – PRD-18.\n65\t\n66\t## Background\n67\t\n68\tTeachers currently keep grades in personal spreadsheets with differing formulas, and the office retypes everything into report cards each term. One gradebook with consistent calculation removes the retyping and lets families see standing during the term rather than only at the end.\n69\t\n70\t## Goals\n71\t\n72\t1. Every graded assignment and quiz appears in the gradebook without manual entry.\n73\t2. Term grades are computed identically across the school from category weights and the grading scale.\n74\t3. The office generates, reviews and publishes report cards for the whole school in under one hour.\n75\t\n76\t## Out of Scope\n77\t\n78\t- Standards-based grading (mastery per standard).\n79\t- GPA and class rank (future work).\n80\t- Transcript across multiple years.\n81\t\n82\t## User Stories\n83\t\n84\t- As an admin, I want to define the school's grading scale so that letter grades are consistent.\n85\t- As a teacher, I want weighted categories (for example Homework 30 %, Quizzes 30 %, Exams 40 %) so that grades reflect my syllabus.\n86\t- As a teacher, I want a spreadsheet-like gradebook with every student and item so that I can see and edit scores quickly.\n87\t- As a teacher, I want to add manual grade items for offline work so that all assessment is in one place.\n88\t- As a student or parent, I want to see current course grades and individual scores so that we know where the student stands.\n89\t- As an admin, I want to generate, review, publish and print report cards each term so that families receive official results.\n90\t\n91\t## Functional Requirements\n92\t\n93\t### FR-1 Data model\n94\t\n95\t```prisma\n96\tenum GradeItemSource { ASSIGNMENT QUIZ MANUAL }\n97\tenum ReportCardStatus { DRAFT PUBLISHED }\n98\t\n99\tmodel GradingScale {\n100\t  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n101\t  name      String                     // \"Standard A–F\"\n102\t  isDefault Boolean  @default(false)\n103\t  bands     Json                       // [{ letter: \"A\", minPercent: 90, gpa?: 4.0, descriptor: \"Excellent\" }], sorted desc\n104\t  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n105\t  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n106\t}\n107\t\n108\tmodel GradeCategory {\n109\t  id            String   @id @default(cuid())\n110\t  courseId      String\n111\t  course        Course   @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n112\t  name          String                     // \"Homework\"\n113\t  weightPercent Decimal  @db.Decimal(5, 2) // 0–100; a course's categories total 100\n114\t  dropLowest    Int      @default(0)       // drop N lowest scores in this category per student\n115\t  order         Int\n116\t}\n117\t\n118\tmodel GradeItem {\n119\t  id          String          @id @default(cuid())\n120\t  courseId    String\n121\t  course      Course          @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n122\t  categoryId  String?\n123\t  category    GradeCategory?  @relation(fields: [categoryId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n124\t  termId      String\n125\t  term        Term            @relation(fields: [termId], references: [id])\n126\t  title       String\n127\t  maxPoints   Decimal         @db.Decimal(6, 2)\n128\t  dueAt       DateTime?\n129\t  source      GradeItemSource\n130\t  sourceId    String?         @unique       // assignmentId or quizId\n131\t  isVisible   Boolean         @default(true) // hidden items do not show to students/parents and do not count\n132\t  createdAt   DateTime        @default(now())\n133\t  updatedAt   DateTime        @updatedAt\n134\t  grades      Grade[]\n135\t}\n136\t\n137\tmodel Grade {\n138\t  gradeItemId String\n139\t  gradeItem   GradeItem @relation(fields: [gradeItemId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n140\t  studentId   String\n141\t  score       Decimal?  @db.Decimal(6, 2)  // null = not graded yet\n142\t  excused     Boolean   @default(false)    // excluded from calculation\n143\t  missing     Boolean   @default(false)    // counts as 0 when the item is past due\n144\t  comment     String?\n145\t  updatedById String\n146\t  updatedAt   DateTime  @updatedAt\n147\t  @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])\n148\t  @@index([studentId])\n149\t}\n150\t\n151\tmodel TermGradeOverride {\n152\t  courseId        String\n153\t  termId          String\n154\t  studentId       String\n155\t  percent         Decimal? @db.Decimal(5, 2)\n156\t  letter          String?\n157\t  teacherComment  String?                  // max 1,000, appears on the report card\n158\t  updatedById     String\n159\t  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt\n160\t  @@id([courseId, termId, studentId])\n161\t}\n162\t\n163\tmodel ReportCard {\n164\t  id               String           @id @default(cuid())\n165\t  studentId        String\n166\t  termId           String\n167\t  status           ReportCardStatus @default(DRAFT)\n168\t  snapshot         Json                     // frozen data: courses, grades, attendance, comments\n169\t  homeroomComment  String?\n170\t  principalComment String?\n171\t  generatedAt      DateTime         @default(now())\n172\t  publishedAt      DateTime?\n173\t  publishedById    String?\n174\t  @@unique([studentId, termId])\n175\t}\n176\t```\n177\t\n178\tAlso add `gradingScaleId String?` to `Course` (null = school default) and `categoryId String?` to `Assignment` and `Quiz` with a category select added to their editors.\n179\t\n180\t### FR-2 Sync from assignments and quizzes (`src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts`)\n181\t1. When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a `GradeItem` (title, maxPoints, dueAt, category, term = term containing `dueAt` / `availableUntil`, falling back to the current term). Unpublishing or archiving sets `isVisible = false`; deleting deletes the item.\n182\t2. When a submission is returned, upsert its `Grade` with `score = finalScore`. Saving without returning does not sync (students must not see unreturned scores). Exemptions set `excused = true`.\n183\t3. When a quiz attempt reaches GRADED and results are visible, upsert `Grade.score` from `getStudentQuizScore` scaled to the quiz maxScore.\n184\t4. A one-time backfill `npm run gradebook:backfill` creates items and grades for data that existed before this PRD; it is idempotent and runs in the seed.\n185\t5. Grades written by sync are read-only in the gradebook UI (edit happens at the source) except `comment`; manual items are fully editable.\n186\t\n187\t### FR-3 Calculation (`src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`, pure functions)\n188\tFor a student, course and term:\n189\t1. Consider visible items in the term whose student grade is not `excused`. An item counts when it has a score, or when it is past due and `missing` (counts as 0). Ungraded, not-missing items are ignored.\n190\t2. Per category: drop the `dropLowest` lowest percentages (never dropping all), then `categoryPercent = Σ score / Σ maxPoints × 100`.\n191\t3. Course percent = weighted mean of category percentages over categories that have at least one counted item, re-normalising weights to the categories present. Items without a category form an implicit \"Uncategorised\" category; if the course has no categories, course percent = total points earned / total possible × 100.\n192\t4. Letter = first band where `percent >= minPercent` in the effective scale. Round percent half-up to 1 decimal place before letter lookup.\n193\t5. `TermGradeOverride` percent/letter replace the computed values when set (letter-only overrides keep the computed percent).\n194\t6. Example: Homework 40 % (scores 18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60 % (scores 70/100): Homework = 27/30 = 90.0 %, Exams = 70.0 %, course = 0.4 × 90 + 0.6 × 70 = 78.0 % → \"C+\" in the seed scale.\n195\t\n196\t### FR-4 Grading scales (`/admin/grading-scales`)\n197\t1. CRUD for scales; band editor with letter, minimum %, optional GPA points and descriptor. Validation: bands strictly descending, lowest band minimum is 0, letters unique. Exactly one default.\n198\t\n199\t### FR-5 Category setup (course \"Gradebook\" settings)\n200\t1. Teacher manages categories: name, weight, drop lowest, order. Weights must total 100 (live sum indicator) before saving. Course grading scale select (defaults to school default).\n201\t\n202\t### FR-6 Gradebook grid (course tab \"Gradebook\", TEACHER/ADMIN)\n203\t1. Term selector. Grid built on MUI X `DataGrid` (MIT: column groups via `columnGroupingModel`, cell editing via `processRowUpdate`; pinned columns are not in the MIT version, so keep the student column first and use the grid's sticky header): first column students (sorted by last name), then items grouped by category (column header shows title, due date, max points, source icon), then category averages and the term percent + letter (bold). Horizontally scrollable; the DataGrid's built-in virtualisation handles up to 60 students × 120 items.\n204\t2. Cell content: score, \"EX\" (excused), \"M\" (missing, red), \"—\" (ungraded). Late submissions show a small clock icon.\n205\t3. Manual items: editable DataGrid cells — type a number, `Enter` / arrow keys move between cells, `E` excuse, `M` missing, `Delete` clears. Changes save on blur with optimistic update and per-cell error state.\n206\t4. Synced cells: clicking opens the source (submission grading page or quiz attempt).\n207\t5. \"Add manual item\" dialog: title, category, max points, date, term.\n208\t6. Student row action: \"Override term grade / comment\" dialog (percent, letter, comment).\n209\t7. Column menu: hide/show item to students, set all ungraded to missing (after due date), view item statistics (average, median, high, low).\n210\t8. \"Export CSV\" exports the grid as displayed.\n211\t\n212\t### FR-7 Student and parent grade views\n213\t1. Register student tab \"Grades\": for the selected term, one card per course with percent, letter and a colour (≥ 80 green, 60–79 amber, < 60 red); expanding shows each visible item (title, category, score/max, percent, comment, missing/excused flags) and category subtotals.\n214\t2. `/grades` page for STUDENT and PARENT (child selector) showing the same.\n215\t3. Course tab \"Grades\" for STUDENT/PARENT shows that course's items only.\n216\t\n217\t### FR-8 Report cards (`/admin/report-cards`)\n218\t1. Select term → table of students (filter by grade level and section) with report card status (Not generated, Draft, Published) and missing-data warnings (for example \"2 courses have ungraded items\", \"No teacher comment for ENG-7A\").\n219\t2. \"Generate drafts\" for the filtered students builds each `snapshot`: school name/logo, student name, admission number, grade level, section, homeroom teacher, term and year; per course: subject, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor, teacher comment (from overrides); attendance summary for the term (rate, absences, lates); grading scale legend. Regenerating a draft refreshes the snapshot; published cards are never changed by regeneration.\n220\t3. Review page per card: rendered report card preview with editable homeroom comment (homeroom teacher or admin) and principal comment (admin). Homeroom teachers also get `/report-cards` listing their section's drafts to write comments.\n221\t4. \"Publish\" (per card or bulk for filtered list) sets status PUBLISHED and sends `report_card.published` to student and parents (default email true). \"Unpublish\" (admin only, requires reason, audited).\n222\t5. Print view `/report-cards/[id]/print`: A4 portrait, school letterhead, tables, signature lines for principal and homeroom teacher; uses `@media print`; \"Print / Save as PDF\" button calls `window.print()`. Bulk \"Print all\" renders filtered published cards with page breaks.\n223\t6. Register student tab \"Report cards\": list of published cards (students/parents) or all (admin/teacher), each opening the print view.\n224\t\n225\t### FR-9 Notifications\n226\t1. `grade.posted` → student + parents when a manual item grade is entered (default email false; batched: one notification per student per item).\n227\t2. `report_card.published` as above.\n228\t\n229\t## API\n230\t\n231\t| Method & path | Role | Notes |\n232\t|---|---|---|\n233\t| `GET/POST /api/grading-scales`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/grading-scales/:id` | GET any, write ADMIN | |\n234\t| `GET/PUT /api/courses/:id/grade-categories` | GET view, PUT manage | PUT replaces full list, validates total 100 |\n235\t| `GET /api/courses/:id/gradebook?termId=` | manage | Items, students, grades, computed results |\n236\t| `POST /api/courses/:id/grade-items` | manage | Manual items |\n237\t| `PATCH /api/grade-items/:id` · `DELETE` | manage | Manual only for most fields; `isVisible` for all |\n238\t| `PUT /api/grade-items/:id/grades/:studentId` | manage | `{ score?, excused?, missing?, comment? }` |\n239\t| `PUT /api/courses/:id/term-overrides/:studentId` | manage | `{ termId, percent?, letter?, teacherComment? }` |\n240\t| `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId=` | view student | Only visible items |\n241\t| `GET /api/report-cards?termId=&gradeLevelId=&sectionId=` | ADMIN, homeroom TEACHER | |\n242\t| `POST /api/report-cards/generate` | ADMIN | `{ termId, studentIds }` |\n243\t| `GET /api/report-cards/:id` | ADMIN, teachers of student, student/parents when published | |\n244\t| `PATCH /api/report-cards/:id` | ADMIN, homeroom teacher (homeroom comment only) | |\n245\t| `POST /api/report-cards/publish` · `/unpublish` | ADMIN | `{ ids, reason? }` |\n246\t\n247\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n248\t\n249\t1. **Correctness:** calculation lives in pure functions with exhaustive unit tests; all arithmetic in `Decimal`.\n250\t2. **Performance:** gradebook for 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms; computing term grades for 600 students × 8 courses for report card generation finishes in under 30 seconds.\n251\t3. **Auditability:** every manual grade change and override writes an audit entry with old and new values.\n252\t4. **Privacy:** hidden items and unreturned scores never appear in student or parent responses.\n253\t\n254\t## Acceptance Criteria\n255\t\n256\t1. Given the FR-3.6 example, then the gradebook and the student Grades tab both show 78.0 % C+.\n257\t2. Given Homework has `dropLowest = 1` and scores 50 %, 90 %, 100 %, then the Homework category percent excludes the 50 %.\n258\t3. Given a returned assignment, then its score appears in the gradebook without manual entry; given a graded-but-not-returned submission, then it does not appear to the student.\n259\t4. Given category weights totalling 90, when the teacher saves, then the save is refused with the live sum showing 90 / 100.\n260\t5. Given an item past due marked missing, then it counts as 0; given it is excused, then it does not count.\n261\t6. Given a letter-only override of \"B\" for Sam, then Sam's card shows the computed percent and letter B.\n262\t7. Given an admin generates drafts for 7A and publishes them, then Sam and Pat receive a `report_card.published` notification and can open the print view; a student in 7B cannot open Sam's card.\n263\t8. Given a published report card, when a teacher changes a grade, then the published card's snapshot does not change.\n264\t9. Given the print view, when printed, then each student's card fits on A4 pages without the app sidebar.\n265\t\n266\t## Test Requirements\n267\t\n268\t- Unit: full calculation matrix (no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, missing vs ungraded, overrides, rounding at band edges like 89.95 → 90.0 → A).\n269\t- Integration: sync hooks from assignment return and quiz grading; backfill idempotency; snapshot immutability.\n270\t- Playwright: teacher edits manual grades with keyboard; admin generates and publishes report cards; parent views a report card.\n271\t\n272\t## Seed Data\n273\t\n274\t- Default scale \"Standard A–F\": A 93, A− 90, B+ 87, B 83, B− 80, C+ 77, C 73, C− 70, D+ 67, D 63, D− 60, F 0, with descriptors.\n275\t- Categories for all 7A courses: Homework 30 %, Quizzes 30 %, Exams 40 % (drop lowest 1 homework).\n276\t- One manual item \"Oral presentation\" in ENG-7A, graded for all students.\n277\t- Draft report cards for 7A for Semester 1, with teacher comments for MATH and ENG.\n278\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6f85ae0-4ad4-4d10-b797-6ff9d3e2b1f5","uuid":"21857884-ff43-4f10-a844-0e60a4245b70","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:15:26.124Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/11-gradebook.md","content":"# PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n\n**Ticket:** SCH-011 · **Depends on:** PRD-00 – PRD-10 · **Run mode:** `--brownfield --tech-stack react`\n\n## Summary\n\nA unified gradebook per course that pulls in assignment and quiz scores automatically, supports manual grade items (for example an in-class presentation), weighted categories, term grades with a school-wide letter grading scale, teacher overrides and comments. At term end, admins generate report cards that combine every course grade with attendance and comments, review them, publish them to students and parents, and print them.\n\n## Platform Context (shared by every SchoolHub PRD)\n\nSchoolHub is a single-school web platform for administrators, teachers, students and parents. It is built incrementally by a sequence of PRDs (PRD-00 … PRD-18). **When this PRD runs, every lower-numbered PRD is already implemented in the workspace.** Reuse existing models, services, components and helpers — never re-scaffold the project, never duplicate a helper that already exists, never rename existing routes or models.\n\n### Fixed technology decisions\n\n| Concern | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| Framework | Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript `strict: true` |\n| UI components | **Material UI only** — `@mui/material` v9 (+ `@emotion/react`, `@emotion/styled`), `@mui/material-nextjs` (App Router cache provider), `@mui/icons-material`. Every component is looked up through the MUI MCP server first (see \"UI component rule\" below) |\n| Theming | MUI `createTheme` with `cssVariables: true` and light/dark `colorSchemes`, `InitColorSchemeScript`, `useColorScheme()` for the toggle; styling only through the theme, the `sx` prop and `styled()` — no Tailwind, no CSS modules |\n| Dates & pickers | `@mui/x-date-pickers` v9 (MIT) with `AdapterDateFns`; `date-fns` + `date-fns-tz` for logic |\n| Database | PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma ORM (`prisma/schema.prisma`), migrations with `prisma migrate` |\n| Auth | Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy, bcrypt password hashes |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts`, shared by client forms and API handlers |\n| Forms | React Hook Form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` |\n| Data tables | `@mui/x-data-grid` v9 (MIT `DataGrid`, server-side pagination/sorting/filtering) wrapped by the shared `DataTable` component |\n| Charts | `@mui/x-charts` v9 (MIT) |\n| Email | Nodemailer via the `EmailOutbox` table (from PRD-04); dev transport logs to console |\n| Calendar UI | `@mui/x-scheduler` (MIT Community `EventCalendar`; pin the exact version found via the MUI MCP — it is in beta) |\n| Tests | Vitest + Testing Library (unit/integration), Playwright (e2e in `tests/e2e`) |\n| Local infra | `docker-compose.yml` with Postgres; `.env.example` documents every env var |\n\n### UI component rule (mandatory — applies to every screen in this PRD)\n\n1. **Material UI components only.** Every visible UI element is built from `@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material` or the MUI X packages listed above (`@mui/x-data-grid`, `@mui/x-date-pickers`, `@mui/x-charts`, `@mui/x-scheduler`) — composed with `Box`, `Stack`, `Grid` and the theme. Hand-styled raw HTML (`<div>`/`<button>`/`<table>` with custom CSS) is not allowed where an MUI component exists.\n2. **Look up every component through the MUI MCP server (`mui-mcp`) before using it.** Call `useMuiDocs` with the package (for example `@mui/material@9.5.0`, `@mui/x-data-grid`) to get the docs index, then `fetchDocs` on the component's page, and use only props, slots and imports documented there for the installed version. Never write MUI code from memory, and never invent props. If the MCP server is unreachable, stop and report it as a blocker instead of guessing.\n3. **Banned:** Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Radix UI, Headless UI, Chakra UI, Ant Design, Bootstrap, `lucide-react`, `next-themes`, `@tanstack/react-table`, Recharts, FullCalendar, `react-select`, `react-datepicker`, `sonner`, `notistack` and any other component or styling library. PRD-00 enforces this with an ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule.\n4. **Allowed non-visual libraries** (they render no UI of their own): React Hook Form, Zod, `@dnd-kit/core` and `@dnd-kit/sortable` (drag behaviour only — draggable items are MUI components), `react-markdown` + `remark-gfm` + `rehype-sanitize` (every Markdown element is mapped to an MUI component through the `components` prop), `papaparse`, `date-fns`. Email templates (`@react-email/components`) are exempt because email clients cannot render MUI.\n5. Shared wrappers live in `src/components/shared/` and are themselves built from MUI. Toasts use MUI `Snackbar` + `Alert` through the shared `useToast()` hook from PRD-00; side panels use `Drawer`; confirmations use `Dialog`; pickers and searchable selects use `Autocomplete`.\n6. Intake must record this rule as a non-functional requirement, and QA must check it: no banned imports, and every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\n\n### Code layout and conventions\n\n- `src/app/(public)/…` public pages, `src/app/(auth)/…` sign-in flows, `src/app/(app)/…` authenticated app with the shared sidebar shell.\n- `src/app/api/<feature>/…/route.ts` REST route handlers. Handlers are thin: parse with Zod → call a service → return JSON.\n- `src/server/services/<feature>.ts` business logic and Prisma access. Server components may call services directly; client components call the REST API. New features follow PRD-05's precedent of a feature-named subdirectory instead: `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts` (for example `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`), not this older flat path — which remains accurate only for the already-built PRD-02/03-era services that still live there.\n- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` exposes `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)` and per-entity access checks. Every handler and every server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\n- Response shape: success `{ \"data\": … }`; list `{ \"data\": [...], \"page\": 1, \"pageSize\": 20, \"total\": 134 }`; error `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"VALIDATION_ERROR\", \"message\": \"…\", \"details\": {…} } }`. Error codes: `VALIDATION_ERROR` (400), `UNAUTHENTICATED` (401), `FORBIDDEN` (403), `NOT_FOUND` (404), `CONFLICT` (409), `RATE_LIMITED` (429), `INTERNAL` (500).\n- Pagination: `?page=` (default 1) and `?pageSize=` (default 20, maximum 100). Sorting: `?sort=field&order=asc|desc`. Search: `?q=`.\n- IDs are `cuid()` strings. Every model has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone from `SchoolSettings.timezone`. Date-only values use `@db.Date`.\n- Sidebar navigation lives in `src/config/navigation.ts` as an array of `{ label, href, icon, roles }`. A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry there.\n- Student detail page `/students/[studentId]` is tab-based; tabs are registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts`. Feature PRDs add a tab there instead of creating a separate student page.\n- Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an `AuditLog` row through `audit()` (from PRD-01).\n- Notifications go through `notify()` (from PRD-04). Notification type keys are registered in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`.\n- No `console.log` in committed code except the dev email transport; use the `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts`.\n\n### Roles\n\n`ADMIN` (school office staff and principal), `TEACHER`, `STUDENT`, `PARENT` (parent or guardian). A user has exactly one role. Parents see data only for students linked to them; students see only their own data; teachers see data for courses they teach and sections they are homeroom teacher of; admins see everything.\n\n### Assumptions and constraints\n\n- **Assumptions:** one school per deployment (no multi-tenancy); English-only UI; the school timezone is the reference for every date rule; users have a modern evergreen browser (last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari).\n- **Constraints:** this PRD is delivered in a single forge run, so its scope must not expand beyond the sections below; do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs; keep all existing tests passing (`npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test`) and add the tests listed in this PRD.\n- **Delivery milestones:** Milestone 1 \"Core platform\" = PRD-00 – PRD-05 · Milestone 2 \"Teaching & learning\" = PRD-06 – PRD-11 · Milestone 3 \"Communication\" = PRD-12 – PRD-15 · Milestone 4 \"Operations & public\" = PRD-16 – PRD-18.\n\n## Background\n\nTeachers currently keep grades in personal spreadsheets with differing formulas, and the office retypes everything into report cards each term. One gradebook with consistent calculation removes the retyping and lets families see standing during the term rather than only at the end.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. Every graded assignment and quiz appears in the gradebook without manual entry.\n2. Term grades are computed identically across the school from category weights and the grading scale.\n3. The office generates, reviews and publishes report cards for the whole school in under one hour.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Standards-based grading (mastery per standard).\n- GPA and class rank (future work).\n- Transcript across multiple years.\n\n## User Stories\n\n- As an admin, I want to define the school's grading scale so that letter grades are consistent.\n- As a teacher, I want weighted categories (for example Homework 30 %, Quizzes 30 %, Exams 40 %) so that grades reflect my syllabus.\n- As a teacher, I want a spreadsheet-like gradebook with every student and item so that I can see and edit scores quickly.\n- As a teacher, I want to add manual grade items for offline work so that all assessment is in one place.\n- As a student or parent, I want to see current course grades and individual scores so that we know where the student stands.\n- As an admin, I want to generate, review, publish and print report cards each term so that families receive official results.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1 Data model\n\n```prisma\nenum GradeItemSource { ASSIGNMENT QUIZ MANUAL }\nenum ReportCardStatus { DRAFT PUBLISHED }\n\nmodel GradingScale {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  name      String                     // \"Standard A–F\"\n  isDefault Boolean  @default(false)\n  bands     Json                       // [{ letter: \"A\", minPercent: 90, gpa?: 4.0, descriptor: \"Excellent\" }], sorted desc\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel GradeCategory {\n  id            String   @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId      String\n  course        Course   @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  name          String                     // \"Homework\"\n  weightPercent Decimal  @db.Decimal(5, 2) // 0–100; a course's categories total 100\n  dropLowest    Int      @default(0)       // drop N lowest scores in this category per student\n  order         Int\n}\n\nmodel GradeItem {\n  id          String          @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String\n  course      Course          @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  categoryId  String?\n  category    GradeCategory?  @relation(fields: [categoryId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  termId      String\n  term        Term            @relation(fields: [termId], references: [id])\n  title       String\n  maxPoints   Decimal         @db.Decimal(6, 2)\n  dueAt       DateTime?\n  source      GradeItemSource\n  sourceId    String?         @unique       // assignmentId or quizId\n  isVisible   Boolean         @default(true) // hidden items do not show to students/parents and do not count\n  createdAt   DateTime        @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime        @updatedAt\n  grades      Grade[]\n}\n\nmodel Grade {\n  gradeItemId String\n  gradeItem   GradeItem @relation(fields: [gradeItemId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  score       Decimal?  @db.Decimal(6, 2)  // null = not graded yet\n  excused     Boolean   @default(false)    // excluded from calculation\n  missing     Boolean   @default(false)    // counts as 0 when the item is past due\n  comment     String?\n  updatedById String\n  updatedAt   DateTime  @updatedAt\n  @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId])\n}\n\nmodel TermGradeOverride {\n  courseId        String\n  termId          String\n  studentId       String\n  percent         Decimal? @db.Decimal(5, 2)\n  letter          String?\n  teacherComment  String?                  // max 1,000, appears on the report card\n  updatedById     String\n  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt\n  @@id([courseId, termId, studentId])\n}\n\nmodel ReportCard {\n  id               String           @id @default(cuid())\n  studentId        String\n  termId           String\n  status           ReportCardStatus @default(DRAFT)\n  snapshot         Json                     // frozen data: courses, grades, attendance, comments\n  homeroomComment  String?\n  principalComment String?\n  generatedAt      DateTime         @default(now())\n  publishedAt      DateTime?\n  publishedById    String?\n  @@unique([studentId, termId])\n}\n```\n\nAlso add `gradingScaleId String?` to `Course` (null = school default) and `categoryId String?` to `Assignment` and `Quiz` with a category select added to their editors.\n\n### FR-2 Sync from assignments and quizzes (`src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts`)\n1. When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a `GradeItem` (title, maxPoints, dueAt, category, term = term containing `dueAt` / `availableUntil`, falling back to the current term). Unpublishing or archiving sets `isVisible = false`; deleting deletes the item.\n2. When a submission is returned, upsert its `Grade` with `score = finalScore`. Saving without returning does not sync (students must not see unreturned scores). Exemptions set `excused = true`.\n3. When a quiz attempt reaches GRADED and results are visible, upsert `Grade.score` from `getStudentQuizScore` scaled to the quiz maxScore.\n4. A one-time backfill `npm run gradebook:backfill` creates items and grades for data that existed before this PRD; it is idempotent and runs in the seed.\n5. Grades written by sync are read-only in the gradebook UI (edit happens at the source) except `comment`; manual items are fully editable.\n\n### FR-3 Calculation (`src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`, pure functions)\nFor a student, course and term:\n1. Consider visible items in the term whose student grade is not `excused`. An item counts when it has a score, or when it is past due and `missing` (counts as 0). Ungraded, not-missing items are ignored.\n2. Per category: drop the `dropLowest` lowest percentages (never dropping all), then `categoryPercent = Σ score / Σ maxPoints × 100`.\n3. Course percent = weighted mean of category percentages over categories that have at least one counted item, re-normalising weights to the categories present. Items without a category form an implicit \"Uncategorised\" category; if the course has no categories, course percent = total points earned / total possible × 100.\n4. Letter = first band where `percent >= minPercent` in the effective scale. Round percent half-up to 1 decimal place before letter lookup.\n5. `TermGradeOverride` percent/letter replace the computed values when set (letter-only overrides keep the computed percent).\n6. Example: Homework 40 % (scores 18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60 % (scores 70/100): Homework = 27/30 = 90.0 %, Exams = 70.0 %, course = 0.4 × 90 + 0.6 × 70 = 78.0 % → \"C+\" in the seed scale.\n\n### FR-4 Grading scales (`/admin/grading-scales`)\n1. CRUD for scales; band editor with letter, minimum %, optional GPA points and descriptor. Validation: bands strictly descending, lowest band minimum is 0, letters unique. Exactly one default.\n\n### FR-5 Category setup (course \"Gradebook\" settings)\n1. Teacher manages categories: name, weight, drop lowest, order. Weights must total 100 (live sum indicator) before saving. Course grading scale select (defaults to school default).\n\n### FR-6 Gradebook grid (course tab \"Gradebook\", TEACHER/ADMIN)\n1. Term selector. Grid built on MUI X `DataGrid` (MIT: column groups via `columnGroupingModel`, cell editing via `processRowUpdate`; pinned columns are not in the MIT version, so keep the student column first and use the grid's sticky header): first column students (sorted by last name), then items grouped by category (column header shows title, due date, max points, source icon), then category averages and the term percent + letter (bold). Horizontally scrollable; the DataGrid's built-in virtualisation handles up to 60 students × 120 items.\n2. Cell content: score, \"EX\" (excused), \"M\" (missing, red), \"—\" (ungraded). Late submissions show a small clock icon.\n3. Manual items: editable DataGrid cells — type a number, `Enter` / arrow keys move between cells, `E` excuse, `M` missing, `Delete` clears. Changes save on blur with optimistic update and per-cell error state.\n4. Synced cells: clicking opens the source (submission grading page or quiz attempt).\n5. \"Add manual item\" dialog: title, category, max points, date, term.\n6. Student row action: \"Override term grade / comment\" dialog (percent, letter, comment).\n7. Column menu: hide/show item to students, set all ungraded to missing (after due date), view item statistics (average, median, high, low).\n8. \"Export CSV\" exports the grid as displayed.\n\n### FR-7 Student and parent grade views\n1. Register student tab \"Grades\": for the selected term, one card per course with percent, letter and a colour (≥ 80 green, 60–79 amber, < 60 red); expanding shows each visible item (title, category, score/max, percent, comment, missing/excused flags) and category subtotals.\n2. `/grades` page for STUDENT and PARENT (child selector) showing the same.\n3. Course tab \"Grades\" for STUDENT/PARENT shows that course's items only.\n\n### FR-8 Report cards (`/admin/report-cards`)\n1. Select term → table of students (filter by grade level and section) with report card status (Not generated, Draft, Published) and missing-data warnings (for example \"2 courses have ungraded items\", \"No teacher comment for ENG-7A\").\n2. \"Generate drafts\" for the filtered students builds each `snapshot`: school name/logo, student name, admission number, grade level, section, homeroom teacher, term and year; per course: subject, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor, teacher comment (from overrides); attendance summary for the term (rate, absences, lates); grading scale legend. Regenerating a draft refreshes the snapshot; published cards are never changed by regeneration.\n3. Review page per card: rendered report card preview with editable homeroom comment (homeroom teacher or admin) and principal comment (admin). Homeroom teachers also get `/report-cards` listing their section's drafts to write comments.\n4. \"Publish\" (per card or bulk for filtered list) sets status PUBLISHED and sends `report_card.published` to student and parents (default email true). \"Unpublish\" (admin only, requires reason, audited).\n5. Print view `/report-cards/[id]/print`: A4 portrait, school letterhead, tables, signature lines for principal and homeroom teacher; uses `@media print`; \"Print / Save as PDF\" button calls `window.print()`. Bulk \"Print all\" renders filtered published cards with page breaks.\n6. Register student tab \"Report cards\": list of published cards (students/parents) or all (admin/teacher), each opening the print view.\n\n### FR-9 Notifications\n1. `grade.posted` → student + parents when a manual item grade is entered (default email false; batched: one notification per student per item).\n2. `report_card.published` as above.\n\n## API\n\n| Method & path | Role | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GET/POST /api/grading-scales`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/grading-scales/:id` | GET any, write ADMIN | |\n| `GET/PUT /api/courses/:id/grade-categories` | GET view, PUT manage | PUT replaces full list, validates total 100 |\n| `GET /api/courses/:id/gradebook?termId=` | manage | Items, students, grades, computed results |\n| `POST /api/courses/:id/grade-items` | manage | Manual items |\n| `PATCH /api/grade-items/:id` · `DELETE` | manage | Manual only for most fields; `isVisible` for all |\n| `PUT /api/grade-items/:id/grades/:studentId` | manage | `{ score?, excused?, missing?, comment? }` |\n| `PUT /api/courses/:id/term-overrides/:studentId` | manage | `{ termId, percent?, letter?, teacherComment? }` |\n| `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId=` | view student | Only visible items |\n| `GET /api/report-cards?termId=&gradeLevelId=&sectionId=` | ADMIN, homeroom TEACHER | |\n| `POST /api/report-cards/generate` | ADMIN | `{ termId, studentIds }` |\n| `GET /api/report-cards/:id` | ADMIN, teachers of student, student/parents when published | |\n| `PATCH /api/report-cards/:id` | ADMIN, homeroom teacher (homeroom comment only) | |\n| `POST /api/report-cards/publish` · `/unpublish` | ADMIN | `{ ids, reason? }` |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n1. **Correctness:** calculation lives in pure functions with exhaustive unit tests; all arithmetic in `Decimal`.\n2. **Performance:** gradebook for 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms; computing term grades for 600 students × 8 courses for report card generation finishes in under 30 seconds.\n3. **Auditability:** every manual grade change and override writes an audit entry with old and new values.\n4. **Privacy:** hidden items and unreturned scores never appear in student or parent responses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Given the FR-3.6 example, then the gradebook and the student Grades tab both show 78.0 % C+.\n2. Given Homework has `dropLowest = 1` and scores 50 %, 90 %, 100 %, then the Homework category percent excludes the 50 %.\n3. Given a returned assignment, then its score appears in the gradebook without manual entry; given a graded-but-not-returned submission, then it does not appear to the student.\n4. Given category weights totalling 90, when the teacher saves, then the save is refused with the live sum showing 90 / 100.\n5. Given an item past due marked missing, then it counts as 0; given it is excused, then it does not count.\n6. Given a letter-only override of \"B\" for Sam, then Sam's card shows the computed percent and letter B.\n7. Given an admin generates drafts for 7A and publishes them, then Sam and Pat receive a `report_card.published` notification and can open the print view; a student in 7B cannot open Sam's card.\n8. Given a published report card, when a teacher changes a grade, then the published card's snapshot does not change.\n9. Given the print view, when printed, then each student's card fits on A4 pages without the app sidebar.\n\n## Test Requirements\n\n- Unit: full calculation matrix (no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, missing vs ungraded, overrides, rounding at band edges like 89.95 → 90.0 → A).\n- Integration: sync hooks from assignment return and quiz grading; backfill idempotency; snapshot immutability.\n- Playwright: teacher edits manual grades with keyboard; admin generates and publishes report cards; parent views a report card.\n\n## Seed Data\n\n- Default scale \"Standard A–F\": A 93, A− 90, B+ 87, B 83, B− 80, C+ 77, C 73, C− 70, D+ 67, D 63, D− 60, F 0, with descriptors.\n- Categories for all 7A courses: Homework 30 %, Quizzes 30 %, Exams 40 % (drop lowest 1 homework).\n- One manual item \"Oral presentation\" in ENG-7A, graded for all students.\n- Draft report cards for 7A for Semester 1, with teacher comments for MATH and ENG.\n","numLines":278,"startLine":1,"totalLines":278}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013DDH65K2raNTSx7KAUptZZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dgnk2ANkN4bLay1mVx99u1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n2\t\n3\tTicket: **SH-11** · Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T17:30:00Z · Status: **complete**\n4\t\n5\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (42 FR + 13 NFR), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-10), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B19, R1–R7), and the source PRD `11-gradebook.md`.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Overview\n10\t\n11\tPRD-11 adds a gradebook to SchoolHub, a brownfield Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/PostgreSQL + MUI 9.5.0 app. It has four parts:\n12\t\n13\t1. **Sync.** Published assignments and quizzes become `GradeItem`s. Returned submissions and released quiz results become `Grade`s.\n14\t2. **Calculation.** A pure Decimal function turns items, grades, categories, a scale and an override into a term percent and letter.\n15\t3. **Views.** A teacher grid (MIT DataGrid), student/parent grade views, and admin pages for scales and categories.\n16\t4. **Report cards.** Frozen JSON snapshots per student and term, with a draft → published workflow, notifications and an A4 print view.\n17\t\n18\tThe design adds **no dependencies** (ADR-1). New server code lives only in `src/server/gradebook/` and `src/server/report-cards/` (NFR-9). Existing services gain one-line calls into the sync module.\n19\t\n20\t### 1.1 Intake blockers\n21\t\n22\t`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`** at 95% confidence. There is nothing to escalate. The flagged assumptions are resolved in §1.2.\n23\t\n24\t### 1.2 Assumptions and design decisions (need product sign-off, none block dev)\n25\t\n26\t| # | Topic | Decision | Req |\n27\t|---|---|---|---|\n28\t| A1 | Exemption removal | Unexempt sets `excused = false` and re-derives `score` from the source: `finalScore` if the submission is RETURNED, otherwise `null`. | FR-6 |\n29\t| A2 | Quiz score source | **Intake's correction:** `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` **already exists** in `src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts` (L359, labelled \"PRD-11 export\"). Call it as is. It does **not** check visibility, so the sync gates on `resultsVisible()` first. This replaces ADR-6's \"add a helper to grading.ts\". Don't create a second one. | FR-7, NFR-9 |\n30\t| A3 | 89.95 rounding | 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale (A is 93). The unit test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter. | FR-13 |\n31\t| A4 | Nav entries | Add `/grades` (STUDENT, PARENT), `/report-cards` (TEACHER), and `/admin/grading-scales` and `/admin/report-cards` (ADMIN, group `Administration`). | FR-16, FR-27, FR-29, FR-33 |\n32\t| A5 | Past due | `now > dueAt` as a UTC instant. Term containment compares school-local dates (`SchoolSettings.timezone`). | NFR-10 |\n33\t| A6 | No term | If no term of the course's academic year contains the date and no term contains today, skip the item and `logger.warn`. | FR-3 |\n34\t| A7 | Teacher hide vs source visibility (R2) | **No extra column** (FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\"). Source sync writes `isVisible` only on source visibility **transitions**: publish / publishOnce → `true`, archive → `false`. Plain edits to an already-published source never touch `isVisible`, so a teacher's hide survives re-saves. | FR-4, FR-24 |\n35\t| A8 | Uncategorised weight (R3) | If the course has categories, the implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket is **shown with its subtotal but has weight 0**, so it's excluded from the weighted mean. If no category has a counted item, fall back to the points total over **all** counted items. If the course has no categories, use the points total. | FR-12 |\n36\t| A9 | `grade.posted` dedupe (R4) | No marker column. Notify only when a MANUAL grade's `score` goes from `null` to a value. That gives one notification per student per item. Later edits are audited but not notified. | FR-38 |\n37\t| A10 | Term drift (R5) | Re-derive `GradeItem.termId` only when `dueAt`/`availableUntil` changes. | FR-3 |\n38\t| A11 | Scale delete (R6) | Return `CONFLICT` if the scale is the default or any `Course.gradingScaleId` references it. Published snapshots embed their own legend, so they're unaffected. | FR-16 |\n39\t| A12 | Percent-only override | Re-derive the letter from the effective scale using the override percent. | FR-14 |\n40\t| A13 | Report card edits | Comments are editable only while `DRAFT`. Unpublish returns the card to `DRAFT` and clears `publishedAt`/`publishedById`. | FR-32, FR-34 |\n41\t| A14 | `Grade.updatedById` on system writes | Sync uses the acting user (grader/teacher) when there is one. Otherwise (auto-graded quiz, maintenance release, backfill) it uses `quiz.createdById`, `assignment.createdById` or, for backfill, `course.teacherId`. The column has no FK, as specified. | FR-1, FR-5, FR-7, FR-8 |\n42\t| A15 | Quiz CLOSED | A CLOSED quiz is **not** unpublished. Its item stays visible. Quizzes have no archive. `deleteQuiz` deletes the item. A practice toggle after publish deletes the item. | FR-3, FR-4 |\n43\t\n44\t---\n45\t\n46\t## 2. Component Breakdown\n47\t\n48\t### 2.1 Data model (one migration: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_gradebook/`)\n49\t\n50\tThe models and enums are **exactly the PRD FR-1 block** (FR-1). On top of that:\n51\t\n52\t- **Additive columns (FR-2):** `Course.gradingScaleId String?` → `GradingScale` (`onDelete: SetNull`). `Assignment.categoryId String?` and `Quiz.categoryId String?` → `GradeCategory` (`onDelete: SetNull`), so deleting a category never deletes sources.\n53\t- **Relation fields:** add only the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.gradeItems`, `Course.gradeCategories`, `Term.gradeItems`, `GradeCategory.items/assignments/quizzes`). There are no new scalar columns beyond the spec.\n54\t- **Keys already in the spec make sync race-safe (B19):** `GradeItem.sourceId @unique`, `Grade @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])`, `TermGradeOverride @@id([courseId, termId, studentId])`, `ReportCard @@unique([studentId, termId])`.\n55\t- **Indexes added:**\n56\t  - `GradeItem @@index([courseId, termId])` (NFR-2, NFR-3)\n57\t  - `TermGradeOverride @@index([termId])` (NFR-3)\n58\t  - `ReportCard @@index([termId, status])` (FR-29)\n59\t- **Raw SQL in the migration:** a partial unique index `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX grading_scale_one_default ON \"GradingScale\" (\"isDefault\") WHERE \"isDefault\";` as the backstop for \"exactly one default\" (FR-16, ADR-3).\n60\t- **Types:** `bands Json` holds `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }[]`, sorted descending and validated by Zod (`bandsSchema`). `gpa` is stored and never computed (NFR-13).\n61\t\n62\t### 2.2 Server modules\n63\t\n64\t| Module | Responsibility | Reuses | Req |\n65\t|---|---|---|---|\n66\t| `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` | **Pure** functions with no Prisma client import (types only): `computeStudentTerm(input)`, `categoryPercent`, `applyDropLowest`, `roundHalfUp1`, `letterFor(percent, bands)`, `applyOverride`, `effectiveScale(course, default)`, `gradeColour(percent)`. Everything is `Decimal`, and rounding happens once at the end. | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `assignments/grading-math.ts` | FR-10–FR-15, FR-26, NFR-1 |\n67\t| `src/server/gradebook/term-placement.ts` | Pure `termFor(date, terms, tz, now)`: picks the containing term in school-local dates, falls back to the term containing today, else returns `null`. | `schoolToday` (attendance-rules), `getSchoolTimezone` | FR-3, NFR-10, A6 |\n68\t| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts` (file name from the PRD) | Idempotent upserts. `upsertItemFromAssignment(tx, id)`, `upsertItemFromQuiz(tx, id)`, `hideItemForSource(tx, sourceId)`, `deleteItemForSource(tx, sourceId)`, `syncSubmissionGrade(tx, assignmentId, studentId, actorId?)`, `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, `syncQuizGrades(quizId)`. It also exports **pure row builders** (`itemFromAssignment`, `gradeFromSubmission`, `gradeFromQuizScore`) that the backfill shares. | `isAssignmentVisible`, `getStudentQuizScore`, `resultsVisible`, `applyScoringPolicy`, `logger` | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-5 |\n69\t| `src/server/gradebook/backfill.ts` | `backfillGradebook()`. Batch-loads per course and runs the same row builders with `upsert`. Idempotent through the unique keys. | `applyScoringPolicy` in memory (no per-student `getStudentQuizScore`) | FR-8, NFR-3 |\n70\t| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-service.ts` | `getGradebook(user, courseId, termId)`, `createManualItem`, `updateItem`, `deleteItem`, `putGrade`, `markAllMissing`, `putTermOverride`, `exportGradebookCsv`. Loads the data, calls grade-calc, enforces FR-9 and writes audit entries. | `assertCanManageCourse`, `audit`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `toCsv` | FR-9, FR-18–FR-25, FR-38, NFR-2, NFR-4 |\n71\t| `src/server/gradebook/categories-service.ts` | `getCategories`, `replaceCategories` (in a transaction: delete removed ids, upsert the rest, `dec(sum).eq(100)`), and `setCourseScale`. | `assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse` | FR-17, FR-40 |\n72\t| `src/server/gradebook/scales-service.ts` | CRUD. `setDefault` runs in a transaction that clears the other defaults. Delete is guarded (A11). | `requireRole('ADMIN')`, `audit` | FR-16 |\n73\t| `src/server/gradebook/student-grades-service.ts` | `getStudentGrades(user, studentId, termId, courseId?)`. Uses the visible-only serializer. Reuses grade-calc and passes **visible items only** into it, so the computed totals match what the student sees. | `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` | FR-26–FR-28, FR-42, NFR-5 |\n74\t| `src/server/gradebook/load.ts` | Shared batched loader: `loadCourseTermData(courseIds[], termId, studentIds?)` returns `{items, grades, categories, overrides, scales}` in 5 `findMany` calls with `in` filters, grouped in memory. Used by the gradebook, student grades and report-card generation. | Prisma | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n75\t| `src/server/report-cards/snapshot.ts` | Zod `snapshotSchema` (`v: 1`) and the pure `buildSnapshot(student, courses, computed, attendance, school, scale)`. | grade-calc | FR-30 |\n76\t| `src/server/report-cards/report-card-service.ts` | `listReportCards` (with warnings), `generateDrafts`, `getReportCard`, `patchComments`, `publish`, `unpublish`, `listForStudent`. | `load.ts`, attendance `getReport`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `audit` | FR-29–FR-34, FR-36, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n77\t| `src/server/report-cards/access.ts` | `assertCanViewReportCard(user, card)`, `canEditHomeroomComment`. | `student-access`, `Section.homeroomTeacherId`, `Enrollment` | FR-32, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n78\t| `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts` | Zod: `bandsSchema`, `scaleSchema`, `categoriesPutSchema`, `manualItemSchema`, `itemPatchSchema`, `gradePutSchema`, `termOverrideSchema` (comment ≤ 1000), `reportCardPatchSchema`, `generateSchema`, `publishSchema`, `unpublishSchema` (reason required). These are shared by client forms and handlers. | Zod | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23, FR-39, FR-40 |\n79\t| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (edit) | Register `grade.posted` (STUDENT+PARENT, `defaultEmail: false`) and `report_card.published` (STUDENT+PARENT, `defaultEmail: true`). | existing registry | FR-38 |\n80\t\n81\t**Hook edits to existing services** (each is one call; behaviour is otherwise unchanged, per NFR-9):\n82\t\n83\t| Existing site | Added call | Req |\n84\t|---|---|---|\n85\t| `assignments-service` `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` / `publishOnce` | `upsertItemFromAssignment(tx, id)`. This sets `isVisible` only on a visibility transition (A7). It re-places the term only if `dueAt` changed (A10). | FR-3, FR-4 |\n86\t| `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` | archive → `hideItemForSource`; hard delete → `deleteItemForSource` in the same transaction (B9) | FR-4 |\n87\t| `gradeSubmission`, `bulkReturn`, `gradeOffline` | `syncSubmissionGrade` when the submission **is** RETURNED after the write. This covers re-grades of returned work. Nothing happens otherwise (AC-3). | FR-5, NFR-5 |\n88\t| `setExemption` (both branches) | `syncSubmissionGrade` (A1) | FR-6 |\n89\t| `quiz-service` `updateQuiz` (→PUBLISHED, or edits to a published quiz) / `deleteQuiz` | `upsertItemFromQuiz` / `deleteItemForSource`. Practice quizzes are skipped; turning practice on deletes the item. Wrap `deleteQuiz` in a transaction. | FR-3, FR-4 |\n90\t| After callers of `recomputeAttempt` commit (`submitAttempt`, `gradeAnswerManually`, `regradeQuiz`) | `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`: no-op unless GRADED, `resultsVisible` and not practice | FR-7 |\n91\t| `releaseResults` (MANUAL) and `quiz/maintenance.ts` AFTER_CLOSE claim (`count === 1`) | `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` (bulk). Without this, delayed-visibility quizzes never sync (R1). | FR-7, NFR-5 |\n92\t| Assignment and quiz Zod validators and editors | Optional nullable `categoryId` plus one MUI `Select` of the course's categories | FR-2 |\n93\t\n94\t### 2.3 API layer (`src/app/api/**/route.ts`, thin: `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok()`)\n95\t\n96\tThese match the PRD API table exactly. `api-contracts.json` (next sub-task) owns the shapes.\n97\t\n98\t| Route | Role check | Service | Req |\n99\t|---|---|---|---|\n100\t| `GET/POST /api/grading-scales`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/grading-scales/[id]` | GET: `requireUser`; writes: ADMIN | scales-service | FR-16, FR-39 |\n101\t| `GET/PUT /api/courses/[id]/grade-categories` | view / manage | categories-service (PUT body also carries `gradingScaleId`) | FR-17, FR-40 |\n102\t| `GET /api/courses/[id]/gradebook?termId=` (`&format=csv` → `text/csv`) | manage | gradebook-service | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, FR-25, NFR-2 |\n103\t| `POST /api/courses/[id]/grade-items` | manage | createManualItem | FR-22 |\n104\t| `PATCH/DELETE /api/grade-items/[id]` | manage (via the item's course) | updateItem / deleteItem. Non-MANUAL items accept only `isVisible`, and DELETE is MANUAL only. | FR-9, FR-24 |\n105\t| `POST /api/grade-items/[id]/mark-missing` | manage | markAllMissing (`now > dueAt`, ungraded rows only) | FR-24 |\n106\t| `PUT /api/grade-items/[id]/grades/[studentId]` | manage + enrolled student | putGrade. Non-MANUAL items accept only `comment` (FR-9). | FR-9, FR-20, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n107\t| `PUT /api/courses/[id]/term-overrides/[studentId]` | manage | putTermOverride | FR-14, FR-23, NFR-4 |\n108\t| `GET /api/students/[id]/grades?termId=&courseId=` | `assertCanViewStudent` | student-grades-service | FR-26–FR-28, FR-42 |\n109\t| `GET /api/report-cards?termId=&gradeLevelId=&sectionId=&studentId=` | ADMIN; homeroom TEACHER (own sections); with `studentId`, view-student rules plus PUBLISHED-only for student/parent | listReportCards / listForStudent | FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |\n110\t| `POST /api/report-cards/generate` | ADMIN | generateDrafts | FR-30, FR-31, NFR-3 |\n111\t| `GET /api/report-cards/[id]` | `assertCanViewReportCard` | getReportCard | FR-37 |\n112\t| `PATCH /api/report-cards/[id]` | field-level (§4) | patchComments | FR-32 |\n113\t| `POST /api/report-cards/publish`, `POST /api/report-cards/unpublish` | ADMIN | publish / unpublish | FR-34 |\n114\t\n115\t`mark-missing` is the only route not in the PRD table. It implements the FR-24 column action server-side, because a client loop of N PUTs would write N audit rows and be slow. The `?format=csv` and `courseId`/`studentId` query parameters extend existing PRD routes rather than adding new ones.\n116\t\n117\t### 2.4 UI (`src/app/(app)/…`, MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, per NFR-7)\n118\t\n119\t| Page / component | Notes | Req |\n120\t|---|---|---|\n121\t| `admin/grading-scales/page.tsx` + `ScaleEditorDialog` | `DataTable` list. The dialog uses a band editor (TextField rows, add/remove) with Zod errors inline and a \"Default\" `Switch`. | FR-16 |\n122\t| `courses/[courseId]/gradebook/settings/page.tsx` | Category rows (name, weight, drop lowest, order), a live `Σ weights / 100` `Chip` (error colour ≠ 100, Save disabled), and a scale `Select` (\"School default\" = null). | FR-17 |\n123\t| `courses/[courseId]/gradebook/page.tsx` + `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx` | The single client component that owns the DataGrid (ADR-4, R7). Term `Select`, `columnGroupingModel` by category, custom `renderHeader` (title, due date, max, source icon), `renderCell` (score / EX / M red / — / late `AccessTime` icon), and `isCellEditable` = MANUAL only. Editing runs through `renderEditCell` + `onCellKeyDown` (digits, E, M, Delete, Enter/arrows), then `processRowUpdate` → PUT, `onProcessRowUpdateError` → per-cell error, and `hideFooter`. There are **no pinned columns**. Toolbar: \"Add manual item\", \"Export CSV\", \"Settings\". | FR-18–FR-25, NFR-8 |\n124\t| `AddManualItemDialog`, `TermOverrideDialog`, `ItemStatsDialog` | Dialogs. Stats (average, median, high, low) are computed client-side from the payload over counted scores. | FR-22, FR-23, FR-24 |\n125\t| `src/components/gradebook/StudentGradesView.tsx` | Course `Card`s with percent, letter and `gradeColour` `Chip`. `Accordion` expands to items and category subtotals. One component serves three hosts: | FR-26–FR-28 |\n126\t| ↳ `students/[id]/grades/page.tsx` | student tab | FR-26 |\n127\t| ↳ `grades/page.tsx` | STUDENT: self. PARENT: child `Select` from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-27 |\n128\t| ↳ `courses/[courseId]/grades/page.tsx` | filtered to one course | FR-28 |\n129\t| `admin/report-cards/page.tsx` | Term / grade level / section filters, `DataTable` with status `Chip` and warnings, and \"Generate drafts\", \"Publish all\", \"Print all\" actions. Confirmations use `ConfirmDialog`. | FR-29, FR-30, FR-34, FR-35 |\n130\t| `report-cards/page.tsx` | Homeroom TEACHER: their sections' cards for the selected term | FR-33 |\n131\t| `report-cards/[id]/page.tsx` | Review page: `ReportCardDocument` preview plus homeroom/principal comment fields (disabled per role or when PUBLISHED), and Publish / Unpublish (reason dialog) for ADMIN | FR-32, FR-34 |\n132\t| `report-cards/[id]/print/page.tsx`, `report-cards/print/page.tsx?termId=&…` | Server components rendering `ReportCardDocument` from the **snapshot only**. `GlobalStyles`: `@page { size: A4 portrait; margin: 12mm }`, `@media print` hides the app shell and buttons, each card gets `break-after: page`, and rows get `break-inside: avoid`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. Bulk print shows filtered PUBLISHED cards only. | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n133\t| `students/[id]/report-cards/page.tsx` | List of cards, each linking to the print view | FR-36 |\n134\t| Config | `courseTabs`: `gradebook` (ADMIN, TEACHER) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). `studentTabs`: `grades` and `report-cards`. `navigation`: the four entries from A4. | FR-18, FR-26–FR-28, FR-33, FR-36 |\n135\t\n136\tEvery page server-checks the role with `requireUser`/`requireRole` plus the same entity assert as its API (NFR-6). It never relies on hidden links.\n137\t\n138\t### 2.5 Scripts and seed\n139\t\n140\t- `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. The script calls `backfillGradebook()` and exits (FR-8, ADR-7).\n141\t- `prisma/seed.ts`:\n142\t  1. scale \"Standard A–F\" (default)\n143\t  2. Homework 30 (drop 1) / Quizzes 30 / Exams 40 for each 7A course\n144\t  3. `backfillGradebook()`\n145\t  4. ENG-7A manual item \"Oral presentation\" graded for all enrolled students\n146\t  5. Semester 1 `TermGradeOverride.teacherComment` for MATH-7A and ENG-7A\n147\t  6. `generateDrafts(S1, 7A students)`\n148\t\n149\t  Categories go in before the backfill so seeded assignments and quizzes can be attached to them (FR-41).\n150\t\n151\t---\n152\t\n153\t## 3. Data Flow\n154\t\n155\t### 3.1 Source → gradebook sync (write path)\n156\t\n157\t```\n158\tTeacher publishes assignment ─► assignments-service (tx) ─► upsertItemFromAssignment(tx)\n159\t                                                              ├─ termFor(dueAt, courseYearTerms, tz)  → null ⇒ warn+skip\n160\t                                                              └─ GradeItem upsert by sourceId (isVisible only on transition)\n161\tTeacher returns submission  ─► gradeSubmission/bulkReturn/gradeOffline (tx)\n162\t                                  └─ status==RETURNED ? syncSubmissionGrade(tx): Grade upsert {score: finalScore,\n163\t                                                                                  excused: exemption exists}\n164\tQuiz attempt graded         ─► recomputeAttempt → commit → syncQuizGrade(quiz, student)\n165\t                                  └─ GRADED ∧ resultsVisible ∧ ¬isPractice ? getStudentQuizScore → scale to maxPoints → upsert\n166\tResults released / closed   ─► releaseResults | maintenance claim ─► syncQuizGrades(quiz)  (bulk, batched)\n167\t```\n168\t\n169\tBecause unreleased scores are **never written** into `Grade`, privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers (NFR-5, layer 1 of 3).\n170\t\n171\tQuiz scaling: `score = result.score / result.maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, where `maxPoints = quiz maxScore`, in Decimal with `fixed2` at write.\n172\t\n173\t### 3.2 Calculation (pure, `grade-calc.ts`)\n174\t\n175\t```\n176\tinput: { items[], grades by itemId, categories[], bands, override?, now }\n177\tcounted(item) = item.isVisible ∧ ¬grade.excused ∧ (grade.score ≠ null ∨ (grade.missing ∧ item.dueAt ∧ now > item.dueAt))\n178\tearned = score ?? 0\n179\tper category: sort counted by pct asc (tie: dueAt, id) → drop min(dropLowest, n−1) → Σearned/Σmax×100\n180\tcourse: categories present with ≥1 counted ⇒ Σ(w·pct)/Σw   (Uncategorised w = 0, A8)\n181\t        no categories / none counted       ⇒ Σearned/Σmax×100 over all counted\n182\t        nothing counted                    ⇒ percent = null, letter = null (\"—\")\n183\tpercent = round half-up to 1 dp (only here) → letter = first band with percent ≥ minPercent\n184\toverride: percent? → replaces percent (letter re-derived unless letter set, A12); letter? → replaces letter only\n185\t```\n186\t\n187\tThe output per student is `{ categories: [{id, name, weight, percent, earned, possible, droppedItemIds}], percent, letter, descriptor, computedPercent, computedLetter, overridden }`. The gradebook, the student views and report-card generation all call this **one** function, which guarantees FR-15 / AC-1 (78.0% C+ in both places).\n188\t\n189\t### 3.3 Gradebook read (NFR-2: 35×80 < 800 ms)\n190\t\n191\t`GET gradebook` → `assertCanManageCourse` → `load.ts`:\n192\t\n193\t1. active enrollments + students, sorted by last name\n194\t2. items `(courseId, termId)`\n195\t3. grades for those item ids\n196\t4. categories\n197\t5. override rows + course scale or default\n198\t\n199\tThen two lookup queries for click-through and late flags: `Submission {id, isLate}` by `assignmentId in` and `QuizAttempt {id}` by `quizId in`. That's seven indexed queries in total. The pure calc runs for each student in memory, and the response is one denormalised payload. The client builds the columns, and the grid virtualises rows and columns.\n200\t\n201\t### 3.4 Manual grade edit\n202\t\n203\t```\n204\tcell edit ─► processRowUpdate ─► PUT /api/grade-items/:id/grades/:studentId\n205\t   service (tx): load old grade → reject non-comment fields if item.source ≠ MANUAL (FR-9)\n206\t                 → upsert → audit('grade.update', {old, new})\n207\t   after commit: old.score == null ∧ new.score ≠ null ∧ MANUAL ⇒ notifyStudentAndParents('grade.posted')  (A9)\n208\t   response: updated grade + recomputed student row (so the term % cell refreshes)\n209\t```\n210\t\n211\tOn error the client rolls back the optimistic value and flags the cell.\n212\t\n213\t### 3.5 Report card lifecycle\n214\t\n215\t```\n216\tgenerate {termId, studentIds} (ADMIN)\n217\t  ├─ load once: students (+section, homeroom, gradeLevel), school settings, term+year, default scale,\n218\t  │             enrollments for those students in courses of the term's year,\n219\t  │             load.ts for all those courseIds (in-filters), attendance getReport(term range) ×1\n220\t  ├─ compute in memory: grade-calc per (student, course) → buildSnapshot(v:1)\n221\t  └─ write (chunks of 100, tx): createMany(skipDuplicates) for new;\n222\t                                updateMany({ where:{ id, status:'DRAFT' }, data:{ snapshot, generatedAt } }) for existing\n223\t     PUBLISHED rows are filtered out by the WHERE clause, which enforces immutability (FR-31 / AC-8)\n224\tpublish {ids}   ─► updateMany({ id in ids, status:'DRAFT' } → PUBLISHED, publishedAt, publishedById)\n225\t                   → audit('reportCard.publish') → after commit notify report_card.published per card\n226\tunpublish {ids, reason} ─► PUBLISHED → DRAFT, clear publishedAt/ById, audit('reportCard.unpublish', {old, new, reason})\n227\tprint            ─► reads snapshot only; never recomputes\n228\t```\n229\t\n230\tNothing in `src/server/gradebook/` imports `src/server/report-cards/` or writes `ReportCard`. Grade edits therefore cannot touch snapshots.\n231\t\n232\t**Snapshot v1 shape**, owned by `snapshotSchema`:\n233\t\n234\t```\n235\t{ v: 1,\n236\t  school:     { name, logoUrl },\n237\t  student:    { name, admissionNumber, gradeLevel, section, homeroomTeacher },\n238\t  term:       { name, startDate, endDate, academicYear },\n239\t  courses:    [{ subject, code, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor, teacherComment }],\n240\t  attendance: { rate, absences, lates, ...counts },\n241\t  scale:      { name, bands } }\n242\t```\n243\t\n244\t`attendance.rate` uses the same formula the existing attendance report consumers use; dev must not invent a new one (B13). Each course's letter uses that course's effective scale. The legend shows the default scale and also lists any course-specific scale used.\n245\t\n246\t**Missing-data warnings (FR-29)** are computed in the same batched pass:\n247\t\n248\t- a count of courses with eligible-but-ungraded items (visible, past due, no score, not missing, not excused)\n249\t- courses with no `teacherComment` override for the student\n250\t\n251\t### 3.6 Student/parent read (privacy, NFR-5 layers 2 and 3)\n252\t\n253\t`GET /api/students/:id/grades`: `assertCanViewStudent` → `load.ts` with `isVisible = true` filtered **in the query** → calc → serializer emits only whitelisted fields (no `updatedById`, no hidden items).\n254\t\n255\tReport-card endpoints apply `assertCanViewReportCard`. STUDENT and PARENT pass only if `card.status === 'PUBLISHED'` and they're the student or a linked parent. Anyone else unauthorised gets **NOT_FOUND**, so a 7B student can't tell that Sam's card exists (AC-7).\n256\t\n257\t---\n258\t\n259\t## 4. Access Control Matrix (NFR-6)\n260\t\n261\t| Action | ADMIN | TEACHER | STUDENT | PARENT |\n262\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n263\t| Read scales | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |\n264\t| Write scales | ✓ | — | — | — |\n265\t| Categories GET | ✓ | view course | view course | view course |\n266\t| Categories PUT | ✓ | teaches course | — | — |\n267\t| Gradebook / items / grades / overrides | ✓ | teaches course (`assertCanManageCourse`) | — | — |\n268\t| Student grades | ✓ | teaches student or is homeroom (existing student-access) | self | linked child |\n269\t| Report cards list / generate | list + generate | list: own homeroom sections | own published (via `studentId`) | child's published |\n270\t| Report card GET | ✓ | teaches any course of the student, or is homeroom | self, PUBLISHED only | linked, PUBLISHED only |\n271\t| `homeroomComment` PATCH | ✓ | homeroom teacher of the student's section, DRAFT only | — | — |\n272\t| `principalComment` PATCH | ✓ (DRAFT only) | — | — | — |\n273\t| Publish / unpublish | ✓ | — | — | — |\n274\t\n275\t---\n276\t\n277\t## 5. Cross-cutting\n278\t\n279\t- **Audit (NFR-4):**\n280\t  - required: `grade.update` (manual, and comment edits on synced grades), `grade.markMissing`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (with reason), each carrying `{old, new}`\n281\t  - extra: `reportCard.publish`, `gradingScale.create/update/delete`, `gradeCategories.replace`\n282\t- **Notifications (FR-38):** sent after commit, using `notify()`, which never throws, so a notification failure can't roll back a grade.\n283\t- **Errors:** `AppError` codes `VALIDATION_ERROR` (weights ≠ 100, bad bands, non-MANUAL field edit, mark-missing before due), `CONFLICT` (scale in use, editing a PUBLISHED card), `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN`.\n284\t- **Logging:** `logger` only, never `console.log` (NFR-9).\n285\t- **Timezone (NFR-10):** all date rules go through `getSchoolTimezone()` + `schoolToday`. UI dates use `DateDisplay`.\n286\t- **Out of scope (NFR-13):** no GPA computation, class rank, transcripts or standards-based grading.\n287\t\n288\t---\n289\t\n290\t## 6. Test Plan Mapping (NFR-12)\n291\t\n292\t| Layer | File | Covers |\n293\t|---|---|---|\n294\t| Unit | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.test.ts` | no categories, empty categories, Uncategorised (A8), drop lowest (AC-2) and never-drop-all, missing vs ungraded vs excused (AC-5), past-due boundary, overrides (letter-only AC-6, percent-only A12), rounding 89.95 → 90.0 → A−, 77.0 → C+, the FR-15 golden 78.0 C+ |\n295\t| Unit | `term-placement.test.ts` | containment at tz day boundaries, current-term fallback, null |\n296\t| Integration | `gradebook-sync.test.ts` | return → Grade, save-without-return → none (AC-3), exemption on/off, quiz GRADED + IMMEDIATE / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL release, practice skipped, archive hides, delete removes, teacher hide survives re-save (A7) |\n297\t| Integration | `backfill.test.ts` | run twice → identical counts |\n298\t| Integration | `report-cards.test.ts` | generate → publish → edit grade → snapshot unchanged (AC-8), regenerate skips PUBLISHED, 7B student gets NOT_FOUND (AC-7), notifications sent |\n299\t| Integration | `perf` (optional, CI-skippable) | 35×80 gradebook < 800 ms, 600×8 generation < 30 s |\n300\t| Playwright | `gradebook.spec.ts`, `report-cards.spec.ts` | keyboard edits (digits, E, M, Delete, Enter/arrows), admin generate + publish, parent opens print view with sidebar hidden under print media |\n301\t\n302\t---\n303\t\n304\t## 7. Requirements Traceability\n305\t\n306\t| Req | Design element(s) |\n307\t|---|---|\n308\t| FR-1 | §2.1 migration: PRD FR-1 models verbatim, plus indexes and the partial unique default index |\n309\t| FR-2 | §2.1 `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment/Quiz.categoryId` (SetNull). §2.2 validator and editor `Select` hooks. |\n310\t| FR-3 | `gradebook-sync.upsertItemFromAssignment/Quiz`, `term-placement.termFor` (A6, A10). Hooks in §2.2. |\n311\t| FR-4 | `hideItemForSource`, `deleteItemForSource` (same transaction). A7, A15. |\n312\t| FR-5 | `syncSubmissionGrade` from `gradeSubmission` / `bulkReturn` / `gradeOffline`, only when RETURNED (§3.1) |\n313\t| FR-6 | `setExemption` → `syncSubmissionGrade` (A1) |\n314\t| FR-7 | `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers, `syncQuizGrades` on release and close, existing `getStudentQuizScore` + `resultsVisible` (A2) |\n315\t| FR-8 | `gradebook/backfill.ts`, `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, npm script, seed call (§2.5) |\n316\t| FR-9 | `putGrade` / `updateItem` reject non-comment and non-`isVisible` fields on synced items. Grid `isCellEditable`. |\n317\t| FR-10 | `grade-calc.ts` `counted()` predicate (§3.2) |\n318\t| FR-11 | `applyDropLowest`, `categoryPercent` |\n319\t| FR-12 | course aggregation with renormalised weights, Uncategorised bucket, points fallback (A8) |\n320\t| FR-13 | `roundHalfUp1` + `letterFor`, `effectiveScale` (A3) |\n321\t| FR-14 | `applyOverride` (A12), `putTermOverride` |\n322\t| FR-15 | single shared calc for the gradebook and student views. Golden unit test. |\n323\t| FR-16 | `scales-service`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `bandsSchema`, partial unique index (A11) |\n324\t| FR-17 | `categories-service`, gradebook settings page with live sum, scale select |\n325\t| FR-18 | `GradebookGrid` (MIT DataGrid, column groups, virtualisation, sticky header), `getGradebook`, `courseTabs.gradebook` |\n326\t| FR-19 | `GradebookGrid` `renderCell`. The payload carries `isLate`. |\n327\t| FR-20 | `renderEditCell` + `onCellKeyDown` + `processRowUpdate`, PUT grade, optimistic update with per-cell error (§3.4) |\n328\t| FR-21 | payload `submissionId` / `attemptId` → links to the existing grading and attempt pages |\n329\t| FR-22 | `AddManualItemDialog`, `POST /api/courses/[id]/grade-items`, `createManualItem` |\n330\t| FR-23 | `TermOverrideDialog`, `PUT term-overrides`, `termOverrideSchema` (≤ 1000) |\n331\t| FR-24 | column menu: `PATCH isVisible`, `POST mark-missing`, `ItemStatsDialog` |\n332\t| FR-25 | `exportGradebookCsv` via `toCsv`, `?format=csv` |\n333\t| FR-26 | `StudentGradesView`, `studentTabs.grades`, `gradeColour` |\n334\t| FR-27 | `/grades` page with parent child select, nav entry (A4) |\n335\t| FR-28 | `courses/[courseId]/grades`, `courseTabs.grades` |\n336\t| FR-29 | `/admin/report-cards`, `listReportCards` with warnings (§3.5) |\n337\t| FR-30 | `generateDrafts`, `buildSnapshot` v1, attendance `getReport` |\n338\t| FR-31 | DRAFT-only `updateMany`. Gradebook never writes ReportCard (§3.5). |\n339\t| FR-32 | `report-cards/[id]` review page, `patchComments`, field-level access (§4, A13) |\n340\t| FR-33 | `/report-cards` homeroom list, TEACHER nav entry |\n341\t| FR-34 | `publish` / `unpublish`, notify after commit, audit with reason (A13) |\n342\t| FR-35 | print pages, `ReportCardDocument`, `@page` A4 + `@media print` GlobalStyles, `PrintButton` |\n343\t| FR-36 | `studentTabs['report-cards']`, `listForStudent` (PUBLISHED-only for student/parent) |\n344\t| FR-37 | `report-cards/access.assertCanViewReportCard` (NOT_FOUND for others) |\n345\t| FR-38 | `types.ts` registrations, `grade.posted` on first score (A9), `report_card.published` |\n346\t| FR-39 | §2.3 route table: `withHandler` → `validators/gradebook.ts` → services, existing course-access |\n347\t| FR-40 | `categories-service.replaceCategories` (transaction, `dec(sum).eq(100)`) |\n348\t| FR-41 | `prisma/seed.ts` sequence (§2.5) |\n349\t| FR-42 | `student-grades-service` (visible-only query + whitelist serializer) |\n350\t| NFR-1 | `grade-calc.ts` pure Decimal, single final rounding, unit matrix (§6) |\n351\t| NFR-2 | `load.ts` 7 indexed queries, in-memory calc, DataGrid virtualisation, `GradeItem(courseId, termId)` index |\n352\t| NFR-3 | batched `load.ts` with `in` filters, one attendance groupBy, chunked writes (§3.5) |\n353\t| NFR-4 | `audit()` calls listed in §5 with `{old, new}` |\n354\t| NFR-5 | three layers: sync gating (§3.1), visible-only serializer (§3.6), PUBLISHED-only card guard |\n355\t| NFR-6 | §4 matrix. Every route and server page calls `requireUser`/`requireRole` plus the entity asserts. |\n356\t| NFR-7 | §2.4 MUI-only components looked up via mui-mcp, `useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`, `Autocomplete` |\n357\t| NFR-8 | `GradebookGrid` MIT props only, no pinned columns |\n358\t| NFR-9 | new code only in `src/server/gradebook/` and `src/server/report-cards/`, one-line hooks, reuse table (§2.2), `logger` |\n359\t| NFR-10 | `term-placement` (tz dates), instant past-due (A5), `DateDisplay` |\n360\t| NFR-11 | A4 `@page`, print media rules, `break-after` / `break-inside` |\n361\t| NFR-12 | §6 test plan |\n362\t| NFR-13 | `gpa` stored only. No rank or transcript components. |\n363\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6f85ae0-4ad4-4d10-b797-6ff9d3e2b1f5","uuid":"aafd1590-10c6-479f-aac6-759d5849a36d","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:15:26.138Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n\nTicket: **SH-11** · Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T17:30:00Z · Status: **complete**\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (42 FR + 13 NFR), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-10), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B19, R1–R7), and the source PRD `11-gradebook.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-11 adds a gradebook to SchoolHub, a brownfield Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/PostgreSQL + MUI 9.5.0 app. It has four parts:\n\n1. **Sync.** Published assignments and quizzes become `GradeItem`s. Returned submissions and released quiz results become `Grade`s.\n2. **Calculation.** A pure Decimal function turns items, grades, categories, a scale and an override into a term percent and letter.\n3. **Views.** A teacher grid (MIT DataGrid), student/parent grade views, and admin pages for scales and categories.\n4. **Report cards.** Frozen JSON snapshots per student and term, with a draft → published workflow, notifications and an A4 print view.\n\nThe design adds **no dependencies** (ADR-1). New server code lives only in `src/server/gradebook/` and `src/server/report-cards/` (NFR-9). Existing services gain one-line calls into the sync module.\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`** at 95% confidence. There is nothing to escalate. The flagged assumptions are resolved in §1.2.\n\n### 1.2 Assumptions and design decisions (need product sign-off, none block dev)\n\n| # | Topic | Decision | Req |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Exemption removal | Unexempt sets `excused = false` and re-derives `score` from the source: `finalScore` if the submission is RETURNED, otherwise `null`. | FR-6 |\n| A2 | Quiz score source | **Intake's correction:** `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` **already exists** in `src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts` (L359, labelled \"PRD-11 export\"). Call it as is. It does **not** check visibility, so the sync gates on `resultsVisible()` first. This replaces ADR-6's \"add a helper to grading.ts\". Don't create a second one. | FR-7, NFR-9 |\n| A3 | 89.95 rounding | 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale (A is 93). The unit test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter. | FR-13 |\n| A4 | Nav entries | Add `/grades` (STUDENT, PARENT), `/report-cards` (TEACHER), and `/admin/grading-scales` and `/admin/report-cards` (ADMIN, group `Administration`). | FR-16, FR-27, FR-29, FR-33 |\n| A5 | Past due | `now > dueAt` as a UTC instant. Term containment compares school-local dates (`SchoolSettings.timezone`). | NFR-10 |\n| A6 | No term | If no term of the course's academic year contains the date and no term contains today, skip the item and `logger.warn`. | FR-3 |\n| A7 | Teacher hide vs source visibility (R2) | **No extra column** (FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\"). Source sync writes `isVisible` only on source visibility **transitions**: publish / publishOnce → `true`, archive → `false`. Plain edits to an already-published source never touch `isVisible`, so a teacher's hide survives re-saves. | FR-4, FR-24 |\n| A8 | Uncategorised weight (R3) | If the course has categories, the implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket is **shown with its subtotal but has weight 0**, so it's excluded from the weighted mean. If no category has a counted item, fall back to the points total over **all** counted items. If the course has no categories, use the points total. | FR-12 |\n| A9 | `grade.posted` dedupe (R4) | No marker column. Notify only when a MANUAL grade's `score` goes from `null` to a value. That gives one notification per student per item. Later edits are audited but not notified. | FR-38 |\n| A10 | Term drift (R5) | Re-derive `GradeItem.termId` only when `dueAt`/`availableUntil` changes. | FR-3 |\n| A11 | Scale delete (R6) | Return `CONFLICT` if the scale is the default or any `Course.gradingScaleId` references it. Published snapshots embed their own legend, so they're unaffected. | FR-16 |\n| A12 | Percent-only override | Re-derive the letter from the effective scale using the override percent. | FR-14 |\n| A13 | Report card edits | Comments are editable only while `DRAFT`. Unpublish returns the card to `DRAFT` and clears `publishedAt`/`publishedById`. | FR-32, FR-34 |\n| A14 | `Grade.updatedById` on system writes | Sync uses the acting user (grader/teacher) when there is one. Otherwise (auto-graded quiz, maintenance release, backfill) it uses `quiz.createdById`, `assignment.createdById` or, for backfill, `course.teacherId`. The column has no FK, as specified. | FR-1, FR-5, FR-7, FR-8 |\n| A15 | Quiz CLOSED | A CLOSED quiz is **not** unpublished. Its item stays visible. Quizzes have no archive. `deleteQuiz` deletes the item. A practice toggle after publish deletes the item. | FR-3, FR-4 |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data model (one migration: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_gradebook/`)\n\nThe models and enums are **exactly the PRD FR-1 block** (FR-1). On top of that:\n\n- **Additive columns (FR-2):** `Course.gradingScaleId String?` → `GradingScale` (`onDelete: SetNull`). `Assignment.categoryId String?` and `Quiz.categoryId String?` → `GradeCategory` (`onDelete: SetNull`), so deleting a category never deletes sources.\n- **Relation fields:** add only the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.gradeItems`, `Course.gradeCategories`, `Term.gradeItems`, `GradeCategory.items/assignments/quizzes`). There are no new scalar columns beyond the spec.\n- **Keys already in the spec make sync race-safe (B19):** `GradeItem.sourceId @unique`, `Grade @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])`, `TermGradeOverride @@id([courseId, termId, studentId])`, `ReportCard @@unique([studentId, termId])`.\n- **Indexes added:**\n  - `GradeItem @@index([courseId, termId])` (NFR-2, NFR-3)\n  - `TermGradeOverride @@index([termId])` (NFR-3)\n  - `ReportCard @@index([termId, status])` (FR-29)\n- **Raw SQL in the migration:** a partial unique index `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX grading_scale_one_default ON \"GradingScale\" (\"isDefault\") WHERE \"isDefault\";` as the backstop for \"exactly one default\" (FR-16, ADR-3).\n- **Types:** `bands Json` holds `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }[]`, sorted descending and validated by Zod (`bandsSchema`). `gpa` is stored and never computed (NFR-13).\n\n### 2.2 Server modules\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reuses | Req |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` | **Pure** functions with no Prisma client import (types only): `computeStudentTerm(input)`, `categoryPercent`, `applyDropLowest`, `roundHalfUp1`, `letterFor(percent, bands)`, `applyOverride`, `effectiveScale(course, default)`, `gradeColour(percent)`. Everything is `Decimal`, and rounding happens once at the end. | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `assignments/grading-math.ts` | FR-10–FR-15, FR-26, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/term-placement.ts` | Pure `termFor(date, terms, tz, now)`: picks the containing term in school-local dates, falls back to the term containing today, else returns `null`. | `schoolToday` (attendance-rules), `getSchoolTimezone` | FR-3, NFR-10, A6 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts` (file name from the PRD) | Idempotent upserts. `upsertItemFromAssignment(tx, id)`, `upsertItemFromQuiz(tx, id)`, `hideItemForSource(tx, sourceId)`, `deleteItemForSource(tx, sourceId)`, `syncSubmissionGrade(tx, assignmentId, studentId, actorId?)`, `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, `syncQuizGrades(quizId)`. It also exports **pure row builders** (`itemFromAssignment`, `gradeFromSubmission`, `gradeFromQuizScore`) that the backfill shares. | `isAssignmentVisible`, `getStudentQuizScore`, `resultsVisible`, `applyScoringPolicy`, `logger` | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-5 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/backfill.ts` | `backfillGradebook()`. Batch-loads per course and runs the same row builders with `upsert`. Idempotent through the unique keys. | `applyScoringPolicy` in memory (no per-student `getStudentQuizScore`) | FR-8, NFR-3 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-service.ts` | `getGradebook(user, courseId, termId)`, `createManualItem`, `updateItem`, `deleteItem`, `putGrade`, `markAllMissing`, `putTermOverride`, `exportGradebookCsv`. Loads the data, calls grade-calc, enforces FR-9 and writes audit entries. | `assertCanManageCourse`, `audit`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `toCsv` | FR-9, FR-18–FR-25, FR-38, NFR-2, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/categories-service.ts` | `getCategories`, `replaceCategories` (in a transaction: delete removed ids, upsert the rest, `dec(sum).eq(100)`), and `setCourseScale`. | `assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse` | FR-17, FR-40 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/scales-service.ts` | CRUD. `setDefault` runs in a transaction that clears the other defaults. Delete is guarded (A11). | `requireRole('ADMIN')`, `audit` | FR-16 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/student-grades-service.ts` | `getStudentGrades(user, studentId, termId, courseId?)`. Uses the visible-only serializer. Reuses grade-calc and passes **visible items only** into it, so the computed totals match what the student sees. | `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` | FR-26–FR-28, FR-42, NFR-5 |\n| `src/server/gradebook/load.ts` | Shared batched loader: `loadCourseTermData(courseIds[], termId, studentIds?)` returns `{items, grades, categories, overrides, scales}` in 5 `findMany` calls with `in` filters, grouped in memory. Used by the gradebook, student grades and report-card generation. | Prisma | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n| `src/server/report-cards/snapshot.ts` | Zod `snapshotSchema` (`v: 1`) and the pure `buildSnapshot(student, courses, computed, attendance, school, scale)`. | grade-calc | FR-30 |\n| `src/server/report-cards/report-card-service.ts` | `listReportCards` (with warnings), `generateDrafts`, `getReportCard`, `patchComments`, `publish`, `unpublish`, `listForStudent`. | `load.ts`, attendance `getReport`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `audit` | FR-29–FR-34, FR-36, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/report-cards/access.ts` | `assertCanViewReportCard(user, card)`, `canEditHomeroomComment`. | `student-access`, `Section.homeroomTeacherId`, `Enrollment` | FR-32, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts` | Zod: `bandsSchema`, `scaleSchema`, `categoriesPutSchema`, `manualItemSchema`, `itemPatchSchema`, `gradePutSchema`, `termOverrideSchema` (comment ≤ 1000), `reportCardPatchSchema`, `generateSchema`, `publishSchema`, `unpublishSchema` (reason required). These are shared by client forms and handlers. | Zod | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (edit) | Register `grade.posted` (STUDENT+PARENT, `defaultEmail: false`) and `report_card.published` (STUDENT+PARENT, `defaultEmail: true`). | existing registry | FR-38 |\n\n**Hook edits to existing services** (each is one call; behaviour is otherwise unchanged, per NFR-9):\n\n| Existing site | Added call | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `assignments-service` `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` / `publishOnce` | `upsertItemFromAssignment(tx, id)`. This sets `isVisible` only on a visibility transition (A7). It re-places the term only if `dueAt` changed (A10). | FR-3, FR-4 |\n| `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` | archive → `hideItemForSource`; hard delete → `deleteItemForSource` in the same transaction (B9) | FR-4 |\n| `gradeSubmission`, `bulkReturn`, `gradeOffline` | `syncSubmissionGrade` when the submission **is** RETURNED after the write. This covers re-grades of returned work. Nothing happens otherwise (AC-3). | FR-5, NFR-5 |\n| `setExemption` (both branches) | `syncSubmissionGrade` (A1) | FR-6 |\n| `quiz-service` `updateQuiz` (→PUBLISHED, or edits to a published quiz) / `deleteQuiz` | `upsertItemFromQuiz` / `deleteItemForSource`. Practice quizzes are skipped; turning practice on deletes the item. Wrap `deleteQuiz` in a transaction. | FR-3, FR-4 |\n| After callers of `recomputeAttempt` commit (`submitAttempt`, `gradeAnswerManually`, `regradeQuiz`) | `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`: no-op unless GRADED, `resultsVisible` and not practice | FR-7 |\n| `releaseResults` (MANUAL) and `quiz/maintenance.ts` AFTER_CLOSE claim (`count === 1`) | `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` (bulk). Without this, delayed-visibility quizzes never sync (R1). | FR-7, NFR-5 |\n| Assignment and quiz Zod validators and editors | Optional nullable `categoryId` plus one MUI `Select` of the course's categories | FR-2 |\n\n### 2.3 API layer (`src/app/api/**/route.ts`, thin: `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok()`)\n\nThese match the PRD API table exactly. `api-contracts.json` (next sub-task) owns the shapes.\n\n| Route | Role check | Service | Req |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET/POST /api/grading-scales`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/grading-scales/[id]` | GET: `requireUser`; writes: ADMIN | scales-service | FR-16, FR-39 |\n| `GET/PUT /api/courses/[id]/grade-categories` | view / manage | categories-service (PUT body also carries `gradingScaleId`) | FR-17, FR-40 |\n| `GET /api/courses/[id]/gradebook?termId=` (`&format=csv` → `text/csv`) | manage | gradebook-service | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, FR-25, NFR-2 |\n| `POST /api/courses/[id]/grade-items` | manage | createManualItem | FR-22 |\n| `PATCH/DELETE /api/grade-items/[id]` | manage (via the item's course) | updateItem / deleteItem. Non-MANUAL items accept only `isVisible`, and DELETE is MANUAL only. | FR-9, FR-24 |\n| `POST /api/grade-items/[id]/mark-missing` | manage | markAllMissing (`now > dueAt`, ungraded rows only) | FR-24 |\n| `PUT /api/grade-items/[id]/grades/[studentId]` | manage + enrolled student | putGrade. Non-MANUAL items accept only `comment` (FR-9). | FR-9, FR-20, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n| `PUT /api/courses/[id]/term-overrides/[studentId]` | manage | putTermOverride | FR-14, FR-23, NFR-4 |\n| `GET /api/students/[id]/grades?termId=&courseId=` | `assertCanViewStudent` | student-grades-service | FR-26–FR-28, FR-42 |\n| `GET /api/report-cards?termId=&gradeLevelId=&sectionId=&studentId=` | ADMIN; homeroom TEACHER (own sections); with `studentId`, view-student rules plus PUBLISHED-only for student/parent | listReportCards / listForStudent | FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |\n| `POST /api/report-cards/generate` | ADMIN | generateDrafts | FR-30, FR-31, NFR-3 |\n| `GET /api/report-cards/[id]` | `assertCanViewReportCard` | getReportCard | FR-37 |\n| `PATCH /api/report-cards/[id]` | field-level (§4) | patchComments | FR-32 |\n| `POST /api/report-cards/publish`, `POST /api/report-cards/unpublish` | ADMIN | publish / unpublish | FR-34 |\n\n`mark-missing` is the only route not in the PRD table. It implements the FR-24 column action server-side, because a client loop of N PUTs would write N audit rows and be slow. The `?format=csv` and `courseId`/`studentId` query parameters extend existing PRD routes rather than adding new ones.\n\n### 2.4 UI (`src/app/(app)/…`, MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, per NFR-7)\n\n| Page / component | Notes | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `admin/grading-scales/page.tsx` + `ScaleEditorDialog` | `DataTable` list. The dialog uses a band editor (TextField rows, add/remove) with Zod errors inline and a \"Default\" `Switch`. | FR-16 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/gradebook/settings/page.tsx` | Category rows (name, weight, drop lowest, order), a live `Σ weights / 100` `Chip` (error colour ≠ 100, Save disabled), and a scale `Select` (\"School default\" = null). | FR-17 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/gradebook/page.tsx` + `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx` | The single client component that owns the DataGrid (ADR-4, R7). Term `Select`, `columnGroupingModel` by category, custom `renderHeader` (title, due date, max, source icon), `renderCell` (score / EX / M red / — / late `AccessTime` icon), and `isCellEditable` = MANUAL only. Editing runs through `renderEditCell` + `onCellKeyDown` (digits, E, M, Delete, Enter/arrows), then `processRowUpdate` → PUT, `onProcessRowUpdateError` → per-cell error, and `hideFooter`. There are **no pinned columns**. Toolbar: \"Add manual item\", \"Export CSV\", \"Settings\". | FR-18–FR-25, NFR-8 |\n| `AddManualItemDialog`, `TermOverrideDialog`, `ItemStatsDialog` | Dialogs. Stats (average, median, high, low) are computed client-side from the payload over counted scores. | FR-22, FR-23, FR-24 |\n| `src/components/gradebook/StudentGradesView.tsx` | Course `Card`s with percent, letter and `gradeColour` `Chip`. `Accordion` expands to items and category subtotals. One component serves three hosts: | FR-26–FR-28 |\n| ↳ `students/[id]/grades/page.tsx` | student tab | FR-26 |\n| ↳ `grades/page.tsx` | STUDENT: self. PARENT: child `Select` from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-27 |\n| ↳ `courses/[courseId]/grades/page.tsx` | filtered to one course | FR-28 |\n| `admin/report-cards/page.tsx` | Term / grade level / section filters, `DataTable` with status `Chip` and warnings, and \"Generate drafts\", \"Publish all\", \"Print all\" actions. Confirmations use `ConfirmDialog`. | FR-29, FR-30, FR-34, FR-35 |\n| `report-cards/page.tsx` | Homeroom TEACHER: their sections' cards for the selected term | FR-33 |\n| `report-cards/[id]/page.tsx` | Review page: `ReportCardDocument` preview plus homeroom/principal comment fields (disabled per role or when PUBLISHED), and Publish / Unpublish (reason dialog) for ADMIN | FR-32, FR-34 |\n| `report-cards/[id]/print/page.tsx`, `report-cards/print/page.tsx?termId=&…` | Server components rendering `ReportCardDocument` from the **snapshot only**. `GlobalStyles`: `@page { size: A4 portrait; margin: 12mm }`, `@media print` hides the app shell and buttons, each card gets `break-after: page`, and rows get `break-inside: avoid`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. Bulk print shows filtered PUBLISHED cards only. | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n| `students/[id]/report-cards/page.tsx` | List of cards, each linking to the print view | FR-36 |\n| Config | `courseTabs`: `gradebook` (ADMIN, TEACHER) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). `studentTabs`: `grades` and `report-cards`. `navigation`: the four entries from A4. | FR-18, FR-26–FR-28, FR-33, FR-36 |\n\nEvery page server-checks the role with `requireUser`/`requireRole` plus the same entity assert as its API (NFR-6). It never relies on hidden links.\n\n### 2.5 Scripts and seed\n\n- `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. The script calls `backfillGradebook()` and exits (FR-8, ADR-7).\n- `prisma/seed.ts`:\n  1. scale \"Standard A–F\" (default)\n  2. Homework 30 (drop 1) / Quizzes 30 / Exams 40 for each 7A course\n  3. `backfillGradebook()`\n  4. ENG-7A manual item \"Oral presentation\" graded for all enrolled students\n  5. Semester 1 `TermGradeOverride.teacherComment` for MATH-7A and ENG-7A\n  6. `generateDrafts(S1, 7A students)`\n\n  Categories go in before the backfill so seeded assignments and quizzes can be attached to them (FR-41).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Source → gradebook sync (write path)\n\n```\nTeacher publishes assignment ─► assignments-service (tx) ─► upsertItemFromAssignment(tx)\n                                                              ├─ termFor(dueAt, courseYearTerms, tz)  → null ⇒ warn+skip\n                                                              └─ GradeItem upsert by sourceId (isVisible only on transition)\nTeacher returns submission  ─► gradeSubmission/bulkReturn/gradeOffline (tx)\n                                  └─ status==RETURNED ? syncSubmissionGrade(tx): Grade upsert {score: finalScore,\n                                                                                  excused: exemption exists}\nQuiz attempt graded         ─► recomputeAttempt → commit → syncQuizGrade(quiz, student)\n                                  └─ GRADED ∧ resultsVisible ∧ ¬isPractice ? getStudentQuizScore → scale to maxPoints → upsert\nResults released / closed   ─► releaseResults | maintenance claim ─► syncQuizGrades(quiz)  (bulk, batched)\n```\n\nBecause unreleased scores are **never written** into `Grade`, privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers (NFR-5, layer 1 of 3).\n\nQuiz scaling: `score = result.score / result.maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, where `maxPoints = quiz maxScore`, in Decimal with `fixed2` at write.\n\n### 3.2 Calculation (pure, `grade-calc.ts`)\n\n```\ninput: { items[], grades by itemId, categories[], bands, override?, now }\ncounted(item) = item.isVisible ∧ ¬grade.excused ∧ (grade.score ≠ null ∨ (grade.missing ∧ item.dueAt ∧ now > item.dueAt))\nearned = score ?? 0\nper category: sort counted by pct asc (tie: dueAt, id) → drop min(dropLowest, n−1) → Σearned/Σmax×100\ncourse: categories present with ≥1 counted ⇒ Σ(w·pct)/Σw   (Uncategorised w = 0, A8)\n        no categories / none counted       ⇒ Σearned/Σmax×100 over all counted\n        nothing counted                    ⇒ percent = null, letter = null (\"—\")\npercent = round half-up to 1 dp (only here) → letter = first band with percent ≥ minPercent\noverride: percent? → replaces percent (letter re-derived unless letter set, A12); letter? → replaces letter only\n```\n\nThe output per student is `{ categories: [{id, name, weight, percent, earned, possible, droppedItemIds}], percent, letter, descriptor, computedPercent, computedLetter, overridden }`. The gradebook, the student views and report-card generation all call this **one** function, which guarantees FR-15 / AC-1 (78.0% C+ in both places).\n\n### 3.3 Gradebook read (NFR-2: 35×80 < 800 ms)\n\n`GET gradebook` → `assertCanManageCourse` → `load.ts`:\n\n1. active enrollments + students, sorted by last name\n2. items `(courseId, termId)`\n3. grades for those item ids\n4. categories\n5. override rows + course scale or default\n\nThen two lookup queries for click-through and late flags: `Submission {id, isLate}` by `assignmentId in` and `QuizAttempt {id}` by `quizId in`. That's seven indexed queries in total. The pure calc runs for each student in memory, and the response is one denormalised payload. The client builds the columns, and the grid virtualises rows and columns.\n\n### 3.4 Manual grade edit\n\n```\ncell edit ─► processRowUpdate ─► PUT /api/grade-items/:id/grades/:studentId\n   service (tx): load old grade → reject non-comment fields if item.source ≠ MANUAL (FR-9)\n                 → upsert → audit('grade.update', {old, new})\n   after commit: old.score == null ∧ new.score ≠ null ∧ MANUAL ⇒ notifyStudentAndParents('grade.posted')  (A9)\n   response: updated grade + recomputed student row (so the term % cell refreshes)\n```\n\nOn error the client rolls back the optimistic value and flags the cell.\n\n### 3.5 Report card lifecycle\n\n```\ngenerate {termId, studentIds} (ADMIN)\n  ├─ load once: students (+section, homeroom, gradeLevel), school settings, term+year, default scale,\n  │             enrollments for those students in courses of the term's year,\n  │             load.ts for all those courseIds (in-filters), attendance getReport(term range) ×1\n  ├─ compute in memory: grade-calc per (student, course) → buildSnapshot(v:1)\n  └─ write (chunks of 100, tx): createMany(skipDuplicates) for new;\n                                updateMany({ where:{ id, status:'DRAFT' }, data:{ snapshot, generatedAt } }) for existing\n     PUBLISHED rows are filtered out by the WHERE clause, which enforces immutability (FR-31 / AC-8)\npublish {ids}   ─► updateMany({ id in ids, status:'DRAFT' } → PUBLISHED, publishedAt, publishedById)\n                   → audit('reportCard.publish') → after commit notify report_card.published per card\nunpublish {ids, reason} ─► PUBLISHED → DRAFT, clear publishedAt/ById, audit('reportCard.unpublish', {old, new, reason})\nprint            ─► reads snapshot only; never recomputes\n```\n\nNothing in `src/server/gradebook/` imports `src/server/report-cards/` or writes `ReportCard`. Grade edits therefore cannot touch snapshots.\n\n**Snapshot v1 shape**, owned by `snapshotSchema`:\n\n```\n{ v: 1,\n  school:     { name, logoUrl },\n  student:    { name, admissionNumber, gradeLevel, section, homeroomTeacher },\n  term:       { name, startDate, endDate, academicYear },\n  courses:    [{ subject, code, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor, teacherComment }],\n  attendance: { rate, absences, lates, ...counts },\n  scale:      { name, bands } }\n```\n\n`attendance.rate` uses the same formula the existing attendance report consumers use; dev must not invent a new one (B13). Each course's letter uses that course's effective scale. The legend shows the default scale and also lists any course-specific scale used.\n\n**Missing-data warnings (FR-29)** are computed in the same batched pass:\n\n- a count of courses with eligible-but-ungraded items (visible, past due, no score, not missing, not excused)\n- courses with no `teacherComment` override for the student\n\n### 3.6 Student/parent read (privacy, NFR-5 layers 2 and 3)\n\n`GET /api/students/:id/grades`: `assertCanViewStudent` → `load.ts` with `isVisible = true` filtered **in the query** → calc → serializer emits only whitelisted fields (no `updatedById`, no hidden items).\n\nReport-card endpoints apply `assertCanViewReportCard`. STUDENT and PARENT pass only if `card.status === 'PUBLISHED'` and they're the student or a linked parent. Anyone else unauthorised gets **NOT_FOUND**, so a 7B student can't tell that Sam's card exists (AC-7).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Access Control Matrix (NFR-6)\n\n| Action | ADMIN | TEACHER | STUDENT | PARENT |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Read scales | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |\n| Write scales | ✓ | — | — | — |\n| Categories GET | ✓ | view course | view course | view course |\n| Categories PUT | ✓ | teaches course | — | — |\n| Gradebook / items / grades / overrides | ✓ | teaches course (`assertCanManageCourse`) | — | — |\n| Student grades | ✓ | teaches student or is homeroom (existing student-access) | self | linked child |\n| Report cards list / generate | list + generate | list: own homeroom sections | own published (via `studentId`) | child's published |\n| Report card GET | ✓ | teaches any course of the student, or is homeroom | self, PUBLISHED only | linked, PUBLISHED only |\n| `homeroomComment` PATCH | ✓ | homeroom teacher of the student's section, DRAFT only | — | — |\n| `principalComment` PATCH | ✓ (DRAFT only) | — | — | — |\n| Publish / unpublish | ✓ | — | — | — |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-cutting\n\n- **Audit (NFR-4):**\n  - required: `grade.update` (manual, and comment edits on synced grades), `grade.markMissing`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (with reason), each carrying `{old, new}`\n  - extra: `reportCard.publish`, `gradingScale.create/update/delete`, `gradeCategories.replace`\n- **Notifications (FR-38):** sent after commit, using `notify()`, which never throws, so a notification failure can't roll back a grade.\n- **Errors:** `AppError` codes `VALIDATION_ERROR` (weights ≠ 100, bad bands, non-MANUAL field edit, mark-missing before due), `CONFLICT` (scale in use, editing a PUBLISHED card), `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN`.\n- **Logging:** `logger` only, never `console.log` (NFR-9).\n- **Timezone (NFR-10):** all date rules go through `getSchoolTimezone()` + `schoolToday`. UI dates use `DateDisplay`.\n- **Out of scope (NFR-13):** no GPA computation, class rank, transcripts or standards-based grading.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Test Plan Mapping (NFR-12)\n\n| Layer | File | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unit | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.test.ts` | no categories, empty categories, Uncategorised (A8), drop lowest (AC-2) and never-drop-all, missing vs ungraded vs excused (AC-5), past-due boundary, overrides (letter-only AC-6, percent-only A12), rounding 89.95 → 90.0 → A−, 77.0 → C+, the FR-15 golden 78.0 C+ |\n| Unit | `term-placement.test.ts` | containment at tz day boundaries, current-term fallback, null |\n| Integration | `gradebook-sync.test.ts` | return → Grade, save-without-return → none (AC-3), exemption on/off, quiz GRADED + IMMEDIATE / AFTER_CLOSE / MANUAL release, practice skipped, archive hides, delete removes, teacher hide survives re-save (A7) |\n| Integration | `backfill.test.ts` | run twice → identical counts |\n| Integration | `report-cards.test.ts` | generate → publish → edit grade → snapshot unchanged (AC-8), regenerate skips PUBLISHED, 7B student gets NOT_FOUND (AC-7), notifications sent |\n| Integration | `perf` (optional, CI-skippable) | 35×80 gradebook < 800 ms, 600×8 generation < 30 s |\n| Playwright | `gradebook.spec.ts`, `report-cards.spec.ts` | keyboard edits (digits, E, M, Delete, Enter/arrows), admin generate + publish, parent opens print view with sidebar hidden under print media |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 migration: PRD FR-1 models verbatim, plus indexes and the partial unique default index |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment/Quiz.categoryId` (SetNull). §2.2 validator and editor `Select` hooks. |\n| FR-3 | `gradebook-sync.upsertItemFromAssignment/Quiz`, `term-placement.termFor` (A6, A10). Hooks in §2.2. |\n| FR-4 | `hideItemForSource`, `deleteItemForSource` (same transaction). A7, A15. |\n| FR-5 | `syncSubmissionGrade` from `gradeSubmission` / `bulkReturn` / `gradeOffline`, only when RETURNED (§3.1) |\n| FR-6 | `setExemption` → `syncSubmissionGrade` (A1) |\n| FR-7 | `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers, `syncQuizGrades` on release and close, existing `getStudentQuizScore` + `resultsVisible` (A2) |\n| FR-8 | `gradebook/backfill.ts`, `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, npm script, seed call (§2.5) |\n| FR-9 | `putGrade` / `updateItem` reject non-comment and non-`isVisible` fields on synced items. Grid `isCellEditable`. |\n| FR-10 | `grade-calc.ts` `counted()` predicate (§3.2) |\n| FR-11 | `applyDropLowest`, `categoryPercent` |\n| FR-12 | course aggregation with renormalised weights, Uncategorised bucket, points fallback (A8) |\n| FR-13 | `roundHalfUp1` + `letterFor`, `effectiveScale` (A3) |\n| FR-14 | `applyOverride` (A12), `putTermOverride` |\n| FR-15 | single shared calc for the gradebook and student views. Golden unit test. |\n| FR-16 | `scales-service`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `bandsSchema`, partial unique index (A11) |\n| FR-17 | `categories-service`, gradebook settings page with live sum, scale select |\n| FR-18 | `GradebookGrid` (MIT DataGrid, column groups, virtualisation, sticky header), `getGradebook`, `courseTabs.gradebook` |\n| FR-19 | `GradebookGrid` `renderCell`. The payload carries `isLate`. |\n| FR-20 | `renderEditCell` + `onCellKeyDown` + `processRowUpdate`, PUT grade, optimistic update with per-cell error (§3.4) |\n| FR-21 | payload `submissionId` / `attemptId` → links to the existing grading and attempt pages |\n| FR-22 | `AddManualItemDialog`, `POST /api/courses/[id]/grade-items`, `createManualItem` |\n| FR-23 | `TermOverrideDialog`, `PUT term-overrides`, `termOverrideSchema` (≤ 1000) |\n| FR-24 | column menu: `PATCH isVisible`, `POST mark-missing`, `ItemStatsDialog` |\n| FR-25 | `exportGradebookCsv` via `toCsv`, `?format=csv` |\n| FR-26 | `StudentGradesView`, `studentTabs.grades`, `gradeColour` |\n| FR-27 | `/grades` page with parent child select, nav entry (A4) |\n| FR-28 | `courses/[courseId]/grades`, `courseTabs.grades` |\n| FR-29 | `/admin/report-cards`, `listReportCards` with warnings (§3.5) |\n| FR-30 | `generateDrafts`, `buildSnapshot` v1, attendance `getReport` |\n| FR-31 | DRAFT-only `updateMany`. Gradebook never writes ReportCard (§3.5). |\n| FR-32 | `report-cards/[id]` review page, `patchComments`, field-level access (§4, A13) |\n| FR-33 | `/report-cards` homeroom list, TEACHER nav entry |\n| FR-34 | `publish` / `unpublish`, notify after commit, audit with reason (A13) |\n| FR-35 | print pages, `ReportCardDocument`, `@page` A4 + `@media print` GlobalStyles, `PrintButton` |\n| FR-36 | `studentTabs['report-cards']`, `listForStudent` (PUBLISHED-only for student/parent) |\n| FR-37 | `report-cards/access.assertCanViewReportCard` (NOT_FOUND for others) |\n| FR-38 | `types.ts` registrations, `grade.posted` on first score (A9), `report_card.published` |\n| FR-39 | §2.3 route table: `withHandler` → `validators/gradebook.ts` → services, existing course-access |\n| FR-40 | `categories-service.replaceCategories` (transaction, `dec(sum).eq(100)`) |\n| FR-41 | `prisma/seed.ts` sequence (§2.5) |\n| FR-42 | `student-grades-service` (visible-only query + whitelist serializer) |\n| NFR-1 | `grade-calc.ts` pure Decimal, single final rounding, unit matrix (§6) |\n| NFR-2 | `load.ts` 7 indexed queries, in-memory calc, DataGrid virtualisation, `GradeItem(courseId, termId)` index |\n| NFR-3 | batched `load.ts` with `in` filters, one attendance groupBy, chunked writes (§3.5) |\n| NFR-4 | `audit()` calls listed in §5 with `{old, new}` |\n| NFR-5 | three layers: sync gating (§3.1), visible-only serializer (§3.6), PUBLISHED-only card guard |\n| NFR-6 | §4 matrix. Every route and server page calls `requireUser`/`requireRole` plus the entity asserts. |\n| NFR-7 | §2.4 MUI-only components looked up via mui-mcp, `useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`, `Autocomplete` |\n| NFR-8 | `GradebookGrid` MIT props only, no pinned columns |\n| NFR-9 | new code only in `src/server/gradebook/` and `src/server/report-cards/`, one-line hooks, reuse table (§2.2), `logger` |\n| NFR-10 | `term-placement` (tz dates), instant past-due (A5), `DateDisplay` |\n| NFR-11 | A4 `@page`, print media rules, `break-after` / `break-inside` |\n| NFR-12 | §6 test plan |\n| NFR-13 | `gpa` stored only. No rank or transcript components. |\n","numLines":363,"startLine":1,"totalLines":363}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Dgnk2ANkN4bLay1mVx99u1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
