{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01223Hz5QirvMbZhiyGKbxHD","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"+\n\n# Data Grid - Column groups\n\nGroup your columns.\n\nGrouping columns lets you have a multi-level hierarchy of columns in your header.\n\n## [Define column groups](#define-column-groups)\n\nYou can define column groups with the `columnGroupingModel` prop. This prop receives an array of column groups.\n\nA column group is defined by at least two properties:\n\n- `groupId`: a string used to identify the group\n- `children`: an array containing the children of the group\n\nThe `children` attribute can contain two types of objects:\n\n- leaves with type `{ field: string }`, which add the column with the corresponding `field` to this group\n- other column groups, making it possible to create nested groups\n\nA column can only be associated with one group.\n\n```jsx\n<DataGrid\n  columnGroupingModel={[\n    {\n      groupId: 'internal data',\n      children: [{ field: 'id' }],\n    },\n    {\n      groupId: 'character',\n      children: [\n        {\n          groupId: 'naming',\n          children: [{ field: 'lastName' }, { field: 'firstName' }],\n        },\n        { field: 'age' },\n      ],\n    },\n  ]}\n/>\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid\n  rows={rows}\n  columns={columns}\n  checkboxSelection\n  disableRowSelectionOnClick\n  columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel}\n/>`\n\n<DataGrid rows={rows} columns={columns} checkboxSelection disableRowSelectionOnClick columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## [Customize column group](#customize-column-group)\n\nIn addition to the required `groupId` and `children`, you can use the following optional properties to customize a column group:\n\n- `headerName`: the string displayed as the column's name (instead of `groupId`).\n- `description`: a text for the tooltip.\n- `headerClassName`: a CSS class for styling customization.\n- `renderHeaderGroup`: a function returning custom React component.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid\n  rows={rows}\n  columns={columns}\n  checkboxSelection\n  disableRowSelectionOnClick\n  columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel}\n/>`\n\n<DataGrid rows={rows} columns={columns} checkboxSelection disableRowSelectionOnClick columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## [Group header height](#group-header-height)\n\nBy default, column group headers are the same height as [column headers](/x/react-data-grid/column-header/#header-height). This will be the default 56 pixels or a custom value set with the `columnHeaderHeight` prop.\n\nThe `columnGroupHeaderHeight` prop can be used to size column group headers independently of column headers.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid\n  rows={rows}\n  columns={columns}\n  columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel}\n  columnGroupHeaderHeight={36}\n/>`\n\n<DataGrid rows={rows} columns={columns} columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel} columnGroupHeaderHeight={36} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## Column reordering\n\nBy default, the columns that are part of a group cannot be dragged to outside their group. You can customize this behavior on specific groups by setting `freeReordering: true` in a column group object.\n\nIn the example below, the `Full name` column group can be divided, but not other column groups.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGridPro\n  rows={rows}\n  columns={columns}\n  checkboxSelection\n  disableRowSelectionOnClick\n  columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel}\n/>`\n\n<DataGridPro rows={rows} columns={columns} checkboxSelection disableRowSelectionOnClick columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## [Collapsible column groups](#collapsible-column-groups)\n\nThe demo below uses [renderHeaderGroup](/x/react-data-grid/column-groups/#customize-column-group) to add a button to collapse/expand the column group.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid\n  rows={rows}\n  columns={columns}\n  checkboxSelection\n  disableRowSelectionOnClick\n  columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel}\n/>`\n\n<DataGrid rows={rows} columns={columns} checkboxSelection disableRowSelectionOnClick columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## [Manage group visibility 🚧](#manage-group-visibility)\n\nThis feature isn't available yet, but it is planned—you can 👍 upvote [this GitHub issue](https://github.com/mui/mui-x/issues/6651) to help us prioritize it. Please don't hesitate to leave a comment there to describe your needs, especially if you have a use case we should address or you're facing specific pain points with your current solution.\n\nWith this feature, users would be able to expand and collapse grouped columns to toggle their visibility.\n\n## Column group ordering 🚧\n\nThis feature isn't available yet, but it is planned—you can 👍 upvote [this GitHub issue](https://github.com/mui/mui-x/issues/9448) to help us prioritize it. Please don't hesitate to leave a comment there to describe your needs, especially if you have a use case we should address or you're facing specific pain points with your current solution.\n\nWith this feature, users would be able to drag and drop grouped headers to move all grouped children at once (which is [already possible for normal columns](/x/react-data-grid/column-ordering/)).\n\n## [API](#api)\n\n- [DataGrid](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid/)\n- [DataGridPro](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid-pro/)\n- [DataGridPremium](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid-premium/)\n+\n\n# Data Grid - Column menu\n\nCustomize your columns menu.\n\n## [Column menu](#column-menu)\n\nEach column header comes with a column menu with quickly accessible Data Grid features like column visibility, sorting, filtering, and others.\n\nIt can be accessed by clicking on the 3-dots icon that appears on hover on a header cell or when focusing on a column header and pressing Ctrl+Enter (or ⌘ Command+Enter on macOS).\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## [Customize column menu items](#customize-column-menu-items)\n\nYou can customize the column menu items by passing the `slots` and `slotProps` props to the `<GridColumnMenu />` component:\n\n- `slots` \\- use this prop to override default column menu slots or add new slots.\n- `slotProps` \\- use this prop to override or pass [displayOrder](/x/react-data-grid/column-menu/#reordering-menu-items) for column menu items. You can also use this to pass extra props to custom column menu slots.\n\n### [Adding a menu item](#adding-a-menu-item)\n\nTo add a new menu item, create a new item slot and pass it to the `slots` prop. In the example below, the new slot is called `columnMenuUserItem` but you can choose any name and it'll be added to the menu automatically. You can also set the `displayOrder` (default `100`) or pass new props to the slots using the `slotProps` prop.\n\n```tsx\nfunction CustomColumnMenu(props: GridColumnMenuProps) {\n  return (\n    <GridColumnMenu\n      {...props}\n      slots={{\n        // Add new item\n        columnMenuUserItem: CustomUserItem,\n      }}\n      slotProps={{\n        columnMenuUserItem: {\n          // set `displayOrder` for the new item\n          displayOrder: 15,\n          // Additional props\n          myCustomValue: 'Do custom action',\n          myCustomHandler: () => alert('Custom handler fired'),\n        },\n      }}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n### [Overriding default menu items](#overriding-default-menu-items)\n\nUse the `slots` prop to override default menu items. Check [this table](/x/react-data-grid/column-menu/#default-column-menu-items) to know the overridable slot name for each menu item.\n\n```tsx\nfunction CustomColumnMenu(props: GridColumnMenuProps) {\n  return (\n    <GridColumnMenu\n      {...props}\n      slots={{\n        // Override `columnMenuFilterItem` component\n        columnMenuFilterItem: CustomFilterItem,\n      }}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n### [Hiding a menu item](#hiding-a-menu-item)\n\nTo hide a menu item, you can set its respective slot in `slots` to `null`. Check [this table](/x/react-data-grid/column-menu/#default-column-menu-items) to know the slot name for each menu item.\n\n```tsx\nfunction CustomColumnMenu(props: GridColumnMenuProps) {\n  return (\n    <GridColumnMenu\n      {...props}\n      slots={{\n        // Hide `columnMenuColumnsItem`\n        columnMenuColumnsItem: null,\n      }}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n### [Reordering menu items](#reordering-menu-items)\n\nEvery item is assigned a `displayOrder` based on which it is shown before or after other items. It works in ascending order; the smaller the number is, the earlier it is displayed on the list. For new items default value for `displayOrder` is **100**.\n\nYou can override `displayOrder` for the default or new items in `slotProps`.\n\nCheck [this table](/x/react-data-grid/column-menu/#default-column-menu-items) to see default `displayOrder` for each menu item.\n\n```tsx\nfunction CustomColumnMenu(props: GridColumnMenuProps) {\n  return (\n    <GridColumnMenu\n      {...props}\n      slotProps={{\n        // Swap positions of filter and sort items\n        columnMenuFilterItem: {\n          displayOrder: 0, // Previously `10`\n        },\n        columnMenuSortItem: {\n          displayOrder: 10, // Previously `0`\n        },\n      }}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n### [Default column menu items](#default-column-menu-items)\n\nAs a reference, here are the column menu `slots` along with the default item components and `displayOrder`.\n\n## [Custom menu component](#custom-menu-component)\n\nYou can also customize and replace the column menu by [passing a fully custom component](/x/react-data-grid/components/#component-slots) to the `columnMenu` slot of the Data Grid. If you want to add some of the default menu items to your custom component, you can import and re-use them.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid\n  {...data}\n  slots={{\n    columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu,\n  }}\n/>`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu, }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n**Tip**: The `columnMenu` component and its components slots receive the `colDef` prop corresponding to the current column; you can use this to conditionally render some items or change some logic.\n\n## [Disable column menu](#disable-column-menu)\n\nBy default, each column header has the column menu enabled. To disable the column menu, set the prop `disableColumnMenu={true}`.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} disableColumnMenu />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} disableColumnMenu />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## Column menu with Pro/Premium features\n\nIn the following demo, in addition to Data Grid MIT features, you can see commercial features like [grouping](/x/react-data-grid/row-grouping/), [aggregation](/x/react-data-grid/aggregation/), and [computed columns](/x/react-data-grid/computed-columns/) in action. Try tweaking the values from respective column menu items.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGridPremium\n  {...data}\n  apiRef={apiRef}\n  featureDependencies={{ formula: formulaFeature }}\n  groupingColDef={groupingColDef}\n  initialState={initialState}\n/>`\n\n<DataGridPremium {...data} apiRef={apiRef} featureDependencies={{ formula: formulaFeature }} groupingColDef={groupingColDef} initialState={initialState} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## [API](#api)\n\n- [DataGrid](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid/)\n- [DataGridPro](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid-pro/)\n- [DataGridPremium](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid-premium/)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6f85ae0-4ad4-4d10-b797-6ff9d3e2b1f5","uuid":"2a4b88b7-a487-4a6d-89e3-e3ded5412cc4","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:35:44.685Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"+\n\n# Data Grid - Column groups\n\nGroup your columns.\n\nGrouping columns lets you have a multi-level hierarchy of columns in your header.\n\n## [Define column groups](#define-column-groups)\n\nYou can define column groups with the `columnGroupingModel` prop. This prop receives an array of column groups.\n\nA column group is defined by at least two properties:\n\n- `groupId`: a string used to identify the group\n- `children`: an array containing the children of the group\n\nThe `children` attribute can contain two types of objects:\n\n- leaves with type `{ field: string }`, which add the column with the corresponding `field` to this group\n- other column groups, making it possible to create nested groups\n\nA column can only be associated with one group.\n\n```jsx\n<DataGrid\n  columnGroupingModel={[\n    {\n      groupId: 'internal data',\n      children: [{ field: 'id' }],\n    },\n    {\n      groupId: 'character',\n      children: [\n        {\n          groupId: 'naming',\n          children: [{ field: 'lastName' }, { field: 'firstName' }],\n        },\n        { field: 'age' },\n      ],\n    },\n  ]}\n/>\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid\n  rows={rows}\n  columns={columns}\n  checkboxSelection\n  disableRowSelectionOnClick\n  columnGroupingModel={columnGroupingModel}\n/>`\n\n<DataGrid rows={rows} columns={columns} checkbox