dit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n### [Overriding default menu items](#overriding-default-menu-items)\n\nUse the `slots` prop to override default menu items. Check [this table](/x/react-data-grid/column-menu/#default-column-menu-items) to know the overridable slot name for each menu item.\n\n```tsx\nfunction CustomColumnMenu(props: GridColumnMenuProps) {\n  return (\n    <GridColumnMenu\n      {...props}\n      slots={{\n        // Override `columnMenuFilterItem` component\n        columnMenuFilterItem: CustomFilterItem,\n      }}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n### [Hiding a menu item](#hiding-a-menu-item)\n\nTo hide a menu item, you can set its respective slot in `slots` to `null`. Check [this table](/x/react-data-grid/column-menu/#default-column-menu-items) to know the slot name for each menu item.\n\n```tsx\nfunction CustomColumnMenu(props: GridColumnMenuProps) {\n  return (\n    <GridColumnMenu\n      {...props}\n      slots={{\n        // Hide `columnMenuColumnsItem`\n        columnMenuColumnsItem: null,\n      }}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n### [Reordering menu items](#reordering-menu-items)\n\nEvery item is assigned a `displayOrder` based on which it is shown before or after other items. It works in ascending order; the smaller the number is, the earlier it is displayed on the list. For new items default value for `displayOrder` is **100**.\n\nYou can override `displayOrder` for the default or new items in `slotProps`.\n\nCheck [this table](/x/react-data-grid/column-menu/#default-column-menu-items) to see default `displayOrder` for each menu item.\n\n```tsx\nfunction CustomColumnMenu(props: GridColumnMenuProps) {\n  return (\n    <GridColumnMenu\n      {...props}\n      slotProps={{\n        // Swap positions of filter and sort items\n        columnMenuFilterItem: {\n          displayOrder: 0, // Previously `10`\n        },\n        columnMenuSortItem: {\n          displayOrder: 10, // Previously `0`\n        },\n      }}\n    />\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\nCopyCopied(or C)\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n### [Default column menu items](#default-column-menu-items)\n\nAs a reference, here are the column menu `slots` along with the default item components and `displayOrder`.\n\n## [Custom menu component](#custom-menu-component)\n\nYou can also customize and replace the column menu by [passing a fully custom component](/x/react-data-grid/components/#component-slots) to the `columnMenu` slot of the Data Grid. If you want to add some of the default menu items to your custom component, you can import and re-use them.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid\n  {...data}\n  slots={{\n    columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu,\n  }}\n/>`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} slots={{ columnMenu: CustomColumnMenu, }} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n**Tip**: The `columnMenu` component and its components slots receive the `colDef` prop corresponding to the current column; you can use this to conditionally render some items or change some logic.\n\n## [Disable column menu](#disable-column-menu)\n\nBy default, each column header has the column menu enabled. To disable the column menu, set the prop `disableColumnMenu={true}`.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGrid {...data} disableColumnMenu />`\n\n<DataGrid {...data} disableColumnMenu />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## Column menu with Pro/Premium features\n\nIn the following demo, in addition to Data Grid MIT features, you can see commercial features like [grouping](/x/react-data-grid/row-grouping/), [aggregation](/x/react-data-grid/aggregation/), and [computed columns](/x/react-data-grid/computed-columns/) in action. Try tweaking the values from respective column menu items.\n\nEdit code\n\n`<DataGridPremium\n  {...data}\n  apiRef={apiRef}\n  featureDependencies={{ formula: formulaFeature }}\n  groupingColDef={groupingColDef}\n  initialState={initialState}\n/>`\n\n<DataGridPremium {...data} apiRef={apiRef} featureDependencies={{ formula: formulaFeature }} groupingColDef={groupingColDef} initialState={initialState} />\n\nPress Enter to start editing\n\n## [API](#api)\n\n- [DataGrid](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid/)\n- [DataGridPro](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid-pro/)\n- [DataGridPremium](/x/api/data-grid/data-grid-premium/)"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01223Hz5QirvMbZhiyGKbxHD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
