omplete\n- TASK-12: Grading scales service + routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Categories service + route — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: Gradebook service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: Gradebook API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: Student grades service + route — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: Report card snapshot + access — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: Report card service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Report card API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Report card integration tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: Course tabs, student tabs, navigation entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: Admin grading scales page + ScaleEditorDialog — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: Course gradebook settings page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-24: Category Select in assignment and quiz editors — ✓ complete\n- TASK-25: AddManualItemDialog, TermOverrideDialog, ItemStatsDialog — ✓ complete\n- TASK-26: GradebookGrid (MIT DataGrid) + gradebook page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-27: StudentGradesView + its three host pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-28: ReportCardDocument, PrintButton, single and bulk print pages — ✓ complete\n- TASK-29: Admin report cards page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-30: Homeroom list + review page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-31: Student \"Report cards\" tab — ✓ complete\n- TASK-32: Seed (scale, 7A categories, backfill, Oral presentation, S1 comments, 7A drafts) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-33: Playwright gradebook.spec.ts + report-cards.spec.ts — ✓ complete\n\n### Verification\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm run lint` | ✔ no warnings or errors |\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | ✔ clean |\n| `next build` | ✔ |\n| New unit tests (`tests/unit/gradebook/*`) | 21/21 pass. Includes the FR-15 golden case (78.0 C+), 89.95 → 90.0 → A-, AC-2, AC-5, AC-6, A8, A12 and tz day boundaries. |\n| New integration tests (sync 8, backfill 1, report cards 5) against Postgres | 14/14 pass |\n| Existing assignment/quiz integration suites after the hooks | pass. assignments was rerun 3× after fixing the race in bug 1 below. |\n| Full `vitest run` | 402/409. 5 of the 7 failures are the pre-existing ones recorded by SH-9/SH-10: attendance-qa FR-22/FR-10, auth-forms, useToast, lockout, auth rate-limit. The other 2 are email-dispatch \"stuck in SENDING\" and qa-sh10 \"autosave < 50 ms\". Both pass when run on their own, twice. They are shared-DB / timing interference under the parallel full run, and neither imports gradebook code. |\n| Playwright `gradebook.spec.ts` + `report-cards.spec.ts` on a prod build (port 3100) | 2/2 pass. The specs cover: keyboard edits (digits+Enter, E, M, Delete) → 78.0% C+, with 6 `grade.update` audit rows; admin generate → publish → 2 notifications; parent print view with sidebar, app bar and print button hidden under `print` media. |\n| Seed | Against temporary 7A fixtures (MATH-7A/ENG-7A, 2 students), the seed creates: the scale, 3 categories per course, backfilled items (7) and grades (6), Oral presentation graded ×2, 4 S1 comment overrides and 2 DRAFT cards with snapshots. A rerun creates 0 items/grades. The fixtures were removed afterwards. The dev DB has no 7A courses, so `npm run db:seed` logs a skip, the same as the assignments/quizzes seeds. The \"Standard A–F\" default scale stays in the dev DB as seed data. |\n\n### Bugs found and fixed during verification\n1. **Concurrent `publishOnce` → duplicate item create.** The read path fires `publishOnce` fire-and-forget, and a second call raced it on `GradeItem.sourceId @unique`. This was caught by qa-sh9 under the full run. Item creation now uses `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })`, and in `publishOnce` the upsert runs only for the notifiedAt claim winner.\n2. **Grid edit wiped other cells.** In `processRowUpdate`, columns not present on the row object were read as \"cleared\", so entering the Exam score erased both HW scores (e2e showed 70.0 instead of 78.0). Only the edited field is now considered.\n3. **Server page called a function exported from a `'use client'` module.** The roster warning text (\"2 courses have ungraded items\", \"No teacher comment for X\") is now computed in `listReportCards` (`warningText`).\n\n### Decisions / deviations (for QA)\n- **Migration:** generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` (same reason as SH-10: the DB role can't create a shadow DB). The partial unique index was appended and the migration applied with `migrate deploy`. `db push` was not used.\n- **MUI lookups (NFR-7):** mui-mcp was reachable. The x-data-grid docs (column groups, column menu) were fetched. mui-mcp serves 9.17 docs, so every prop used (`columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, `onProcessRowUpdateError`, `isCellEditable`, `onCellKeyDown` + `defaultMuiPrevented`, `GridColumnMenu` slots/`displayOrder`, `hideMenu`, `hideFooter`) was also checked against the installed 9.5.0 `.d.ts`. No pinned columns are used.\n- **Grid editing:** the grid uses the DataGrid's built-in numeric edit cell (digits start editing, Enter/Tab commit and move, blur commits) instead of a custom `renderEditCell`. E / M / Delete are handled in `onCellKeyDown` in view mode. Saves are optimistic, with rollback and a per-cell error outline and tooltip.\n- **Lists use DataGrid directly** for scales and the admin report-card roster, not the shared `DataTable`. `DataTable` is URL/server-paginated and has a search box, which doesn't suit complete client-side lists. The contract requires the roster to be unpaginated for \"Publish all\".\n- **A7 visibility transitions:** `upsertItemFromAssignment/Quiz(db, id, { wasVisible })`. The hook passes the source's pre-write visibility, so plain edits never touch `isVisible`.\n- **Quiz hooks run after commit and never throw** (logged), like `notify()`. Assignment hooks run inside the caller's transaction, so `gradeSubmission`, `bulkReturn`, `gradeOffline`, `setExemption` and archive are now transactions.\n- **`syncQuizGrade`** sets the score back to null if a regrade leaves the student with no GRADED attempt.\n- **Snapshot builder signature** gained a `term` argument. The design listed 6 args, but the v1 shape needs term name/dates/year.\n- **Report card comment edits** are audited as `reportCard.comment`. Generation is audited as `reportCard.generate`. Both are extras beyond NFR-4.\n- **`/report-cards` for ADMIN** redirects to `/admin/report-cards`.\n- **Manual item date** is chosen with a DatePicker and stored as 23:59 school-local on that day.\n- **Out of scope noted, not built:** the optional perf integration test (35×80 < 800 ms, 600×8 < 30 s) listed as \"optional, CI-skippable\" in system-design §6 isn't in the plan's file list.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":71,"newStart":1,"newLines":75,"lines":["-# Dev Log — SH-10 (PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams)","+# Dev Log — SH-11 (PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards)"," ","-> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-9 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-9's).","-> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-10. This is SH-10's first dev iteration.","-> `dev-rerun-count.json` was left untouched (engine-owned).","+> Before this run, this file held the SH-10 log and `task-completion-markers.json` held SH-10's markers. Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-11. This is SH-11's first dev iteration.","+> `dev-rerun-count.json` was left untouched because the engine owns it."," "," ## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)"," ","-All 23 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in","-`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 51 matrix paths were verified on disk.","+All 33 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json`."," "," ### Checklist","-- TASK-1: Prisma schema + migration 20261110000000_add_quizzes (partial unique index) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-2: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete","-- TASK-3: Pure grading core grading.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete","-- TASK-4: Student serializers + no-`correct`-key unit test — ✓ complete","-- TASK-5: quiz.published / quiz.results_released types + 'quiz' file context — ✓ complete","-- TASK-6: access.ts assertCanAccessAttempt — ✓ complete","-- TASK-7: attempt-service.ts — ✓ complete","-- TASK-8: quiz-service.ts — ✓ complete","-- TASK-9: analytics.ts — ✓ complete","-- TASK-10: maintenance.ts + dispatch route wiring — ✓ complete","-- TASK-11: Quiz & question CRUD route handlers — ✓ complete","-- TASK-12: Regrade / release / analytics / accommodation routes — ✓ complete","-- TASK-13: Attempt route handlers — ✓ complete","-- TASK-14: Integration tests (attempts, regrade) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-15: Course Quizzes tab, list page, view, new page — ✓ complete","-- TASK-16: Quiz player, take page, useAutosave — ✓ complete","-- TASK-17: QuestionList + QuestionEditor — ✓ complete","-- TASK-18: Builder shell (edit page, QuizBuilder, QuizSettingsPanel) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-19: Attempt result page — ✓ complete","-- TASK-20: Manual grading page + workspace — ✓ complete","-- TASK-21: Analytics page + x-charts BarChart — ✓ complete","-- TASK-22: Seed: three quizzes (FR-36) — ✓ complete","-- TASK-23: Playwright e2e quizzes.spec.ts — ✓ complete","+- TASK-1: Prisma schema + migration 20261111000000_add_gradebook (partial unique index grading_scale_one_default) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-2: Zod validators src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts — ✓ complete","+- TASK-3: Pure Decimal grade-calc.ts + unit matrix — ✓ complete","+- TASK-4: term-placement.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-5: gradebook-sync.ts (item/grade sync + pure row builders) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-6: Assignment hooks + categoryId in assignment validators — ✓ complete","+- TASK-7: Quiz hooks (quiz-service, attempt-service, maintenance) + categoryId in quiz validators — ✓ complete","+- TASK-8: Sync integration tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-9: Backfill module, CLI script, npm script, idempotency test — ✓ complete","+- TASK-10: Batched loader load.ts — ✓ complete","+- TASK-11: grade.posted / report_card.published notification types — ✓ complete","+- TASK-12: Grading scales service + routes — ✓ complete","+- TASK-13: Categories service + route — ✓ complete","+- TASK-14: Gradebook service — ✓ complete","+- TASK-15: Gradebook API routes — ✓ complete","+- TASK-16: Student grades service + route — ✓ complete","+- TASK-17: Report card snapshot + access — ✓ complete","+- TASK-18: Report card service — ✓ complete","+- TASK-19: Report card API routes — ✓ complete","+- TASK-20: Report card integration tests — ✓ complete","+- TASK-21: Course tabs, student tabs, navigation entries — ✓ complete","+- TASK-22: Admin grading scales page + ScaleEditorDialog — ✓ complete","+- TASK-23: Course gradebook settings page — ✓ complete","+- TASK-24: Category Select in assignment and quiz editors — ✓ complete","+- TASK-25: AddManualItemDialog, TermOverrideDialog, ItemStatsDialog — ✓ complete","+- TASK-26: GradebookGrid (MIT DataGrid) + gradebook page — ✓ complete","+- TASK-27: StudentGradesView + its three host pages — ✓ complete","+- TASK-28: ReportCardDocument, PrintButton, single and bulk print pages — ✓ complete","+- TASK-29: Admin report cards page — ✓ complete","+- TASK-30: Homeroom list + review page — ✓ complete","+- TASK-31: Student \"Report cards\" tab — ✓ complete","+- TASK-32: Seed (scale, 7A categories, backfill, Oral presentation, S1 comments, 7A drafts) — ✓ complete","+- TASK-33: Playwright gradebook.spec.ts + report-cards.spec.ts — ✓ complete"," "," ### Verification"," | Check | Result |"," |---|---|","-| `npm run lint` | ✔ no warnings/errors |","+| `npm run lint` | ✔ no warnings or errors |"," | `npx tsc --noEmit` | ✔ clean |","-| `tests/unit/quiz/*` (validators, grading, serializers) | 37/37 pass |","-| `tests/integration/quiz/*` against Postgres (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`) | 8/8 pass; rerun 6× to shake out races (see bug 1 below) |","-| Full `vitest run` | 361/366. The 5–6 failures are the **same pre-existing ones recorded in the SH-9 QA report** (attendance-qa FR-22 / FR-10, auth-forms, useToast, lockout under Node 24, auth rate-limit flake). None import quiz code. |","-| `next build` | ✔ (the \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines are pre-existing static-render noise from other routes) |","-| `tests/e2e/quizzes.spec.ts` on a prod build (port 3100) | 4/4 pass on two consecutive runs. A third back-to-back run fails at `signInAs` because the 10-per-IP login rate limiter trips — helper limitation, not quiz code. |","-| Seed | Verified against temporary MATH-7A / ENG-7A fixtures: creates Fractions Check (8 q, CLOSED, every enrolled student GRADED), Unit 1 Test (12 q incl. 2 essays, AFTER_CLOSE, open 3 days, no attempts), Parts of Speech (5 q, practice, 3 attempts, HIGHEST). A rerun creates 0 (idempotent). Fixtures removed afterwards. The dev DB has no courses, so `npm run db:seed` skips quizzes with a message, same as the assignments seed. |","+| `next build` | ✔ |","+| New unit tests (`tests/unit/gradebook/*`) | 21/21 pass. Includes the FR-15 golden case (78.0 C+), 89.95 → 90.0 → A-, AC-2, AC-5, AC-6, A8, A12 and tz day boundaries. |","+| New integration tests (sync 8, backfill 1, report cards 5) against Postgres | 14/14 pass |","+| Existing assignment/quiz integration suites after the hooks | pass. assignments was rerun 3× after fixing the race in bug 1 below. |","+| Full `vitest run` | 402/409. 5 of the 7 failures are the pre-existing ones recorded by SH-9/SH-10: attendance-qa FR-22/FR-10, auth-forms, useToast, lockout, auth rate-limit. The other 2 are email-dispatch \"stuck in SENDING\" and qa-sh10 \"autosave < 50 ms\". Both pass when run on their own, twice. They are shared-DB / timing interference under the parallel full run, and neither imports gradebook code. |","+| Playwright `gradebook.spec.ts` + `report-cards.spec.ts` on a prod build (port 3100) | 2/2 pass. The specs cover: keyboard edits (digits+Enter, E, M, Delete) → 78.0% C+, with 6 `grade.update` audit rows; admin generate → publish → 2 notifications; parent print view with sidebar, app bar and print button hidden under `print` media. |","+| Seed | Against temporary 7A fixtures (MATH-7A/ENG-7A, 2 students), the seed creates: the scale, 3 categories per course, backfilled items (7) and grades (6), Oral presentation graded ×2, 4 S1 comment overrides and 2 DRAFT cards with snapshots. A rerun creates 0 items/grades. The fixtures were removed afterwards. The dev DB has no 7A courses, so `npm run db:seed` logs a skip, the same as the assignments/quizzes seeds. The \"Standard A–F\" default scale stays in the dev DB as seed data. |"," "," ### Bugs found and fixed during verification","-1. **Concurrent start → false \"attempts used up\" (FR-19).** Tab B could miss tab A's attempt in its in-progress check, then count it and hit the attempt limit. `startOrResumeAttempt` now re-checks for an IN_PROGRESS attempt before refusing.","-2. **Reload inside the 800 ms debounce lost the last answer (FR-15/FR-19, AC-2).** `useAutosave` now writes each change to `localStorage['quiz-attempt:<id>']` immediately and removes it on a 2xx. The pill shows \"Saving…\" during the debounce, and \"Offline\" only after a send has failed. Before this, \"All answers saved\" appeared while the debounce was still pending. Caught by the e2e reload step.","-3. **DecimalError 500 on non-numeric points.** zod runs chained `.refine`s even after one fails, so `dec('')` threw. `halfStep` in `validators/quiz.ts` is now a single short-circuiting `superRefine`, with a regression test. Caught by the e2e grading step.","-4. **Save-status chip contrast.** The theme's `success` chip measured 3.53:1 (axe, serious). The pill is now an outlined default-colour chip with Cloud icons.","+1. **Concurrent `publishOnce` → duplicate item create.** The read path fires `publishOnce` fire-and-forget, and a second call raced it on `GradeItem.sourceId @unique`. This was caught by qa-sh9 under the full run. Item creation now uses `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })`, and in `publishOnce` the upsert runs only for the notifiedAt claim winner.","+2. **Grid edit wiped other cells.** In `processRowUpdate`, columns not present on the row object were read as \"cleared\", so entering the Exam score erased both HW scores (e2e showed 70.0 instead of 78.0). Only the edited field is now considered.","+3. **Server page called a function exported from a `'use client'` module.** The roster warning text (\"2 courses have ungraded items\", \"No teacher comment for X\") is now computed in `listReportCards` (`warningText`)."," "," ### Decisions / deviations (for QA)","-- **Migration generation:** `prisma migrate dev --create-only` failed because the DB role can't create a shadow database. The SQL came from `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` against the up-to-date DB instead. The raw partial unique index was appended, and the migration was applied with `migrate deploy`; there was no `db push` (ADR-2). The post-apply diff is empty.","-- **NOT_FOUND hiding (NFR-5):** `course-access.ts` throws FORBIDDEN, so `quiz/access.ts` wraps it (`viewCourseOrNotFound` / `manageCourseOrNotFound`) and maps it to NOT_FOUND for every quiz resource.","-- **Lazy auto-submit uses the 30 s grace** (`deadlineAt + ANSWER_GRACE_MS`), the same as the maintenance sweep. A GET inside the grace window therefore doesn't race the client's final save.","-- **Edit lock compares values, not keys:** the builder sends the whole question, so the lock only rejects keys whose values actually changed.","-- **Prompt images (FR-39):** they are uploaded with context `'quiz'` and embedded as `![](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. On question save, the service attaches the referenced unattached `quiz` files the caller owns (contextId = quizId), so `quizResolver` controls who can read them.","-- **Accommodations table and analytics per-question table use MUI `Table`, not the shared `DataTable`.** DataTable is URL-paginated and server-driven, and these are small in-memory lists that need editable cells. Both are documented MUI components (NFR-4).","-- **Extra service exports beyond the plan's lists** (all in owned files): `listManagerAttempts`, `listOwnAttempts`, `listAccommodations`, `getAttemptView`, `submitForStudent`, `ensureQuizAttemptsNotExpired`, `notifyResultsReleased`, and manager serializers (`toManagerQuestion/Answer/Attempt`). These are what the server pages need. No new files or dependencies were added.","-- **Attempt ids** are cuid-shaped (`c` + base36 time + 16 hex chars) and generated up front for the shuffle seed. No cuid package is installed (marked with a `ponytail:` comment).","-- **mui-mcp (ADR-7):** reachable. Docs fetched: x-charts Bars (first x-charts use), RadioGroup, LinearProgress, Tooltip. The other components follow the usage already established in the codebase.","-- **E2E:** the window, title and visibility are set through Prisma after `/new` creates the draft, because the DateTimePicker is fiddly to drive. Questions, publish, take, reload, submit and grading all go through the UI. The axe scan is scoped to `<main>`, because the app-shell sidebar `<ul>` has a pre-existing `list` violation.","-","-### Observed, not in SH-10 scope","-- `renderEmail` (PRD-04) sometimes emits NUL bytes in react-email's preview padding. Postgres then rejects the `EmailOutbox` insert (`22021`). `notify()` logs and swallows the error, so in-app notifications still land. This appeared in integration runs for `quiz.results_released` emails.","-- `validators/assignments.ts` `decimal()` uses the same chained-refine pattern as bug 3, so it probably throws a DecimalError on non-numeric input too.","-- The app-shell sidebar has an axe `list` violation (serious).","-- `saveAnswer` vs submit race: an upsert landing after the submit claim is left ungraded until a Regrade. Marked with a `ponytail:` comment.","+- **Migration:** generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` (same reason as SH-10: the DB role can't create a shadow DB). The partial unique index was appended and the migration applied with `migrate deploy`. `db push` was not used.","+- **MUI lookups (NFR-7):** mui-mcp was reachable. The x-data-grid docs (column groups, column menu) were fetched. mui-mcp serves 9.17 docs, so every prop used (`columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, `onProcessRowUpdateError`, `isCellEditable`, `onCellKeyDown` + `defaultMuiPrevented`, `GridColumnMenu` slots/`displayOrder`, `hideMenu`, `hideFooter`) was also checked against the installed 9.5.0 `.d.ts`. No pinned columns are used.","+- **Grid editing:** the grid uses the DataGrid's built-in numeric edit cell (digits start editing, Enter/Tab commit and move, blur commits) instead of a custom `renderEditCell`. E / M / Delete are handled in `onCellKeyDown` in view mode. Saves are optimistic, with rollback and a per-cell error outline and tooltip.","+- **Lists use DataGrid directly** for scales and the admin report-card roster, not the shared `DataTable`. `DataTable` is URL/server-paginated and has a search box, which doesn't suit complete client-side lists. The contract requires the roster to be unpaginated for \"Publish all\".","+- **A7 visibility transitions:** `upsertItemFromAssignment/Quiz(db, id, { wasVisible })`. The hook passes the source's pre-write visibility, so plain edits never touch `isVisible`.","+- **Quiz hooks run after commit and never throw** (logged), like `notify()`. Assignment hooks run inside the caller's transaction, so `gradeSubmission`, `bulkReturn`, `gradeOffline`, `setExemption` and archive are now transactions.","+- **`syncQuizGrade`** sets the score back to null if a regrade leaves the student with no GRADED attempt.","+- **Snapshot builder signature** gained a `term` argument. The design listed 6 args, but the v1 shape needs term name/dates/year.","+- **Report card comment edits** are audited as `reportCard.comment`. Generation is audited as `reportCard.generate`. Both are extras beyond NFR-4.","+- **`/report-cards` for ADMIN** redirects to `/admin/report-cards`.","+- **Manual item date** is chosen with a DatePicker and stored as 23:59 school-local on that day.","+- **Out of scope noted, not built:** the optional perf integration test (35×80 < 800 ms, 600×8 < 30 s) listed as \"optional, CI-skippable\" in system-design §6 isn't in the plan's file list."]}],"originalFile":"# Dev Log — SH-10 (PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams)\n\n> The previous content of this file was the stale SH-9 log (and `task-completion-markers.json` was SH-9's).\n> Following the established precedent, both were replaced for SH-10. This is SH-10's first dev iteration.\n> `dev-rerun-count.json` was left untouched (engine-owned).\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-09)\n\nAll 23 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in\n`file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 51 matrix paths were verified on disk.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma schema + migration 20261110000000_add_quizzes (partial unique index) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Zod validators + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: Pure grading core grading.ts + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Student serializers + no-`correct`-key unit test — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: quiz.published / quiz.results_released types + 'quiz' file context — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: access.ts assertCanAccessAttempt — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: attempt-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: quiz-service.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: analytics.ts — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: maintenance.ts + dispatch route wiring — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Quiz & question CRUD route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: Regrade / release / analytics / accommodation routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Attempt route handlers — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: Integration tests (attempts, regrade) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: Course Quizzes tab, list page, view, new page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: Quiz player, take page, useAutosave — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: QuestionList + QuestionEditor — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: Builder shell (edit page, QuizBuilder, QuizSettingsPanel) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Attempt result page — ✓ complete\n- TASK-20: Manual grading page + workspace — ✓ complete\n- TASK-21: Analytics page + x-charts BarChart — ✓ complete\n- TASK-22: Seed: three quizzes (FR-36) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-23: Playwright e2e quizzes.spec.ts — ✓ complete\n\n### Verification\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm run lint` | ✔ no warnings/errors |\n| `npx tsc --noEmit` | ✔ clean |\n| `tests/unit/quiz/*` (validators, grading, serializers) | 37/37 pass |\n| `tests/integration/quiz/*` against Postgres (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`) | 8/8 pass; rerun 6× to shake out races (see bug 1 below) |\n| Full `vitest run` | 361/366. The 5–6 failures are the **same pre-existing ones recorded in the SH-9 QA report** (attendance-qa FR-22 / FR-10, auth-forms, useToast, lockout under Node 24, auth rate-limit flake). None import quiz code. |\n| `next build` | ✔ (the \"Dynamic server usage\" log lines are pre-existing static-render noise from other routes) |\n| `tests/e2e/quizzes.spec.ts` on a prod build (port 3100) | 4/4 pass on two consecutive runs. A third back-to-back run fails at `signInAs` because the 10-per-IP login rate limiter trips — helper limitation, not quiz code. |\n| Seed | Verified against temporary MATH-7A / ENG-7A fixtures: creates Fractions Check (8 q, CLOSED, every enrolled student GRADED), Unit 1 Test (12 q incl. 2 essays, AFTER_CLOSE, open 3 days, no attempts), Parts of Speech (5 q, practice, 3 attempts, HIGHEST). A rerun creates 0 (idempotent). Fixtures removed afterwards. The dev DB has no courses, so `npm run db:seed` skips quizzes with a message, same as the assignments seed. |\n\n### Bugs found and fixed during verification\n1. **Concurrent start → false \"attempts used up\" (FR-19).** Tab B could miss tab A's attempt in its in-progress check, then count it and hit the attempt limit. `startOrResumeAttempt` now re-checks for an IN_PROGRESS attempt before refusing.\n2. **Reload inside the 800 ms debounce lost the last answer (FR-15/FR-19, AC-2).** `useAutosave` now writes each change to `localStorage['quiz-attempt:<id>']` immediately and removes it on a 2xx. The pill shows \"Saving…\" during the debounce, and \"Offline\" only after a send has failed. Before this, \"All answers saved\" appeared while the debounce was still pending. Caught by the e2e reload step.\n3. **DecimalError 500 on non-numeric points.** zod runs chained `.refine`s even after one fails, so `dec('')` threw. `halfStep` in `validators/quiz.ts` is now a single short-circuiting `superRefine`, with a regression test. Caught by the e2e grading step.\n4. **Save-status chip contrast.** The theme's `success` chip measured 3.53:1 (axe, serious). The pill is now an outlined default-colour chip with Cloud icons.\n\n### Decisions / deviations (for QA)\n- **Migration generation:** `prisma migrate dev --create-only` failed because the DB role can't create a shadow database. The SQL came from `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel` against the up-to-date DB instead. The raw partial unique index was appended, and the migration was applied with `migrate deploy`; there was no `db push` (ADR-2). The post-apply diff is empty.\n- **NOT_FOUND hiding (NFR-5):** `course-access.ts` throws FORBIDDEN, so `quiz/access.ts` wraps it (`viewCourseOrNotFound` / `manageCourseOrNotFound`) and maps it to NOT_FOUND for every quiz resource.\n- **Lazy auto-submit uses the 30 s grace** (`deadlineAt + ANSWER_GRACE_MS`), the same as the maintenance sweep. A GET inside the grace window therefore doesn't race the client's final save.\n- **Edit lock compares values, not keys:** the builder sends the whole question, so the lock only rejects keys whose values actually changed.\n- **Prompt images (FR-39):** they are uploaded with context `'quiz'` and embedded as `![](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. On question save, the service attaches the referenced unattached `quiz` files the caller owns (contextId = quizId), so `quizResolver` controls who can read them.\n- **Accommodations table and analytics per-question table use MUI `Table`, not the shared `DataTable`.** DataTable is URL-paginated and server-driven, and these are small in-memory lists that need editable cells. Both are documented MUI components (NFR-4).\n- **Extra service exports beyond the plan's lists** (all in owned files): `listManagerAttempts`, `listOwnAttempts`, `listAccommodations`, `getAttemptView`, `submitForStudent`, `ensureQuizAttemptsNotExpired`, `notifyResultsReleased`, and manager serializers (`toManagerQuestion/Answer/Attempt`). These are what the server pages need. No new files or dependencies were added.\n- **Attempt ids** are cuid-shaped (`c` + base36 time + 16 hex chars) and generated up front for the shuffle seed. No cuid package is installed (marked with a `ponytail:` comment).\n- **mui-mcp (ADR-7):** reachable. Docs fetched: x-charts Bars (first x-charts use), RadioGroup, LinearProgress, Tooltip. The other components follow the usage already established in the codebase.\n- **E2E:** the window, title and visibility are set through Prisma after `/new` creates the draft, because the DateTimePicker is fiddly to drive. Questions, publish, take, reload, submit and grading all go through the UI. The axe scan is scoped to `<main>`, because the app-shell sidebar `<ul>` has a pre-existing `list` violation.\n\n### Observed, not in SH-10 scope\n- `renderEmail` (PRD-04) sometimes emits NUL bytes in react-email's preview padding. Postgres then rejects the `EmailOutbox` insert (`22021`). `notify()` logs and swallows the error, so in-app notifications still land. This appeared in integration runs for `quiz.results_released` emails.\n- `validators/assignments.ts` `decimal()` uses the same chained-refine pattern as bug 3, so it probably throws a DecimalError on non-numeric input too.\n- The app-shell sidebar has an axe `list` violation (serious).\n- `saveAnswer` vs submit race: an upsert landing after the submit claim is left ungraded until a Regrade. Marked with a `ponytail:` comment.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013wqzVZQiVpHVpSLMVkHVJ7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
