{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsU7B3bSk5qcRgPhuC2y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 33 SH-11 tasks are implemented at the paths in the file ownership matrix, and every listed file exists. Lint, typecheck and the production build all pass with no errors.\n\n**Tests:**\n- **New unit tests:** 21/21 pass, including the 78.0% C+ golden case, 89.95 → 90.0 → A−, drop-lowest, missing/excused and overrides.\n- **New integration tests:** 14/14 pass (sync, backfill, report cards) against the local Postgres.\n- **New Playwright specs:** both pass on a production build. They cover a teacher entering grades by keyboard (ending on 78.0% C+), an admin generating and publishing report cards, and a parent opening the print view with the sidebar hidden.\n- **Full suite:** 402/409 pass. Five failures are ones the SH-9/SH-10 logs already recorded. The other two (email dispatch \"stuck in SENDING\" and the quiz autosave < 50 ms timing check) failed only in the full parallel run. Each passed twice on its own, and neither touches gradebook code. My report-card tests do add email rows to the shared outbox, which may contribute to the email-dispatch one.\n\n**Bugs I found and fixed while verifying:**\n- **Duplicate gradebook item:** two overlapping assignment-publish calls could both try to create the same item. Creation now tolerates the duplicate, and only the call that wins the publish claim creates it.\n- **Grid erasing scores:** entering one score in the gradebook wiped the student's other scores in that row. Only the cell actually edited is saved now.\n- **Server page calling client code:** the teacher's report-card list called a function from a browser-only module, which would fail at runtime. The warning text is now built on the server.\n\n**Seed:** the dev database has no 7A courses, so `npm run db:seed` skips the gradebook demo data with a log message, like the existing assignment and quiz seeds. I checked the full path against temporary 7A courses: a rerun added no items or grades. I then removed those temporary courses. The \"Standard A–F\" default scale stays in the dev database as seed data.\n\n**Where I departed from the design:**\n- **Grid editing:** cells use the grid's built-in number editor rather than a custom edit cell. E (excused), M (missing) and Delete are handled as key presses. Saves show immediately and roll back with a red outline on the cell if the server rejects them.\n- **List pages:** the grading-scales page and the admin report-card list use the data grid directly, not the shared `DataTable`. `DataTable` pages and searches on the server, but \"Publish all\" needs the whole filtered list loaded at once.\n- **Migration:** generated with `prisma migrate diff`, because the database user can't create a shadow database (same as SH-10). It was applied with `migrate deploy`, never `db push`.\n- **Not built:** the optional performance test (35 students × 80 items, 600 × 8 report cards) from the system design wasn't in the task list.\n\nThe full log with the task checklist is in `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md`. All 33 IDs are in `artifacts/dev/task-completion-markers.json` under ticket SH-11. I didn't touch `dev-rerun-count.json`, and nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1203,"cache_read_input_tokens":420584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1203,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6f85ae0-4ad4-4d10-b797-6ff9d3e2b1f5","uuid":"c97d56a3-de12-4da5-960a-bd5e479db951","timestamp":"2026-11-09T13:55:15.500Z","request_id":"req_011CgsU7AjyT9NV4zjyK13Ar"}
